  Observe reach_scene at runners_reach when true "Inside the curve of the thirtieth link the runners have bolted a platform of planks, and on it a shrine: a horseshoe of iron, five candles, five names cut on a board: the links they have cut since 2715. The Chain sways a few metres, slowly. Below, Hornwake is a horseshoe of toys.".
  Observe wet_scene at wet_cradle when true "Inside the cloud. A Concord rest-cradle of iron, older than anything else on the Chain, hung inside the curve of a link. Everything is wet; everything drips. Where the sixty-first link and the sixty-second grind together, just above you, the grinding has words in it.".
  Observe swing_scene at the_swing when true "Above the cloud, in the swing. The Chain moves tens of metres with every gust, slowly, so that the whole world tilts and comes back. The air is thin. The Linkmoot here is silent, or asleep, or listening.".
  Observe cradles_scene at cable_cradles when true "The cable-cradles: great troughs cut into the granite underside of Hightown, and in them the first link of the Chain, held as a bow is held. Inside the curve of that link, riveted, a tally-chain. Above you the mountain's underside goes off in every direction, ribbed, like the inside of a bowl turned over.".
  Hazard chain_ice "ice on the links" means "Deal (1d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  // The ice strikes whoever comes up into the cloud. (A long way kept dangerous by a thing on it turns the company back
  // on the way, so the ice is met on arrival instead.)
  Relation iced(group).
  Rule ice_on_the_links when at(party, wet_cradle) and not iced(party)
    says "The links in the cloud are glazed with ice, and your hands are numb before you are halfway. Somebody slips, and hangs, and is hauled in." {
    Assert iced(party). Assert strikes(chain_ice, party).
  }
  Rule ice_forgotten when iced(party) and not at(party, wet_cradle) { Retract iced(party). }

  // Links 61 and 62 remember the first campaign, and the night of 2641.
  Person hask "Hask of the Sixty-First Link" at wet_cradle {
    Role "a soul bound in the Chain, speaking where the links grind". Peaceable.
  }
  Topic hask_rise with hask "Ask Hask what happened to the Chain on the night of the Unfall" when true once {
    Says "The grinding of iron on iron makes words, slowly. 'The star tore loose and went,' says Hask. 'We felt it go. Like a tooth. The horn broke and the whole of us went up, all of us, the mountain and all, up and up, until enough of us hung in the air to hold it.' A long grind. 'Since then they cut us off the bottom, one by one. Every one they cut, we go up a little, and the ones in it go quiet. One more, in this cold. One. Two, and we all go up and never stop. I told the Teake woman. She thinks I'm mad. Some of us are.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, cut_limit). }
  }
  Action read_first_tally(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Teshen to read the tally inside the first link" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cable_cradles) and travelsWith(teshen, actor)
      and not knows(actor, first_tally).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, first_tally). }
    Result "Teshen hooks her arm through the link and reads with her free hand, two and a half kilometres up, as calmly as at her grandmother's hearth. 'Drevka Venmort holds the last,' she finishes. She looks down, a long way down, at the horn. 'She did, too. Grandmother met her.'".
  }
  Discovery first_tally "The tally riveted in the first link at the cradles, read by touch: 'Hearth Orrisk and the hearths hold the star. Four thousand and one hundred hold. Iron holds iron. Bone holds iron. The water-people talked. Drevka Venmort holds the last.'".
}

data/adventures/let-one-remember/keld.ky:
Module corrow "Let One Remember" {
  Description "Keld: thirty corbelled houses in a cluster of sinkholes, whose people came back from the Margin in 2606 and cannot be forgotten.".

  Place saska_b "Mother Saska's hearth" is building within keld.
  Place bede_b "Bede Orrisk's forge" is building within keld.
  Place keld_green "the sinkhole green" is room within keld at 1, 1.
  Place keld_road "the Keld end of the drove road" is room within keld at 2, 1.
  Place west_field "the west field" is room within keld at 0, 1.
  Place keld_chapel "the Hold chapel at Keld" is room within keld at 1, 0.
  Place saska_hearth "Mother Saska's hearth" is room within saska_b at 1, 2.
  Place bede_forge "Bede Orrisk's forge" is room within bede_b at 2, 2.

  Passage keld_drove "the drove road over the sinkhole country" is road between drove_gate and keld_road taking 6 hours.
  Passage keld_in "the way down into the green" is steps between keld_road and keld_green.
  Passage field_gate "the west field gate" is gate between keld_green and west_field.
  Passage chapel_steps "the chapel steps" is steps between keld_green and keld_chapel.
  Passage saska_door "Mother Saska's door" is door between keld_green and saska_hearth.
  Passage forge_door "the forge door" is door between keld_green and bede_forge.

  Observe keld_road_scene at keld_road when true "The drove road comes over the last rise and there is Keld: no village to be seen at all, only turf roofs in the bottoms of a cluster of sinkholes, with smoke coming up out of the ground.".
  Observe keld_green_scene at keld_green when true "The sinkhole green: a bowl of short turf with houses sunk round its rim, corbelled stone roofed with turf, juniper on every sill. Children in wool cut in a fashion two thousand years old are playing with a ball from Wendmouth. Every face that turns to look at you, you will remember. You can feel it happening.".
  Observe west_field_scene at west_field when true "A walled field on the west side of Keld, sheep-cropped, the wall walked aloud every spring. Its gate is tied with juniper.".
  Observe chapel_k_scene at keld_chapel when true "A Concord chapel of the Hold: a corbelled room with skulls in niches round its wall, each with a name scratched above it and a fresh sprig of juniper. The newest skull is ninety years old. People are looked at here.".
  Observe saska_scene at saska_hearth when true "A corbelled hall with a central hearth and skulls in the north wall. An old woman sits by the fire in a chair with arms, very upright, with a girl of nineteen sitting on the hearthstone at her feet with a book she is not reading.".
  Observe saska_settling at saska_hearth when settling(saska_hearth) "There is a man sitting in the second chair by the fire, quite at home, mending a harness. Nobody remarks on him. When you look at him you cannot quite remember when he came in, or whether he was always there.".
  Observe forge_scene_k at bede_forge when true "A cold forge: no hearth fire, because what Bede Orrisk works does not soften in fire. A water-hammer, idle. Drifts and punches in racks, all of them worn bright. On a hook by the bed, where he can reach it in the night, a smith's hammer of black iron that drinks the lamplight.".

  Person saska "Mother Saska" at saska_hearth {
    Role "eldest of Keld". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
  }
  Person teshen "Teshen" at saska_hearth {
    Role "Saska's granddaughter, nineteen, who wants to go somewhere nobody knows her". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Peaceable.
    Joins "Teshen is on her feet before you have finished asking. 'Two silver a day,' she says, 'and I read the chains, and I don't lie, and nobody we meet will ever forget me.' She takes her coat off the peg. 'You'll get used to it.'".
  }
  Person bede "Bede Orrisk" at bede_forge {
    Role "the last cold-forger of deadiron, eighty-four". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
  }
  Person keldfolk "the people of Keld" at keld_green {
    Role "Keld households". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Initially Set hire(teshen) to 2.

  Topic saska_kept with saska "Ask Mother Saska how the Keld speak of the past" when true once {
    Says "'Carefully,' says Mother Saska. 'When I say a thing was kept, I saw it. When I say it was laid, it is in stone and I have read it. When I say it was let, somebody told me, or I have let it go, and you may weigh it as you like.' She looks at you. 'The Calvessa spoke so. We came back from the grey still speaking so. It makes us bad liars and good witnesses, and the valley does not love us for either.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, evidential_known). }
  }
  Topic saska_strays with saska "Ask Mother Saska about the Strays in the fields" when true once {
    Says "'They come at dawn,' says Saska. 'Three, four. They stand at the edge of the west field and look at the houses. Things that went into the grey all the way and came back with nothing: no name, no place, no people.' Her hands are still on the chair-arms. 'They want belonging, and we are made of it. My grandmother said they mutter. They do. Always the same word, each one his own word.' She will not say what the words are.".
  }
  Topic saska_syllable with saska "Ask Mother Saska what she has sworn never to say" when true once {
    Says "The fire ticks. 'My grandmother heard a thing said, in the grey, before they brought her back,' says Saska. 'One piece of a name. She said it once to me, when I was eight, and made me swear. I have kept it seventy years by never saying it.' She smiles very slightly. 'A man from the consulate in Wendmouth came to ask me about the grey last month. A pleasant man. The dogs did not bark at him. I have been thinking about that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, webb_at_keld). }
  }
  Discovery webb_at_keld "Corin Webb of the Lusk consulate has been to Keld asking Mother Saska about the grey; the Keld dogs did not bark at him.".
  Topic saska_hollow with saska "Ask Mother Saska how many came back from Keld Hollow" when true once {
    Says "'A hundred and forty,' says Saska. 'Out of a hundred and forty-one. The one they never found was a young man, Corin, son of the Hollow's reeve, who had gone out to the far field when the fog came and was not in the village with the rest. They called and called for him.' She looks into the fire. 'The anchors could not hold a name nobody had seen for two hundred years, they said. He stayed.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hollow_missing). }
  }
  Discovery hollow_missing "Of the hundred and forty-one people of Keld Hollow, the 2606 expedition brought back a hundred and forty. The one left in the grey was Corin, son of the Hollow's reeve, who had gone out to the far field when the fog came.".
  Topic saska_lift with saska "Tell Mother Saska what you know of where Hightown came from" when knows(actor, origin_known) and not knows(actor, method_known) once {
    Says "Saska is quiet a long time. 'So you know,' she says. 'Then you had better know the rest, or you will do harm with it.' She speaks as if reciting. 'It was kept, by my grandmother's grandmother, who had it from hers, who lived in 412, when the Lift was three lifetimes back and the Concord engineers still walked the Drag: if ever the mountain must come down, it comes down as its people come to know their place. Not all at once. Let one remember at a time.' She lets out her breath. 'Kept, not let. Weigh it so.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, method_known). }
  }

  // Teshen: the restless child, who cannot be forgotten, and who met the real secretary.
  Topic teshen_stranger with teshen "Ask Teshen what she wants" when not travelsWith(teshen, actor) once {
    Says "'To be a stranger,' says Teshen. 'Do you know what it's like to never be a stranger? Everyone I have ever met remembers my face for life. If I went to the Hartmark I'd be the girl from Keld by the second day and they'd remember me at ninety.' She shuts the book. 'I'd give an arm to be forgotten for a week. Failing that, I'd go anywhere with anyone who's going somewhere.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(teshen, actor). }
  }
  Topic teshen_secretary with teshen "Ask Teshen whether she knows the consul's secretary in Wendmouth" when knows(actor, displaced_clerk) or knows(actor, payroll_known) or knows(actor, webb_at_keld) {
    Says "'I witnessed a land deal at the consulate in 2729,' says Teshen. 'The secretary was a tall man with a cough who apologised for the ink. Absalom, they called him.' She frowns. 'Grandmother says the man who came here is called Webb and has been secretary for eleven years. He's short and he doesn't cough. I remember everyone. I can't help it.' She looks at you. 'Somebody's wrong, and it isn't me.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, webb_wrong_face). }
  }
  Discovery webb_wrong_face "Teshen of Keld, who cannot forget a face, witnessed a deal at the Lusk consulate in 2729 before a secretary called Absalom, tall, with a cough; Corin Webb is short and does not cough.".

  Topic teshen_grey with teshen "Ask Teshen whether she still wants to be forgotten" when travelsWith(teshen, actor) and knows(actor, open_hand_plan) once {
    Says "Teshen walks a while without answering. 'There's one place I'd be a stranger,' she says. 'Across the lake at the bottom of the low road. Over there nobody remembers anybody; that's what it is.' She glances at you. 'My great-great-grandmother came back from it with the rest of the Hollow, and none of us has been forgettable since. If I went in, I'd be the first Keld in a hundred and twenty years that nobody could see.' She shrugs, too carefully. 'If I came out, I'd be the same as ever. If I didn't, I'd be a stranger for good.'".
  }

  // The Strays, at dawn, at the edge of the west field.
  Person strays "the Strays" at limbo {
    Role "people who came back from the grey with nothing". Ancestry human. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
  }
  Rule strays_come when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 9 and at(strays, limbo) and not namedStrays(keld) and not strayTaken(keld) { Assert at(strays, west_field). }
  Rule strays_go when (hour(clock) < 6 or hour(clock) >= 9) and at(strays, west_field) { Assert at(strays, limbo). }
  Relation namedStrays(place). Relation strayTaken(place).
  // In the fourth week the Open Hand come for the Strays at Keld, with ropes and kindness, and take them to the Grey
  // Mile to listen to them.
  Rule strays_taken when watch(clock) >= 3168 and not namedStrays(keld) and not strayTaken(keld) and not turned(ferran)
    says "Word comes up the drove road: grey-coated people from the Open Hand were at Keld at dawn with a cart, and took the three Strays out of the west field, gently, the way you would take a lost child home, and the Keld stood at their doors and let them." {
    Assert strayTaken(keld). Assert at(strays, grey_mile).
  }
  Observe strays_scene at west_field when at(strays, west_field) "At the edge of the west field, just inside the wall, three people stand in the grass and look at the houses of Keld. Their clothes are of no fashion at all. Their faces are of no family. Your eye slides off them the way a hand slides off wet glass. Each is saying something under his breath, over and over.".
  Topic strays_listen with strays "Listen to what the Strays are saying" when at(strays, west_field) once {
    Says "You stand close enough to hear. Each of them is saying one syllable, over and over, as a child says a word to keep from losing it. Three different syllables. None of them is a word. When you step closer the nearest one turns to you, and looks at you as a hungry man looks at a lit window.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, stray_syllables). }
  }
  Discovery stray_syllables "Each of the Strays at Keld mutters one syllable over and over, each his own; together they are pieces of something.".
  Action name_strays(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Teshen to give each Stray a name and a place, aloud, as the Keld do" {
    Description "A Stray named aloud by someone who means it, and given a place, stops taking.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(strays, site) and travelsWith(teshen, actor)
      and not namedStrays(keld).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert namedStrays(keld). Assert at(strays, keld_green). }
    Result "Teshen walks up to the first of them and takes his hands, and he lets her. 'You're Tam,' she says. 'Tam of the west field. You sleep in the byre at Hallows' and you help with the lambing.' The man's face does something, slowly, like water settling. She does it three times, three names, three places. When she is done, three people walk into Keld behind her, and one of them is crying, and none of them is muttering anything at all.".
  }
  Observe strays_named at keld_green when namedStrays(keld) "Three newcomers are being shown how a Keld house is kept: Tam, Ollo and Mag, whom nobody knew this morning and everyone now greets by name.".

  // Bede Orrisk, and Drevka's hammer.
  Topic bede_hammer with bede "Ask Bede Orrisk about the hammer by his bed" when true once {
    Says "'Drevka's,' says Bede. 'She made it in the Binding and closed the last rivet with it in 2601 and gave it to me in 2667 with her last breath, more or less.' He does not look at it. 'It opens a scarf weld clean. It breaks a laid band in one blow. Nothing else in the world does either.' His hands shake on his knees. 'I've had nine come asking to learn. I sent them all home. You don't learn this. You give your life to it, and then you're eighty-four.'".
  }
  Topic bede_link with bede "Ask Bede Orrisk whether the link in the Well could be split" when knows(actor, forge_contract) once {
    Says "Bede's head comes up. 'Who told you there was a scarf?' You tell him: the contract of 1210. 'Ah,' he says, and something in his face wakes. 'A third along the near limb. I'd want to see it. Forty days, with drifts, and a lad to hold them, and the Ninepans off my back.' He looks at his hands. 'I'm eighty-four. That's forty days I'd not get back.' A long pause. 'Ask me again in the spring.'".
  }

  // Corin Webb comes for Saska's syllable in the third week. She refuses; and one of the Strays begins to settle into her household.
  Relation settling(place).
  Rule webb_comes_to_keld when watch(clock) >= 2592 and not webbNamed(webb) and able(webb) and not settling(saska_hearth) and not webbVisited(saska)
    says "Word comes, the way word comes on the drove roads: the consul's secretary was at Keld yesterday, asking Mother Saska again about the grey, and went away without what he came for." {
    Assert webbVisited(saska). Assert settling(saska_hearth).
  }
  Relation webbVisited(group).
  Topic teshen_chair with teshen "Ask Teshen what is troubling her" when settling(saska_hearth) and not namedStrays(keld) once {
    Says "'Grandmother's chair,' says Teshen. 'The second one, by the fire. Everyone at home has started calling it Rab's chair, as if Rab had always sat there.' Her voice is very steady. 'There's no Rab. I'd remember. I remember everyone.' She looks toward the west field. 'One of them's come in.'".
  }
  Rule settler_named when namedStrays(keld) and settling(saska_hearth) { Retract settling(saska_hearth). }
}

Module corrow "Let One Remember" {
  // The Corrow as a country beyond a march: the company that comes up the Peleth road is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
}

data/adventures/let-one-remember/scarp.k:
Module corrow "Let One Remember" {
  Description "The Peleth road up the Scarp, and the Stake ruins on the rim of the Emptied Well.".

  Place cistern_inn "the Rope and Lantern" is building within stake.
  Place hold_chapel "the Hold chapel" is building within stake.
  Place guild_house "the cistern guild" is building within stake.

  Place scarp_foot "the foot of the Scarp" is room within scarp at 0, 1.
  Place eighth_bend "the eighth bend of the Peleth road" is room within scarp at 0, 0.
  Place collar "the Collar" is room within stake at 1, 1.
  Place chimneys "the street of chimneys" is room within stake at 0, 1.
  Place rim "the rim of the Well" is room within stake at 2, 1.
  Place drove_gate "the drove-road gate" is room within stake at 0, 0.
  Place furrow_end "the north edge of the ruins" is room within stake at 1, 0.
  Place inn_room "the Rope and Lantern" is room within cistern_inn at 1, 2 underground.
  Place chapel_room "the Hold chapel" is room within hold_chapel at 2, 2.
  Place guild_room "the cistern guild's office" is room within guild_house at 0, 2.

  Passage scarp_bends "the bends of the Peleth road" is road between scarp_foot and eighth_bend taking 4 hours.
  Passage last_bend "the ninth bend" is road between eighth_bend and chimneys taking 30 minutes.
  Passage chimney_way "the way between the chimneys" is path between chimneys and collar.
  Passage collar_rim "the lee of the Collar" is path between collar and rim.
  Passage cistern_steps "the cistern steps" is steps between collar and inn_room.
  Passage chapel_door "the chapel door" is doorway between collar and chapel_room.
  Passage guild_door "the guild's door" is door between chimneys and guild_room.
  Passage drove_lane "the drove lane" is path between chimneys and drove_gate.
  Passage north_lane "the north lane" is path between collar and furrow_end.

  // Arrival (Player Portfolio). The company comes up the Scarp on a carter's wagon.
  Entity arrived: fact "You have come up the Scarp into the Corrow.".
  Observe arrival at eighth_bend when not knows(party, arrived) "The Peleth road climbs the Scarp in nine bends, and at the eighth the wind finds you. It comes off the plateau flat and cold, smelling of sheep and wet limestone. At the top the country opens: grey grass, pale stone breaking through it like knuckles, and a hollow every few hundred paces where the ground has simply sunk. Ahead, a cluster of chimneys stands without the houses that went with them. Smoke rises from a few. Beyond the chimneys the ground stops at the edge of a hole you cannot see across the bottom of. To the north a line runs up out of the plateau into the sky, thin as a thread. You follow it up past one layer of cloud and then another, and at the top, where it ends, something dark sits in the sky the way a stone sits on water, with lights along its rim. The carter beside you does not look up. 'That's Hightown,' she says. 'You get used to it. You'll want the Rope and Lantern. It's in a cistern. Mind the steps.' She sets you down and turns her mules for the descent." teaches arrived.
  Observe bend_scene at eighth_bend when knows(party, arrived) "The eighth bend of the Peleth road, where the wind off the plateau finds you. Below, the road goes down the Scarp in long loops to Wendhead; above, the chimneys of the Stake ruins.".
  Observe scarp_foot_scene at scarp_foot when true "The Peleth road leaves the valley at the foot of the Scarp, a grey cliff three hundred metres high pocked with cave-mouths, and starts up it in long bends. Yew grows in the cracks.".

  Observe chimneys_scene at chimneys when not dark() "Brannock's Stake burned ninety years ago when the slowed fire came up the shaft, and what stood up afterwards was chimneys: stone stacks without houses, a whole street of them, and between them salvagers' huts of salvaged timber and canvas. Smoke rises from a few. Everything is pointed toward the hole.".
  Observe chimneys_night at chimneys when dark() "The chimneys stand black against a sky with one low cluster of lights in it, to the north, high up. A dog barks at nothing.".
  Observe collar_scene at collar when true "The Collar was a ring of bronze-clad stone sixty metres across that guided the Chain into the Well. The fire slagged it into lumps like a burnt loaf. The market stands in its lee: rope, lamps, oatcake, rumour. Wind comes up out of the ground on the far side, warm, at a walking pace.".
  Observe rim_scene at rim when true "The rim of the Emptied Well. Four hundred metres across, and black glass for the first thirty down, then broken rock, then darkness. Warm air rises past your face out of it, and a scrap of paper someone dropped goes up with it and does not come down. Salvagers' ropes go over the edge from iron pins, swaying. To the left a spiral stair is cut into the wall, with a brass bell at its head.".
  Observe drove_gate_scene at drove_gate when true "A field gate at the west end of the ruins, where the drove road goes off over the sinkhole country toward Keld, eighteen kilometres. A shepherd's staff leans by the post for anyone to borrow: the ground out there falls in.".
  Observe furrow_end_scene at furrow_end when true "The north edge of the ruins. From here you can see the furrow: a raw trench three metres deep running north across the plateau, and at the end of it, ten kilometres off, a smudge of smoke and timber where the Chain comes down out of the sky to the ground.".
  Observe inn_scene at inn_room when true "The Rope and Lantern is a Peleth cistern with a floor laid over the water: you can hear it under the boards. It is warm and low and smells of lamp-oil and wet wool. Coils of rope and lamps for hire hang from the vaulting, and the regulars sit with their backs to the curve of the wall.".
  Observe chapel_scene at chapel_room when true "The Hold chapel's walls stood through the fire; its roof is new turf. In the north wall is a niche, empty, scorched black round its edges, the height of a man. Juniper has been put in it anyway.".
  Observe guild_scene at guild_room when true "The cistern guild's office: a counting table, a rack of brass dippers, and ledgers going back to before the fire in an iron press that kept them. Whoever has the water at the Stake has the Stake.".

  // The Rope and Lantern.
  Person agnes "Agnes Ruddle" at inn_room {
    Role "keeper of the Rope and Lantern". Ancestry human. Profession innkeeper. Peaceable.
    Sells rations for 1 coin from 12.
    Sells lamp for 2 coin from 4.
    Sells lamp_oil for 1 coin from 8.
    Sells rope for 3 coin from 4.
    Sells torch for 1 coin from 10.
  }
  Topic agnes_well with agnes "Ask Agnes Ruddle about going down the Well" when true once {
    Says "'Two ways,' says Agnes, polishing a lamp-glass she has polished already. 'The stair, which is the Registry's, two silver a head, and they write you down going and write you down coming back. Or the ropes, which are nobody's, and nobody writes anything.' She holds the glass to the lamp. 'The machine hears the ropes anyway, mostly. It's a deaf old thing these days, they say, but not that deaf. Take lamps. Magic lights go out down there near the iron, and the glass people will tell you to shutter them anyway.'".
  }
  Topic agnes_hightown with agnes "Ask Agnes Ruddle about Hightown" when true once {
    Says "'It's moving,' says Agnes. 'It always moved; it moves faster now. The runners cut the tail and sell the links, and it gets lighter, and it goes north on the gales.' She jerks her chin at the vault, as if the sky were up there. 'Hornwake goes after it with the horn. You can't miss Hornwake. It's the town that won't stay put.'".
  }
  Topic agnes_returns with agnes "Ask Agnes Ruddle about the Returns" when true once {
    Says "'Things come back,' says Agnes. 'Not here so much. In the valley, and out on the drove roads. My mother's thimble came back on the bar one morning, the one she lost in seventy-one. I didn't want it.' She shrugs. 'The ones nobody wants go on the Lost Nail in Wendmouth for a year, then the Fair sells them.'".
  }

  // The hook: everybody wants someone to go down the Well for them, and says so on the board by the steps.
  Discovery jobs_known "The notes on the Rope and Lantern's board, some of them weeks old: THE REGISTRY will enter in its roll as COLLEAGUE whoever brings it heat. J. PENNICK, of the Keepstone Court, will pay for any means to read a blank stone. C. NINEPAN buys deadiron droplets, sixty silver the sack, and says Lamplighter's Camp is still somewhere under the Breach. A. FENNIMORE, of Hightown, will pay for word of any Concord chain on the Drag. The WENDHEAD HOSPICE asks after anyone who has seen a man nobody can name. KELD GUIDES, two silver: ask at Saska's hearth. And one in a fine hand, newer than the rest: STRAYS WANTED, alive, for their own good. Apply at the Grey Mile. F. COSK, for the Open Hand." {
    Source board_notes "the notes on the board by the cistern steps" at inn_room readable by party.
  }
  Observe board_seen at inn_room when not knows(party, jobs_known) "By the cistern steps a board is stuck all over with notes. Every one of them wants somebody to go somewhere they would rather not.".

  // A Return to a Changed Place (Player Portfolio): back up some other way than the stair, after days below.
  Event back_unlogged_blown at inn_room when unclosed(party) and at(party, inn_room) and watch(clock) - wentDown(party) >= 432 and lastGale(hightown) > wentDown(party) "Agnes Ruddle looks at you over the counter for a moment too long. 'The Registry has you down as not come back,' she says. 'Went down the stair and never came up it. I let your room. Your pack's in the store. Most of it.' It has blown while you were below. 'Shifted,' Agnes says. 'The whole of Hornwake, and the mountain with it; you'll see from the door. And there's a woman from the Ninepan House been in asking after you.' She pours you something hot. 'You'll want to go to the Registry and tell it you're alive. It gets upset.'" then {
    Retract unclosed(party).
  }
  Event back_unlogged at inn_room when unclosed(party) and at(party, inn_room) and watch(clock) - wentDown(party) >= 432 and lastGale(hightown) <= wentDown(party) "Agnes Ruddle looks at you over the counter for a moment too long. 'The Registry has you down as not come back,' she says. 'Went down the stair and never came up it. I let your room. Your pack's in the store. Most of it.' She pours you something hot. 'You'll want to go to the Registry and tell it you're alive. It gets upset.'" then {
    Retract unclosed(party).
  }

  // A stone-reader, drunk, who knows a thing nobody believes.
  Person tobin "Tobin Reach" at inn_room {
    Role "a stone-reader from Wendhead, drinking". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
  }
  Discovery seam_reads "A blank keepstone carried down to the bottom of the low road, to the chamber where the jewel lay, reads again for about a month." { Known by tobin. }
  Topic tobin_stones with tobin "Ask Tobin Reach about the blank stones" when true once {
    Says "Tobin puts his cup down with great care. 'They're not dead,' he says. 'Everybody says they're dead. They're sleeping. You take one down, all the way down, down the old road to the cup where the star's heart sat, and you put it on the wet wall and you wait, and it wakes up.' He picks the cup up again. 'For a month. Then it goes off again, up here. I've seen it. I had a stone of my granddad's wedding.' He drinks. 'Nobody listens to a stone-reader. We sell fakes.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, seam_reads). }
  }

  // The Collar's tally, under the slag, for anyone who can read link-script.
  Action read_collar(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Teshen to read the tally under the Collar's slag" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, collar) and travelsWith(teshen, actor)
      and not knows(actor, collar_tally).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, collar_tally). }
    Result "Teshen goes along the inner face of the Collar on her knees, feeling under the slag with her fingertips for the iron links set in the stone. 'Here,' she says, and reads it out, slowly, in the old speech and then in March. At 'the water-people talked' she makes a face. 'That's not fair,' she says. 'They forgot half of who they were, doing it.'".
  }
  Discovery collar_tally "The near-copy of the first link's tally on the Collar's inner face, read by touch under the slag: 'Hearth Orrisk and the hearths hold the star. Four thousand and one hundred hold. Iron holds iron. Bone holds iron. The water-people talked. Drevka Venmort holds the last.'".

  // The cistern guild remembers who drew water on the night of the Unfall.
  Person warden_sall "Warden Sall" at guild_room {
    Role "warden of the cistern guild". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
  }
  Discovery unfall_water "The cistern guild's ledger for the night of the Unfall, 2641: every household at the Stake drew water against the fire, by name. One line is different: 'Coyle, W., of Wendmouth, aged 69, lodging at the Lantern. Drew none. Went down the stair at the ninth bell.'" {
    Source water_ledger "the guild's ledger for 2641" at guild_room readable by party.
    Known by warden_sall.
  }
  Topic sall_water with warden_sall "Ask Warden Sall about the night of the Unfall" when true once {
    Says "'The ledger has it,' says Sall. 'Every bucket. My grandmother's grandmother kept it with the town burning round her, because if you don't write down who had water, somebody says afterwards it was them.' He taps the press. 'Go on and look. It's not secret. It's just old.'".
  }

  // ── Wendhead ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place hospice "the Wendhead hospice" is building within wendhead.
  Place wend_bridge "Wendhead bridge" is room within wendhead at 1, 0.
  Place wend_pool "the Wendhead pool" is room within wendhead at 2, 0.
  Place hospice_hall "the hospice hall" is room within hospice at 0, 1.
  Place long_ward "the long ward" is room within hospice at 1, 1.
  Place hospice_archive "the hospice archive" is room within hospice at 0, 2.
  Place hospice_under "the hospice cellars" is level within hospice.
  Place hospice_cellar "the hospice cellar" is room within hospice_under at 1, 2 underground.

  Passage wendhead_road "the valley road" is road between wend_bridge and scarp_foot taking 30 minutes.
  Passage pool_path "the pool path" is path between wend_bridge and wend_pool.
  Passage hospice_gate "the hospice gate" is gate between wend_bridge and hospice_hall.
  Passage ward_door "the ward door" is doorway between hospice_hall and long_ward.
  Passage archive_door "the archive door" is door between hospice_hall and hospice_archive.
  Passage cellar_stair "the cellar stair" is stair between hospice_hall and hospice_cellar.

  Observe bridge_scene at wend_bridge when true "Wendhead: a mill, a bridge, a quarry, and on the far bank the hospice behind a wall of grey stone with roses over it. Upstream, a round pool of dark water turns slowly under the Scarp.".
  Observe pool_scene at wend_pool when true "The Wendhead pool is sixty metres across and very deep, and it rises: you can see the water lift and turn at its centre, where the river comes up out of the ground from a cave below the Scarp. Old men say it used to steam in winter. It does not now. On the bank, eelers' tackle is drying on a rail.".
  Observe hospice_hall_scene at hospice_hall when true "A whitewashed hall with benches, a fire, and the smell of camomile and lye. A sister goes by with a basin and smiles at you without stopping.".
  Observe ward_scene at long_ward when true "A long room of beds under high windows. Most of the patients are old and some are dying, and the sisters move among them talking quietly, the way people talk to horses.".
  Observe archive_scene at hospice_archive when true "A small room of shelves and boxes, very dry, with a reading desk. Letting records go back seven hundred years: who came, what they wished to put down, whether they did.".
  Observe cellar_scene at hospice_cellar when true "The hospice cellar runs back into the rock of the Scarp further than a cellar should. At the far end is a door of old oak, bound in iron, with a lock and a Letting sign carved over it: an open hand.".

  Person rook "Prioress Imelda Rook" at hospice_hall {
    Role "prioress of the Wendhead hospice". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 3. Trait vitalist. Peaceable.
  }
  Person sisters "the Letting sisters" at long_ward {
    Role "nurses of the hospice". Ancestry human. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
    Offers healing "a month's nursing, paid as you can" for 3 coin.
  }
  Topic rook_rite with rook "Ask Prioress Rook about the anchoring rite" when true once {
    Says "'We keep it,' says the prioress. 'Nobody has asked for it in thirty years. If someone goes across, into the grey, the anchors stay up here and say their name aloud without stopping, in relays, day and night, until they come back. If every anchor falls silent, they stay.' She smiles a little. 'It is the only rite we have left that is about remembering instead of letting go. I am fonder of it than I ought to be.'".
  }
  Topic rook_record with rook "Ask Prioress Rook about the Short Grey" when true once {
    Says "'Before my time,' says the prioress. 'Brother Cosk's rite, in 2604. Three months of fog, and the Grey Mile below the bridge where nothing grows right still. Our sisters kept a record of it: who was lost, who came back, what was heard in the fog.' She glances toward the archive. 'There's a man from the consulate in Wendmouth who has asked twice to read it. A very pleasant man. I said I would think about it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, webb_asked). }
  }
  Discovery webb_asked "Corin Webb, the Lusk consul's secretary, has twice asked the hospice to let him read its record of the Short Grey.".

  // The record of the Short Grey, with a syllable in it; and the manual's warning.
  Kind grey_record "the Letting record of the Short Grey" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1.
  Item short_grey "the Letting record of the Short Grey" is grey_record at hospice_archive owned by rook.
  Discovery short_grey_syllable "In the Letting record of the Short Grey, among things heard in the fog in 2604, one word is written down as heard, a single syllable, and a sister has written beside it: not a word of ours.".
  Discovery anchoring_warning "The hospice's anchoring manual, in a hand of the 2600s: 'Do not say in the chamber what the fog said.'" {
    Source anchoring_manual "the anchoring manual" at hospice_archive readable by party.
    Known by rook.
  }
  Discovery letting_prayer "The Letting prayer, sung at deathbeds, copied with the old marks glossed: '[let] There was a road under the water. [let] We were many who walked it. [kept] I do not walk it. [laid] The stone walks it for me. [let] One walks it, always one.' A sister's note: kept is what the singer saw herself; let is what she was told, or what she has let go." {
    Source prayer_card "a copy of the Letting prayer, with its old marks glossed" at hospice_archive readable by party.
  }
  Observe prayer_grammar near party when knows(party, letting_prayer) and not knows(party, evidential_known) "The sister's note stays with you: kept is what the singer saw; let is what she was told, or let go. The old tongue says how it knows a thing before it says the thing." teaches evidential_known.
  Observe grey_read near party when carries(party, short_grey) and not knows(party, short_grey_syllable) "You turn the pages of the Short Grey record. Names of the lost, names of the found, the weather of each day: fog, fog, fog. On the fortieth day, in a list of things heard in the fog, one word is written as it sounded, a single syllable, and beside it, in another hand: not a word of ours." teaches short_grey_syllable.

  // The nameless man in the long ward, whom nobody knows, his own wife included.
  Person nameless "the nameless man" at long_ward {
    Role "a man nobody can name". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    State unknown "In the end bed a man of fifty sits with his hands on the blanket, quite well, looking at the door. The sisters call him 'love' and 'dear'. Nobody has ever been able to keep his name in their head for longer than a sentence.".
    State known "Absalom Prew sits on the end bed in his coat, waiting for his wife, with his name on him like a coat as well.".
  }
  Topic nameless_who with nameless "Ask the man in the end bed who he is" when state(nameless, unknown) once {
    Says "'I had a desk,' he says, carefully, as if reading it off the inside of his own forehead. 'In Wendmouth. A good desk. I wrote letters for a man with a seal.' He looks at you hard. 'Seven months ago I went in to work and there was a man at my desk, and he looked up at me as if I were a stranger, and so did the consul, and so did my wife that night.' His hands open on the blanket. 'Everyone says I've been here for ever. I haven't. I'd remember.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, displaced_clerk). }
  }
  Discovery displaced_clerk "A man in the hospice's long ward, whose name nobody can keep, says he was a secretary at the Lusk consulate in Wendmouth until seven months ago, when another man was at his desk and nobody, his wife included, knew him.".

  // The cellar door: the old way into the Commonplace, which the Lettings keep locked.
  Thing commonplace_door "the oak door with the open hand" on bright_way {
    State locked blocking "The oak door with the open hand over it is locked.".
    State open "The oak door stands open on darkness and the sound of dripping.".
    Change unlock "Unlock the oak door with the prioress's key" from locked to open needing cellar_key.
  }
  Kind letting_key "the prioress's iron key" like cell_key worth 0 weighing 0.
  Item cellar_key "the prioress's iron key" is letting_key at limbo owned by rook.
  Topic rook_door with rook "Ask Prioress Rook where the road under the water begins" when (knows(actor, low_road_known) or knows(actor, letting_prayer)) and state(commonplace_door, locked) {
    Says "The prioress looks at you for a long time. 'The Commonplace is going dark,' she says. 'The bright galleries are blank already. Past them it is faint, and past that, at the Root, it is still clear, and from the Root the old road goes down to where the jewel lay.' She takes a key from her belt. 'The Lettings have kept that door for nine hundred years so that nobody goes down it by accident. You are not going by accident.' She gives it to you. 'Bring it back.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(rook, cellar_key, actor). Assert at(cellar_key, hospice_hall). }
  }

  // ── The Open Hand, at the Grey Mile ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Brother Cosk's great-grandson keeps a school of forgetting where the Short Grey left the valley wrong. He believes
  // the grey has people in it who want to go home, and that the 412 rite should be finished. He gathers Strays, and
  // what they say.
  Place grey_mile "the Grey Mile" is room within wendhead at 3, 1.
  Passage grey_mile_path "the river path below the bridge" is path between wend_bridge and grey_mile taking 30 minutes.
  Observe grey_mile_scene at grey_mile when true "Below the bridge the valley goes wrong for a mile: the grass grows grey and short, the pears on the old trees ripen with no taste, birds cross it without landing. A long barn stands in the middle of it, freshly limewashed, with an open hand painted over the door.".
  Person ferran "Ferran Cosk" at grey_mile {
    Role "master of the Open Hand". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Person open_hand "the Open Hand" at grey_mile {
    Role "brothers and sisters of the Open Hand, in grey". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Topic ferran_hand with ferran "Ask Ferran Cosk what the Open Hand is for" when true once {
    Says "'Letting,' says Ferran Cosk, as if it were the simplest word in March. He has kind eyes and ink on his cuffs. 'My great-grandfather tried to let the star go into the Lap, and failed, and the valley called it a crime. The star went anyway. And in the grey there is something that has been waiting since 412 to go home, and speaks to us through the Strays, a syllable at a time.' He smiles. 'We are writing it down. When we have all of it, we will say it at the Seam, and it can go where it belongs. That is all mercy is: letting a thing go where it belongs.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, open_hand_plan). }
  }
  Discovery open_hand_plan "The Open Hand are gathering the syllables the Strays repeat, to say the whole word at the Seam and let 'what has waited in the grey since 412' go home.".
  Relation turned(group).

  // Where things wait that are nowhere yet.
  Place limbo "nowhere" is room within scarp at 5, 5.
}

data/adventures/let-one-remember/wendmou:
Module corrow "Let One Remember" {
  Description "Wendmouth: a grey-slate port where the Wend meets the tide, whose land titles are on stones that have gone blank.".

  Place court_b "the Keepstone Court" is building within wendmouth.
  Place consulate_b "the Lusk consulate" is building within wendmouth.
  Place ninepan_b "the Ninepan House" is building within wendmouth.
  Place coyle_b "the Coyle house" is building within wendmouth.

  Place valley_road "the valley road below Wendhead" is room within wendmouth at 1, 0.
  Place well_square "the well square" is room within wendmouth at 1, 1.
  Place quay "the quay" is room within wendmouth at 2, 2.
  Place cemetery "the cemetery on the ridge" is room within wendmouth at 0, 1.
  Place courtroom "the Keepstone Court" is room within court_b at 0, 2.
  Place consulate "the Lusk consulate" is room within consulate_b at 1, 2.
  Place counting_room "the Ninepan counting-room" is room within ninepan_b at 2, 1.
  Place coyle_kitchen "the Coyle house" is room within coyle_b at 0, 0.

  Passage valley_way "the valley road" is road between wend_bridge and valley_road taking 2 hours.
  Passage into_town "the bridge into town" is bridge between valley_road and well_square taking 10 minutes.
  Passage quay_lane "the quay lane" is path between well_square and quay.
  Passage cemetery_lane "the cemetery lane" is path between well_square and cemetery taking 10 minutes.
  Passage court_steps "the court steps" is steps between well_square and courtroom.
  Passage consulate_door "the consulate door" is door between well_square and consulate.
  Passage ninepan_door "the Ninepan House door" is door between quay and counting_room.
  Passage coyle_door "the Coyle house door" is door between valley_road and coyle_kitchen.

  Observe valley_road_scene at valley_road when true "The valley road comes down between orchards, half of them grubbed up for apple and half still pear, to a five-arched Peleth bridge and a grey-slate town on a gravel ridge. On the river below the bridge, weirs of ash stakes stand with half their stakes gone. An old house stands by itself at the bridge-end with an eel-trap over the door.".
  Observe square_scene at well_square when true "A square round a stone well, and on the well-head a great iron nail, and on the nail and on pegs and lines around it, things: a glove, a child's shoe, a brass button, a hat, a doll with one eye, a dog-collar with no dog. The Lost Nail. Everything found in the street is hung here so it stays; and these days, every Return nobody has claimed.".
  Observe quay_scene at quay when true "The Peleth mole runs out into the estuary. Salt pans steam on the flats beyond. A Hartmark grain ship lies at the quay with a crowd of salt-boilers watching it unload, not kindly. Eelers mend tackle on the steps.".
  Observe cemetery_scene at cemetery when true "The cemetery runs along the ridge above the river. A grave-caller in a black coat walks the rows reading names aloud from a book, unhurried. His round ends at a stone near the gate: MARRA COYLE, and two dates of death, 2588 and 2679, and under them a line in Calvessan: calve calve. Kept twice.".
  Observe court_scene at courtroom when not deedsBack(pennick) "The Keepstone Court: a high room of grey stone, benches, a bar, and on the shelves behind the judge's chair hundreds of keepstone plates in rows, each in its slot, each labelled with a farm's name. You do not need to touch them to know: they are blank. A guard stands by the judge's door.".
  Observe consulate_scene at consulate when true "The Lusk consulate: a counting-house with a crest over the door, two desks, files to the ceiling. A brown dog sleeps by the stove and thumps its tail for anyone who comes in.".
  Observe counting_scene_w at counting_room when true "A Peleth counting-house on the quay: a bank, a chandlery and a shipping office in one long room. Clerks, ledgers, a strongroom door, and through the back window a coal yard.".
  Observe coyle_scene at coyle_kitchen when true "The Coyle house: a kitchen with a smoke-loft for eels over it, gone cold, and a lens-grinder's bench by the window that nobody has used in ninety years and nobody has moved.".

  // The Lusk consul's secretary, whom everyone remembers as having held the post for eleven years.
  Person webb "Corin Webb" at consulate {
    Role "secretary to the Lusk consul". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 3. Peaceable.
  }
  Observe dog_ignores at consulate when at(webb, consulate) and able(webb) and not webbNamed(webb) and not knows(party, dog_noticed) "The brown dog by the stove looks up when anyone moves: the consul, a clerk, you. When the secretary gets up and crosses the room, it does not look up at all. It does not even seem to know he is there." teaches dog_noticed.
  Discovery dog_noticed "The consulate's dog does not notice Corin Webb at all.".
  Observe webb_mutters at consulate when at(webb, consulate) and able(webb) and not webbNamed(webb) and knows(party, dog_noticed) and knows(party, stray_syllables) and not knows(party, webb_is_stray) "Webb bends over his letters. Under his breath, when he thinks nobody is listening, he is saying one syllable, over and over, the way the Strays at Keld do." teaches webb_is_stray.
  Observe webb_seen_through near party when knows(party, webb_wrong_face) and knows(party, payroll_known) and not knows(party, webb_is_stray) "Teshen's tall secretary with the cough; the payroll with Absalom Prew on it until seven months ago and Corin Webb after it with no letter of appointment; the man in the hospice whose name nobody can keep. Corin Webb did not come to the consulate. He came into someone's place." teaches webb_is_stray.
  Discovery webb_is_stray "Corin Webb is a Settled Stray: something that came back from the grey with nothing, and has taken a real man's place so well that everyone remembers Webb in it, and nobody remembers the man.".
  Relation webbNamed(group). Measure syllables(group).
  Initially Set syllables(webb) to 1.
  Topic webb_talk with webb "Ask Corin Webb about his work" when not webbNamed(webb) once {
    Says "'Letters,' says Webb, with a pleasant, forgettable smile. 'The consul writes to Lusk, Lusk writes to the consul, and I write it all down so it stays.' He tidies a stack that is already tidy. 'I take an interest in old things. The Short Grey. The Keld. The grey country they came back from.' He says the last words as if tasting them. 'Eleven years I've been here. You'd think I'd be bored of it.'".
  }
  Action name_webb(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Teshen to give Corin Webb his own name and his own place, aloud" {
    Description "He is Corin, son of the reeve of Keld Hollow, who was in the far field when the fog came, and was never found.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(webb, site) and travelsWith(teshen, actor)
      and knows(actor, webb_is_stray) and knows(actor, hollow_missing) and not webbNamed(webb) and able(webb).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert webbNamed(webb). }
    Result "Teshen goes and stands in front of the secretary's desk until he looks up. 'You're Corin,' she says. 'Son of the reeve of Keld Hollow. You were in the far field when the fog came, and they called and called.' Webb's pleasant face goes still. 'Your place is at Keld,' says Teshen. 'With us. There's a house. Come home.' For a moment nothing happens. Then the brown dog by the stove lifts its head, and looks at him, and growls; and the consul in the next room says, puzzled, 'Absalom?'; and Corin Webb puts his face in his hands.".
  }
  Rule prew_remembered when (webbNamed(webb) or not able(webb)) and state(nameless, unknown) {
    Assert state(nameless, known). Assert prewBack(nameless).
  }
  Relation prewBack(group).
  Rule webb_goes_home when webbNamed(webb) and at(webb, consulate) { Assert at(webb, keld_green). }
  Observe webb_at_keld_after at keld_green when webbNamed(webb) and at(webb, keld_green) "Corin of the Hollow is at Keld, splitting kindling at the door of an empty house that the hearth-moot has given him. He works slowly, like someone learning his own hands. Now and then he stops, as if listening for a word he used to say, and does not find it, and goes on.".
  Observe prew_home at long_ward when prewBack(nameless) and not knows(party, prew_reunited) "A woman in a good grey coat is sitting on the end bed of the long ward, holding the hands of the man who sits there, and both of them are crying, and the sisters have drawn the curtain round them as well as they can. 'Absalom,' she keeps saying, as if she could not say it often enough. 'Absalom Prew.'" teaches prew_reunited.
  Discovery prew_reunited "Absalom Prew is known again, and his wife has come for him.".

  // Webb's syllables. He takes the Short Grey record in the second week, if it is still in the hospice archive.
  Rule webb_takes_record when watch(clock) >= 1440 and at(short_grey, hospice_archive) and not webbNamed(webb) and able(webb) and not guarded(rook)
    says "From Wendhead, word comes down the valley road: there has been a theft at the hospice. A record from the archive. The prioress will not say which, and is very angry with someone." {
    Assert at(short_grey, limbo). Increase syllables(webb) by 1.
  }
  Relation guarded(group).
  Topic rook_webb with rook "Tell Prioress Rook what Corin Webb is" when knows(actor, webb_is_stray) and not guarded(rook) once {
    Says "The prioress hears you out with her hands folded. 'A pleasant man,' she says at last. 'I nearly let him read it.' She gets up. 'The Short Grey record goes into the strongbox under my bed tonight, and the key round my neck.' At the door she turns back. 'Do not say in the chamber what the fog said. Our manual says that. I always thought it was poetry.'".
    On discuss { Assert guarded(rook). }
  }

  // Judge Orla Pennick and the blank stones.
  Person pennick "Judge Orla Pennick" at courtroom {
    Role "judge of the Keepstone Court". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
  }
  Person court_guard "the judge's guard" at courtroom {
    Role "a guard at the judge's door". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable.
  }
  Topic pennick_ruling with pennick "Ask Judge Pennick about her ruling" when true once {
    Says "'I ruled that a blank stone proves nothing,' says the judge, 'because the alternative was letting whoever shouted loudest own the valley.' She gestures at the shelves. 'Half the land in the Wend is on those, and they have gone blank from the outside in, like frost going off a window. My own house is on one.' She looks at you over her spectacles. 'The law is a way of remembering on purpose. If the stones can't remember, then we must, and we're worse at it. Is there any way to read a dead stone? Nobody has been able to tell me.'".
  }
  Topic pennick_seam with pennick "Tell Judge Pennick that a blank stone reads again at the bottom of the low road" when knows(actor, seam_reads) and not lends(pennick, deeds, actor) and not deedsBack(pennick) {
    Says "The judge takes off her spectacles. 'A stone-reader told you this. Drunk.' She does not wait for you to answer. 'I have heard worse evidence in this room and ruled on it.' She takes a crate from under the bench, a dozen plates packed in straw, and sets it on the bar. 'Twelve deeds from the suits I have before me. Mine among them. If they come back readable, I will hear every case in the valley again, Keld and all, and the stones can say who is lying.' She holds your eye. 'Bring them back.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(pennick, deeds, actor). Assert at(deeds, courtroom). }
  }
  Item deeds "a crate of the court's blank deeds" is blank_deeds at limbo owned by pennick.
  Relation deedsBack(group).
  Event deeds_returned near pennick when keeps(pennick, deeds) and itemKind(deeds, woken_deeds) "Judge Pennick lays her palm on the first plate and closes her eyes, and you watch her live a man walking a boundary in the hay. She goes through all twelve without a word. Then she sits back. 'The Hallows of Hesk did buy their low field from a Keld in 2650. The Keld were right about the Brookhouse meadow. The Pruetts have lied to my face for a year.' She laughs, once. 'And my house is mine.' She counts thirty silver out of the court's box onto the bar. 'For the carriage. A month, you said, before they go off again? Then I sit every day this month.'" then {
    Assert deedsBack(pennick). Increase quantity(party, gold) by 30.
  }
  Initially Assert wants(pennick, woken_deeds).

  // Bram Coyle, Wenna's grandson, and his drawer of Returns.
  Person bram "Bram Coyle" at coyle_kitchen {
    Role "last of the Coyle weir-holders". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
  }
  Topic bram_wenna with bram "Ask Bram Coyle about Wenna Coyle" when true once {
    Says "'Everybody asks,' says Bram, and answers anyway. 'My grandmother. She was keeper eight years, and on the night of the Unfall she went up to the Stake and down the Well and took the thing out of the ground and went, and the star went after her, and the Stake burned.' He wipes the bench with his sleeve, though it is clean. 'She was sixty-nine. People in the Stake ruins say she did it to steal the star. She did it so it would follow her and not stay. That's what we say in this house, anyway.'".
  }
  Topic bram_drawer with bram "Ask Bram Coyle about the drawer under the bench" when true once {
    Says "Bram pulls it open. Inside: a ring, a bill of sale for a boat, a child's tooth in a twist of paper, a keepstone plate, and a lens wrapped in chamois. 'Returns,' he says. 'They come back to the house. That ring was my great-great-grandmother's. That plate came up in an eel-trap in 2722, out of the river that comes from under the Well, and it reads, when every other stone in Wendmouth is blank.' He unwraps the lens and holds it to the window, and the window stands in it whole. 'Wenna's. The sixth of a set she ground for the Lusk surveyors in 2601, that she never delivered. It went with her in 2641. It came back on the doorstep in 2719.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, seam_reads). Assert knows(actor, lens_known). }
  }
  Discovery lens_known "Bram Coyle keeps Wenna Coyle's sixth lens, a flawless piece of Choir-glass, in his drawer of Returns.".
  Kind wenna_lens_kind "Wenna Coyle's lens, wrapped in chamois" is treasure worth 20 weighing 0.
  Item wenna_lens "Wenna Coyle's lens" is wenna_lens_kind at limbo owned by bram.
  Topic bram_lend with bram "Ask Bram Coyle for the loan of Wenna's lens" when knows(actor, lens_known) and not lends(bram, wenna_lens, actor) {
    Says "Bram turns the lens in his fingers for a long time. 'She kept it in the drawer with her mother's ring,' he says. 'Where she kept things so they'd stay.' He wraps it and holds it out. 'It went away once already. Bring it back.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(bram, wenna_lens, actor). Assert at(wenna_lens, coyle_kitchen). }
  }
  // Through the lens, from Hornwake, the ribs of Hightown's underside; beside the Socket chart, the same ribs.
  Observe lens_and_chart near party when carries(party, wenna_lens) and carries(party, chart) and at(party, ?p) and inHornwake(?p) and not crashed(hightown) and not lost(hightown) and not knows(party, origin_known) "You hold Wenna's lens to your eye and find Hightown's underside, two and a half kilometres up: not a dark blot through this glass but granite, ribbed, rib after rib curving away like the inside of a bowl turned over. You count them. You unroll the Lusk chart of the Socket on a wagon-tail and count the ribs of the lake's bowl. Same count; same spacing; the same broken rib on the eastern side. The lake is the mountain's place." teaches origin_known.
  Relation inHornwake(place).
  Initially Assert inHornwake(horn_foot). Initially Assert inHornwake(hoist_feet). Initially Assert inHornwake(wagons). Initially Assert inHornwake(tail).

  // Clemence Ninepan, who holds the debt.
  Person clemence "Clemence Ninepan" at counting_room {
    Role "head of the Ninepan House". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    Sells coal_order for 20 coin from 3.
    Sells eel_kit for 15 coin from 2.
    Buys droplet_sack for 60 coin.
  }
  Kind eel_kit "an eeler's diving kit: grease, weights, lines, a sealed lamp" is treasure worth 15 weighing 3.
  Topic clemence_link with clemence "Ask Clemence Ninepan about the link in the Well" when true once {
    Says "'Eleven hundred tonnes of deadiron lying on an anvil four hundred metres down,' says Clemence. 'The Registry says it's the Registry's under a contract of 1210. The Linkmoot says it's theirs. Hightown wants to hang it on the tail. I say salvage.' She smiles. 'None of us can lift it. I have a derrick on the rim and a survey crew below, and they tell me pulleys, and I tell them gods.' She closes a ledger. 'Coal, if you're going down. The Registry's buying, at my price.'".
  }
  Discovery hartmark_coin "The Ninepan ledgers show Hartmark silver changed into Corrow coin, every week since spring, for 'E. of H., wages to Teake's crew'." {
    Source ninepan_ledger "the Ninepan exchange ledger" at counting_room readable by party.
  }

  // Midwinter, for the rest of the country.
  Observe webb_gone_down near party when midwinter(corrow) and syllables(webb) >= 2 and not webbNamed(webb) and able(webb) and not knows(party, webb_epilogue) "At midwinter the Registry's roll has a new line in it: the consul's secretary, licensed for one, gone down the Peleth stair, purpose stated as 'study'. He has not come back up it." teaches webb_epilogue.
  Entity webb_epilogue: fact "Where Corin Webb went at midwinter.".
  Observe court_awake at courtroom when deedsBack(pennick) "The Keepstone Court: a high room of grey stone, benches, a bar, and shelves of keepstone plates behind the judge's chair. Twelve of them, on the bar, are awake.".
  Observe court_sitting at courtroom when deedsBack(pennick) "The court sits every day this month. A Keld witness and a farmer from the valley stand at the bar together with a plate between them, and the judge has her hand on it.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/clock.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The long clock (Overview): beneath the factions' weeks runs this one, in years. The Corbel descends about two
  // metres a day and docks in about four years; then the Tip descends three metres a day, and in six months reaches
  // the Vault. If Ithmar is still there, the Patient takes back its heart and the Keeping comes unbound.
  Measure corbelHeight(place). Measure tipDistance(place). Measure coverWork(place).
  Initially Set corbelHeight(corbel_site) to 3000.
  Initially Set tipDistance(undersun) to 500.
  Relation docked(place). Relation unbound(place). Relation covered(place).
  Rule corbel_descends when hour(clock) == 0 and corbelHeight(corbel_site) >= 2 and not covered(ghessil) and not docked(corbel_site)
    and not exiled(corbel_site) and not rebound(corbel_site) { Decrease corbelHeight(corbel_site) by 2. }
  Rule corbel_docks when corbelHeight(corbel_site) < 2 and not docked(corbel_site)
    says "Far off, felt in the knees before it is heard, the plateau takes a blow like a door slammed under the world. The Corbel has docked at the Pit floor." {
    Assert docked(corbel_site). }
  Rule tip_descends when docked(corbel_site) and hour(clock) == 0 and tipDistance(undersun) >= 3 { Decrease tipDistance(undersun) by 3. }
  Rule keeping_unbound when docked(corbel_site) and tipDistance(undersun) < 3 and inside(ithmar, cage) and not unbound(ghessil)
    says "The hourly note under the Pit stops. After it, nothing; and then the plateau begins, very quietly, to forget last week." {
    Assert unbound(ghessil). }

  // What can be seen of it, year by year.
  Observe spire_visible at collar_top when corbelHeight(corbel_site) <= 1500 "Over the Pit, out of the bottom of the Standing Cloud, hangs a dark spire two kilometres long, point down, in full daylight. Nobody on the Collar looks at it for long.".
  Observe spire_square at square when corbelHeight(corbel_site) <= 1500 "Every face in the market turns south-east now and then, to the dark spire hanging in the sky over the Pit, and turns back.".
  // A quarried season: Quell's 370s go, and the town cannot agree what happened in them (year 383).
  Observe quarried_quell at square when day(clock) >= 1050 and not rebound(corbel_site) "Two families are standing in the square with the same deed, each sure the house is theirs, each unable to say who lived in it in the year 74. The clerks cannot either; that season's ledgers are blank.".
  Observe unbound_world near party when unbound(ghessil) "Something is wrong with yesterday. You know you did things in it; you cannot say what.".

  // A Second Covering, if the Concord passes it: three years of umber, a race against the Corbel's four.
  Rule covering_starts when passed(motion_cover) and coverWork(ghessil) == 0 says "The Crown's carts come up the Stair again, loaded with umber; the Collar is to be finished." {
    Set coverWork(ghessil) to 1. }
  Rule covering_works when coverWork(ghessil) >= 1 and hour(clock) == 0 and not covered(ghessil) { Increase coverWork(ghessil) by 1. }
  Rule covering_done when coverWork(ghessil) >= 1080 and not covered(ghessil)
    says "The last light is cut at the Pit. The Corbel stops where it hangs. And every held one on the plateau wakes in the glass, in the dark." {
    Assert covered(ghessil). }

  // The endings the world provides (The Keeping and the Masonry, How it can end); others are the party's.
  Relation rebound(place). Relation exiled(place). Relation seated(place).
  Objective long_clock when knows(party, corbel_seen) and not docked(corbel_site) and not rebound(corbel_site) and not exiled(corbel_site) "Something is coming down the light toward the Pit, two metres a day. When it docks, the growth beneath will drill for the stone that sings.".
  Objective find_stone when knows(party, tone_below) and not knows(party, way_found) and not carries(party, ithmar) "Under the Pit, something sounds once an hour. Saro wants it; the mother-church wants it; the king says it is his.".
  Objective end_it when carries(party, ithmar) and not rebound(corbel_site) and not exiled(corbel_site) "You carry Ithmar. The Masonry knows it. Bind it tighter, cast out what its heart belongs to, or seat it and let the past go.".
  // Kyr keeps a world going after any ending; the endings are told, once, wherever the company is.
  Entity ending_told: fact "How it ended.".
  Observe end_rebound near party when rebound(corbel_site) and not knows(party, ending_told) "Ithmar is bound tighter than the Virina bound it. Under the Pit the seed has stopped building; over it, by the next dawn, the Corbel has drawn back up into the cloud, and by the next month it is gone. The light still burns, the glass still spreads, the held still breathe once an hour. The plateau's troubles are its own again, and so are its memories." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_exiled near party when exiled(corbel_site) and not fellWith(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Patient has fallen out past the planes, and its citadel with it. The Corbel lets go of the light and goes up into the dark as if pulled. The Keeping is still bound; the jewel sings once an hour to nothing at all." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_fell near party when fellWith(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "You did not let go. The Masonry falls, and you fall with it, out past the planes, holding the fall of a thing that was thrown out of the world; and Imbar keeps its past, and will remember you in it." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_seated near party when seated(ghessil) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Patient has its heart again. Far off, in Imbar, last week is already going, and the week before." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_unbound near party when unbound(ghessil) and not seated(ghessil) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Tip reached the Vault, and the jewel was there. Imbar's past has begun to go, from the newest year backward: a season a month, then faster." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_bargained near party when bargained(party) and not heldToLine(corbel_site) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The terms are kept, exactly. Some of the dead come back, blinking, into a world that is forgetting them; and the plateau forgets, from last week backward." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_line near party when heldToLine(corbel_site) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Masonry keeps the line you named, and cuts from the beginning, not the face: it will be ten thousand years reaching anything anyone remembers. It is very patient." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_covered near party when covered(ghessil) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Pit is covered. The Corbel hangs where it stopped, a dark spire over the plateau, and does not come down. In the glass, the held are dead." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_laid near party when laidIn(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "You are part of the Masonry now, a moment with a mind in it, bearing weight." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_set near party when setInPresent(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "You are kept in the present, on the shore, while everything goes on past you." teaches ending_told.
  // The module's Goal is a hint to the planner, not an ending (ledger, 28).
  Goal rebound(corbel_site) or exiled(corbel_site).
}

data/adventures/patient-star/company.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // The company: one cutter, in debt (placed.kyr is the world's own company, come in by the Shift Market).
  Company party "You" of 1 at square.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 9.
  Initially Assert inDebtTo(party, dagny). Initially Set owes(party, dagny) to 28.
}

data/adventures/patient-star/corbel.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Standing Cloud and the Corbel (Tier III): a fastness two kilometres tall lowering itself down the pillar of
  // light, point first, built of moments taken from other worlds. Its tip is three kilometres above the Pit.
  Place sky "the Standing Cloud" is wilderness within ghessil at 8, 0.
  Place corbel_site "the Corbel" is site within ghessil at 3, 4.
  Place cloud_base "the bottom of the Standing Cloud" is room within sky at 0, 2 outdoors.
  Place thick_low "the Thick, low" is room within sky at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place thick_high "the Thick, high" is room within sky at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place crane_rest "a held crane, halfway up the filament" is room within sky at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place c_low "the Corbel's lower reach" is level within corbel_site.
  Place c_mid "the Corbel's middle reach" is level within corbel_site.
  Place c_high "the Corbel's upper reach" is level within corbel_site.
  Place lintel_room "the Lintel" is room within c_low at 0, 0.
  Place weathers "the Hall of Weathers" is room within c_low at 1, 0.
  Place sea_far "the far side of the upright sea" is room within c_low at 2, 0.
  Place procession "the Procession" is room within c_mid at 0, 0.
  Place dormitory "the Dormitory" is room within c_mid at 1, 0.
  Place offers "the Offers" is room within c_mid at 2, 0.
  Place rail "the Rail" is room within c_high at 0, 0.
  Place interlocutor_room "the Interlocutor's chamber" is room within c_high at 1, 0.
  Place seam "the Seam" is room within c_high at 2, 0 outdoors.

  // Up the filament: three kilometres of direct light, resting on held cranes; in full felt about eight points by
  // the top.
  Passage filament_low "the filament, the lower half" is path between pit_floor and crane_rest taking 16 hours needing rope or climbing.
  Passage filament_high "the filament, the upper half" is shaft between crane_rest and lintel_room taking 16 hours needing rope or climbing.
  Initially Set wayDose(filament_low) to 384. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(filament_low) to 96.
  Initially Set wayDose(filament_high) to 384. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(filament_high) to 96.
  Initially Assert litGround(crane_rest).
  // Or by the Warden's balloon to the bottom of the Cloud on a calm autumn dawn, and up the Thick.
  Passage balloon_ride "the Warden's fire-balloon" is passage between balloon_yard and cloud_base taking 2 hours
    opening when admits(aske, party) and season(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) <= 7 "The balloon's silk lies folded in its shed. The Warden lets it go up only for those he admits, on a calm autumn dawn.".
  Passage thick_climb "the Thick, pressed into handholds" is path between cloud_base and thick_low taking 8 hours needing climbing or rope.
  Passage thick_climb2 "the Thick, higher" is path between thick_low and thick_high taking 8 hours needing climbing or rope.
  Passage thick_top "into the Corbel's tip" is shaft between thick_high and lintel_room taking 2 hours.
  Initially Assert litGround(thick_low). Initially Assert litGround(thick_high).

  Observe crane_scene at crane_rest when true "A crane hangs in the air in the light, wings half spread, as it has for centuries; it holds your weight as long as nothing gives it time. Below, the Pit is a coin of fire. Above, the filament goes up into grey.".
  Observe base_scene at cloud_base when true "The balloon's basket bumps against the underside of the Cloud, and above you the fog stands up in a column two hundred metres across, dense as wet wool, and lit from inside.".
  Observe thick_low_scene at thick_low when true "You climb by pressing hands and feet into the fog, slowly, as into a snowbank, and it closes behind you. Hanging in it, here and there, are translucent bells as big as a man.".
  Observe thick_high_scene at thick_high when true "Higher, hailstones the size of plums hang in the air, faintly turning, and cranes hang among them with their wings half spread. Above, something dark and coursed closes off the sky.".
  // Rime-bells: drifting colonies of algae in slowed water, which cling to anything warm. Salt makes them let go.
  Thing rime_bell "a rime-bell" on thick_climb2 {
    State drifting dangerous "A rime-bell drifts across the line of the climb, a translucent bell two metres across that turns toward warmth.".
    State shrunk "A rime-bell has let go and drifts off, puckered, where the salt struck it.".
    Change salt_bell "Throw salt on the rime-bell" from drifting to shrunk consuming salt.
    Hurts with bell_drown when drifting then drifting.
  }
  Hazard bell_drown "a rime-bell closing" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless strength save against (13).".
  // The Long Hail: a stone pushed aside resumes the fall it had, at the speed it had.
  Thing hail "the Long Hail" at thick_high {
    State hanging_hail "Hailstones hang in the light, some of them for three hundred years.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(hail).
  Hazard hailstone "a hailstone, resuming" means "Deal (1d10) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Rule hail_resumes when touched(hail) says "The stone turns slowly under your stick, and then it is gone downward at the speed of a hailstone, and the one below it, and the one below that." {
    Retract touched(hail). Assert strikes(hailstone, party). }

  // Every room of the Corbel is laid: what is said aloud in it is taken, and the Interlocutor speaks with it.
  Initially Assert laidRoom(lintel_room). Initially Assert laidRoom(weathers). Initially Assert laidRoom(procession).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(dormitory). Initially Assert laidRoom(offers). Initially Assert laidRoom(rail).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(interlocutor_room).
  // C1: the Lintel, a door made from a guard's moment. Speak the first syllable, or pass on the side the blow is not
  // aimed at, which the stance shows.
  Observe lintel_scene at lintel_room when true "At the Corbel's tip a door with no frame stands closed, and in its place a figure taller than a man, armoured in something like bark, stopped in the act of raising a weapon.".
  Discovery first_syllable "The first syllable of the Voice, from the First Course, from the Keeping's first new moon, or from Saro.".
  Discovery stance_read "The Lintel's guard is raising its weapon over its right shoulder: the blow comes down on its left.".
  Thing lintel "the Lintel" on lintel_way {
    State guarding blocking "The guard stands in the doorway with its weapon raised.".
    State passed_l "The Lintel stands as it stood; you are through it.".
    Change speak_first "Speak the first syllable of the Voice" from guarding to passed_l after learning first_syllable.
    Change pass_side "Pass on the side the blow is not aimed at" from guarding to passed_l after learning stance_read.
    Tries looking.
  }
  Observe stance_seen beside lintel_way when tried(lintel, looking) "Its weight is on the back foot, the weapon up over its right shoulder. Whatever it was guarding, the blow will come down on its left." teaches stance_read.
  Observe saro_syllable at lintel_room when travelsWith(saro, party) and not knows(party, first_syllable) "Saro says a sound before you can ask her: the first one. 'It is the door's,' she says." teaches first_syllable.
  Hazard lintel_blow "the Lintel's blow" means "Deal (4d8) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Action rush_lintel(actor: group, site: place) "Rush past the Lintel" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lintel_room) and state(lintel, guarding).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert strikes(lintel_blow, actor). Assert at(actor, weathers). }
    Result "The guard completes the blow it was stopped in. It is a real blow, from a world where guards were very large.".
  }
  Passage lintel_way "through the Lintel" is doorway between lintel_room and weathers.

  // C2: the Hall of Weathers. Green lightning stopped mid-branch; rain hanging; a sea set on end.
  Observe weathers_scene at weathers when true "A hall three hundred metres high. Through it runs a bolt of green lightning, stopped mid-branch, its forks thicker than a man. Rain hangs beyond it, each drop holding a point of light. At the far end is a wall of dark water standing upright, with a sun shining from its bottom.".
  Thing lightning "the green lightning" at weathers {
    State forked "The green bolt hangs mid-branch.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(lightning).
  Hazard green_bolt "the green lightning" means "Deal (3d10) lightning damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Rule lightning_strikes when touched(lightning) says "For the length of your touch the bolt finishes its stroke, and you are in the middle of it." {
    Retract touched(lightning). Assert strikes(green_bolt, party). }
  Passage upright_sea "the upright sea, swum" is passage between weathers and sea_far taking 5 minutes.
  Hazard drowning "forty metres of a sea set on end" means "Deal (2d8) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (13).".
  Rule sea_swum when tookWay(?c, upright_sea) and company(?c) and not swum(?c) {
    Assert strikes(drowning, ?c). Assert swum(?c). }
  Relation swum(group).
  Rule sea_dry when swum(?c) and not tookWay(?c, upright_sea) { Retract swum(?c). }
  Observe sea_far_scene at sea_far when true "You come out of the water on a slope of coursed glass, streaming, and the water stands behind you like a wall, lit from beneath by a sun you will never see the sky of.".

  // C3: the Procession. One bearer is a keystone with a mind; given time by touch, it speaks.
  Passage far_up "a coursed ramp" is passage between sea_far and procession taking 30 minutes.
  Observe procession_scene at procession when true "A broad ramp of figures, stopped: slender, many-jointed, taller than horses, carrying a long box between them on poles, in a frieze that runs upward out of sight. A banner hangs over them in a script of overlapping circles.".
  Thing bearer "the foremost bearer" at procession {
    State bearing_box "The foremost bearer's head is turned, as if it were about to speak to the one behind.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(bearer).
  Discovery bearer_words "The procession's bearer, given time, speaks a few words in a language nobody on Imbar knows.".
  Observe bearer_speaks near bearer when touched(bearer) and not travelsWith(saro, party) "Under your hand the bearer turns its long head and says something, slowly, in a language like water running over pebbles, and is still." teaches bearer_words.
  Observe bearer_translated near bearer when touched(bearer) and travelsWith(saro, party) "The bearer speaks, slowly, and Saro, beside you, says it after it in Tovashi, a word at a time: 'They took our past first, from the newest backward. And when they reached the beginning, we were not.'" teaches newest_backward.

  // C4: the Dormitory. Masons at rest, each with a trowel; one niche empty, with a human shape.
  Passage proc_dorm "a shaft lined with niches" is passage between procession and dormitory taking 30 minutes.
  Observe dorm_scene at dormitory when true "A shaft lined with niches from top to bottom, hundreds of them, each holding a stopped figure. The figures are all different; some are human and some are not. Each holds a trowel. One niche is empty, and it has a human shape.".
  Observe saro_niche at dormitory when travelsWith(saro, party) "Saro stands in front of the empty niche a long time. 'This is mine,' she says. 'I do not remember it.' She puts her hand flat on its back wall, which has no temperature, like her hand.".

  // C5: the Offers. Returned moments: people played back out of masonry into the present, alive.
  Passage dorm_offers "a gallery of small rooms" is passage between dormitory and offers taking 10 minutes.
  Observe offers_scene at offers when true "A gallery of small rooms, each with a single figure in it, lit. A woman carrying a basket. A young man laughing. A child asleep. Each one is breathing. None of them knows where they are.".
  Observe offers_doran at offers when knows(party, held_feed) "In the last room a thin man stands with his hands at his sides and his mouth a little open, breathing, looking about him at a place he has never seen. It is Doran of Ennick, alive, as he was the night Ilis laid him.".

  // C6: the Rail. Courses grip the pillar; unlaying one lets the Corbel slip two metres and stalls it a month.
  Passage offers_rail "a stair round the core" is passage between offers and rail taking 30 minutes.
  Observe rail_scene at rail when true "At the Corbel's core a great column of light runs straight up through the building and out of sight. Around it, courses grip the light like fingers; the ones that touch it glow brightest.".
  Initially Assert litGround(rail).
  Thing rail_course "the brightest rail-course" at rail {
    State gripping "The brightest course grips the pillar of light like a finger.".
    State unlaid_r "Where the brightest course gripped the light there is a gap, and Masons are already climbing toward it.".
    Change unlay_rail "Unlay the brightest rail-course with the trowel" from gripping to unlaid_r needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Measure railRepair(entity).
  Rule rail_slips when state(rail_course, unlaid_r) and railRepair(rail_course) == 0 says "The Corbel slips two metres down the light with a sound like the whole sky clearing its throat. Anyone on its outside falls." {
    Set railRepair(rail_course) to 30. Increase corbelHeight(corbel_site) by 60. }
  Rule rail_mends when state(rail_course, unlaid_r) and railRepair(rail_course) > 0 and hour(clock) == 0 { Decrease railRepair(rail_course) by 1. }
  Rule rail_mended when state(rail_course, unlaid_r) and railRepair(rail_course) == 1 { Assert state(rail_course, gripping). Set railRepair(rail_course) to 0. }

  // C7: the Interlocutor. It speaks only with syllables laid in its presence, in the visitor's own voice, assembled
  // from what they said on the way up; it cannot lie, and chooses what to leave out. Under Selane's Veil nothing said
  // can be taken.
  Passage rail_chamber "a plain door" is doorway between rail and interlocutor_room.
  Observe chamber_scene_i at interlocutor_room when true "A plain room, its walls finely coursed.".
  Person interlocutor "the Interlocutor" at interlocutor_room {
    Role "the Masonry's voice, from the walls". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns it.
    Greets "The walls of the chamber take a breath that is your own breath, from the stair.".
  }
  Query veiled(c: group) means memberOf(?m, c) and wearing(?v, ?m) and itemKind(?v, veil_kind).
  Observe interlocutor_silent near interlocutor when wordsLaid(party) < 20 or veiled(party) "The walls listen. Nothing speaks. You have said too little on the way up, or nothing that could be taken, for anything here to answer you with.".
  Observe interlocutor_voice near interlocutor when wordsLaid(party) >= 20 and not veiled(party) "When it speaks it is your own voice, out of the walls: words you said on the way up, in the Riot Hall, at the Lintel, to Saro on the stair, taken apart and put back together. It is very courteous.".
  Topic interlocutor_wants with interlocutor "Ask the Interlocutor what it wants" when wordsLaid(actor) >= 20 and not veiled(actor) once {
    Says "'That this bracket join the seed,' it says, in your voice, 'and that the seed be left whole until it does.' A pause. 'You would harm the seed. I would ask you not to. That is all I cannot bear.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, seed_tender). }
  }
  Discovery seed_tender "The Interlocutor cannot bear the seed being harmed before the Corbel docks, and says so: the one place to press.".
  Topic interlocutor_offer with interlocutor "Ask the Interlocutor what it offers" when wordsLaid(actor) >= 20 and not veiled(actor) once {
    Says "'Any moment returned,' it says. 'The dead of Kell. Your Doran. A daughter at her council.' Your voice is very warm. 'And terms. We will take Imbar's past only as far as the Separation, which nobody alive remembers.' It does not say from which end it will start.".
  }
  Topic interlocutor_end with interlocutor "Ask the Interlocutor from which end it takes a world's past" when knows(actor, newest_backward) and wordsLaid(actor) >= 20 and not veiled(actor) once {
    Says "There is a silence of the kind a thing that cannot lie keeps. 'From the newest,' it says. 'It is how a building is quarried. You start at the face.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, held_feed). }
  }
  Relation bargained(group).
  Action accept_terms(actor: group, site: place) "Accept the Interlocutor's terms" {
    Description "Some dead come back. The Masonry takes the past from the newest moment backward, as far as the line agreed.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, interlocutor_room) and wordsLaid(actor) >= 20
      and not veiled(actor) and not bargained(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert bargained(actor). }
    Result "'Agreed,' says your own voice, out of the walls, and somewhere below, very far down, last week begins to go.".
  }

  // C8: the Seam, the edge of Imbar, five kilometres up, where the light leaves the sky.
  Passage chamber_seam "a stair up into black" is passage between interlocutor_room and seam taking 1 hour.
  Observe seam_scene at seam when true "The light leaves the sky. The stars are close and do not twinkle. The cold is like nothing on earth, because heat does not move here at all. The building goes on upward into black.".
  Hazard seam_cold "the cold of the Seam" means "Deal (1d8) cold damage to ally.".
  Rule seam_cold_bites when at(party, seam) and not seamBitten(party) { Assert strikes(seam_cold, party). Assert seamBitten(party). }
  Relation seamBitten(group).
  Rule seam_leaves when seamBitten(party) and not at(party, seam) { Retract seamBitten(party). }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/ennick.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // The heath and the Ramp: four hours from Quell to the Ramp head, three down it to Ennick on the gorge floor.
  Place ramp_head "the Ramp head" is room within heath at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Passage quell_road "the Quell road" is road between square and ramp_head taking 4 hours.
  Observe ramp_head_scene at ramp_head when true "The heath is flat and grey-green to the edge of the sky and smells of ashwort. Here the road tips over the gorge rim and goes down the Ramp in long switchbacks. Far to the south-east a line of light stands straight up from the ground into a small cloud, and does not move.".

  Place inn "the Lower Inn" is building within ennick.
  Place holders "the holder's house" is building within ennick.
  Place ilis_house "Ilis's house" is building within ennick.
  Place lower_road "Ennick's lower road" is room within ennick at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Place taproom "the Lower Inn" is room within inn at 2, 2.
  Place holders_room "the holder's house" is room within holders at 0, 2.
  Place ilis_room "Ilis's kitchen" is room within ilis_house at 1, 3.
  Place terraces "the upper terraces" is room within ennick at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place shrine "the shrine" is room within ennick at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place weeping_wall "the Weeping Wall" is room within ennick at 0, 0 outdoors.

  Passage ramp "the Ramp" is road between ramp_head and lower_road taking 3 hours.
  Passage inn_door "the Lower Inn's door" is door between lower_road and taproom.
  Passage holders_door "the holder's door" is door between lower_road and holders_room.
  Passage ilis_door "Ilis's door" is door between lower_road and ilis_room.
  Passage terrace_steps "the terrace steps" is steps between lower_road and terraces taking 10 minutes.
  Passage cliff_path "the west cliff path" is path between lower_road and shrine taking 10 minutes.
  Passage wall_climb "the climb to the Weeping Wall" is path between shrine and weeping_wall taking 20 minutes.
  // The Outfall: nine kilometres of Seridane drain, a metre and a half high, wet, from the Weeping Wall to the Flood
  // Line. Shut by the flood until it falls in autumn.
  Passage outfall "the Outfall" is crawl between weeping_wall and flood_line taking 8 hours
    opening when flood(flood_water) < 60 "Ten paces in, the Outfall's roof meets black water, and the water does not stop.".

  Observe road_scene at lower_road when not washedOut(lower_road) "Terraces, walnut trees and the river. Carts go through here or not at all: the gorge floor is the only grade a wagon can climb.".
  Observe road_washed at lower_road when washedOut(lower_road) "The lower road is gone under a skin of red mud and gravel where the Weeping Wall's spring came down it in spate. A cart stands axle-deep in it, abandoned.".
  Observe taproom_scene at taproom when true "A low room with a walnut-wood bar and very few people in it. A Glass Office notice is nailed beside the door: THIS HOUSE IS THE OFFICE'S POST ON THE GORGE ROAD.".
  Observe holders_scene at holders_room when true "A holder's house: tally cords hung on pegs by the door, felt hoods, sacks of clean sieved sand, and a map of the glass above the village drawn in charcoal on the wall, with knots for marks.".
  Observe ilis_scene at ilis_room when true "A kitchen with a walnut fire and two chairs. An old felt cloak, stiff at the shoulders from years of folding, hangs by the door.".
  Observe terraces_scene at terraces when true "The upper terraces are glass. Apricot trees stand in it to the knee, held, in the light coming up from under their roots, with the leaves of the year 370 still on them. Ennick's children dare each other to touch them.".
  Initially Assert litGround(terraces).
  Observe weeping_scene at weeping_wall when true "Sixty metres above the village a spring comes out of a low cave in the cliff and falls in a long white thread. The Holdfolk call it the Weeping Wall. In the pool at its foot, thin glass eels flicker.".
  Discovery elvers_seen "Elvers swim up into the Weeping Wall: whatever is in there is warm, and goes a long way back." {
    Found by searching weeping_wall "Behind the falling water the cave goes back into the cliff, low and square-cut. It is not a cave: it is a drain, with tool-marks on its walls, and warm air comes out of it.".
  }

  // The shrine: the Answerer chant-wall, which plays when a stylus is drawn along it (In-world sources 1).
  Thing chant_wall "the chant-wall" at shrine {
    State silent "A face of stillglass four metres long in the cliff, worn smooth at hand height. Walnuts lie in a heap at its foot.".
    State playing "A man's voice, faint and level, in a language older than Tovashi: a long speech, and at the end a line said slower than the rest, as a threat is.".
    Change play_wall "Draw a stylus along the chant-wall" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Rule wall_ends when state(chant_wall, playing) and not at(party, shrine) { Assert state(chant_wall, silent). }

  // The holders. Bren keeps the office; his mother Ilis kept it before him. The holder's door is bolted with an iron
  // pin that is the Collar culvert's missing gate pin, which nobody in this slice yet knows to look for.
  Person bren "Bren of Ennick" at holders_room {
    Role "the holder of Ennick". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
  }
  Person ilis "Ilis of Ennick" at ilis_room {
    Role "the old holder, seventy-eight". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
  }
  Person mirel "Mirel" at holders_room {
    Role "a Holdfolk carrier". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Joins "Mirel takes down her hood and her tally cord from the pegs. 'I will carry,' she says. 'You will not ask me to wake anyone.'".
    Leaves "Mirel takes off her hood and hands it back to nobody. 'I carry for the held,' she says, 'not against them.' She goes home.".
  }
  Person kerra "Kerra Vane" at taproom {
    Role "keeper of the Lower Inn". Profession innkeeper. Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Sells rations for 1 coin from 6.
  }
  Initially Assert slowable(mirel). Initially Assert feltClad(mirel). Initially Set hire(mirel) to 1.
  Thing bolt "the bolt on the holder's door" on holders_door {
    State home "The holder's door is bolted with a long iron pin, square in section, too heavy for the job, rusted where hands do not wear it.".
    Tries looking.
  }
  Discovery bolt_is_pin "The bolt on the holder's door in Ennick is a square iron pin, too heavy for a door: a sluice-gate pin.".
  Observe bolt_looked beside holders_door when tried(bolt, looking) "The pin is square in section, as thick as a thumb, with a hole through one end for a chain that is not there. It was made for a sluice-gate, not a door." teaches bolt_is_pin.

  Discovery prayer_heard "The Ennick holding prayer, spoken over each person as they are laid in the light: 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.' Held until the hour, keepers of the deep water watch; held until the hour, the light remembers." {
    Known by bren, ilis, mirel.
  }
  Topic bren_held with bren "Ask Bren about the held" when true once {
    Says "'They are alive,' says Bren. 'You can watch them breathe if you have the patience, and the felt. My father lies nine hundred paces in. A carrier who goes to him and back loses a night and an afternoon to it.' He looks at the map on the wall. 'Nobody held is woken without their own word. A held man cannot give it. So nobody is woken.'".
  }
  Topic bren_garret with bren "Tell Bren about Garret in the vault" when knows(actor, garret_held) once {
    Says "Bren hears you out. 'He was not laid,' he says. 'He walked into it, reaching for a jar. That is not holding, that is a man caught.' He nods slowly. 'Get him out. If you mean to go by the drain, take Mirel. She knows it.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(mirel, actor). }
  }
  Topic bren_prayer with bren "Ask Bren what is said when someone is laid" when true once {
    Says "Bren says it without thinking, the way a man says a thing he has said over his own father. 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.' Then, in Tovashi: 'Held until the hour, keepers of the deep water watch. Held until the hour, the light remembers.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prayer_heard). }
  }
  Topic mirel_outfall with mirel "Ask Mirel about the Weeping Wall" when true once {
    Says "'It is the old drain,' says Mirel. 'It goes all the way under the heath to the city, nine kilometres, on your hands and knees. My grandfather went up it once. The flood closes it all summer, and opens it when the leaves turn.' She looks at your boots. 'Eight hours, wet. You come out in warm water, with eels.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, outfall_known). }
  }
  Topic ilis_held with ilis "Ask Ilis whether the held are truly alive" when true once {
    Says "'Ours breathe,' says Ilis. 'I have watched Doran take a breath every month for forty years, and it takes longer every year. The old ones further in, from before the Covering, do not breathe. Those are not ours.' She folds her hands. 'Ask me something else.'".
  }
  Topic ilis_prayer with ilis "Ask Ilis about the holding prayer" when true once {
    Says "Ilis says it, slowly, the way her mother taught her: 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.' She does not say what it means.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prayer_heard). }
  }
  // What Ilis has not said in forty years: she says it to someone who has already seen it.
  Discovery prayer_label "The holding prayer is not a prayer. It is a Seridane granary formula, painted on the grain jars and said over each by the clerks: hold this one season, then give it out. The Holdfolk have been saying a label over their dying for three hundred years." {
    Known by ilis.
  }
  Topic ilis_jars with ilis "Tell Ilis about the words on the granary jars" when (knows(actor, jars_painted) or knows(actor, tally_words)) and knows(actor, prayer_heard) and not knows(actor, prayer_label) once {
    Says "Ilis looks at you for a long time. 'So you have seen the jars,' she says. 'The prior at Stairhead read them for me forty years ago. Hold one season, then issue. A grain jar's label.' She looks at the old cloak by the door. 'I said it over my husband. I have said it over half this village. I have never told Bren.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prayer_label). }
  }
  // Or the company puts the two together itself: the clerk's line on the plate is the prayer.
  Observe prayer_recognised near party when knows(party, tally_words) and knows(party, prayer_heard) and not knows(party, prayer_label) "The clerk's line, said over each jar he counted in, is the line the Holdfolk say over their dying, word for word." teaches prayer_label.

  // The holders' cord and the glass: up the goat cleft from the terraces to the rim, and the red felt rope a hundred
  // paces from the edge of the light. At dusk the umber wolves come along the cord, and wait for whoever comes back
  // across it slowed.
  Place cord "the holders' cord" is room within fields at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place margin "the edge of the glass" is room within fields at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place near_held "three hundred paces in" is room within fields at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place doran_place "Doran's brick" is room within fields at 3, 1 outdoors.
  Passage goat_cleft "the goat cleft" is path between terraces and cord taking 1 hour.
  Passage onto_glass "the edge of the glass" is path between cord and margin taking 10 minutes.
  Passage glass_in "the glass" is path between margin and near_held taking 30 minutes.
  Passage glass_deep "the glass, further in" is path between near_held and doran_place taking 1 hour.
  Initially Assert litGround(margin). Initially Assert litGround(near_held). Initially Assert litGround(doran_place).
  Observe cord_scene at cord when true "Red felt rope on iron pins runs along the heath a hundred paces short of the glass. A cairn stands where the path comes up, and people sit down at it whether they mean to or not.".
  Observe cord_night at cord when dark() "Past the cord your shadow changes: a second light, low and level, comes out of the east through the edge of the glass, and every shadow on the heath lies down pointing west.".
  Observe margin_scene at margin when true "The heath stops and the ground goes clear. There is no slope and no rim: sand and needlegrass, and then the sand is clear and the grass roots stand in it like hair in water. It has no temperature underfoot. Every shadow points west.".
  Observe near_scene at near_held when true "Umber bricks the size of loaves lie on the glass in a scatter, each with a knot cut in the top. Under each, a finger's depth down and more, someone lies on their back in the clear stone.".
  Observe doran_scene at doran_place when true "An umber brick with a holder's knot cut in it sits on the glass. Under it a man lies in a trench a little deeper than an arm is long, with his hands at his sides and his mouth a little open. The glass in front of his face has a fan of bright lines in it, where the sand was not quite clean.".
  Measure watchedDoran(group).
  Rule watching_doran when at(party, doran_place) and not benighted(party) { Increase watchedDoran(party) by 1. }
  Rule doran_reset when not at(party, doran_place) and watchedDoran(party) > 0 { Set watchedDoran(party) to 0. }
  Discovery doran_breathed "Doran, held forty years nine hundred paces into the glass, breathed: once, in most of an hour of watching." .
  Observe doran_breath at doran_place when watchedDoran(party) >= 5 and not knows(party, doran_breathed) "It begins so slowly that you could not say when it began. There is a time when his chest is down and a time when it is not, and between them the shirt lifts over the bone and the cloth draws tighter at the shoulder." teaches doran_breathed.

  Species umber_wolf "an umber wolf" like wolf temperament territorial
    described "A plateau wolf crusted iron-red to the shoulder from wallowing in umber mud, which lets it hunt an hour or two into the light.".
  Person wolves "the umber wolves" at cord {
    Role "a pack of umber wolves, the colour of the cliffs". Species umber_wolf. Numbers 4.
    Seen when dark().
    Warns "On the far side of the cord, in the juniper, four of them stand still that were not standing there before. They walk when you walk, twenty paces off, keeping level.".
  }
  // They do not come at a company that can run. They come at one that cannot.
  Initially Assert tolerates(wolves, party).
  Rule wolves_close when dark() and at(party, cord) and slowedCompany(party) and tolerates(wolves, party) says "The wolves have stopped keeping level. They are coming in." {
    Retract tolerates(wolves, party). Assert assails(wolves, party). }
  Rule wolves_wait when not dark() and not tolerates(wolves, party) and not assails(wolves, party) { Assert tolerates(wolves, party). }

  // The Sluice sends its water down the Outfall to the Weeping Wall, and from there onto the lower road.
  Rule road_washes when sluiced(flood_water) and not washedOut(lower_road) and hour(clock) == 5 says "Down in Ennick, at first light, the Weeping Wall comes down in spate, red with mud, and goes over the lower road." { Assert washedOut(lower_road). }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/hour.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Granaries' landward rooms, and the Hour: Tamaun's lowest level, 130 to 210 metres down, flooded outside the
  // mantle the Late Sun has boiled dry, and 40 to 60 degrees inside it (Tamaun, H1 to H6).
  Place hour "the Hour" is level within tamaun.
  Place watch_room "the Watch Room" is room within granaries at 0, 0 underground.
  Place steam_top "the head of the Steam Stair" is room within granaries at 2, 0 underground.
  Place listening_hall "the Listening Hall" is room within hour at 1, 0 underground.
  Place hot_gallery "the hot gallery" is room within hour at 1, 1 underground.
  Place last_hour "the Last Hour" is room within hour at 0, 1 underground.
  Place coverers_works "the Coverers' Works" is room within hour at 2, 1 underground.
  Place stair_wall "the Wall of the Stair" is room within hour at 3, 1 underground.
  Place courses_face "the Courses" is room within hour at 1, 2 underground.

  Passage watch_door "the Watch Room arch" is arch between ring and watch_room.
  Passage to_steam "the passage to the Steam Stair" is passage between ring and steam_top taking 3 minutes.
  Passage steam_stair "the Steam Stair" is stair between steam_top and listening_hall taking 20 minutes.
  // In autumn the flood falls, and a swimmer can go down the flooded stairs from the Flood Line to the Hall (G4).
  Passage flood_swim "the flooded stairs" is passage between flood_line and listening_hall taking 20 minutes
    opening when flood(flood_water) < 60 "The flooded stairs go down into water too hot to bear past the first turn.".
  Passage hot_way "the hot gallery" is passage between listening_hall and hot_gallery taking 5 minutes.
  Passage chamber_door "the bronze door of the Last Hour" is doorway between hot_gallery and last_hour.
  Passage works_way "the rammed-clay passage" is passage between hot_gallery and coverers_works taking 5 minutes.
  Passage archive_door "the Coverers' archive door" is door between coverers_works and stair_wall.
  Passage courses_way "the lowest gallery" is passage between hot_gallery and courses_face taking 5 minutes.
  Initially Assert darkRoom(watch_room). Initially Assert darkRoom(steam_top). Initially Assert darkRoom(hot_gallery).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(coverers_works). Initially Assert darkRoom(stair_wall).
  // The Listening Hall is lit from below, through its glass floor; the Last Hour by its channel; the Courses by their
  // own light.
  Initially Assert litGround(courses_face).

  Observe watch_room_scene at watch_room when true "A guardroom with an Office lamp, a table, a ledger and a cot. A bronze bell hangs on a cord that runs up a stair cut in red clay.".
  Discovery kings_book "The King's Book: the Office clerk's record of the old king below, written three days a month. In Haysel he answered at about a sixth of a man's speed and asked for honey and for his daughter by name." {
    Source kings_book_copy "the King's Book" at watch_room readable by party.
  }

  // H1: the Steam Stair. A blast comes up the tube about every fifty minutes, after twenty breaths of hissing; six
  // niches give room for two. A company that watches one cycle can time the run.
  Thing steam "the steam in the stair" on steam_stair is scenery {
    State quiet "The Steam Stair spirals down inside a tube of red ceramic, wet and hot through boot leather. Six niches are cut in its wall, scratched with tally marks.".
    State hissing "A hiss is rising from below in the Steam Stair, louder with each breath.".
    State blasting dangerous "A blast of steam roars up the Steam Stair and out of its head in a white column.".
    Hurts with scald when blasting then quiet.
  }
  Hazard scald "a blast of steam" means "Deal (2d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Measure steamTick(entity).
  Rule steam_ticks when state(steam, ?s) { Increase steamTick(steam) by 1. }
  Rule steam_hisses when steamTick(steam) == 4 and state(steam, quiet) { Assert state(steam, hissing). }
  Rule steam_blasts when steamTick(steam) == 5 and state(steam, hissing) { Assert state(steam, blasting). }
  Rule steam_spent when steamTick(steam) >= 6 { Set steamTick(steam) to 0. Assert state(steam, quiet). }
  // Half way down when the hiss starts: the blast finds whoever started down hissing.
  Rule caught_on_stair when tookWay(?c, steam_stair) and company(?c) and state(steam, blasting) and not niched(?c) {
    Assert strikes(scald, ?c). Assert niched(?c). }
  Relation niched(group).
  Rule niche_clears when niched(?c) and not tookWay(?c, steam_stair) { Retract niched(?c). }
  Discovery steam_timed "The Steam Stair blasts about every fifty minutes, after twenty breaths of hissing; the niches hold two each.".
  Observe steam_learned at steam_top when state(steam, blasting) and not knows(party, steam_timed) "The blast comes up out of the stair-head in a column you could lean on, and is gone. You count, after: it is near enough fifty minutes to the next, and the hiss before it is twenty breaths long." teaches steam_timed.

  // H2: the Listening Hall, and the Waiting who listen there without leave.
  Observe hall_scene_h at listening_hall when true "A round chamber with a stillglass floor, very warm. Light comes up through the floor from below, and lies on the undersides of things.".
  Person listeners "six of the Waiting" at listening_hall {
    Role "six Listeners of the Waiting, on felt mats with their ears to the glass". Ancestry human. Numbers 6. Peaceable.
    Wants night_honey.
  }
  Observe tone_heard at listening_hall when hour(clock) == 12 or hour(clock) == 0 "Through the floor, far below, a single low note sounds, and goes on in the bones after it has stopped. The Listeners look at one another and say nothing.".
  Discovery tone_below "Since 378 a low tone sounds from deep below the Pit once an hour; the Waiting have heard it, and told no one.".
  Topic listeners_tone with listeners "Ask the Listeners what they hear" when true once {
    Says "'Nothing, since the year 71,' says a woman with wax in her hair. 'Not the Voice.' She looks at the others. 'Since 78, when the growth broke into the lowest gallery and let the air carry it, there is a note. Once an hour. Deep. It is not a syllable. It is not anything.' She presses her ear back to the glass. 'Ruan does not know yet. Do not tell the Office.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, tone_below). }
  }
  Topic listeners_names with listeners "Ask the Listeners what they are copying" when true once {
    Says "'The Waking Ward names,' says a young man, and turns his tablet so you can see the columns. 'Every name has its syllable. Read in the order they were given, they are the Voice, before anyone counted.' He taps one column. 'And these are the hour-names the sick counted their time by. Twelve of them, round and round.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ward_names). }
  }
  Discovery ward_names "The Waking Ward names, copied in order: each carries its Voice syllable, and among them the twelve Seridane hour-names the sick counted time by.".

  // H3: the Last Hour, and Amaru, ninth Dane of the Hour, waking. His rate goes from a sixth to a third, to a half, to a
  // man's speed, by the week (Amaru's waking).
  Observe last_hour_scene at last_hour when true "A domed chamber tiled in bronze, its ceiling pierced by a stillglass rod as thick as a forearm. Grey light comes down the rod and spreads weakly. Couches stand round the walls, and honey jars lie about, all open and scraped clean.".
  Person amaru "Amaru" at last_hour {
    Role "the ninth Dane of the Hour, in a robe gone colourless". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Wants night_honey.
    Objects "Amaru's eyes come round to his seal in your hands, over a long time. When his voice arrives it is very quiet. 'Put it back.'".
  }
  Person kesset "Kesset" at last_hour {
    Role "the Dane's chamberlain, on a couch in the shadow". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Calling bard. Plans 14 steps. Uses go.
    Joins "Kesset gets up as a young man would and an old man feels it. 'I will find Halu,' he says. 'And I will tell you what the doors say.'".
  }
  Measure amaruRate(group).
  Initially Set amaruRate(amaru) to 6.
  Rule amaru_third when day(clock) >= 29 and amaruRate(amaru) == 6 { Set amaruRate(amaru) to 3. }
  Rule amaru_half when day(clock) >= 71 and amaruRate(amaru) == 3 { Set amaruRate(amaru) to 2. }
  Rule amaru_whole when day(clock) >= 127 and amaruRate(amaru) == 2 { Set amaruRate(amaru) to 1. }
  Initially Assert asleep(kesset).
  Rule kesset_wakes when day(clock) >= 36 and asleep(kesset) { Retract asleep(kesset). Assert willing(kesset, party). }
  Observe amaru_sixth near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 6 "When you step closer, the old man's eyes come round to you over several seconds. His lips begin a word, and you wait a long time for the rest of it.".
  Observe amaru_third_seen near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 3 "The old man in the chair turns his head toward you at a third of a man's speed, and his hands are shaking, and not with age.".
  Observe amaru_half_seen near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 2 "The old king watches you come in with something like anger. He is quicker now; quick enough to argue.".
  Observe amaru_awake near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 1 "An old man sits in a dead city in a chair too big for him, at a man's speed, and looks at you.".
  // What he says, by how far he has woken: formal, then hungry and afraid, then disbelieving, then an old man.
  Topic amaru_first with amaru "Speak to the king" when amaruRate(amaru) == 6 once {
    Says "It takes him half a minute to say what would take you five seconds, and you wait for every word. 'You are not of my household.' A long time. 'Where is my daughter? Where is the honey? Tell the granary-keepers to come to me.' His eyes close and open, slowly. 'Is the Voice still speaking?'".
  }
  Topic amaru_hungry with amaru "Speak to the king" when amaruRate(amaru) == 3 once {
    Says "'The honey is gone,' says Amaru, as if you had taken it. 'The household is hungry. Kesset is too thin.' His eyes go to the empty couch. 'Halu went up for bread. She has not come back.' He grips the arm of the chair. 'What year is it, above?'".
  }
  Topic amaru_year with amaru "Tell the king what year it is" when amaruRate(amaru) <= 3 once {
    Says "You tell him: the three hundred and eightieth since the Unlidding; sixteen hundred and forty since the Covering. Amaru looks at you a long time. 'Some weeks,' he says. 'It has been some weeks.' He does not believe you, and you can see him deciding not to.".
  }
  Topic amaru_hour with amaru "Ask the king whether the hour was given" when true once {
    Says "'It was given,' says Amaru, as slowly as he has said anything. 'The lake asked for an hour and the hour came down. It speaks to the keepers, one sound in each moon.' His eyes are steady. 'My daughter says it fell. My daughter is a clerk.'".
  }
  Topic amaru_stone with amaru "Ask the king about a stone that sings" when amaruRate(amaru) <= 3 once {
    Says "Something moves in his face. 'There is no stone,' he says. 'There is the hour.' He looks at the rod of light over him. 'I have heard it sixteen hundred years. It is the hour's own heart. It is mine.'".
  }
  Topic amaru_daughter with amaru "Tell the king how his daughter died" when knows(actor, selane_murdered) once {
    Says "You tell him what the Wall of the Stair says. Amaru hears it out without moving at all, which at his speed is no sign of anything. Then he closes his eyes, and keeps them closed so long that you think he has gone back into the light. 'Loyal men,' he says. 'Loyal to me.' When he opens his eyes he takes the seal off its stand and holds it out to you. 'Open her doors,' he says. 'All of them.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(amaru, seal, actor). Retract inside(seal, seal_stand). Assert at(seal, last_hour). Assert grieves(amaru). }
  }
  Relation grieves(group).
  Event amaru_honey near amaru when keeps(amaru, ?j) and itemKind(?j, night_honey) "It takes the king a long time to lift the jar, and longer to open it. He eats with two fingers, slowly, and gives the rest to Kesset without being asked." then { Assert fed(amaru). }
  Relation fed(group).

  // His seal, the Long Hour on its stand, and the royal seed behind his chair.
  Kind amaru_seal "Amaru's seal" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A palm-sized stillglass plate. Drawn past a stylus it says, in an old man's voice, a name and one syllable.".
  Kind long_hour_plates "the Long Hour" is treasure worth 600 weighing 12
    described "About five thousand syllables of the Voice on stillglass plates, the Seridane transcript of the Long Hour.".
  Kind royal_seed "a jar of royal seed barley" is treasure worth 200 weighing 2
    described "Barley held in the light for sixteen hundred years and alive.".
  Thing seal_stand "the stand beside the chair" at last_hour {
    Holds.
    State standing "A stand of stillglass plates stands beside the chair: the Long Hour, and on top, a single palm-sized plate.".
  }
  Item seal "Amaru's seal" is amaru_seal in seal_stand owned by amaru.
  Item long_hour "the Long Hour" is long_hour_plates in seal_stand owned by amaru.
  Thing niche "a sealed niche behind the chair" at last_hour {
    Holds.
    State sealed closed "A niche is sealed into the wall behind the chair with red clay, and stamped.".
    State opened "The sealed niche behind the chair stands open.".
    Change break_niche "Break the clay seal on the niche" from sealed to opened needing digging.
  }
  Item seed_jar "a jar of royal seed barley" is royal_seed in niche owned by amaru.
  Discovery long_hour_read "The Long Hour, read: about five thousand syllables of the Voice, in order. Laid as the citadel was built, one course to a syllable, they are a plan of the Undersun's Seridane Reach.".
  Thing reading_stand "the Long Hour on its stand" at last_hour is scenery {
    State shelved "The plates of the Long Hour are racked in order, and a stylus hangs on a cord beside them.".
    State read "The plates of the Long Hour have been read through, and are a little out of order.".
    Change read_plates "Read the Long Hour through with a stylus" from shelved to read needing stylus.
  }
  Observe long_hour_known at last_hour when state(reading_stand, read) "Syllable after syllable, an hour and more of them. Where a syllable is open the course it laid is open; where it is closed, solid; where it repeats, a stair." teaches long_hour_read.
  Rule bren_seed when keeps(bren, ?j) and itemKind(?j, royal_seed) and not seeded(ennick) { Assert seeded(ennick). }
  Relation seeded(place).
  Event bren_seed_told near bren when seeded(ennick) "Bren holds the jar to the light and pours a little into his palm. 'Alive,' he says. 'Sixteen hundred years, and alive.' He does not thank you; he asks what you need.".

  // H4: the Coverers' Works and the Plumb, Selane's borehole, 400 metres toward the stone that sings.
  Observe works_scene at coverers_works when true "Walls of rammed red clay block three passages. In the middle of the floor a round shaft half a metre across goes straight down, lined with clear glass. Over it stand a bronze winch and a frame of rods.".
  Observe plumb_note at coverers_works when hour(clock) == 12 or hour(clock) == 0 "With an ear to the liner you hear it: a long low note, coming up four hundred metres of glass.".
  // A sounding lock: twelve stillglass rods, rung in the order of the hour-names carved over the door (Sounding
  // locks). Three wrong attempts in an hour drop the counterweight; it must then be dug out.
  Thing sounding_lock "the sounding lock" on archive_door {
    State shut blocking "Over the Coverers' archive door seven symbols of the sun's place are carved in a row; a row of short stillglass rods is set in the frame.".
    State jammed blocking "The counterweight has dropped into its locked seat. The door will have to be dug out.".
    State released "The archive door stands open on its counterweight.".
    Change ring_names "Ring the hour-names in the carved order" from shut to released after learning hour_names.
    Change ring_seal "Draw Amaru's seal past the rods" from shut to released needing seal.
    Change dig_out "Dig the counterweight out of its seat" from jammed to shut needing digging.
  }
  Measure misses(entity).
  Action ring_guess(actor: group, site: place) "Ring the rods in an order you guess" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, coverers_works) and state(sounding_lock, shut)
      and not knows(actor, hour_names).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Increase misses(sounding_lock) by 1. }
    Result "The rods ring, one after another, and the bar does not drop.".
  }
  Rule lock_jams when misses(sounding_lock) >= 3 and state(sounding_lock, shut) says "Something heavy drops inside the door frame with a sound like a dropped anvil." {
    Assert state(sounding_lock, jammed). Set misses(sounding_lock) to 0. }
  Discovery hour_names "The twelve Seridane hour-names, in order and with their pitches: what the sounding locks are keyed to.".
  Discovery rhyme_known "The Weirs' counting rhyme for the cranes: twelve words in a ring.".
  // Any two of the three sources give the names (the Weirs' rhyme, the Ward names, the Plate Hall song).
  Observe names_assembled near party when not knows(party, hour_names) and ((knows(party, rhyme_known) and knows(party, ward_names)) or (knows(party, rhyme_known) and knows(party, song_heard)) or (knows(party, ward_names) and knows(party, song_heard))) "The Weirs' twelve counting words, the twelve names the sick counted by, the children's twelve on the plate: they are one ring of hour-names, and you have them in order." teaches hour_names.

  // H5: the Wall of the Stair. A Coverer's record of Selane's last weeks; beneath it, folded, her Veil.
  Thing stair_record "the Wall of the Stair" at stair_wall {
    State silent "A single chant-wall two metres long, untouched, in a small chamber.".
    State playing "A woman's voice, faint, steady: the grain riots, Selane's order to open the reserve vaults, and her murder at the top of the Stair, by men of her father's party, who told the city it was the mob. Then the names of the men.".
    Change play_record "Draw a stylus along the Wall of the Stair" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Rule record_ends when state(stair_record, playing) and not at(party, stair_wall) { Assert state(stair_record, silent). }
  Discovery selane_murdered "Selane did not die in the grain riots: Answerer loyalists killed her at the top of the Stair and told the city it was the mob.".
  Observe record_heard at stair_wall when state(stair_record, playing) "A Coverer cut this, the year Tamaun emptied." teaches selane_murdered.
  Kind veil_kind "Selane's Veil" like cloak_of_protection worth 0 weighing 0
    described "Lace of drawn barrow-iron wire, three hundred grams, which covers its wearer from head to waist. Nothing said under it can be taken.".
  Initially Assert shields(veil_kind).
  Item veil "Selane's Veil" is veil_kind at stair_wall.
  Observe veil_seen at stair_wall when at(veil, stair_wall) "Folded on the floor beneath the wall lies a square of dark iron lace.".

  // H6: the Courses, the growth beneath the Late Sun breaking into the city. Saro opens them; a Mason's trowel does.
  Observe courses_scene at courses_face when true "At the bottom of the passage the wall is not stone. Bands of dark metal and clear glass are laid in perfect courses without a seam. Light runs inside them along their curves, around the corner of the passage. A cutter's boot sticks out of the third course.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/keeping.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Keeping (Tier IV): the plane where every moment of Imbar's past is kept, as a place. Geography is chronology:
  // walking inward goes back in time, walking across goes elsewhere in Imbar at the same moment. Near the shore a
  // careful walker covers a year in an hour; in deep time, where less happened, a thousand. Time passes for visitors
  // at its ordinary rate, and Imbar's clocks run while they are away.
  Place keeping "the Keeping" is plane.
  Place kept_imbar "the Keeping of Imbar" is region within keeping.
  Place shore "the shore of the present" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 0, 0.
  Place kept_plateau "the plateau's past" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 1, 0.
  Place hollows "the Quarried Reaches" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 1, 1.
  Place deep_time "deep time" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 2, 0.
  Place far_east "far east of Imbar's known lands" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 2, 1.
  Place wall_site "the Outer Wall" is site within kept_imbar at 3, 0.

  Place tideline "the Tideline" is room within shore at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place collar_years "the Collar's years" is room within kept_plateau at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place year_zero "the night of the Unlidding" is room within kept_plateau at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place covering_years "the Covering" is room within kept_plateau at 2, 0 outdoors.
  Place stair_murder "the top of the Stair, 1,575 BP" is room within kept_plateau at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place new_moons "the new moons" is room within kept_plateau at 3, 0 outdoors.
  Place kept_fall "the fall" is room within kept_plateau at 4, 0 outdoors.
  Place quarry_edge "a quarried hollow" is room within hollows at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place descent_k "the Descent" is room within deep_time at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place separation "the Separation" is room within deep_time at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place absence "an absence" is room within far_east at 0, 0.
  Place outer_wall "the Outer Wall" is room within wall_site at 0, 0 outdoors.

  // In: a living hand on Ithmar, with whoever touches that person. Out: walk back to the shore and step through.
  // Without Ithmar, only where you came in; with it, anywhere.
  Relation cameInAt(group, place).
  Action touch_ithmar(actor: group, site: place) "Lay a hand on Ithmar" {
    Description "A living hand that touches Ithmar enters the Keeping, together with anyone touching that person, at the moment and place of the touch.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, arbiter_vault)
      and (inside(ithmar, cage) or carries(actor, ithmar)).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract at(actor, arbiter_vault). Assert at(actor, tideline). Assert cameInAt(actor, arbiter_vault). }
    Result "The jewel is not cold, or warm. The white room goes on being there and you are not in it: you stand on a shore where the present is setting like wet sand.".
  }
  Passage step_back "the way you came in" is passage between tideline and arbiter_vault taking 10 minutes.
  Relation keepingWay(passage).
  Passage out_quell "out into Quell, now" is passage between tideline and square taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "The shore runs on, every place of Imbar this minute, soft as wet sand. Without the jewel you cannot step out anywhere but where you came in.".
  Passage out_orrel "out into New Orrel, now" is passage between tideline and no_market taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "Without the jewel there is no stepping out here.".
  Passage out_ennick "out into Ennick, now" is passage between tideline and lower_road taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "Without the jewel there is no stepping out here.".
  Passage out_stairhead "out at Stairhead, now" is passage between tideline and stair_top taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "Without the jewel there is no stepping out here.".
  Passage out_corbel "out at the Corbel's tip, at the moment it came" is passage between collar_years and lintel_room taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "In the year 71 something comes down the light out of the black, and stops in the cloud. Without the jewel, you can only watch it come.".
  Initially Assert keepingWay(out_quell). Initially Assert keepingWay(out_orrel). Initially Assert keepingWay(out_ennick).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(out_stairhead). Initially Assert keepingWay(out_corbel).
  // Every step through the Keeping with the jewel lays one of the wearer's own moments into its setting: a memory gone,
  // and everyone else forgets that moment too.
  Relation stepPaid(group, passage).
  Rule step_costs when tookWay(?c, ?w) and keepingWay(?w) and carries(?c, ithmar) and not stepPaid(?c, ?w) and memories(?c) >= 1
    says "Something of yours goes into the jewel's setting as you step: a morning, a face, a word somebody said once. You do not know which. Nobody does." {
    Decrease memories(?c) by 1. Assert stepPaid(?c, ?w). }
  Rule step_paid_clears when stepPaid(?c, ?w) and not tookWay(?c, ?w) { Retract stepPaid(?c, ?w). }
  Observe no_past near party when memories(party) == 0 "You have stepped so often that there is almost nothing behind you. You remember Saro. You do not remember why.".

  // Inward: back in time. Near the shore, a year an hour.
  Passage to_collar_years "inland, thirty years" is path between tideline and collar_years taking 32 hours.
  Passage to_year_zero "inland, three hundred and fifty years" is path between collar_years and year_zero taking 14 days.
  Passage to_covering "inland, through the craneless centuries" is path between year_zero and covering_years taking 3 days.
  Passage to_murder "across, to the Stair" is path between covering_years and stair_murder taking 4 hours.
  Passage to_moons "inland, through Tamaun's seven centuries" is path between covering_years and new_moons taking 10 days.
  Passage walk_moons "the new moons, walked a minute a moon" is path between new_moons and kept_fall taking 60 hours.
  Passage to_hollows "across, into the blank" is path between collar_years and quarry_edge taking 2 hours.
  // Deep time, where there are no landmarks: without the Tally or a guide, years of wandering.
  Passage to_descent "inland, into deep time" is path between kept_fall and descent_k taking 30 hours needing tally_kind or wayfinding.
  Passage to_separation "inland, to the Separation" is path between descent_k and separation taking 2 hours.
  Passage to_absence "across, far to the east" is path between descent_k and absence taking 2 days needing tally_kind or wayfinding.
  Passage to_wall "inland, before the beginning" is path between separation and outer_wall taking 4 hours.
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_collar_years). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_year_zero). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_covering).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_murder). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_moons). Initially Assert keepingWay(walk_moons).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_hollows). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_descent). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_separation).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_absence). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_wall).
  Action wander(actor: group, site: place) "Strike out into deep time without the Tally or a guide" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, kept_fall)
      and not holding(actor, tally_kind) and not capable(actor, wayfinding).
    Time 144.
    On success { Assert strikes(archivore_bite, actor). }
    Result "There are no landmarks. You walk a day and do not know if it was a day or a century, and something like a page turning follows you, and bites.".
  }

  // K1: the Tideline. Everything in Imbar that is happening now is here, still soft: a scrying ground.
  Observe tideline_scene at tideline when true "A shore where the present is setting, like wet sand hardening. Everything in Imbar that is happening now is here, still soft; you can walk across it and see any place you choose, as it is this minute.".
  Observe tide_orrel at tideline when at(amaru, barracks) "In New Orrel, this minute, an old king lies on a cot under three blankets and looks at a ceiling.".
  Observe tide_crew at tideline when argued(crew) and asleep(garret) "In the Granary Ring, this minute, two cutters sit with their backs to the wall by the ninth vault, waiting.".
  Observe tide_corbel at tideline when not docked(corbel_site) "Over the Pit, this minute, the Corbel is two metres lower than it was yesterday.".
  Observe tide_concord at tideline when convened(chapter) "In Stairhead's chapter house, this minute, the Concord is sitting, and nobody is sitting next to anybody they can help it.".
  Observe tide_saro at tideline when not travelsWith(saro, party) "At the Tip of the Undersun, this minute, a woman with no temperature lays a course and calls its syllable.".
  // Standing still on the Tideline, a visitor begins to set into the present.
  Measure tideWatches(group).
  Rule tide_counts when at(party, tideline) { Increase tideWatches(party) by 1. }
  Rule tide_resets when not at(party, tideline) and tideWatches(party) > 0 { Set tideWatches(party) to 0. }
  Observe tide_setting near party when at(party, tideline) and tideWatches(party) >= 4 "Your feet have sunk into the shore to the ankle, and it is hardening around them. Your own hand, when you lift it, comes up slowly.".
  Rule tide_takes when at(party, tideline) and tideWatches(party) >= 6 and not setInPresent(party) says "The present sets around you, and you are kept." {
    Assert setInPresent(party). Assert hobbled(party). }
  Relation setInPresent(group).
  Person shore_remembrancer "a Remembrancer of the shore" at tideline {
    Role "a servant of the Virina, tall, made of the sound of bells". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Wants quarried_moment.
  }
  Topic shore_quarried with shore_remembrancer "Ask the Remembrancer about the hollows" when true once {
    Says "'Cut,' says the Remembrancer, in bells. 'Carried out of the Keeping into the Masonry. Bring back what was cut, and we will set it again where it was kept, and it will be remembered.'".
  }
  Event moment_returned near shore_remembrancer when keeps(shore_remembrancer, ?q) and itemKind(?q, quarried_moment) "The Remembrancer takes the moment between two long fingers and sets it into the shore, somewhere inland, and in Imbar a season that nobody could remember is remembered again.".
  Rule dane_returned when keeps(shore_remembrancer, dane_moment) and not reanchored(fourth_dane) { Assert reanchored(fourth_dane). }

  // K2: the plateau's past.
  Observe collar_years_scene at collar_years when true "Inland from the shore the plateau gets younger: the Collar going up, then a storm, then down; carts; the Breach opening in a white roar of steam and coming back closed; Quell growing smaller.".
  Observe year_zero_scene at year_zero when true "A night of steam. Half of a town going into a hole in the ground. Then the light comes up out of the old Clear Fields everywhere at once, and sixty people at a fair stop where they stand, and their kin come with sand.".
  Observe covering_scene at covering_years when true "Thousands of people carrying red clay in baskets, for years, into a pit; and then the last light cut, and in the glass of the fields, all at once, eleven thousand people wake in the dark.".
  // The murder at the Stair: walked through, it plays; given time by touch, the faces.
  Observe murder_scene at stair_murder when true "The top of the falls at night, in riot-time. A young woman in a council robe on the path, and four men coming up behind her who are not rioters.".
  Thing murderers "the four men on the path" at stair_murder {
    State coming "Four men in Answerer badges come up the path behind Selane, hands under their cloaks.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(murderers).
  Observe murder_seen near murderers when touched(murderers) "For the length of your touch it plays: they reach her, and the knives come out, and one of them says the Dane's name as if it were a prayer. When they turn to go you see their faces, and their badges." teaches selane_murdered.
  // The new moons: the Voice's syllables as they were spoken, one at each new moon since the fall. Walking the first
  // three centuries of them recovers the Crown's plan, and the first syllable.
  Observe moons_scene at new_moons when true "Moonless nights, one after another, inland, each with a single sound passing through the rock near a young pit: a syllable, felt in the knees.".
  Observe moons_walked at kept_fall when not knows(party, crown_map) "Sixty hours of moonless nights, a syllable each, and you have them all in order: the Crown's plan, the Voice's first three hundred years." teaches crown_map.
  Observe first_from_moons at kept_fall when not knows(party, first_syllable) "The first of them you will not forget: it was the first sound the seed made in the world." teaches first_syllable.
  Discovery delver_seen "At the fall, riding the seed's wake out of a clear sky, very small: a figure with a trowel, the first Mason, who laid the First Course and went down into the dark with the stem.".
  Observe fall_scene_k at kept_fall when true "An autumn night out of a clear sky; a light coming down; the lake villages watching. Riding its wake, very small, visible only to someone looking for it, is a figure with a trowel." teaches delver_seen.

  // K3: the Quarried Reaches: blankness, a fog in which things have no reasons; Masons cutting at the edges.
  Observe hollow_scene at quarry_edge when true "History stops here. Not darkness: blankness, a fog in which things have no reasons. A road goes into it and does not come out. At its edges, figures with trowels are cutting, and the cut edges are clean.".
  Person cutters "a crew of Masons, cutting" at quarry_edge {
    Role "three Masons at the edge of the blank, cutting a season out of the plateau's last year". Ancestry human. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
  }
  Relation cutStopped(place).
  Topic cutters_stop with cutters "Ask the Masons to stop cutting" when true once {
    Says "They stop, because you asked, and look at you with honest puzzlement. 'It is the work,' says one. 'If we do not, another crew will.' But they put their trowels down, and that season stays where it is.".
    On discuss { Assert cutStopped(quarry_edge). }
  }
  Person clea "Clea Tull" at quarry_edge {
    Role "a Haldrish seer, lost, who walks here in her sleep". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Joins "'I know the way inward,' says Clea, 'better than anyone living. I have been lost in it for forty years.' She takes your sleeve like a child.".
  }
  Initially Assert willing(clea, party).
  Topic clea_where with clea "Tell Clea Tull where she is" when true once {
    Says "'The Keeping,' she says after you, as if it were a word in a dream. 'I have always called it the long country.' She looks at her hands. 'Something bites me here. A little, every night, for forty years.' She does not know that her body is dying in a bed in Sorne, and you do not tell her.".
  }
  // Archivores: the Keeping's predators. They feed on what belongs to no moment, and cannot enter one that is playing.
  Species archivore "an archivore" like wraith temperament ambush
    described "A flat shape like a page turning, seen edge-on as a line. A bite takes time from the rest of a life: a day for a graze, years for a deep wound.".
  Person archivores "archivores" at quarry_edge { Role "two flat shapes like pages turning". Species archivore. Numbers 2. }
  Hazard archivore_bite "an archivore's bite" means "Deal (2d8) necrotic damage to ally unless wisdom save against (14).".
  Measure yearsTaken(group).

  // K4: deep time. The Descent, and the Separation: the most dangerous place, and the most valuable.
  Observe descent_scene at descent_k when true "A night sky full of falling fire, every fall stopped, and the land under it burning.".
  Thing falling_fire "the falling fire" at descent_k { State falling "Fire hangs in the sky, coming down.". }
  Initially Assert kept(falling_fire).
  Hazard landed "a falling thing, landing" means "Deal (4d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Rule fire_lands when touched(falling_fire) says "For the length of your touch it falls, and lands." { Retract touched(falling_fire). Assert strikes(landed, party). }
  Observe separation_scene at separation when true "A sky divided: half full of figures with light for wings, half full of figures of darkness and hooks, all stopped in the act of striking, across a distance the eye cannot measure. Below them, tall robed figures in white stand in a ring, holding the world apart like the pages of a book. In the centre of the ring a hand is setting a jewel into stone.".
  Thing blows "the war overhead" at separation { State struck "Every blow overhead is stopped an inch from landing.". }
  Initially Assert kept(blows).
  Hazard unmaking "a blow of the Separation" means "Deal (10d10) force damage to ally.".
  Rule blow_lands when touched(blows) says "You touch a blow that nearly unmade the world, and for a moment it goes on." { Retract touched(blows). Assert strikes(unmaking, party). }
  Discovery sigils_known "How the sigils on Ithmar are cut, and so how a binding is made: watched at the Separation, stroke by stroke, a hand setting a jewel into stone.".
  Relation watchedBinding(group).
  Action watch_binding(actor: group, site: place) "Watch the hand in the ring cut the sigils, stroke by stroke" {
    Description "Walk slowly round the ring, letting the moment play, and do not touch anything.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, separation) and not watchedBinding(actor)
      and not benighted(actor).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert watchedBinding(actor). }
    Result "You walk the ring for two hours, slowly, so that it plays and does not stop, and you watch a hand cut the sigils on a jewel into its setting, one stroke at a time, until you could do it.".
  }
  Observe binding_learned near party when watchedBinding(party) and not knows(party, sigils_known) "You have the strokes. You know how it is bound; and so how it could be bound tighter." teaches sigils_known.

  // K5: an absence. Saro, at the last moment she still had; around her, nothing.
  Observe absence_scene at absence when true "A mountain hall, ages ago, and a woman standing in it with a jewel at her throat. Around her, in every direction, the Keeping is empty: a hole shaped like a life.".
  Discovery saro_remembers "Saro has seen herself: a woman who wore a Kiritarun, and spent her whole past using it, and was taken. She remembers her name.".
  Observe saro_sees at absence when travelsWith(saro, party) and not knows(party, saro_remembers) "Saro stands in front of the woman with the jewel for a long time. 'That is mine,' she says, the way she said it of the niche. Then, very quietly, she says a name, and it is not Saro, and she weeps, which she did not know how to do." teaches saro_remembers.

  // K6: the Outer Wall: the quarry face, and the road to the Masonry.
  Observe wall_scene_k at outer_wall when true "At the far inland edge, before the beginning, a wall. Through it, moments are being carried out on long tendrils of course-work into black.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/masonry.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Masonry (Tier V): the Patient's citadel beyond the planes, built of the pasts of other worlds. Five laws: air
  // is kept, not given; everything doses; stillness is laid; touch gives time; wings are histories.
  Place masonry "the Masonry" is plane.
  Place masonry_land "the Masonry" is region within masonry.
  Place citadel "the citadel of the Patient" is site within masonry_land at 0, 0.
  Place m_spine "the Spine" is level within citadel.
  Place m_wings "the wings" is level within citadel.
  Place m_heart "the heart" is level within citadel.
  Place spine "the Spine" is room within m_spine at 0, 0.
  Place finished_door "a wing door carved with circles" is room within m_wings at 0, 0.
  Place finished_city "a city of slender towers" is room within m_wings at 1, 0.
  Place finished_wild "fields, then forest, then rock" is room within m_wings at 2, 0.
  Place finished_beginning "the end of the wing" is room within m_wings at 3, 0.
  Place imbar_wing "the Imbar Wing" is room within m_wings at 0, 1.
  Place empty_niches "the empty niches" is room within m_wings at 1, 1.
  Place nave "the Nave of Sockets" is room within m_heart at 0, 0.
  Place heart "the Heart" is room within m_heart at 0, 1.

  // From the Corbel's Seam, or the Keeping's Outer Wall.
  Passage spine_from_seam "up into the black, onto the Spine" is passage between seam and spine taking 20 minutes.
  Passage spine_from_wall "along a tendril of course-work through the Wall" is passage between outer_wall and spine taking 20 minutes.
  Passage spine_wing "the bridge to a wing door" is passage between spine and finished_door taking 20 minutes.
  Passage wing_in "into the wing" is doorway between finished_door and finished_city.
  Passage wing_back "back through the world's history" is passage between finished_city and finished_wild taking 6 hours.
  Passage wing_end "to the wing's end" is passage between finished_wild and finished_beginning taking 6 hours.
  Passage spine_imbar "the bridge to the new wing" is passage between spine and imbar_wing taking 20 minutes.
  Passage imbar_niches "past the court, into the gallery" is passage between imbar_wing and empty_niches taking 30 minutes.
  Passage spine_nave "down into the heart" is stair between spine and nave taking 30 minutes.
  Passage wing_nave "down from the Imbar Wing" is stair between imbar_wing and nave taking 20 minutes.
  Passage nave_heart "beneath the beating socket" is passage between nave and heart taking 30 minutes.

  // Everything doses.
  Initially Assert litGround(spine). Initially Assert litGround(finished_door). Initially Assert litGround(finished_city).
  Initially Assert litGround(finished_wild). Initially Assert litGround(finished_beginning). Initially Assert litGround(imbar_wing).
  Initially Assert litGround(empty_niches). Initially Assert litGround(nave). Initially Assert litGround(heart).

  // Air is kept, not given: between moments there is no air at all. Visitors breathe the air of the moments they walk
  // through, and some worlds' air is poison.
  Kind airkind. Entity air_good: airkind "breathable air". Entity air_poison: airkind "poison". Entity air_none: airkind "no air".
  Relation airOf(place, airkind).
  Initially Assert airOf(spine, air_none). Initially Assert airOf(finished_door, air_good). Initially Assert airOf(finished_city, air_good).
  Initially Assert airOf(finished_wild, air_poison). Initially Assert airOf(finished_beginning, air_none).
  Initially Assert airOf(imbar_wing, air_good). Initially Assert airOf(empty_niches, air_none).
  Initially Assert airOf(nave, air_none). Initially Assert airOf(heart, air_good). Initially Assert airOf(seam, air_none).
  Measure breath(group).
  Rule breathes when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_good) and breath(party) < 12 { Set breath(party) to 12. }
  Rule holds_breath when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) and breath(party) >= 1 { Decrease breath(party) by 1. }
  Hazard airless "no air" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally.".
  Hazard bad_air "the air of another world" means "Deal (1d10) poison damage to ally unless constitution save against (13).".
  Rule suffocates when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) and breath(party) < 1 { Assert strikes(airless, party). }
  Rule poisoned when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_poison) { Assert strikes(bad_air, party). }
  Observe air_note near party when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) "There is no air here. You are breathing what you brought.".
  Observe breath_short near party when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) and breath(party) <= 4 "Your chest is burning. You have perhaps half an hour of what you carried in your lungs and your clothes.".
  Initially Set breath(party) to 12.
  // A company on its way between two places is at neither, so the rules above are silent for the length of a walk;
  // the air a way costs is said of the way, as the dose of a lit way is (ledger, 26).
  Measure wayAir(passage). Relation airPaid(group, passage).
  Initially Set wayAir(spine_from_seam) to 2. Initially Set wayAir(spine_from_wall) to 2. Initially Set wayAir(spine_wing) to 2.
  Initially Set wayAir(spine_imbar) to 2. Initially Set wayAir(spine_nave) to 3. Initially Set wayAir(wing_nave) to 2.
  Rule way_air when tookWay(party, ?w) and wayAir(?w) > 0 and not airPaid(party, ?w) and breath(party) >= wayAir(?w) {
    Decrease breath(party) by wayAir(?w). Assert airPaid(party, ?w). }
  Rule way_air_short when tookWay(party, ?w) and wayAir(?w) > 0 and not airPaid(party, ?w) and breath(party) < wayAir(?w)
    says "Halfway across there is nothing left in your lungs to breathe." {
    Set breath(party) to 0. Assert airPaid(party, ?w). Assert strikes(airless, party). }
  Rule way_air_clears when airPaid(party, ?w) and not tookWay(party, ?w) { Retract airPaid(party, ?w). }

  // Stillness is laid: a visitor who stays still for an hour is taken into the next course.
  Measure stillness(group). Relation lastPlace(group, place) exclusive. Relation laidIn(group).
  Rule still_counts when at(party, ?p) and lastPlace(party, ?p) and laidRoomM(?p) { Increase stillness(party) by 1. }
  Rule moved_on when at(party, ?p) and not lastPlace(party, ?p) { Assert lastPlace(party, ?p). Set stillness(party) to 0. }
  Relation laidRoomM(place).
  Initially Assert laidRoomM(spine). Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_door). Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_city).
  Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_wild). Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_beginning). Initially Assert laidRoomM(imbar_wing).
  Initially Assert laidRoomM(empty_niches). Initially Assert laidRoomM(nave). Initially Assert laidRoomM(heart).
  Observe still_warning near party when stillness(party) >= 4 and not laidIn(party) "The course under your feet is warmer than it was, and your boots will not lift as easily as they did.".
  Rule laid_in when stillness(party) >= 6 and not laidIn(party) says "You have stood still an hour. The next course is laid over your feet, and your knees, and you are part of the Masonry." {
    Assert laidIn(party). Assert hobbled(party). }

  // M1: the Spine.
  Observe spine_scene at spine when true "A bridge of dark banded stone crossing black. On either side the Masonry fills half the sky: towers and buttresses of stopped worlds, lit along their edges, going on past seeing. Far off, other long brackets like the Corbel reach out into the dark toward other points of light. Eleven of them.".

  // M2: a finished world. Walking the wing is walking that world's history backward to its beginning.
  Observe fdoor_scene at finished_door when true "A wing door carved with the overlapping circles of the procession's banner.".
  Observe fcity_scene at finished_city when true "A city of slender towers, stopped. Walking on, it gets younger, and smaller.".
  Observe fwild_scene at finished_wild when true "The city is fields, then forest, then bare rock, then fire. The air tastes of metal and burns going down.".
  Observe fbegin_scene at finished_beginning when true "At the very end of the wing a single course, no bigger than a hearthstone, holds the moment that world began. Then nothing.".
  Thing beginning "the moment the world began" at finished_beginning { State unbegun "A single course holds a world's first moment.". }
  Initially Assert kept(beginning).
  Observe world_begins near beginning when touched(beginning) "For the length of your touch a world begins around you: light, and heat, and rock coming together out of nothing, as long as someone holds on. It cannot be carried out.".

  // M3: the Imbar Wing. Everything quarried from Imbar so far is here; carried back through the Keeping to a
  // Remembrancer, each is set again where it was kept.
  Observe imbar_wing_scene at imbar_wing when true "A new wing, half built. Near its door are rooms that look like places you know: a stretch of the Quell road, a Weirs kitchen, a Tovash camp. Beyond them, a king's court whose king's face you cannot hold.".
  Kind quarried_moment "a quarried moment" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A moment cut out of the Keeping, the size of a coin, with a season of somebody's life in it.".
  Item dane_moment "the fourth Dane's reign" is quarried_moment at imbar_wing.
  Item quell_moment "a season of Quell's year 74" is quarried_moment at imbar_wing.
  Observe niches_scene at empty_niches when true "A long gallery of empty niches, waiting, each the size of a year.".
  Relation quellAnchored(place).
  Rule quell_returned when keeps(shore_remembrancer, quell_moment) and not quellAnchored(quell) { Assert quellAnchored(quell). }

  // M4: the Nave of Sockets. Nine sockets, all empty; one beats.
  Observe nave_scene at nave when true "A nave so tall its roof cannot be seen, with nine sockets cut into its floor in a ring, each large enough for a hen's egg and each empty. One socket beats, faintly, like a pulse felt through stone.".
  Action seat_ithmar(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Set Ithmar in the beating socket" {
    Description "The Patient is restored, and Imbar's past is quarried from the newest year backward, at the Masonry's own speed.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nave) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(ithmar, carrier).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve drop(ithmar, carrier).
    On success { Assert seated(ghessil). Assert unbound(ghessil). }
    Result "The jewel goes into its socket as if it had never been out. The beat stops being faint. All round you, in the walls, the Laid stir, as at a voice.".
  }
  // Rebind: with the sigils seen being cut at the Separation, the jewel bound again, tighter. A binding needs a kept
  // moment as its seal: the binder's own, and the binder becomes part of the Keeping, dead and remembered forever.
  Action rebind(actor: group, carrier: member, binder: member, site: place) "Bind Ithmar tighter, {binder} giving the binding their own moment" {
    Description "The Patient's heart-bond breaks; the seed stops and the Corbel withdraws. The binder is set in the jewel, and dies, and everyone will remember them.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, nave) or at(actor, arbiter_vault))
      and knows(actor, sigils_known) and memberOf(carrier, actor) and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(ithmar, carrier)
      and memberOf(binder, actor) and awake(binder) and not rebound(corbel_site).
    Time 30 minutes.
    Resolve inter(binder).
    On success { Assert rebound(corbel_site). }
    Result "Stroke by stroke, as you watched it done at the Separation, the binding is cut tighter, and {binder} lays a hand on the jewel and is in it: you can see them, very small and clear, in the dark opal. Far off, felt in the knees, the seed stops building.".
  }

  // M5: the Heart: the Patient's own moment of expulsion, kept as its heart. Given time, the expulsion resumes: for as
  // long as the touch lasts the Patient goes on falling, farther from the planes, and the Masonry falls with it.
  Observe patient_heart_scene at heart when true "A chamber made of one moment. It is a fall: something vast, dark and many-limbed, too large to see whole, caught in the instant of being thrown out of the world. Around it, stopped, white robes and outstretched hands.".
  Thing patient_heart "the Patient's fall" at heart { State first_instant "The fall is stopped at its first instant.". }
  Initially Assert kept(patient_heart).
  Measure fallHeld(entity).
  Rule heart_falls when touched(patient_heart) { Increase fallHeld(patient_heart) by 1. }
  Observe heart_falling near patient_heart when touched(patient_heart) and fallHeld(patient_heart) < 6 "Under your hand the vast thing goes on falling, away, and everything around you leans after it. Your hand is going with it.".
  Rule exile_done when fallHeld(patient_heart) >= 6 and touched(patient_heart) and not exiled(corbel_site)
    says "You have held an hour. The Patient is gone out past the planes, and the Masonry with it, and you with it, because you did not let go." {
    Assert exiled(corbel_site). Assert fellWith(party). }
  Relation fellWith(group).
  Action touch_and_step(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Touch the Heart and step away through the Keeping at once" {
    Description "Only a wearer of Ithmar can: touch, and be gone at the speed of thought, at the jewel's own cost.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(ithmar, carrier) and memories(actor) >= 3 and not exiled(corbel_site).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Decrease memories(actor) by 3. Assert exiled(corbel_site). Retract at(actor, heart). Assert at(actor, tideline). }
    Result "You touch the fall, and it falls, and you are gone through the jewel before it can take you: three of your own moments go into the setting as you step. Behind you, the Patient falls out past the planes, and the Masonry with it.".
  }
  // Saro, who has no past to lose, may offer to hold on.
  Action saro_holds(actor: group, holder: member, site: place) "Let Saro hold on" {
    Description "She will hold the Heart for as long as it takes, and fall with it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart) and travelsWith(saro, actor)
      and memberOf(holder, actor) and joinedAs(holder, saro) and not exiled(corbel_site).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve inter(holder).
    On success { Assert exiled(corbel_site). Retract travelsWith(saro, actor). }
    Result "'Go,' says Saro, with both hands on the fall. 'I know how to be still.' The last you see of her she is falling with it, out past the planes, and she is not afraid.".
  }
  // Bargain at the heart: terms better than the Corbel's. Name a line in history and hold the Masonry to it.
  Action heart_bargain(actor: group, site: place) "Name a line in history to the Interlocutor, here, and hold the Masonry to it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart) and knows(actor, newest_backward)
      and carries(actor, ithmar) and not bargained(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert bargained(actor). Assert heldToLine(corbel_site). }
    Result "Your own voice out of the walls of the Heart agrees: nothing after the Separation; and, because you know from which end it cuts, it agrees to cut from the beginning, not the face. The Masonry will be very patient about it.".
  }
  Relation heldToLine(place).
}

data/adventures/patient-star/moments.kyr:
Module moments "Kept moments: what the stilling took, laid as masonry, and given time by a hand" {
  // Where the stilling stops matter wholly it takes the moment, and the Masonry lays it as building stone (the
  // Undersun, the Corbel, the Masonry), and the Keeping keeps every moment of Imbar's past as a place. Three rules hold
  // in all of them: a kept thing touched resumes its moment for as long as the touch lasts; words spoken aloud are
  // laid into the course beneath; nothing kept can be changed, only cut.

  // A kept thing: a stopped flame, a man mid-word, a curtain of smoke, a falling stone.
  Relation kept(entity).
  // Being touched, now: its moment plays.
  Relation touched(entity).
  // Whoever has touched a thing at least once, and what they saw of it played.
  Relation playedFor(entity, group).
  Action touch(actor: group, target: entity, site: place) "Lay a hand on {target}" {
    Description "A kept thing touched takes up its moment again for as long as the hand stays on it, and stops when it is taken away.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and kept(target) and reaches(actor, target)
      and not touched(target) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert touched(target). Assert playedFor(target, actor). }
  }
  Action let_go(actor: group, target: entity, site: place) "Take your hand from {target}" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and touched(target) and reaches(actor, target).
    Time 0.
    On success { Retract touched(target). }
  }
  // A hand cannot stay on a thing the company has walked away from.
  Rule touch_lost when touched(?t) and company(?c) and not reaches(?c, ?t) { Retract touched(?t). }

  // Speech is laid: words said aloud in course-work are taken into the course beneath, and give the Laid near them a
  // few seconds of their moment. Whispered, nothing is taken. The company is aloud until it chooses to whisper.
  Relation whispering(group).
  Relation laidRoom(place).
  Action whisper(actor: group) "Speak only in whispers" {
    Description "Below, words said aloud are taken into the stone, and wake whatever is laid there for a breath.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and not whispering(actor) and at(actor, ?r) and laidRoom(?r). Time 0.
    On success { Assert whispering(actor). }
    Result "You drop your voice to a breath, and so does everyone with you.".
  }
  Action speak_up(actor: group) "Speak aloud again" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and whispering(actor). Time 0.
    On success { Retract whispering(actor). }
    Result "You speak up again.".
  }
  // Every word spoken aloud in a laid room is a course laid down: the Masons can play it back, and the Interlocutor
  // speaks with it.
  Measure wordsLaid(group).
  Relation spokeAloud(group).
  // Every Mason carries a trowel: it lays and unlays course-glass, and in the Keeping cuts moments out.
  Kind trowel_kind "a Mason's trowel" like dagger worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A blade of something like stopped iron, set in a handle with no temperature. Laid against course-glass it lays or unlays.".
  Item spare_trowel "a Mason's trowel" is trowel_kind at tip_dome hidden until trowel_paid.
}

data/adventures/patient-star/neworrel.ky:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // New Orrel, the Collar and the Pit; the dark glass, the Tovash wells and the Split Ear camp; the Sixty and the Ear.
  Place new_orrel "New Orrel" is settlement within ghessil at 2, 0.
  Place collar "the Collar" is site within ghessil at 3, 0.
  Place dark_sector "the Dark Sector" is wilderness within ghessil at 4, 0.
  Place lit_fields "the lit fields" is wilderness within ghessil at 4, 1.

  Place no_gate "the Collar Road gate" is room within new_orrel at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place no_market "the market road" is room within new_orrel at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place barracks_house "the Warden's house" is building within new_orrel.
  Place barracks "the Warden's room" is room within barracks_house at 2, 1.
  Place widows "the Widows' Board" is room within new_orrel at 1, 2.
  Place waiting_house "the House of the Waiting" is room within new_orrel at 0, 2.
  Place storehouse "the Warden's storehouse" is room within new_orrel at 2, 0.
  Place sink "the Sink" is room within new_orrel at 3, 2 outdoors.
  Place balloon_yard "the balloon shed" is room within new_orrel at 3, 1 outdoors.

  Place collar_top "the top of the Collar" is room within collar at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place plumb_tower "the plumb station" is room within collar at 1, 0.
  Place breach "the Breach" is room within collar at 2, 0 outdoors.
  Place inner_fill "the inner fill" is room within collar at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place pit_floor "the Pit floor" is room within collar at 1, 2 outdoors.

  Place dark_glass "the dark glass" is room within dark_sector at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place quarry "the Office quarry" is room within dark_sector at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place tovash_wells "the Tovash wells" is room within dark_sector at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place split_ear_camp "the Split Ear camp" is room within dark_sector at 1, 1 outdoors.

  Place the_sixty "the Sixty" is room within lit_fields at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place the_ear "the Ear" is room within lit_fields at 1, 0.

  // The Collar Road: seven kilometres of rammed umber a metre above the lit glass, with a parapet on the Pit side.
  Passage collar_road "the Collar Road" is causeway between square and no_gate taking 5 hours.
  Initially Set wayDose(collar_road) to 72. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(collar_road) to 18.
  Passage no_street "the gate street" is road between no_gate and no_market taking 5 minutes.
  Passage warden_door "the Warden's door" is door between no_market and barracks.
  Passage widows_door "the Board's door" is door between no_market and widows.
  Passage waiting_door "the Waiting's door" is door between no_gate and waiting_house.
  Passage store_door "the storehouse door" is door between no_market and storehouse.
  Passage sink_lane "the east lane" is path between no_market and sink taking 5 minutes.
  Passage balloon_lane "the lane to the balloon shed" is path between sink and balloon_yard taking 5 minutes.
  Passage collar_ramp "the haul ramp" is path between no_market and collar_top taking 20 minutes.
  Passage tower_door "the plumb tower door" is door between collar_top and plumb_tower.
  Passage collar_walk "the Collar path" is path between collar_top and breach taking 40 minutes.
  Passage fill_slope "the inner slope" is path between collar_top and inner_fill taking 20 minutes.
  Passage pit_descent "the slumping fill into the Pit" is path between inner_fill and pit_floor taking 40 minutes.
  // The Coverers' Stair: a Seridane stair under the old Barrow, the Office's own door to the Granaries.
  Passage coverers_stair "the Coverers' Stair" is stair between storehouse and watch_room taking 30 minutes.
  // Across the dark glass from the Breach, and from Quell by the north-east, without dose: it carries no light.
  Passage dark_way "the dark glass" is path between breach and dark_glass taking 30 minutes.
  Passage quell_dark "the north-east margin" is path between old_quell and dark_glass taking 3 hours.
  Passage quarry_way "the quarry track" is track between dark_glass and quarry taking 10 minutes.
  Passage wells_way "the way to the wells" is path between dark_glass and tovash_wells taking 20 minutes.
  Passage camp_way "the camp path" is path between tovash_wells and split_ear_camp taking 15 minutes.
  // The wells: Seridane air shafts two metres across, a hundred metres to the water; side openings on the Shallows at
  // thirty-five and the Granaries at eighty-five.
  Passage well_shaft "a Tovash well shaft, by the rope" is shaft between tovash_wells and bunks taking 20 minutes needing rope.
  Passage well_deep "the same shaft, further down" is shaft between bunks and ring taking 20 minutes needing rope.
  // Out across the lit fields from the Collar's foot: three and a half kilometres of glass to the Sixty.
  Passage fields_way "the lit glass to the Sixty" is path between collar_top and the_sixty taking 1 hour.
  Initially Set wayDose(fields_way) to 24. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(fields_way) to 6.
  Passage ear_way "the glass to the Ear" is path between the_sixty and the_ear taking 15 minutes.
  Initially Assert litGround(the_sixty). Initially Assert litGround(the_ear). Initially Assert litGround(pit_floor).
  Initially Assert litGround(inner_fill).

  Observe gate_scene_no at no_gate when true "The Collar Road comes off the glass onto an island of red spoil. Ahead the Collar stands up like a red cliff thirty metres high, and the town is packed against its foot.".
  Observe market_no at no_market when true "A road of red dust between houses built of the Collar's own spoil. Everything sold here costs what it cost to bring up the Stair.".
  Observe sink_scene at sink when true "The ground has dropped two metres here since 374. The houses lean into one another like drunks, doors hanging, and nobody lives in them.".
  Observe store_scene at storehouse when true "The Warden's storehouse: sacks, barrels, and at the back a cut stone arch with a stair going down, a lamp, two guards and a clerk at a table.".
  Observe collar_top_scene at collar_top when true "A path wide enough for carts runs round the top of the ring. Rusted horse-whims stand at intervals, with wooden chutes running down the inside slope into the Pit's haze.".
  Observe tower_scene at plumb_tower when true "A wooden tower on the Collar top. A bronze plumb line on a drum goes down through a hole in the floor, and survey logs fill a shelf.".
  Observe breach_scene at breach when true "The ring is broken by a gap forty metres wide, its edges baked white. Beside it a drainage culvert of cut stone runs under the path. Beyond, the clear fields are dark: the same clear rock, with no light in it.".
  Observe fill_scene at inner_fill when true "Inside the Collar the fill slopes down toward the shaft in long red terraces, cracked like old mud. The heat comes up off it, and the light.".
  Observe pit_scene at pit_floor when true "The Pit floor is melt-rock and ceramic slag, too hot to stand on long, too bright to look across. From a dark mouth in the middle a thread of light goes straight up into the cloud, and beside it, hanging from nowhere, a cord as thick as a wrist, glowing along its whole length.".
  Hazard pit_heat "the Pit's heat" means "Deal (1d6) fire damage to ally.".
  Rule pit_burns when at(party, pit_floor) and not pitScorched(party) { Assert strikes(pit_heat, party). Assert pitScorched(party). }
  Relation pitScorched(group).
  Rule pit_cools when pitScorched(party) and not at(party, pit_floor) { Retract pitScorched(party). }
  // The fill is moving: a party on the inner slope may be carried down toward the light and heat.
  Hazard fill_slide "a slide of fill" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Rule fill_slides when at(party, inner_fill) and dice(inner_fill) <= 4 says "The terrace you are on lets go with a sound like a sigh and carries you down toward the light." {
    Assert strikes(fill_slide, party). Assert at(party, pit_floor). }

  // The Warden and the Office in New Orrel.
  Person aske "Ivo Aske" at barracks {
    Role "Warden of the Collar". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
  }
  Person office_guard "the Coverers' Stair guard" at storehouse {
    Role "two Office men and a clerk at the stair". Ancestry human. Numbers 2. Peaceable.
    Guards coverers_stair.
    State posted blocking "Two Office men and a clerk sit at the head of the Coverers' Stair.".
  }
  Initially Assert serves(office_guard, aske).
  Rule licence_stair when licensed(party) and not tolerates(office_guard, party) { Assert tolerates(office_guard, party). }
  Topic aske_king with aske "Ask the Warden about the king below" when true once {
    Says "'Royal property,' says Aske, 'and a wonder. When he is well enough I mean to bring him up to Sorne, and the court will see what the Crown holds under this plateau.' He smiles without warmth. 'You will have heard he wakes. I have it in a book.'".
  }
  Topic aske_balloon with aske "Ask the Warden about the shed by the Sink" when true once {
    Says "'A fire-balloon,' says Aske. 'Haldrish silk and Haldrish craftsmen. It will lift six to the bottom of the Cloud on a calm autumn dawn.' He watches you. 'Whoever goes up in it goes in the Crown's name. Bring me something from up there the court can hold in its hands, and you go in mine.'".
    On discuss { Assert offered(aske, actor). }
  }
  Action pay_aske(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Warden twenty crowns toward his men's wages" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(aske, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 20
      and not admits(aske, actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 20. Increase quantity(aske, gold) by 20. Assert admits(aske, actor).
      Assert serves(office_guard, aske). }
    Result "Aske counts it twice. 'The Crown is grateful,' he says, and writes you a pass for the Coverers' Stair and a place on the balloon.".
  }
  // In the eighth week, if nobody has taken the king, Aske's men carry him up the Coverers' Stair; at his age and
  // rate, without careful feeding, he has a fever within a fortnight.
  Rule king_carried when day(clock) >= 56 and at(amaru, last_hour) and not grieves(amaru) says "Word comes up the Coverers' Stair: the Warden's men have carried the old king up out of the Hour on a litter." {
    Retract at(amaru, last_hour). Assert at(amaru, barracks). Assert fevered(amaru). }
  Relation fevered(group).
  Observe king_in_barracks near amaru when at(amaru, barracks) and fevered(amaru) "The old king lies on a cot in the Warden's room under three blankets, burning with fever, and looks at the ceiling as if waiting for light to come down it.".

  // Annet Coyle and the Breach widows; Lenna Marsh and the sinking; Ruan Dace and the Waiting.
  Person coyle "Annet Coyle" at widows {
    Role "speaker for the Breach widows". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
  }
  Topic coyle_breach with coyle "Ask Annet Coyle about the Breach" when true once {
    Says "'Sixty-three men,' says Annet Coyle. 'Mine among them. Somebody cut the Collar's drain in the storm of 352 and let the water into the Pit, and the steam came back up the chutes. Nobody was hanged for it.' She looks at you. 'They say the Tovash did it. I want the name. And I want the pensions, which have not been paid since 71.'".
  }
  Topic coyle_named with coyle "Tell Annet Coyle who cut the Breach" when knows(actor, breach_cut) once {
    Says "She hears it out without sitting down. 'Bren of Ennick,' she says. 'Who holds the dying.' For a long time she says nothing. 'I will go to Ennick myself,' she says, 'and look at his door.'".
    On discuss { Assert accused(coyle, bren). }
  }
  Relation accused(group, group).
  Person lenna "Lenna Marsh" at plumb_tower {
    Role "Glass Office surveyor at the plumb station". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
  }
  Discovery sinking "The Late Sun is sinking about a metre a year, twenty-five times the old rate, and the Collar's inner face will slide into the shaft within ten years. Lenna Marsh's logs show it month by month since 372." {
    Source marsh_logs "Lenna Marsh's survey logs" at plumb_tower readable by party.
    Known by lenna.
  }
  Discovery footprints "Lenna Marsh's log for the 3rd of Frost 379: a single line of bare footprints on the inner fill near the Breach, going up from the Pit's edge.".
  Topic marsh_logs_t with lenna "Ask Lenna Marsh what her logs say" when true once {
    Says "'That the Sun is going down a metre a year,' says Marsh, 'and nobody in Sorne reads past the first line.' She flips back a year. 'And this. Third of Frost, last year: bare footprints on the fill, going up from the edge. I took it for a soldier's prank.' She closes the book. 'Nobody walks up out of that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, footprints). }
  }
  // At dawn from the Collar top, for a few minutes before the sun washes it out, something long and dark shows in the
  // Standing Cloud.
  Discovery corbel_seen "At dawn from the Collar, a long dark shape hangs point-down in the Standing Cloud, high over the Pit, for a few minutes before the sun washes it out.".
  Observe corbel_dawn at collar_top when hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) <= 6 "Before the sun clears the heath, high in the Standing Cloud over the Pit, something long and dark hangs point-down, like a bracket on a wall with no wall. Then the light comes and it is gone." teaches corbel_seen.
  Person ruan "Ruan Dace" at waiting_house {
    Role "Elder of the Waiting". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
  }
  Topic ruan_voice with ruan "Ask Ruan Dace what the Waiting wait for" when true once {
    Says "'For the answer,' says Ruan. 'Teodar said the name was finished in 71, and what comes after is not more of the name but what it called.' He spreads his hands. 'We listen. The Office has closed the Hour to us, and my people go down without leave.'".
  }
  Topic ruan_tone with ruan "Tell Ruan Dace about the tone below" when knows(actor, tone_below) once {
    Says "Ruan sits down. 'Once an hour,' he says. 'And they did not tell me.' After a while he laughs, very quietly. 'Then it has answered. Teodar was right.' He gives you a tablet from his sleeve: the Waiting's copy of the transcript. 'Take it to whoever can read it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ward_names). }
  }

  // The Collar's culvert and the missing pin; the holder's bolt in Ennick (The Collar, Referee).
  Thing culvert "the drainage culvert" at breach {
    State standing "A culvert of cut stone runs under the Collar path beside the Breach, with a sluice frame at its mouth.".
    Tries looking.
  }
  Discovery herd_mark "Inside the culvert's sluice frame a Split Ear herd-mark is cut, and the gate's iron pin is missing from its square socket.".
  Observe culvert_looked near culvert when tried(culvert, looking) "On the inside of the sluice frame someone has cut a herd-mark: two notches and a split. The gate's pin is gone; its socket is square, and big as a thumb." teaches herd_mark.
  Discovery breach_cut "The Collar's drainage was cut in the storm of 352 by Ayzhe of the Split Ear and Bren of Ennick, with two Tovash riders, to flood the works and stop the Covering. They thought the fill would soak the water up.".
  Observe pin_matched near party when knows(party, herd_mark) and knows(party, bolt_is_pin) and not knows(party, breach_cut) "A Split Ear mark in the culvert, a sluice pin bolting the holder's door: whoever cut the Collar's drain was of the Split Ear, and was in Ennick after. You know of only one holder who was twenty-two that year." teaches breach_cut.

  // The dark glass: no light in it since 357, so it can be cut without dose, and Kell's forty-one dead stand in it.
  Observe dark_scene at dark_glass when true "The same clear rock as the lit fields, with no light in it at all. People stand in it, chest-deep, a little way off: men and women of Kell, held in 353 and dead when the fill cut the light four years later.".
  Observe quarry_scene at quarry when not halted(quarry) "Office crews are cutting blocks out of the dark glass with saws and grit. The quarry face is sixty metres from the nearest of Kell's dead, and pegs and string mark a line straight through them.".
  Observe quarry_halted at quarry when halted(quarry) "The quarry is quiet. The saws are racked and covered; somebody has pulled up the pegs that ran toward Kell's dead.".
  Relation halted(place).
  Measure quarryFace(place).
  Initially Set quarryFace(quarry) to 60.
  Rule quarry_cuts when not halted(quarry) and hour(clock) == 14 and quarryFace(quarry) > 0 and dice(quarry) <= 30 { Decrease quarryFace(quarry) by 2. }
  Observe quarry_reaches at quarry when quarryFace(quarry) <= 0 "The quarry face has reached the first of Kell's dead. A man stands in a block on a sledge, still chest-deep, looking at nothing, ready to go down the Stair.".
  Topic bren_quarry with bren "Tell Bren the Office is cutting toward Kell's dead" when true once {
    Says "Bren's face does not move. 'Then the road shuts,' he says. 'No Office cart comes up through Ennick while that quarry cuts.' He is already reaching for his coat.".
    On discuss { Assert roadClosed(ennick). }
  }
  Relation roadClosed(place).
  Rule aske_halts when roadClosed(ennick) and not halted(quarry) and day(clock) >= 10 says "Word comes across the plateau: the Warden has stopped the dark-glass quarry, and blames the licencer." { Assert halted(quarry). }

  Observe wells_scene at tovash_wells when true "Three stone rings stand on the dark glass, two metres across, with wooden frames for rope. Swallows go down one of them at dusk and do not come out.".
  Observe wells_swallows at tovash_wells when dark() "In the last of the light the swallows come in over the heath in ones and twos, fold their wings at the lip of the middle well, and drop down it.".

  // The Split Ear: Ayzhe, who cut the Breach; Ezh, who would ride with you; and, from the fifth week, Halu.
  Person ayzhe "Ayzhe of the Split Ear" at split_ear_camp {
    Role "clan-mother of the Split Ear". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner proud.
  }
  Person ezh "Ezh of the Split Ear" at split_ear_camp {
    Role "a young rider". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
  }
  Initially Set hire(ezh) to 2.
  Topic ayzhe_wife with ayzhe "Ask Ayzhe what she wants" when true once {
    Says "'The drum-maker's wife,' says Ayzhe. 'Out among the Sixty. We count our line from her, ten mothers back.' She looks toward the light. 'The last time someone buried the Pit, every held one on this plateau woke in the glass and choked. I will not leave her there for the next.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(ezh, actor). }
  }
  Discovery moot_count "The Split Ear moot song's beat: the count the drum at the fair was playing when the Sixty were held.".
  Topic ayzhe_drum with ayzhe "Ask Ayzhe about the drum at the fair" when true once {
    Says "'The moot song,' says Ayzhe at once, and beats it on her knee: three, a rest, two, three. 'It is what the drum was playing when the light came up at the fair. My grandmother's grandmother told it.' She stops. 'Why?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, moot_count). }
  }
  Topic ayzhe_breach with ayzhe "Ask Ayzhe who cut the Collar's drain" when knows(actor, breach_cut) once {
    Says "Ayzhe looks at you a long time. 'We thought the fill would drink it,' she says. 'Sixty-three. I count them every night.' She does not ask you what you will do.".
  }
  Person halu "Halu" at last_hour {
    Role "a woman of the old people, speaking Old Seridan". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
  }
  Initially Retract at(halu, last_hour).
  Rule halu_climbs when day(clock) >= 33 and not walkedOut(halu) says "Word goes round the Tovash camps: a dead woman of the old people climbed out of one of the wells in the night, talking." {
    Assert at(halu, split_ear_camp). Assert walkedOut(halu). }
  Relation walkedOut(group).
  Topic halu_kesset with halu "Tell Halu that Kesset is looking for her" when travelsWith(kesset, actor) or knows(actor, kings_book) once {
    Says "Halu understands one word in three of what you say, and the one she understands is the chamberlain's name. She sits down on the glass and weeps, and then she gets up and asks, in Old Seridan, the way to the city above.".
    On discuss { Assert willing(halu, actor). }
  }

  // The Sixty and the Ear (The Sixty; The Ear).
  Observe sixty_scene at the_sixty when true "A fair caught in the glass, chest-deep: horses in harness, a cauldron with its steam gone solid, children with their arms out, a man with a drum held against his chest. Their eyes are open.".
  Measure sixtyWatched(group).
  Rule watching_sixty when at(party, the_sixty) and not benighted(party) { Increase sixtyWatched(party) by 1. }
  Rule sixty_reset when not at(party, the_sixty) and sixtyWatched(party) > 0 { Set sixtyWatched(party) to 0. }
  Observe sixty_moved at the_sixty when sixtyWatched(party) >= 6 "You have watched an hour. A child's hand is higher than it was. The drum-maker's wife has turned her head a finger's width toward her husband.".
  Thing wife_block "the drum-maker's wife" at the_sixty {
    State held "A woman in a red felt cap stands in the glass beside the drummer, half-turned toward him.".
    State cut_free "The drum-maker's wife sits on a blanket on the glass, wrapped in felt, staring at the fair she was part of.".
    Change cut_wife "Grind the drum-maker's wife out of the glass" from held to cut_free needing digging.
  }
  Rule wife_tovash when state(wife_block, cut_free) and not freedWife(ayzhe) says "Two Split Ear riders come across the glass at a gallop and kneel by the woman in the red cap." { Assert freedWife(ayzhe). Assert grateful(ayzhe, party). }
  Relation freedWife(group).
  Observe ear_scene at the_ear when true "A low hut of umber brick with no floor. Inside, the bare glass is worn smooth in six places where people have knelt. In the corner an old man sits against the wall, cross-legged, head bowed, with his ear toward the glass. He has been dead since 368, and looks a week dead.".
  Discovery listeners_count "Teodar Lusk's count, year 0 to year 371: every syllable of the Voice heard since the Unlidding, in order; the plan of the Undersun's lowest built reach.".
  Thing count_shelf "the shelf of wax tablets" at the_ear {
    State shelved "A shelf of wax tablets runs along one wall: the count, year by year.".
    State read "The count's tablets have been taken down and read, and put back out of order.".
    Change read_count "Read the count through" from shelved to read.
  }
  Observe count_read at the_ear when state(count_shelf, read) "Three hundred and seventy years of syllables, a moon to a line. Teodar's last tablet says the name was finished, and what comes next will be an answer." teaches listeners_count.
}

data/adventures/patient-star/placed.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // The Ghessil Uplands as a country beyond a march: the company that comes into the Shift Market is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/quell.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  Description "Quell, the Granaries of Tamaun and Ennick, late in Haying of the year 380: a cutter's uncle held eleven months in an open granary vault, and the people who want him, or his jars, brought up.".

  // The plateau, as far as this slice goes: Quell on the western margin, the heath and the Ramp to the gorge,
  // Ennick on the gorge floor, the Clear Fields above it, and the city under the glass.
  Place imbar "Imbar" is plane.
  Place ghessil "the Ghessil Uplands" is region within imbar.
  Place quell "Quell" is settlement within ghessil at 0, 1.
  Place heath "the heath" is wilderness within ghessil at 1, 1.
  Place ennick "Ennick" is settlement within ghessil at 2, 2.
  Place fields "the Clear Fields above Ennick" is wilderness within ghessil at 3, 1.
  Place tamaun "Tamaun" is site within ghessil at 1, 0.

  Place mutual_house "the Mutual's hall" is building within quell.
  Place lazar_house "the lazar house" is building within quell.
  Place office_house "the Glass Office" is building within quell.
  Place square "the Shift Market" is room within quell at 1, 1.
  Place mutual_yard "the Mutual's yard" is room within quell at 1, 0.
  Place mutual_hall "the Mutual's hall" is room within mutual_house at 1, 0.
  Place ward "the lazar ward" is room within lazar_house at 0, 1.
  Place weighing "the weighing yard" is room within office_house at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place well_head "the North Well head" is room within quell at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place old_quell "Old Quell" is room within quell at 2, 0 outdoors.

  Passage yard_gate "the Mutual's yard gate" is gate between square and mutual_yard.
  Passage hall_door "the hall door" is door between mutual_yard and mutual_hall.
  Passage lazar_door "the lazar house door" is door between square and ward.
  Passage weighing_gate "the weighing-yard gate" is gate between square and weighing.
  Passage well_lane "the well lane" is path between square and well_head taking 5 minutes.
  Passage east_gate "the old east gate" is gate between square and old_quell.

  Observe square_scene at square when not dark() "The square is umber brick on every side, the colour of dried blood, and not one window looks east. Sledges hiss on the cobbles between the shifts. At the weighing-yard gate a clerk calls the grades: 'One. One. Three. Reject.'".
  Observe square_night at square when dark() "The square is empty but for the dusk crew coming in, hoods back, grey in the face. Somebody coughs, dry and short, and does not stop for a while.".
  Observe yard_scene at mutual_yard when true "The Mutual's yard: sledges up on their ends against the wall, grit-sacks, coils of rope, and a trough of grey water where the cutters wash the glitter off their hands.".
  Observe hall_scene at mutual_hall when true "A long room with a hearth at one end and the Mutual's tally-boards along the wall: crews, shifts, debts, chalked and rubbed out and chalked again. Your own name is up there, with a number beside it.".
  Observe ward_scene at ward when true "Twenty beds, eighteen of them full. The cough here is the same cough as the square's, only slower.".
  Observe weighing_scene at weighing when true "The Glass Office's yard, in what were the Company's yards: scales, a stamp-table, blocks of clear stone stacked under red cloth, and a board by the gate that says LICENCES DRAWN FIRST OF THE MONTH.".
  Observe well_scene at well_head when true "The North Well is a round head of old cut stone, older than the town, with a stair going down inside it to the water.".
  Observe well_water at well_head when not drained(quell_wells) "Far down, the water is a coin of light. It comes up at blood heat, and smells faintly of iron.".
  Observe well_water_low at well_head when drained(quell_wells) "Far down, the water has sunk below the last of the old marks on the stair. Women are queuing at the well with their jars and arguing about it.".
  Observe old_quell_scene at old_quell when true "Three streets of umber-brick houses stand on clear ground, their doors open the way their owners left them in 355. Where a floor was beaten earth and not brick, the house is lit from below, and the light comes up through the doorway and lies along the street like water. Every shadow points west.".
  Initially Assert litGround(old_quell).

  // What Quell sells: felt, true and false; a stylus; honey from the Tovash.
  Kind umber_felt "an umber felt cloak" like cloak_of_protection worth 2 weighing 6
    described "Wool felted with iron clay, red-brown and heavy, with hood and mitts. Rubbed with a wet thumb, it leaves a rust mark.".
  Initially Assert shields(umber_felt).
  Kind madder_felt "an umber felt cloak" like cloak_of_protection worth 1 weighing 2
    described "Wool dyed red-brown, with hood and mitts. It is lighter than it looks.".
  Kind stylus "a stillglass stylus" is tool worth 2 weighing 0
    described "A needle of stillglass in a bone handle, for drawing along a voice-plate's growth lines.".
  Entity salt: good "handful of salt".
  // Glass lanterns are confiscated at the Stair: on the plateau a lantern is horn.
  Kind horn_lantern "a horn lantern" like lantern worth 1
    described "A tallow lantern in a horn case. No glass: up here, glass carries the light.".
  Kind night_honey "a jar of night honey" is gear worth 1 weighing 1
    described "Dark, slightly bitter honey from bees that work by cloudlight. It keeps for decades.".
  Kind stillglass_knife "an unstamped stillglass knife" like dagger worth 5 weighing 1
    described "A stillglass blade with no Office stamp on the tang. The edge has never needed sharpening.".
  Person rusk "Rusk" at square {
    Role "the felt-lender, with her bales of red felt". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Sells umber_felt for 2 coin from 3.
    Sells stylus for 2 coin from 1.
    Sells horn_lantern for 1 coin from 2.
    Sells lamp_oil for 1 coin from 4.
    Sells rope for 1 coin from 2.
  }
  Person barrow_boy "a boy with a barrow" at square {
    Role "selling felt cloaks off a barrow, cheap". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he.
    Sells madder_felt for 1 coin from 4.
  }
  Person honey_seller "Ezh's aunt" at square {
    Role "a Tovash woman selling night honey by the jar". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Sells night_honey for 1 coin from 4.
    Sells salt for 1 coin from 6.
  }
  Topic rusk_felt with rusk "Ask Rusk about the barrow boy's felt" when true once {
    Says "'Madder,' says Rusk, without looking. 'Dyed wool. Wet your thumb and rub it: real felt leaves rust on you. That stuff leaves nothing, and lets everything through. Weigh it in your hand, while you are about it. A cloak of mine is six kilos and you feel every one.'".
  }

  // The Mutual: Dagny Ferrow, its Master, and Garret's crew.
  Person dagny "Dagny Ferrow" at mutual_hall {
    Role "Master of the Cutters' Mutual". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
  }
  Person ness "Ness Oakum" at mutual_yard {
    Role "a cutter of Garret's old crew". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Plans 14 steps. Uses go, change_thing. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
  }
  Person crew "Dagny's crew" at mutual_yard {
    Role "two cutters of the Mutual, felted, with poles and a sledge". Ancestry human. Numbers 2. Peaceable. Plans 14 steps. Uses go, change_thing.
  }
  Person grit "Grit" at mutual_yard {
    Role "the Mutual's yard dog, grey about the muzzle". Species dog. Pronouns she.
  }
  Observe grit_scene near grit of grit when at(grit, mutual_yard) "A grey bitch lies across the hall doorstep with her chin on her paws, and thumps her tail once for anyone in felt.".
  Initially Assert serves(ness, dagny). Initially Assert serves(crew, dagny).

  Discovery garret_held "Garret, a cutter of the Mutual, walked into an open granary vault in Tamaun last autumn to take the jars, and has stood in its light for eleven months, held." {
    Known by dagny, ness, crew.
  }
  Topic dagny_garret with dagny "Ask Dagny about Garret" when not cameUp(garret) once {
    Says "'Your uncle,' says Dagny. 'You know as much as I do, or you should. Last Harvest he went into an open vault in the Granary Ring to take jars, and the light had him before he was three steps in. Ness saw him from the doorway. She could not get to him and nor could anyone.' She rubs out a chalk mark on the board with the side of her fist. 'He is not dead. He is standing in there with his hand out, the way you'd reach for a jar.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, garret_held). }
  }
  Relation offered(group, group).
  Topic dagny_offer with dagny "Ask Dagny what she would have you do" when not cameUp(garret) and not offered(dagny, actor) once {
    Says "'Your debt to this hall is fourteen felt-lengths,' says Dagny. 'Twenty-eight crowns. I will rub out half of it the day Garret walks into this room on his own feet. The crew goes down when it has the felt, in three days or four. Go with them, or go down alone and before them, I don't care which. Only bring him up.' She looks at your hands. 'And keep that knife of yours out of Pike's sight. It has no stamp.'".
    On discuss { Assert offered(dagny, actor). }
  }
  Topic dagny_way with dagny "Ask Dagny how the crew goes down" when not cameUp(garret) once {
    Says "'By the North Well and the West Gallery, the way we always have,' says Dagny. 'There is an Office chain on the well-head. A licence opens it, and the licences are drawn on the first of the month. Hal Brewin keeps the chain, and Hal drinks.' She shrugs. 'Four hours from the well to the city, if the Neck lets you through. It is late summer: there is a metre of air under the Neck now, more than most years.'".
  }
  Topic ness_vault with ness "Ask Ness about the vault where Garret is" when not cameUp(garret) once {
    Says "'Ninth vault of the Ring, on the north side,' says Ness. 'Shutter open, light coming down off the ceiling like a white post. Jars all round him. Forty jars in a vault, umber-glazed and not a crack in one, and a collector in Sorne pays three crowns a jar.' She spits. 'He is not dying, you know. Nobody held is dying. He'll keep.'".
  }
  Topic crew_plan with crew "Ask the crew when they go down" when not cameUp(garret) and not descended(crew) once {
    Says "'When the felt comes, three days, four,' says the elder of the two. 'Felt, poles, rope, a sledge-cloth to drag him on. Ness knows the vault.' He does not look at Ness when he says it.".
  }
  Relation descended(group).

  // Saro and Sister Wenda, at the lazar house.
  Person wenda "Sister Wenda" at ward {
    Role "an Arbitral sister, who keeps the lazar house". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Wants night_honey.
  }
  Person saro "Saro" at ward {
    Role "a woman who walked out of the deep glass last autumn". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 6. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Joins "Saro stands at once, as if she had been waiting for nothing else. 'Down,' she says. 'Yes.'".
    Carries trowel_kind.
  }
  // Her bones and teeth are stillglass: the light does not slow her, in the company or out of it.
  Initially Assert unslowed(saro). Initially Assert unslowed(member_saro_person).
  Discovery saro_cold "Saro never warms. Her hands have no temperature at all, like stillglass, and she has been in the lazar house since last autumn without once being cold or hot." {
    Known by wenda.
  }
  Topic wenda_saro with wenda "Ask Sister Wenda about Saro" when true once {
    Says "'She came in last Frost, walking, from the east,' says Wenda. 'No fever, no cough, nothing I can treat. She eats, a little. She learns.' She lowers her voice. 'She does not warm. I have held her hands in mine for an hour by the stove and they are no warmer at the end than at the start, and no colder. The others have started to notice.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, saro_cold). }
  }
  Event wenda_honey near wenda when keeps(wenda, ?j) and itemKind(?j, night_honey) "Sister Wenda turns the jar to the window and smiles for the first time. 'For the coughers,' she says. 'A spoon at night, and they sleep.' She puts it on the shelf with the other two." then { Assert thanked(wenda, party). }
  Relation thanked(group, group).
  Topic saro_stone with saro "Ask Saro what she wants" when true once {
    Says "Saro answers in a Tovashi a month old and already good. 'To go back into the glass. Down, where it is being built.' She looks at you with great attention. 'Do you know of a stone that sings? Under here. It sings once in each hour. Everyone I ask says no.'".
  }
  Topic saro_down with saro "Tell Saro you are going down into Tamaun" when knows(actor, garret_held) and not willing(saro, actor) and not travelsWith(saro, actor) once {
    Says "'Into the old city,' says Saro. 'Down.' She has already stood up. 'I will come. I do not need felt.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(saro, actor). }
  }

  // The Glass Office: Halloran Pike, the licence lottery, and Hal Brewin at the chain.
  Person pike "Halloran Pike" at weighing {
    Role "the Glass Office licencer". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
  }
  Person hal "Hal Brewin" at well_head {
    Role "the Office's man at the North Well chain". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Guards well_stair.
    State watching blocking "Hal Brewin sits on a stool by the chain-gate with a cudgel across his knees.".
    State drunk "Hal Brewin is asleep on his stool with his mouth open.".
  }
  Topic pike_licence with pike "Ask Pike about a salvage licence" when not licensed(actor) once {
    Says "'Ten crowns to put your name in,' says Pike, 'and the names are drawn at this gate on the first of the month, one in four. Win, and the North Well chain opens to you for the month. Lose, and the ten crowns are the Crown's.' He blots a figure. 'Nobody goes down the Well without a licence. Nobody.'".
  }
  Topic pike_son with pike "Ask Pike about the cough in his house" when true once {
    Says "Pike's pen stops. 'My son,' he says. 'Glass-lung, at nineteen. There is a physician in Sorne who will see him for twenty crowns a visit, and I am paid nine a month.' He starts writing again, harder.".
  }
  Relation licensed(group). Relation entered(group).
  Action enter_lottery(actor: group, site: place) "Put your name in for this month's licences, ten crowns" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pike, site) and not licensed(actor)
      and not entered(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 10.
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Increase quantity(pike, gold) by 10. Assert entered(actor). }
    Result "Pike writes your name on a slip, folds it twice, and drops it in a box with a great many others.".
  }
  // The draw, at dawn on the first of the month; one in four.
  Rule lottery_won when entered(party) and hour(clock) == 8 and day(clock) == 6 and dice(party) <= 25 says "At the weighing-yard gate the clerk calls the names drawn for the month. Yours is the third." {
    Retract entered(party). Assert licensed(party). Assert tolerates(hal, party). }
  Rule lottery_lost when entered(party) and hour(clock) == 8 and day(clock) == 6 and dice(party) > 25 says "The licences for the month are called at the weighing-yard gate. Your name is not among them." {
    Retract entered(party). }
  // Hal can be had for wine, or for coin, and is asleep by midnight most nights.
  Action bribe_hal(actor: group, site: place) "Give Hal Brewin a crown to look the other way" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hal, site) and state(hal, watching)
      and not tolerates(hal, actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Increase quantity(hal, gold) by 1. Assert tolerates(hal, actor). }
    Result "Hal looks at the crown, and up the lane, and puts it in his boot. 'Never saw you,' he says, and unhooks the chain.".
  }
  Rule hal_sleeps when hour(clock) == 0 and state(hal, watching) { Assert state(hal, drunk). Assert asleep(hal). }
  Rule hal_wakes when hour(clock) == 6 and state(hal, drunk) { Assert state(hal, watching). Retract asleep(hal). }
  Thing chain_gate "the chain-gate" on well_stair {
    State locked blocking "An Office chain-gate hangs across the stair-head, padlocked.".
    State unhooked "The Office chain hangs unhooked from its staple.".
    Change unhook "Unhook the chain-gate" from locked to unhooked at well_head.
  }
  // The chain is Hal's to open, and the Mutual's crews go through it as he lets them.
  Initially Assert keyholder(hal, chain_gate). Initially Assert tolerates(hal, crew). Initially Assert tolerates(hal, ness).
  Rule chain_open_licensed when tolerates(hal, party) and state(chain_gate, locked) and (at(party, well_head) or at(party, well_foot)) { Assert state(chain_gate, unhooked). }
  // Unhooked under his nose, it is hooked again, and he remembers who did it.
  Rule chain_rehooked when state(chain_gate, unhooked) and perceives(hal, party) and not tolerates(hal, party)
    says "Hal Brewin gets up off his stool, hooks the chain back on its staple, and stands in front of it. 'No,' he says." {
    Assert state(chain_gate, locked). }
  Rule chain_shut when state(chain_gate, unhooked) and not at(party, well_head) and not at(party, well_foot) and state(hal, watching) { Assert state(chain_gate, locked). }

  // The knife has no stamp, and an Office man who sees it says so.
  Item knife "your stillglass knife" is stillglass_knife at square.
  Observe knife_here at square when at(knife, square) "Your own knife is on the cobbles where you set it down to haggle, an unstamped stillglass blade that has never needed sharpening.".
  Relation seized(item).
  Event knife_seen when carries(party, knife) and (perceives(pike, party) or perceives(hal, party)) and not seized(knife) "'That blade has no stamp,' says the Office man, and holds out his hand. 'A fifth of its worth to the Crown, now, or the next one costs you the hand that holds it.' You pay him a crown." then {
    Assert seized(knife). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 1. }

  // The bargain: half the debt, the day Garret walks into the hall with the one Dagny made it with.
  Relation forgiven(group).
  Event dagny_keeps_word near dagny when (travelsWith(garret, party) or following(garret, party)) and offered(dagny, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) and not forgiven(party) "Dagny looks at Garret for a long moment, and then at you. She takes the rag off its nail and rubs out the number beside your name on the board, and chalks in another, half the size. 'Fourteen crowns,' she says. 'I keep my word. Sit him by the fire before he falls down.'" then {
    Assert forgiven(party). Assert cameUp(garret). Decrease owes(party, dagny) by 14. }
  Relation broughtBy(group, group).
  Rule brought_by when travelsWith(garret, party) and not broughtBy(garret, party) { Assert broughtBy(garret, party). }
  Rule led_by when following(garret, party) and not broughtBy(garret, party) { Assert broughtBy(garret, party). }
  Event crew_brought_him near dagny when at(garret, mutual_hall) and not broughtBy(garret, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) "Garret is by the hall fire with a blanket round him and a bowl in his hands, and the crew who brought him up are drinking. Dagny does not look at you. Your number on the board is the same as it was.".

  Objective find_garret when not cameUp(garret) and asleep(garret) "Garret, your uncle, is held in an open granary vault under Quell. Dagny will halve your debt if you bring him up.".
  Objective bring_garret when not cameUp(garret) and not asleep(garret) "Garret is awake, and slow, and hungry, a long way under Quell. Bring him up to the Mutual's hall.".
  Objective held_alive when knows(party, garret_held) and not knows(party, doran_breathed) and not knows(party, prayer_label) "Are the held truly alive? In Ennick they visit theirs once a month to watch them breathe.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/stairhead.k:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // Stairhead House on the lip of the Scarp, the Arbiters' Way beneath it, and the Vault at its foot.
  Place stairhead "Stairhead House" is settlement within ghessil at 0, 3.
  Place arbiters_way "the Arbiters' Way" is site within ghessil at 0, 4.
  Place stair_top "the head of the Stair" is room within stairhead at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place chapel_sh "the chapel of Stairhead" is room within stairhead at 1, 1.
  Place vestry_sh "the vestry" is room within stairhead at 2, 1.
  Place strongroom "the strongroom" is room within stairhead at 2, 2.
  Place chapter "the chapter house" is room within stairhead at 1, 2.
  Place platform "the platform" is room within stairhead at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place way_upper "the upper Way" is level within arbiters_way.
  Place way_lower "the lower Way" is level within arbiters_way.
  Place way_door_room "under the platform" is room within way_upper at 0, 0 underground.
  Place counting_stair "the Stair That Counts" is room within way_upper at 0, 1 underground.
  Place separation_gallery "the Gallery of the Separation" is room within way_lower at 0, 2 underground.
  Place vault_ward "the Ward of the Vault" is room within way_lower at 0, 3 underground.
  Place arbiter_vault "the Arbiters' Vault" is room within way_lower at 0, 4 underground.

  Passage gorge_road "the gorge road" is road between lower_road and stair_top taking 4 hours.
  Passage chapel_door_sh "the chapel door" is door between stair_top and chapel_sh.
  Passage vestry_door "the vestry door" is door between chapel_sh and vestry_sh.
  Passage strong_door "the strongroom door" is door between vestry_sh and strongroom.
  Passage chapter_door "the chapter house door" is door between chapel_sh and chapter.
  Passage platform_steps "the platform steps" is steps between stair_top and platform.
  // The House's platform, which its brothers take for a Seridane signal station, is the Way's door.
  Passage way_mouth "a stair under the platform's flagstones" is stair between platform and way_door_room hidden until way_found.
  Passage way_down "the Way, past the Door" is passage between way_door_room and counting_stair taking 2 hours.
  Passage counted_way "the ringing steps" is stair between counting_stair and separation_gallery taking 3 hours.
  Passage gallery_way "the length of the relief" is passage between separation_gallery and vault_ward taking 12 hours.
  Passage ward_way "the Ward's threshold" is doorway between vault_ward and arbiter_vault.

  Observe stair_top_scene at stair_top when true "The Stair road comes up beside the falls to a walled house of grey stone on the lip of the Scarp. Bells mark the offices. Below, four falls stand one above another, and the lowland goes off green to the edge of the sky.".
  Observe chapel_scene_sh at chapel_sh when true "A plain Arbitral chapel. The brothers sing seven offices a day; at the night office the cellarer hangs his keys in the vestry, and every man of them is in here.".
  Observe vestry_scene at vestry_sh when true "A narrow vestry of copes and candles, with a row of iron hooks by the door.".
  Observe platform_scene at platform when true "An old stone platform older than the House, set with bronze fittings in a ring. The brothers dry washing on it. The fittings are mirror mounts, though nobody here knows it.".
  Discovery way_found "Under the platform's centre flagstones a stair goes down into rock that has not changed since it was cut: the Way's door is the House's own platform." {
    Found by searching platform "The centre flagstones ring hollow. Under them, a stair of white stone goes down into rock that has the look of something that has never once been touched by weather.".
  }

  // Prior Aurel Mance and Brother Tam (Stairhead House).
  Person mance "Prior Aurel Mance" at chapel_sh {
    Role "Prior of Stairhead House". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
  }
  Person tam "Brother Tam" at chapel_sh {
    Role "the cellarer". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
  }
  Initially Assert serves(tam, mance).
  Topic mance_stone with mance "Ask the prior what the mother-church wants" when true once {
    Says "'The Long Hour, which the old king keeps below,' says Mance, 'and whatever comes up the Plumb.' He folds his hands. 'The mother-church believes there is a relic of the Virina under this plateau. A stone that sings. I am to have it before the Crown does.'".
  }
  // Buys reads only the shared catalog, so a kind of this module's own cannot be bought by Buys (ledger, 24).
  Action sell_plates(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Sell the Long Hour to the prior for six hundred crowns" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mance, site) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(long_hour, carrier).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve drop(long_hour, carrier).
    On success { Assert keeps(mance, long_hour). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 600. }
    Result "Mance turns every plate to the light before he counts out the coin, and then he counts it twice.".
  }
  Kind strong_key "the strongroom key" is tool worth 0 weighing 0 described "A heavy iron key on a ring.".
  Thing key_hooks "the hooks by the vestry door" at vestry_sh {
    Holds.
    State empty_hook "The hooks by the vestry door are empty.".
    State keys_hung "The cellarer's keys hang on the hook by the vestry door.".
  }
  Item strongkey "the strongroom key" is strong_key in key_hooks owned by tam.
  // The night office: the brothers in chapel, the keys on the hook, the vestry unwatched.
  Rule night_office when hour(clock) == 0 and state(key_hooks, empty_hook) and inside(strongkey, key_hooks) { Assert state(key_hooks, keys_hung). }
  Rule office_ends when hour(clock) == 1 and state(key_hooks, keys_hung) { Assert state(key_hooks, empty_hook). }
  Thing strong_lock "the strongroom lock" on strong_door {
    State locked blocking "The strongroom door is iron-bound and locked.".
    State open "The strongroom door stands open.".
    Change unlock_strong "Unlock the strongroom" from locked to open needing strongkey.
    Change pick_strong "Pick the strongroom lock" from locked to open needing lockwork.
  }
  Observe strong_scene at strongroom when true "Chests, a reliquary, and a shelf of sealed papers under the prior's seal. On a cushion, as if it were holy, a clear block the size of a hearthstone.".
  Discovery ottavine_note "Prior Ottavine's note on the Ennick holding prayer: a Seridane granary formula, painted on the grain jars; it means hold one season, then give it out." {
    Source ottavine_papers "Prior Ottavine's sealed papers" at strongroom readable by party.
  }
  Observe ottavine_label near party when knows(party, ottavine_note) and not knows(party, prayer_label) "Ottavine had it forty years ago, in a hand that does not shake: the prayer is a grain jar's label." teaches prayer_label.
  Discovery church_letters "Letters from the mother-church to Stairhead, eighty years of them, asking about 'a stone that sings below'.".
  Thing letters_box "a box of letters" at strongroom {
    State shut_box "A box of letters under the mother-church's seal.".
    State read_box "The mother-church's letters lie open, eighty years of them.".
    Change read_letters "Break the seal and read the mother-church's letters" from shut_box to read_box.
  }
  Observe letters_read at strongroom when state(letters_box, read_box) "Every one asks the same thing in other words: whether the prior has heard of a stone that sings, below." teaches church_letters.
  Thing ilis_block "Ilis's block" at strongroom {
    State resting "A clear block the size of a hearthstone sits on a cushion. It has no temperature.".
    Tries listening.
  }
  Observe block_wind near ilis_block when tried(ilis_block, listening) "It gives back a sound, very faint, from the day it stopped, out on the heath before anyone was born. It is only wind.".

  // The Arbiters' Way (The Undersun, The Arbiters' Way): ordinary rock kept unchanged by the Virina, which nothing of
  // the Varakiiri can enter. Four gates test whoever walks it; each is answered from the world's own history.
  Observe way_door_scene at way_door_room when true "A door of white stone with no hinges, in white rock. Over it, in a hand the eye follows easily, is carved one question: WAS THE HOUR GIVEN?".
  Discovery hour_fell "The hour was not given: it fell. A thing came down out of a clear sky on an autumn night, and the crane-priests of the lake wrote it down before any Seridane claimed it.".
  Thing the_door "the Door" on way_down {
    State asking blocking "The Door asks whether the hour was given.".
    State answered "The Door stands open.".
    State sealed_year blocking "The Door is shut, and will be, the carving says, for a year and a day.".
    Change answer_fell "Answer that the hour fell, and was not given" from asking to answered after learning hour_fell.
    Change answer_argued "Answer as the Coverers argued: it fell" from asking to answered after learning coverer_case.
  }
  Measure doorSealedAt(entity).
  Action answer_given(actor: group, site: place) "Answer that the hour was given" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, way_door_room) and state(the_door, asking).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert state(the_door, sealed_year). Set doorSealedAt(the_door) to watch(clock). }
    Result "The Door does not move. Below the question, letters you had not seen fill with light: a year and a day.".
  }
  Rule door_reopens when state(the_door, sealed_year) and watch(clock) >= doorSealedAt(the_door) + 52704 { Assert state(the_door, asking). }

  Observe counting_scene at counting_stair when true "The Way goes down by a stair of nine thousand steps. Each rings a note when trodden, and each note is different, and they do not repeat.".
  Thing ringing "the ringing steps" on counted_way is scenery {
    State uncounted blocking "The steps ring under your feet. A walker who loses the count, the carving at the top says, comes back to the top.".
    State counted "You have the count of the steps, and the stair lets you down.".
    Change count_names "Count the steps aloud in the twelve hour-names, round and round" from uncounted to counted after learning hour_names.
  }
  Action count_numbers(actor: group, site: place) "Count the steps in numbers" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, counting_stair) and state(ringing, uncounted).
    Time 18.
    Result "Somewhere past four thousand the notes run together, and you find you have said a number twice. You are standing at the top again, and three hours have gone.".
  }

  Observe relief_scene at separation_gallery when true "A relief two kilometres long, carved by no hand you know: a war across a sky divided, figures with light for wings and figures made of darkness and hooks, struck and striking; and below them tall figures in white, in a ring, holding the world apart like the pages of a book.".
  Relation wroteDown(group).
  Action write_as_you_walk(actor: group, site: place) "Walk the relief writing down only what you see" {
    Description "A day's walk. The Remembrancer at its end asks what you saw, and lets through only those who add nothing.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, separation_gallery) and not wroteDown(actor) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 72.
    On success { Assert wroteDown(actor). }
    Result "You walk it slowly, a day long, and write down what is carved and nothing else. Your hand aches.".
  }
  Person gallery_keeper "a Remembrancer" at separation_gallery {
    Role "a servant of the Virina, tall, made of the sound of bells". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Guards gallery_way.
    State asking_g blocking "At the end of the relief a figure made of the sound of bells waits to ask what you saw.".
  }
  Topic keeper_tell with gallery_keeper "Tell the Remembrancer what you saw" when wroteDown(actor) once {
    Says "You read it from what you wrote. The Remembrancer hears it through to the last line and does not interrupt. 'Nothing added,' it says, in many bells. 'Go down.'".
    On discuss { Assert tolerates(gallery_keeper, actor). }
  }
  Topic keeper_memory with gallery_keeper "Tell the Remembrancer what you remember of it" when not wroteDown(actor) and not tolerates(gallery_keeper, actor) {
    Says "You tell it. Somewhere in the telling you say the dark figures had faces, and they had not. 'Added,' says the Remembrancer, gently, and you are standing at the start of the relief.".
  }

  // The Ward of the Vault: three questions, in order. A party guessing is turned away for a year.
  Discovery held_feed "What the held feed: the instant a person is held, their moment is taken and laid in the Undersun as a keystone. The Holdfolk's mercy has been building the Masonry's vaults for three hundred and forty years.".
  Observe ward_scene_v at vault_ward when true "A round white chamber with a white door, and over it three questions in a ring: WAS THE HOUR GIVEN? WHO KILLED THE KEEPER'S DAUGHTER? WHAT DO THE HELD FEED?".
  Thing vault_seal "the Ward" on ward_way {
    State first_q blocking "The first question is lit: was the hour given?".
    State second_q blocking "The second question is lit: who killed the keeper's daughter?".
    State third_q blocking "The third question is lit: what do the held feed?".
    State warded "The Ward is dark, and the white door stands open.".
    State turned blocking "The Ward is dark and the door shut. It will be so for a year.".
    Change ward_one "Answer: it fell" from first_q to second_q after learning hour_fell.
    Change ward_one_argued "Answer: it fell, as the Coverers said" from first_q to second_q after learning coverer_case.
    Change ward_two "Answer: Answerer loyalists, her father's men" from second_q to third_q after learning selane_murdered.
    Change ward_three "Answer: the Masonry; the held are its keystones" from third_q to warded after learning held_feed.
  }
  Action ward_guess(actor: group, site: place) "Answer the lit question as best you can guess" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, vault_ward)
      and (state(vault_seal, first_q) or state(vault_seal, second_q) or state(vault_seal, third_q)).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert state(vault_seal, turned). Set doorSealedAt(vault_seal) to watch(clock). }
    Result "The light goes out of the questions one by one, and the white door does not open.".
  }
  Rule ward_reopens when state(vault_seal, turned) and watch(clock) >= doorSealedAt(vault_seal) + 52560 { Assert state(vault_seal, first_q). }

  // U6, the Arbiters' Vault: Ithmar in its cage of rods, the Tally, and a Remembrancer at the door.
  Kind ithmar_kind "Ithmar" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A hen's egg of something like dark opal, cut with sigils the mind will not name. It hums at the pitch of the note under the Pit.".
  Kind tally_kind "the Virina's Tally" is tool worth 0 weighing 2
    described "A rod of white metal marked like a ruler. It shows how much of the Keeping has been cut away; in the Keeping, how far any moment is from now.".
  Observe arbiter_scene at arbiter_vault when true "A white chamber, round, plain, very old and perfectly clean. The floor hums.".
  Thing cage "a cage of white rods" at arbiter_vault {
    Holds.
    State caged "In the centre of the chamber a jewel the size of a hen's egg hangs in the air in a cage of white rods. It is engraved with sigils the eye can follow and the mind will not name.".
  }
  Item ithmar "Ithmar" is ithmar_kind in cage.
  Item tally "the Virina's Tally" is tally_kind at arbiter_vault owned by remembrancer.
  Observe tally_seen at arbiter_vault when at(tally, arbiter_vault) "Against the wall leans a rod of white metal, marked like a ruler.".
  Person remembrancer "the Remembrancer of the Vault" at arbiter_vault {
    Role "a servant of the Virina, at the door". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Objects "'Why do you carry the Tally away?' asks the Remembrancer, in many bells. 'Say it truly, and it is lent.'".
  }
  Discovery quarrying "The Masonry is cutting Imbar's past away through the seed, a season at a time, and since the year 371 more than thirty hollows have been quarried from the Keeping; the Tally measures how much.".
  Topic remembrancer_tally with remembrancer "Tell the Remembrancer why you would carry the Tally" when knows(actor, quarrying) once {
    Says "'To prove to the plateau how fast its past is being taken,' you say, 'and to find my way in the Keeping.' The Remembrancer is silent a long time, which is many bells not ringing. 'True,' it says, 'and sufficient. It is lent.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(remembrancer, tally, actor). }
  }
  Topic remembrancer_help with remembrancer "Ask the Remembrancer to help keep Imbar" when true once {
    Says "'It is yours to keep,' says the Remembrancer, courteously and at length. 'The planes were parted so that each could keep itself. We tend what is kept. We do not fight for it.' It inclines its head toward the jewel. 'A living hand on Ithmar walks the Keeping. Whoever touches the hand goes with it.'".
  }
  Topic remembrancer_quarry with remembrancer "Ask the Remembrancer what the Tally shows" when true once {
    Says "'How much of the Keeping has been cut away,' says the Remembrancer. 'Since your year 371, thirty-one hollows, most of them in your last years. Each is a season nobody can remember, and claims that rested on it are loose.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, quarrying). }
  }

  // The Concord (The Corbel and the Concord), compactly: called to Stairhead when the Corbel can no longer be denied;
  // each seat for or against three motions; evidence shown moves the seats that care about it; a vote.
  Kind motion. Entity motion_cover: motion "cover the Pit again". Entity motion_descend: motion "a sanctioned descent for Ithmar".
  Entity motion_bargain: motion "bargain with the Interlocutor".
  Relation favours(group, motion). Relation seat(group). Relation convened(place). Relation redLine(group, motion).
  Measure tally_of(motion). Relation counted(group, motion). Relation passed(motion). Relation voting(place).
  Rule concord_called when not convened(chapter) and ((knows(party, corbel_seen) and knows(party, sinking)) or day(clock) >= 720)
    says "Riders go out from Sorne along every road on the plateau: the Crown calls a Concord at Stairhead House, of every power that will come." {
    Assert convened(chapter). Assert at(aske, chapter). Assert at(ayzhe, chapter). Assert at(bren, chapter).
    Assert at(dagny, chapter). Assert at(mance, chapter). Assert at(ruan, chapter). }
  Initially Assert seat(aske). Initially Assert seat(ayzhe). Initially Assert seat(bren). Initially Assert seat(dagny).
  Initially Assert seat(mance). Initially Assert seat(ruan).
  Initially Assert favours(aske, motion_cover). Initially Assert favours(aske, motion_descend).
  Initially Assert favours(mance, motion_descend).
  Initially Assert redLine(bren, motion_cover). Initially Assert redLine(aske, motion_bargain).
  Observe concord_scene at chapter when convened(chapter) "The chapter house is full: the Warden in his sash for the Crown; Ayzhe of the Split Ear; Bren of Ennick with his hood in his hands; Dagny Ferrow for the Mutual; the prior at the head of the table; Ruan Dace for the Waiting. Nobody sits next to anybody they can help it.".
  // Evidence, shown with its proof, moves every seat that cares about it.
  Action show_feeding(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Concord what the held feed" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, held_feed) and not shownTo(chapter, held_feed).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, held_feed). Retract redLine(bren, motion_cover). }
    Result "Bren asks for a recess, and is gone an hour. When he comes back he says that Ennick will stop holding, and that it will not have the Pit covered while one of its held is still in the glass.".
  }
  Action show_procession(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Concord the procession's warning: the Masonry takes from the newest backward" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, newest_backward) and not shownTo(chapter, newest_backward).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, newest_backward). Assert redLine(ruan, motion_bargain). Assert favours(ruan, motion_descend). }
    Result "The Waiting's elder goes white. Nobody at the table will speak for bargaining after that.".
  }
  Action show_way(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Concord that the Way to the jewel is under this house" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, way_found) and not shownTo(chapter, way_found).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, way_found). Assert favours(dagny, motion_descend). Assert favours(ruan, motion_descend). }
    Result "The prior's seat is suddenly worth a great deal, and he knows it. The Mutual and the Waiting come round to a sanctioned descent.".
  }
  Action show_breach(actor: group, site: place) "Name to the Concord who cut the Breach" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, breach_cut) and not shownTo(chapter, breach_cut).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, breach_cut). Retract at(ayzhe, chapter). Assert at(ayzhe, split_ear_camp). }
    Result "Ayzhe stands up before you have finished, and does not look at Bren, who has not moved. The Split Ear ride south that afternoon. The Tovash seat is empty.".
  }
  Relation shownTo(place, fact).
  Discovery newest_backward "The Masonry quarries a world's past from the newest moment backward: when it reached the beginning of the procession's world, that world was not.".
  Action call_vote(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Concord to vote" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter) and not voting(chapter).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert voting(chapter). }
    Result "The prior calls the seats, one by one.".
  }
  // A motion passes when four seats there favour it and no seat there holds a red line against it.
  Rule vote_counts when voting(chapter) and seat(?s) and at(?s, chapter) and favours(?s, ?m) and not counted(?s, ?m) {
    Increase tally_of(?m) by 1. Assert counted(?s, ?m). }
  Query blocked(m: motion) means redLine(?s, m) and at(?s, chapter).
  Relation onTable(motion).
  Initially Assert onTable(motion_cover). Initially Assert onTable(motion_descend). Initially Assert onTable(motion_bargain).
  Rule motion_passes when voting(chapter) and onTable(?m) and tally_of(?m) >= 4 and not blocked(?m) and not passed(?m)
    says "The Concord resolves: {?m}." { Assert passed(?m). }
  Observe concord_descend at chapter when passed(motion_descend) and not knows(party, way_found) "The Concord has sanctioned a descent. The prior, very stiffly, tells the seats what the mother-church has always suspected and he has lately confirmed: there is a stair under his platform." teaches way_found.
  Rule descent_sanctioned when passed(motion_descend) and not admits(aske, party) { Assert admits(aske, party). }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/stilling.ky:
Module stilling "The stilling: what the Late Sun's direct light does to whatever drinks it" {
  // The four laws (The Land and Its Laws): the stilling travels only in direct light, silica passes it and stops,
  // water and flesh drink it and slow, iron sheds it as heat. This module is the third law, as it bears on people:
  // where the light falls, who is in it, what they wear, how slow it leaves them, and how they come back.

  // Ground the light falls on: lit glass, a lamp-chamber, a vault with its shutter open, a leak in the plaster. A
  // place is lit by a fact (litGround) or by a rule (lit), so that a shutter or a mirror can light and darken it.
  Relation litGround(place). Relation shadeOf(place).
  Query lit(p: place) means litGround(p) and not shadeOf(p).

  // Dose, in twenty-fourths of a point: an hour bare in direct light is a point (24); an hour in full felt a
  // quarter of one (6). Recovery is two points an hour out of the light, faster while someone is deeply slowed.
  Measure dose(entity).
  // Full umber felt: the cloak, the hood and the mitts. Counterfeit felt looks the same and is no felt at all.
  // What sheds the stilling when worn: umber felt, Selane's Veil.
  Relation shields(itemkind).
  Query felted(m: member) means wearing(?f, m) and itemKind(?f, ?k) and shields(?k).
  // Someone the light does not slow (Saro, whose bones are stillglass).
  Relation unslowed(entity).
  // Someone who is not of the company and wears felt, by what is said of them.
  Relation feltClad(group).

  Rule soaks when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and at(?c, ?p) and lit(?p) and not felted(?m) and not unslowed(?m)
    and not heldDeep(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by 4. }
  Rule soaks_felted when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and at(?c, ?p) and lit(?p) and felted(?m)
    and not unslowed(?m) and not heldDeep(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by 1. }
  Rule others_soak when at(?g, ?p) and lit(?p) and slowable(?g) and not feltClad(?g) and not heldDeep(?g) {
    Increase dose(?g) by 4. }
  Rule others_soak_felted when at(?g, ?p) and lit(?p) and slowable(?g) and feltClad(?g) and not heldDeep(?g) {
    Increase dose(?g) by 1. }
  // Out of the light: two points an hour, and twelve an hour while someone is held deeper than a tenth.
  Query unlitFor(x: entity) means (memberOf(x, ?c) and at(?c, ?p) and not lit(?p)) or (at(x, ?q) and not lit(?q)).
  // A decrease that would go below nothing stops play, and there is no min(), so the last of it is set to nothing.
  Rule recovers when unlitFor(?x) and dose(?x) >= 8 and dose(?x) <= 288 { Decrease dose(?x) by 8. }
  Rule recovers_last when unlitFor(?x) and dose(?x) > 0 and dose(?x) < 8 { Set dose(?x) to 0. }
  Rule recovers_deep when unlitFor(?x) and dose(?x) > 288 { Decrease dose(?x) by 48. }
  // A way across lit ground (the Collar Road, the filament, a leak across a doorway) doses whoever crosses it, once
  // per crossing: so much bare, so much in felt. There is no division, so both are said.
  Measure wayDose(passage). Measure wayDoseFelted(passage).
  Relation dosedOn(member, passage).
  Rule way_doses when tookWay(?c, ?w) and company(?c) and wayDose(?w) > 0 and memberOf(?m, ?c) and not dosedOn(?m, ?w)
    and not felted(?m) and not unslowed(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by wayDose(?w). Assert dosedOn(?m, ?w). }
  Rule way_doses_felted when tookWay(?c, ?w) and company(?c) and wayDoseFelted(?w) > 0 and memberOf(?m, ?c)
    and not dosedOn(?m, ?w) and felted(?m) and not unslowed(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by wayDoseFelted(?w). Assert dosedOn(?m, ?w). }
  Rule way_passed when dosedOn(?m, ?w) and memberOf(?m, ?c) and not tookWay(?c, ?w) { Retract dosedOn(?m, ?w). }
  // Who the light can slow besides the company: the people of a module that says so.
  Relation slowable(group).

  // At a point, half speed: everything takes twice as long and companions seem to hurry. A slowed member goes at half
  // their speed (the shared rules' speed, in hundredths), and the company at its slowest member's; when the dose is
  // gone, their own. (Written at first as no capacity to carry, the only pace a module could then change: ledger, 1.)
  Query slowedMember(m: member) means dose(m) >= 24.
  Query slowedCompany(c: group) means memberOf(?m, c) and slowedMember(?m).
  Rule slowing when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and slowedMember(?m) and speed(?m) != 50 { Set speed(?m) to 50. }
  Rule quickening when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and not slowedMember(?m) and speed(?m) == 50 { Set speed(?m) to 0. }
  // In a fight, slowed is Orsino's slow: a blow fewer, late to move. Laid on whoever is slowed, an hour at a time.
  Hazard stilled "the stilling" means "Apply slow to ally for 1 hour.".
  Relation slowLaid(group). Measure slowSince(group).
  Rule slow_laid when company(?c) and slowedCompany(?c) and not slowLaid(?c) {
    Assert strikes(stilled, ?c). Assert slowLaid(?c). Set slowSince(?c) to watch(clock). }
  Rule slow_renewed when company(?c) and slowLaid(?c) and watch(clock) >= slowSince(?c) + 6 { Retract slowLaid(?c). }
  // At twelve points, a tenth: they cannot leave without being led.
  Query stoppedMember(m: member) means dose(m) >= 288.
  Rule stopping when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and stoppedMember(?m) and not hobbled(?c) { Assert hobbled(?c). }
  Rule starting when hobbled(?c) and company(?c) and not stoppedCompany(?c) and stilled(?c) {
    Retract hobbled(?c). Retract stilled(?c). }
  Query stoppedCompany(c: group) means memberOf(?m, c) and stoppedMember(?m).
  Relation stilled(group).
  Rule stilled_mark when hobbled(?c) and company(?c) and stoppedCompany(?c) and not stilled(?c) { Assert stilled(?c). }
  // Held: past a hundred points, one breath every few minutes.
  Query heldDeep(x: entity) means dose(x) >= 2400.

  Observe slow_feel near ?c when company(?c) and slowedCompany(?c) and not stoppedCompany(?c) "Your own footsteps sound late on the stone, your limbs are heavy, and the world has begun to hurry around you.".
  Observe stopped_feel near ?c when company(?c) and stoppedCompany(?c) "Every thought takes an hour to finish. You could not walk out of here alone if your life hung on it.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/tamaun.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // Tamaun's upper city: the West Gallery from Quell and the Neck, the Shallows lit by mirrors, and the Granaries
  // lit by direct light through channels. Everything here is underground and dark unless a mirror throws light on it.
  Place gallery "the West Gallery" is level within tamaun.
  Place shallows "the Shallows" is level within tamaun.
  Place granaries "the Granaries" is level within tamaun.

  Place well_foot "the foot of the North Well" is room within gallery at 0, 0 underground.
  Place before_neck "the West Gallery, at the Neck" is room within gallery at 1, 0 underground.
  Place west_gate "the West Gate" is room within shallows at 0, 1 underground.
  Place road_north "the Mirror Road, north stretch" is room within shallows at 1, 0 underground.
  Place lamp_chamber "the third lamp-chamber" is room within shallows at 2, 0 underground.
  Place road_south "the Mirror Road, south stretch" is room within shallows at 1, 2 underground.
  Place bunks "the Bunks" is room within shallows at 0, 2 underground.
  Place plate_hall "the Plate Hall" is room within shallows at 2, 2 underground.
  Place ring "the Granary Ring" is room within granaries at 1, 1 underground.
  Place vault "the ninth vault" is room within granaries at 1, 0 underground.
  Place fox_vault "the fourth vault" is room within granaries at 2, 1 underground.
  Place waking_ward "the Waking Ward" is room within granaries at 0, 1 underground.
  Place flood_line "the Flood Line" is room within granaries at 1, 2 underground.
  Place sluice_head "the Sluice" is room within granaries at 2, 2 underground.

  Passage well_stair "the North Well stair" is stair between well_head and well_foot.
  Passage west_gallery "the West Gallery" is tunnel between well_foot and before_neck taking 3 hours.
  Passage neck "the Neck" is crawl between before_neck and west_gate taking 20 minutes.
  Passage gate_arch "the West Gate arch" is arch between west_gate and road_north.
  Passage slot_north "the north light-slot gallery" is passage between road_north and lamp_chamber taking 3 minutes.
  Passage mirror_road "the Mirror Road" is passage between road_north and road_south taking 5 minutes.
  Passage bunks_way "the passage to the Bunks" is passage between road_south and bunks taking 3 minutes.
  Passage hall_way "the Plate Hall doorway" is doorway between road_south and plate_hall.
  // My addition: a Seridane service stair from the Plate Hall down to the Granaries.
  Passage granary_stair "the service stair" is stair between plate_hall and ring.
  Passage vault_door "the ninth vault's doorway" is doorway between ring and vault.
  Passage fox_door "the fourth vault's doorway" is doorway between ring and fox_vault.
  Passage ward_door "the Waking Ward door" is doorway between ring and waking_ward.
  Passage flood_slope "the slope to the flood" is passage between ring and flood_line taking 3 minutes.
  Passage sluice_tunnel "the sluice tunnel" is passage between flood_line and sluice_head taking 5 minutes.

  // Dark, unless a mirror throws light here. The galleries a mirror serves are lit while it is aimed at them.
  Relation darkRoom(place).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(well_foot). Initially Assert darkRoom(before_neck). Initially Assert darkRoom(west_gate).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(road_north). Initially Assert darkRoom(road_south). Initially Assert darkRoom(bunks).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(plate_hall). Initially Assert darkRoom(ring). Initially Assert darkRoom(waking_ward).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(flood_line). Initially Assert darkRoom(sluice_head).
  Rule unlit_here when darkRoom(?p) and not bright(?p) and not unlit(?p) { Assert unlit(?p). }
  Rule lit_here when darkRoom(?p) and bright(?p) and unlit(?p) { Retract unlit(?p). }

  Observe well_foot_scene at well_foot when true "The stair comes down into a round chamber at the water's edge. The well water is warm as a bath. A tunnel two metres wide runs off east beside it, with a channel along one side.".
  Observe gallery_scene at before_neck when true "The West Gallery runs on east, wet underfoot, the water in its channel very still. Ahead, the roof comes down to meet the water.".

  // The Neck: the roof drops until there is a metre of air under it in late summer. The water in the West Gallery is
  // falling a hand a month, because the growth under the Late Sun is opening a channel that drains it (S1).
  Entity neck_water: scenery "the water at the Neck".
  Measure airGap(entity).
  Initially Set airGap(neck_water) to 100.
  Rule neck_falls when hour(clock) == 4 and dice(neck_water) <= 13 { Increase airGap(neck_water) by 1. }
  Observe neck_scene at before_neck when airGap(neck_water) < 110 "The ceiling drops until you wade with your face near the stone; under the Neck there is about a metre of air. On the wall a line of white crust shows where the water stood a season ago, a hand above where it stands now.".
  Observe neck_scene_low at before_neck when airGap(neck_water) >= 110 "Under the Neck there is more than a metre of air now. The white crust of the old waterline stands well above the water.".
  // Whoever marks the water and comes back to it learns it is falling.
  Measure markedAt(group).
  Relation marked(group).
  Action mark_water(actor: group, site: place) "Scratch a mark at the waterline under the Neck" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, before_neck) and not marked(actor) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert marked(actor). Set markedAt(actor) to airGap(neck_water). }
    Result "You scratch a line in the crust at the very edge of the water with the point of your knife.".
  }
  Discovery water_falling "The water in the West Gallery is falling, faster than any season accounts for: the mark at the Neck is dry above it within days. Something below is drawing it off." .
  Observe mark_dry at before_neck when marked(party) and airGap(neck_water) >= markedAt(party) + 2 "The line you scratched at the waterline is dry now, two fingers above the water." teaches water_falling.

  Observe gate_scene at west_gate when true "Beyond the Neck a cut-stone arch opens on a gallery. Chalk on the arch reads J.H. 341.".

  // The Mirror Road and the third lamp-chamber. The chamber's mirror throws safe, bounced light down one of three
  // galleries: the north stretch, the south stretch, or the Bunks. The chamber itself is a straight room: the Late Sun
  // is behind its window, and every minute there is dose (S4).
  Initially Assert litGround(lamp_chamber).
  Thing mirror "the great mirror" at lamp_chamber {
    State to_north "A bronze mirror two metres across stands on a cradle with a crank and worm-gear, throwing a beam out through the north slot. Brass scales are scratched on the cradle, and its pointer stands near the end of them.".
    State to_south "The great mirror is cranked round to the south slot, and its beam goes out that way.".
    State to_bunks "The great mirror is cranked round to the low slot that serves the Bunks.".
    Change north_south "Crank the mirror round to the south slot" from to_north to to_south.
    Change north_bunks "Crank the mirror round to the Bunks slot" from to_north to to_bunks.
    Change south_north "Crank the mirror round to the north slot" from to_south to to_north.
    Change south_bunks "Crank the mirror round to the Bunks slot" from to_south to to_bunks.
    Change bunks_north "Crank the mirror round to the north slot" from to_bunks to to_north.
    Change bunks_south "Crank the mirror round to the south slot" from to_bunks to to_south.
  }
  Relation aims(condition, place).
  Initially Assert aims(to_north, road_north). Initially Assert aims(to_south, road_south). Initially Assert aims(to_bunks, bunks).
  Query bright(p: place) means state(mirror, ?s) and aims(?s, p).
  Observe chamber_scene at lamp_chamber when true "A round chamber at the inner end of the gallery. One wall is a single sheet of stillglass three metres across, with blinding light behind it. Your shadow lies flat behind you on the floor.".
  Discovery mirrors_ending "The lamp-chamber mirrors are at the end of their travel. Their scales were set for a Late Sun that sank four centimetres a year; whatever they are aimed at now, they will not reach for long." {
    Found by searching lamp_chamber "The pointer on the cradle's brass scale stands two finger-widths from its stop. Below the last scratched mark, someone recently has scratched another, and another below that.".
  }

  // The gardens walk with the light: where bounced light has lain a long while, moss and fern and grass; where it has
  // left, they brown and die (S2). Greenness is reckoned by the watch, from none to a thousand.
  Measure green(place).
  Initially Set green(road_north) to 1000. Initially Set green(road_south) to 300. Initially Set green(bunks) to 0.
  Rule greening when darkRoom(?p) and bright(?p) and green(?p) < 1000 and dice(?p) <= 50 { Increase green(?p) by 1. }
  Rule browning when darkRoom(?p) and not bright(?p) and green(?p) > 0 { Decrease green(?p) by 1. }
  Observe north_lit at road_north when bright(road_north) "A ring gallery four metres wide. A bronze disc as big as a cartwheel is set in a ceiling niche, throwing grey-gold light along the passage. Swallows nest on its rim.".
  Observe north_dark at road_north when not bright(road_north) "A ring gallery four metres wide. A bronze disc as big as a cartwheel sits dull in its ceiling niche, and the swallows on its rim are quiet.".
  Observe north_garden at road_north when green(road_north) >= 600 "Moss covers the floor, ferns grow out of the cracks in the left-hand wall, and pale grass stands up to your knees.".
  Observe north_fading at road_north when green(road_north) < 600 and green(road_north) >= 200 "The grass lies over and is turning yellow. The ferns have begun to brown at the tips.".
  Observe north_dead at road_north when green(road_north) < 200 "Dead ferns, brown and dry, break when you brush them. The grass lies flat.".
  Observe south_lit at road_south when bright(road_south) "Light comes down the south stretch from a ceiling disc, onto stone that was bare not long ago.".
  Observe south_dark at road_south when not bright(road_south) "The south stretch of the Mirror Road is dark. A disc hangs dull in the ceiling niche.".
  Observe south_garden at road_south when green(road_south) >= 600 "A garden has come up here: moss, fern, and pale grass to the knee.".
  Observe south_shoots at road_south when green(road_south) < 600 and green(road_south) >= 100 "New green shoots, very small, come up between the stones in a band as straight as the edge of a shadow.".

  // A leak: a crack in the plaster where the Mirror Road meets the Plate Hall throws a blade of direct light across
  // the doorway. It is the commonest hazard in the city; it moves only when the plaster falls.
  Thing leak "a blade of white light" on hall_way {
    State shining "Where the plaster has cracked over the Plate Hall doorway, a blade of hard white light comes through and lies across the threshold.".
    State shaded "A hood of umber felt has been hung over the crack above the Plate Hall doorway.".
    Change shade "Hang felt over the crack" from shining to shaded consuming felt_scrap.
  }
  Initially Set wayDose(hall_way) to 2.
  Rule leak_shaded when state(leak, shaded) and wayDose(hall_way) > 0 { Set wayDose(hall_way) to 0. }

  // The Bunks: the Mutual's unlicensed crews, and their cold hearth.
  Observe bunks_scene at bunks when true "Rooms off the ring: bed niches cut in the rock, reading mirrors on pegs, tally marks by the doors. In one block, bedrolls, a cold hearth, Mutual tallies and a wine jar. One of the bed niches is yours.".
  Observe bunks_lit at bunks when bright(bunks) "Grey-gold light falls into the Bunks from the low slot in the ceiling. Someone has hung a shirt up to dry in it.".
  Person bunks_crew "the Bunks crew" at bunks {
    Role "four of the Mutual's unlicensed cutters, between shifts". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Relation grumbled(group).
  // An event happens once, seen or not; the crew grumble whenever someone comes in on them in the dark, so it is said
  // each time it is so.
  Observe bunks_darkened at bunks as event when not bright(bunks) and at(bunks_crew, bunks) and green(bunks) > 0 "One of the cutters in the Bunks looks up at the dead slot in the ceiling. 'Somebody's been at the third mirror again,' she says. 'Swing it back before the ferns go, or we'll be sleeping in the dark.'".
  Topic bunks_neck with bunks_crew "Ask the Bunks crew about the way down to the Granaries" when true once {
    Says "'Service stair, out of the back of the Plate Hall,' says a woman with her boots off. 'Mind the doorway. There's a crack in the plaster over it, and a blade of the straight light comes through. Run it, or hang a bit of felt over the crack.' She throws you a scrap of old felt. 'Keep that.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, felt_scrap) by 1. }
  }
  Topic bunks_outfall with bunks_crew "Ask the Bunks crew about other ways out" when true once {
    Says "'The Holdfolk say the old drain comes out above Ennick,' says the woman. 'The Outfall. Nine kilometres on your belly, and shut by the flood from Sowing to the end of summer. It should open any day now.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, outfall_known). }
  }
  Entity felt_scrap: good "scrap of felt".
  Discovery outfall_known "The Outfall, the Seridane's drain, runs nine kilometres from the Granaries' flood line to a spring cave in the cliff above Ennick; it is shut by the flood from Sowing to the end of summer.".

  // The Plate Hall: voice-plates in racks, a stylus on a cord, and Halu's stack by the door (S5).
  Observe plate_hall_scene at plate_hall when true "A long hall of racks for thin stillglass plates, most of the slots empty. By the door, twelve plates are stacked neatly, edges squared, as if someone meant to carry them away and will be back for them.".
  Thing tally_plate "a plate from the granary racks" at plate_hall {
    State silent "One rack is labelled with the sign the Seridane painted on their grain jars. A plate stands in it.".
    State playing "A clerk's voice, faint as wind, counts jars into a vault: a number, a breath, and then a line said quickly the same way each time, the way you would say a thing a thousand times a day. 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.'".
    Change play_tally "Draw a stylus along the granary plate" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Thing song_plate "a plate on its own on a shelf" at plate_hall {
    State silent "On a shelf by itself, a plate scratched along one edge with children's tally marks.".
    State playing "Children's voices, very small and far away, count in a ring: twelve words, round and round, and on the twelfth they all shout.".
    Change play_song "Draw a stylus along the children's plate" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Thing debate_plate "a plate from the debate" at plate_hall {
    State silent "In the end rack, two plates are cut with the Answerer and Coverer signs.".
    State playing "A woman's voice, a Coverer's: 'It was not given. Nothing gives a thing it cannot see. It fell, as a stone falls from a sling, and the lake wrote it down.' And a man, an Answerer, louder, threatening her by name.".
    Change play_debate "Draw a stylus along the debate plate" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Rule debate_ends when state(debate_plate, playing) and not at(party, plate_hall) { Assert state(debate_plate, silent). }
  Discovery coverer_case "The Coverers argued, on the debate plates, that the hour was not given but fell, and that the lake's own records said so.".
  Observe debate_heard at plate_hall when state(debate_plate, playing) "The Coverers said it fell." teaches coverer_case.
  Rule tally_ends when state(tally_plate, playing) and not at(party, plate_hall) { Assert state(tally_plate, silent). }
  Rule song_ends when state(song_plate, playing) and not at(party, plate_hall) { Assert state(song_plate, silent). }
  Discovery song_heard "The Plate Hall's counting song: children count twelve words in a ring, each on its own note.".
  Observe song_learned at plate_hall when state(song_plate, playing) "Each of the twelve words has its own note." teaches song_heard.
  Discovery tally_words "A Seridane granary clerk, counting jars into a vault, said the same line over each: 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.'".
  Observe tally_heard at plate_hall when state(tally_plate, playing) "The same line, over each jar." teaches tally_words.

  // The Granary Ring and its vaults. Each vault has an umber shutter on a pulley; open, a bar of direct light comes
  // down its channel from the Pit wall and holds whatever is under it; shut, it lets whatever it held go (G2). The
  // pulley's cord is made off on a cleat by the doorway, so that the shutter is worked from outside the beam.
  Observe ring_scene at ring when true "A curving passage with forty vaults off it, numbered in Seridane signs over their doorways. In some, a bar of hard white light comes straight down from the ceiling onto the floor.".
  Discovery jars_painted "Every jar in the Granary Ring is painted with the same line of Seridane writing, and holds black dust.".
  Observe jars_seen at ring when not benighted(party) "Every jar in every vault is red-glazed and painted with the same line of words, and every jar you can see into holds black dust." teaches jars_painted.

  Thing shutter "the ninth vault's shutter" on vault_door {
    State open "In the ceiling of the ninth vault an umber shutter hangs open on its pulley, and a bar of white light comes down through the channel above it onto the floor.".
    State shut "The ninth vault's shutter is down. The vault is dark.".
    Change close_nine "Pull the shutter cord at the doorway" from open to shut at ring.
    Change open_nine "Let the shutter cord run" from shut to open at ring.
  }
  Initially Assert litGround(vault).
  Rule vault_lit when state(shutter, open) and not litGround(vault) { Assert litGround(vault). }
  Rule vault_unlit when state(shutter, shut) and litGround(vault) { Retract litGround(vault). Assert unlit(vault). }
  Rule vault_bright when state(shutter, open) and unlit(vault) { Retract unlit(vault). }
  Observe cleat_seen at ring when state(shutter, open) "Beside the ninth vault's doorway, a cord comes down out of the ceiling and is made off on a bronze cleat.".
  Observe vault_scene at vault when state(shutter, open) "Rows of red-glazed jars stand under the beam, each painted with the same line of words. In the middle of them a man in a cutter's felt hood stands with one hand out toward a jar, his eyes open.".
  Observe vault_dark_scene at vault when state(shutter, shut) "Rows of red-glazed jars, and the smell of old dust.".
  Kind granary_jars "a sack's worth of umber-glazed jars" is treasure worth 12 weighing 8
    described "Red-glazed Seridane grain jars, not a crack in one, each painted with the same line of writing and holding black dust. A collector in Sorne pays three crowns a jar.".
  Item jars "the ninth vault's jars" is granary_jars at vault.

  // The fourth vault holds a fox.
  Thing fox_shutter "the fourth vault's shutter" on fox_door {
    State open "An umber shutter hangs open in the ceiling, and the light comes down onto a fox that stands in it with its tail half lifted.".
    State shut "The fourth vault's shutter is down.".
    Change close_fourth "Pull the fourth vault's shutter cord" from open to shut at ring.
  }
  Initially Assert litGround(fox_vault).
  Person fox "a fox" at fox_vault { Role "a dog fox, held in the light mid-step". Species fox. Pronouns he. }
  Initially Assert asleep(fox). Initially Assert slowable(fox). Initially Set dose(fox) to 2400.
  Rule fox_unlit when state(fox_shutter, shut) and litGround(fox_vault) { Retract litGround(fox_vault). }
  Rule fox_wakes when asleep(fox) and dose(fox) < 288 { Retract asleep(fox). }
  Event fox_runs near fox when not asleep(fox) and at(fox, fox_vault) "The fox finishes its step, and the next. It looks round at the dark with its ears flat, and is gone down the ring like smoke." then {
    Retract at(fox, fox_vault). Assert at(fox, flood_line). }

  // The Waking Ward: where the Seridane held their sick, and where they woke in the dark when the light was cut (G3).
  Observe ward_scene_t at waking_ward when true "Long rooms of stone beds with leather straps rotted to threads. The ceiling channels are shuttered and dark.".
  Observe ward_walls at waking_ward when not benighted(party) "The writing starts at the door, scratched into the stone at the height of someone sitting up. Further in it is everywhere: walls, bed-edges, floor. Some is neat; some runs downhill. Near the far end it is low, at the height of someone lying down, and the scratches are shallow. You cannot read it, but you can tell that it was written in the dark. One word near the door has the same shape as the line on the granary jars.".
  Discovery ward_written "The Seridane held their sick in the Waking Ward. When the light was cut, the held woke in the dark and wrote on the walls until they died: names, and words over and over." {
    Found by searching waking_ward "Among the scratches, the same few words come again and again, low down and shallow at the end. One of them has been written so many times that the stone is worn smooth around it.".
  }

  // The Flood Line and the Sluice: the outer passages slope into warm clear water. In autumn the flood falls; from
  // Sowing to Haying it closes the Outfall's last stretch (G4). The Sluice lowers it, and sends it all down to Ennick.
  Measure flood(entity).
  Entity flood_water: scenery "the flood in the Granaries".
  Initially Set flood(flood_water) to 100.
  Relation sluiced(entity).
  Rule flood_falls when season(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) == 3 and flood(flood_water) > 40 { Decrease flood(flood_water) by 15. }
  Rule flood_sluiced when sluiced(flood_water) and hour(clock) == 3 and flood(flood_water) > 0 { Decrease flood(flood_water) by 20. }
  Observe flood_scene at flood_line when flood(flood_water) >= 60 "The passages slope down into still, warm, clear water. White shrimp scatter from your light. Where the Outfall goes on west, the water stands to the roof.".
  Observe flood_scene_low at flood_line when flood(flood_water) < 60 "The water has drawn back down the slope. Where the Outfall goes on west, there is air above the water now, a hand of it, then more.".
  Species outfall_eel "an Outfall eel" like great_pike temperament ambush
    described "An eel of the Ammer that swam up the warm Outfall as an elver two hundred years ago and never left: three metres of it, white about the jaw.".
  Person eels "Outfall eels" at flood_line {
    Role "two old eels lying in the flooded doorway". Species outfall_eel. Numbers 2.
  }
  Thing sluice "the Sluice" at sluice_head {
    State closed "A bronze gate stands in a stone frame at the head of a broad tunnel, with a geared wheel the size of a man. A trickle comes through it.".
    State opened "The Sluice stands open. The water goes through it with a sound like wind.".
    Change open_sluice "Wind the Sluice open" from closed to opened.
    Change close_sluice "Wind the Sluice shut" from opened to closed.
  }
  Rule sluice_runs when state(sluice, opened) and not sluiced(flood_water) { Assert sluiced(flood_water). }
  Rule sluice_stops when state(sluice, closed) and sluiced(flood_water) { Retract sluiced(flood_water). }
  Entity quell_wells: scenery "Quell's wells".
  Relation drained(entity). Relation washedOut(entity).
  Rule wells_drop when sluiced(flood_water) and flood(flood_water) < 40 and not drained(quell_wells) { Assert drained(quell_wells). }

  // Garret, held eleven months at about a hundredth, in the beam among the jars.
  Person garret "Garret" at vault {
    Role "a cutter of the Mutual, held in the light". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Plans 14 steps. Uses go, change_thing. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Joins "Garret puts a hand on your shoulder, to steady himself as much as anything. 'Up, then,' he says. 'Slowly.'".
  }
  Initially Assert kin(party, garret). Initially Assert kinship(garret, uncle).
  Entity uncle: fact "your uncle".
  Initially Assert asleep(garret). Initially Assert slowable(garret). Initially Assert feltClad(garret).
  Initially Set dose(garret) to 2400.
  Measure watchedFor(entity).
  Rule watching_garret when at(party, vault) and heldDeep(garret) and at(garret, vault) and not benighted(party) { Increase watchedFor(garret) by 1. }
  Observe garret_moved at vault when heldDeep(garret) and at(garret, vault) and watchedFor(garret) >= 6 "You have watched him for an hour. His hand is a finger's width nearer the jar than it was, and his chest is higher.".
  Observe garret_slowing at vault when not heldDeep(garret) and asleep(garret) and at(garret, vault) "Garret's eyes are moving. They come round to you over a long time, and his lips part.".
  Observe garret_ring at ring when asleep(garret) and at(garret, ring) and not heldDeep(garret) "Garret lies on the floor of the Ring where he was dragged, his eyes moving very slowly from one thing to the next.".
  Rule garret_wakes when asleep(garret) and dose(garret) < 288 { Retract asleep(garret). Assert acceptsEscort(garret, party). }
  // He comes round whether or not anyone is there to see. What it was like is told to whoever first sees him awake:
  // an event would be spent unseen, so it is an observation that teaches its own having been seen (ledger, 4).
  Rule garret_willing when not asleep(garret) and not willing(garret, party) and not travelsWith(garret, party) and not cameUp(garret) { Assert willing(garret, party). }
  Entity garret_woke: fact "Garret has come round from eleven months in the light.".
  Observe garret_comes_round near garret as event when not asleep(garret) and not cameUp(garret) and not knows(party, garret_woke) "Garret finishes the reach he began eleven months ago, closes his hand on nothing, and sits down hard. 'Where's the light gone?' he says. 'Ness was just there.' He looks at you a long time. 'You were never this tall. What month is it?' Told, he says nothing for a while. 'I'm hungry,' he says at last, as if that settled it." teaches garret_woke.
  Topic garret_month with garret "Tell Garret how long he stood there" when not asleep(garret) once {
    Says "'Eleven months,' Garret says after you, as if trying the words for size. 'It was Harvest. I had my hand out.' He looks at his hand. 'Ness said the light would not reach past the door. Ness said a lot of things.'".
  }
  Topic garret_ness with garret travelling "Ask Garret about Ness" when not asleep(garret) once {
    Says "'She wanted the jars,' says Garret. 'Three crowns a jar in Sorne, and there's forty in that vault. I said the light was moving, I'd seen it on the floor. She said go on then, if you're frightened.' He laughs, not much. 'So I went on.'".
  }
  // Pulled out by hand: whoever does it stands in the beam to do it.
  Action drag_out(actor: group, site: place) "Go into the beam and drag Garret out of it" {
    Description "Into the light, an arm round him, and back out to the Ring. It takes a few minutes in the beam.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, vault) and at(garret, vault)
      and state(shutter, open) and asleep(garret) and not hobbled(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Retract at(garret, vault). Assert at(garret, ring). Retract at(actor, vault). Assert at(actor, ring).
      Assert dragged(garret). }
    Result "You go in among the jars, get an arm round Garret, and haul. He comes like a felled tree, stiff and very slow, and you get him out over the threshold onto the Ring.".
  }
  Relation dragged(group).
  Relation cameUp(group).
  // Joined, he is a member of the company with a body of his own, and the dose was on the person he was: it is
  // carried over by hand (ledger, 6).
  Rule garret_dose_joins when travelsWith(garret, party) and dose(garret) > 0 {
    Set dose(member_garret_person) to dose(garret). Set dose(garret) to 0. }
  // Once he can walk, and nobody leads him, he makes his own slow way home to the Mutual's hall.
  Pursuit go_home for garret "making his slow way up to Quell" priority 20 when not asleep(garret) and not following(garret, party) and not travelsWith(garret, party) and not cameUp(garret) seeks at(garret, mutual_hall).
  Pursuit stay_close for garret "keeping close to you" priority 30 when following(garret, party) seeks together(garret, party).
  Rule garret_home when at(garret, mutual_hall) and not cameUp(garret) { Assert cameUp(garret). }
  Rule garret_brought when travelsWith(garret, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) and not cameUp(garret) { Assert cameUp(garret). }
  Initially Assert keyholder(garret, chain_gate).

  // Dagny's crew goes down on the fourth morning, when it has the felt, and Ness with them. At the Ring they argue; the crew pull the cord,
  // and Ness takes the jars.
  Rule crew_sets_out when day(clock) >= 4 and hour(clock) == 6 and not descended(crew) { Assert descended(crew). }
  Initially Assert keyholder(crew, chain_gate). Initially Assert keyholder(ness, chain_gate).
  Pursuit go_down for crew "going down after Garret" priority 20 when descended(crew) and asleep(garret) seeks at(crew, ring).
  Pursuit go_down for ness "going down with the crew" priority 20 when descended(crew) and not keeps(ness, jars) seeks at(ness, ring).
  Relation argued(group).
  Event crew_argue near crew when at(crew, ring) and at(ness, ring) and asleep(garret) and not argued(crew) "At the ninth vault's doorway Dagny's crew stand arguing in low voices. 'He'll keep,' Ness is saying. 'He's kept a year. Take the jars and come back for him with the sledge.' 'We came for him,' says the elder. 'And we go in for him when Dagny sends the long poles down, not before. I'll not have two of us stood in there.'" then { Assert argued(crew). Set arguedOn(crew) to day(clock). }
  Measure arguedOn(group).
  Pursuit free_him for crew "pulling the shutter cord on Garret" priority 25 when argued(crew) and day(clock) >= arguedOn(crew) + 3 and state(shutter, open) seeks state(shutter, shut).
  Action pack_jars(actor: group, site: place) "Pack the ninth vault's jars into a sack" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, ring) and at(jars, vault) and state(shutter, shut) and distinct(actor, party).
    Time 3.
    On success { Retract at(jars, vault). Assert keeps(actor, jars). }
    Seen "{actor} packs the jars from the ninth vault into a sack, wrapping each in straw.".
  }
  Pursuit take_jars for ness "packing the ninth vault's jars" priority 30 when at(ness, ring) and state(shutter, shut) and at(jars, vault) seeks keeps(ness, jars) using pack_jars.
  Pursuit go_back for ness "taking the jars up to sell" priority 20 when keeps(ness, jars) seeks at(ness, mutual_yard).
  Pursuit go_back for crew "going back up" priority 10 when descended(crew) and not asleep(garret) seeks at(crew, mutual_yard).
}

data/adventures/patient-star/undersun.ky:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Undersun (Tier II): an inverted citadel beneath the Late Sun, 300 metres across at its crown and 700 deep,
  // narrowing to a drilling tip. Every room is a moment cut from the plateau's past. Five rules: a room is a moment;
  // touch gives time; speech is laid; course-light doses; the name is the plan.
  Place undersun "the Undersun" is site within ghessil at 5, 1.
  Place crown "the Crown" is level within undersun.
  Place reach "the Seridane Reach" is level within undersun.
  Place silent_reach "the Silent Reach" is level within undersun.
  Place shaft_600 "the shaft at six hundred metres" is level within undersun.
  Place shaft_700 "the shaft at seven hundred metres" is level within undersun.
  Place shaft_foot "the foot of the shaft" is level within undersun.
  Place lreach "the Listeners' Reach" is level within undersun.
  Place tip "the Tip" is level within undersun.

  Place crown_entry "where the Courses broke through" is room within crown at 1, 0 underground.
  Place fall_chamber "the Fall" is room within crown at 0, 0 underground.
  Place fire_heart "the heart of the fire" is room within crown at 0, 1 underground.
  Place first_course "the First Course" is room within crown at 2, 0 underground.
  Place burning_wood "the Burning Wood" is room within crown at 1, 1 underground.
  Place crown_foot "the foot of the Crown" is room within crown at 1, 2 underground.

  Place reach_head "the head of the Seridane Reach" is room within reach at 1, 0 underground.
  Place granary_noon "the Granary at Noon" is room within reach at 0, 0 underground.
  Place schism "the Council of the Schism" is room within reach at 2, 0 underground.
  Place riot_hall "the Riot Hall" is room within reach at 1, 1 underground.
  Place bathhouse "the Bathhouse" is room within reach at 0, 1 underground.
  Place quarried "the Quarried Gallery" is room within reach at 2, 1 underground.
  Place reach_foot "the foot of the Seridane Reach" is room within reach at 1, 2 underground.

  Place shaft_top "the top of the shaft" is room within silent_reach at 0, 0 underground.
  Place plumb_mouth "the Plumb's mouth" is room within shaft_600 at 0, 1 underground.
  Place saro_stair "the top of Saro's stair" is room within shaft_700 at 0, 2 underground.
  Place shaft_bottom "the bottom of the shaft" is room within shaft_foot at 0, 3 underground.

  Place lreach_head "the head of the Listeners' Reach" is room within lreach at 1, 0 underground.
  Place breach_moment "the Breach, stopped" is room within lreach at 0, 0 underground.
  Place keystone_gallery "the Keystone Gallery" is room within lreach at 2, 0 underground.
  Place fair_moment "the Fair" is room within lreach at 1, 1 underground.
  Place tip_dome "the Tip" is room within tip at 0, 0 underground.

  // Course-light: every room of the Undersun is direct light for dose, and every room is laid.
  Initially Assert litGround(crown_entry). Initially Assert litGround(fall_chamber). Initially Assert litGround(fire_heart).
  Initially Assert litGround(first_course). Initially Assert litGround(burning_wood). Initially Assert litGround(crown_foot).
  Initially Assert litGround(reach_head). Initially Assert litGround(granary_noon). Initially Assert litGround(schism).
  Initially Assert litGround(riot_hall). Initially Assert litGround(bathhouse). Initially Assert litGround(quarried).
  Initially Assert litGround(reach_foot). Initially Assert litGround(shaft_top). Initially Assert litGround(plumb_mouth).
  Initially Assert litGround(saro_stair). Initially Assert litGround(shaft_bottom). Initially Assert litGround(lreach_head).
  Initially Assert litGround(breach_moment). Initially Assert litGround(keystone_gallery). Initially Assert litGround(fair_moment).
  Initially Assert litGround(tip_dome).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(granary_noon). Initially Assert laidRoom(riot_hall). Initially Assert laidRoom(schism).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(keystone_gallery). Initially Assert laidRoom(fair_moment). Initially Assert laidRoom(tip_dome).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(breach_moment). Initially Assert laidRoom(bathhouse).

  // The ways in: following Saro, or with a trowel, through the face of the Courses; or down the Plumb.
  Passage into_courses "into the Courses" is crawl between courses_face and crown_entry taking 20 minutes
    opening when travelsWith(saro, party) or holding(party, trowel_kind) "Course-glass cannot be cut, pierced or broken by anything you carry. A Mason's trowel lays and unlays it.".
  Passage plumb "the Plumb, by the rope" is shaft between coverers_works and plumb_mouth taking 1 hour needing rope.
  Initially Set wayDose(plumb) to 24. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(plumb) to 6.

  // The Crown's syllables were spoken before anyone listened: only the Keeping holds them, at the new moons; or
  // Lirem's astrolabe, held in the course-light, reads them off the courses.
  Discovery crown_map "The Crown's plan: its syllables, from the new moons of its first three centuries, laid out as rooms.".
  Passage fall_arch "a ribbed arch" is arch between crown_entry and fall_chamber.
  Passage dog_way "a round passage" is passage between crown_entry and first_course taking 3 minutes hidden until crown_map.
  Passage wood_edge "the edge of the Wood" is passage between crown_entry and burning_wood taking 5 minutes.
  Passage wood_line "the safe line through the smoke" is passage between burning_wood and crown_foot taking 20 minutes hidden until smoke_line.
  Passage fire_gaps "the gaps in the stopped fire" is passage between fall_chamber and fire_heart taking 5 minutes.
  Passage crown_down "the grammar stair" is stair between crown_foot and reach_head taking 10 minutes.

  Observe crown_entry_scene at crown_entry when true "Inside the Courses, light runs along every curve. The passage is coursed like masonry, banded dark and clear, without a seam, and it turns in ways stone would not.".
  Observe astrolabe_reads at crown_entry when carries(party, astrolabe) and not knows(party, crown_map) "Lirem's astrolabe swings in your hand until its pointer lies along the course-light. The rings turn of themselves, syllable by syllable, and you are reading a plan of rooms." teaches crown_map.

  // The Fall: the instant of impact, 2,290 BP. Stopped fire, a shock-front of compressed air, and the Splinter.
  Observe fall_scene at fall_chamber when true "A chamber sixty metres across, full of fire that does not move. Arcs of molten rock hang in the air like thrown ribbons. A curved sheet of something clear and rippled stands across the room, bending everything seen through it.".
  Thing shock_front "the shock-front" at fall_chamber {
    State standing "The clear rippled sheet stands across the chamber: air, compressed and stopped mid-blast.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(shock_front).
  Hazard slap "the shock-front's slap" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Rule front_released when touched(shock_front) says "The air goes. It throws you ten metres back through the arch." {
    Retract touched(shock_front). Assert strikes(slap, party). Assert at(party, crown_entry). }
  Thing stopped_fire "the stopped fire" on fire_gaps {
    State unmapped dangerous "Between the ribbons of fire there are gaps, but you cannot tell from in among them which go through.".
    State mapped "You have the gaps in the fire mapped from the door: a crooked way in, a crooked way out.".
    Change map_gaps "Map the gaps in the fire from the doorway" from unmapped to mapped.
    Hurts with burn when unmapped then unmapped.
  }
  Hazard burn "the stopped fire" means "Deal (2d8) fire damage to ally.".
  Observe heart_scene at fire_heart when true "At the heart of the fire, in a hollow of stopped flame, lies a fist-sized lump of something that gives off light of its own.".
  Kind splinter_kind "the Splinter" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A fist-sized piece of the seed, broken off when it fell. Warm to the hand; it gives off direct light, enough to hold a person at arm's length within a day.".
  Item splinter "the Splinter" is splinter_kind at fire_heart.
  // A very small Late Sun: whoever carries it stands in direct light, wherever they are.
  Relation carriesLight(group).
  Rule splinter_carried when carries(?c, splinter) and company(?c) and not carriesLight(?c) { Assert carriesLight(?c). }
  Rule splinter_dropped when carriesLight(?c) and not carries(?c, splinter) { Retract carriesLight(?c). }
  Rule splinter_doses when carriesLight(?c) and memberOf(?m, ?c) and not unslowed(?m) and not heldDeep(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by 2. }

  // The First Course: the shepherd's dog, the first moment the seed took. The Masons treat it as a shrine.
  Observe dog_scene at first_course when not state(dog_course, unlaid) "In a small round chamber of black-and-clear banding, a dog, mid-stride, its ears back.".
  Thing dog_course "the First Course" at first_course {
    State laid_dog "The dog is the cornerstone of everything below it.".
    State unlaid "The round chamber is empty. Something huge has settled above, and the way down is shut by fallen courses.".
    Change unlay_dog "Unlay the First Course with the trowel" from laid_dog to unlaid needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Initially Assert kept(dog_course).
  Observe dog_runs near dog_course when touched(dog_course) "Under your hand the dog finishes its stride, and the next, and you feel its heart going like a bird's; it is a long way from home and frightened. When you take your hand away it stops again, mid-stride.".
  Rule crown_falls when state(dog_course, unlaid) and not crownDropped(undersun) says "The whole Crown drops three metres onto the Reach below, with a sound that goes on for a long time." {
    Assert crownDropped(undersun). }
  Relation crownDropped(place).

  // The Burning Wood: smoke stopped in curtains; a flake of ash given time drifts along the safe line.
  Observe wood_scene at burning_wood when true "A pine forest on fire, stopped, with birds fixed in the air above it and smoke standing in solid grey curtains between the trunks.".
  Thing smoke "the curtains of smoke" at burning_wood {
    State rigid "The smoke stands in grey curtains, rigid as cloth on a frame.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(smoke).
  Hazard choke "the smoke, given time" means "Deal (1d8) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Rule smoke_flows when touched(smoke) says "The curtain goes soft under your hand and pours over you, choking and hot, until you pull your hand back." {
    Retract touched(smoke). Assert strikes(choke, party). }
  Thing ash "a flake of ash" at burning_wood {
    State hanging "A single flake of ash hangs in the air at the height of your eyes.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(ash).
  Discovery smoke_line "The safe line through the Burning Wood: where a flake of ash, given time, drifts between the curtains.".
  Observe ash_drifts near ash when touched(ash) "Given time, the flake drifts, and does not fall: it goes sideways between two curtains, and turns, and turns again, along a line you could walk." teaches smoke_line.
  Observe crown_foot_scene at crown_foot when true "The Crown narrows to a stair that goes down by repeated forms: the same step laid again and again, as the same syllable was spoken again and again.".

  // The Seridane Reach: moments of Tamaun's life. Mapped by the Long Hour.
  Passage reach_noon "a granary arch" is arch between reach_head and granary_noon.
  Passage reach_schism "a council door" is doorway between reach_head and schism hidden until long_hour_read.
  Passage reach_riot "the way into the crowd" is passage between reach_head and riot_hall taking 3 minutes.
  Passage riot_exit "the Grammar door" is doorway between riot_hall and reach_foot.
  Passage bath_door "a bathhouse door" is doorway between riot_hall and bathhouse.
  Passage quarry_hollow "a smooth hollow" is passage between reach_head and quarried taking 5 minutes hidden until long_hour_read.
  Passage reach_drop "the stem, looped by rope" is shaft between reach_foot and shaft_top taking 30 minutes needing rope.

  Observe reach_head_scene at reach_head when true "The Reach opens under the Crown in galleries that are Tamaun's: plaster, bronze, a Seridane arch with its keystone carved; only no one living built any of it.".
  // The Granary at Noon: forty Laid, mid-task; Lirem with his astrolabe, his other hand toward the gong.
  Observe noon_scene at granary_noon when true "A vault full of Seridane workers, forty of them, mid-task: carrying jars, sweeping, one laughing with her head back. A scribe sits at a table with a stylus over a tablet. A thin man at the end of the room holds a bronze instrument of rings and pointers, his other hand raised toward a gong.".
  Observe noon_wakes at granary_noon when spokeAloud(party) "At the sound of your voice the whole granary moves: forty people take three steps, the laughing woman finishes her laugh, a jar is set down. Then they stop again where they are.".
  Discovery granary_plan "The scribe's tablet: a plan of Tamaun's Granary Ring with the channel settings for every vault.".
  Thing scribe_tablet "the scribe's tablet" at granary_noon {
    State on_table "A wax tablet under the scribe's stylus, ruled in a plan.".
    Tries looking.
  }
  Observe tablet_read near scribe_tablet when tried(scribe_tablet, looking) "It is a plan of the Granary Ring, with the angle of every channel marked beside its vault." teaches granary_plan.
  Thing lirem_hand "Lirem's hand" at granary_noon {
    Holds.
    State holding_it "Lirem's thin hand holds a bronze instrument of rings and pointers.".
    State empty_hand "Lirem's hand is empty, still raised a little toward the gong.".
  }
  Kind astrolabe_kind "Lirem's astrolabe" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A bronze instrument of rings and pointers. Set to the Late Sun's depth it shows where any ray will fall; held in course-light, it reads the name-grammar.".
  Item astrolabe "Lirem's astrolabe" is astrolabe_kind in lirem_hand.
  Relation gonged(place).
  Rule hand_emptied when not inside(astrolabe, lirem_hand) and state(lirem_hand, holding_it) says "Lirem's hand, with nothing in it, finishes its movement: it strikes the gong." {
    Assert state(lirem_hand, empty_hand). Assert gonged(granary_noon). }
  Observe gong_alarm at granary_noon when gonged(granary_noon) and not gongPassed(party) "The gong's note goes out through the Reach, and everywhere, for a few seconds, the Laid take up their moments: you hear the riot in the next hall roar and stop.".
  Relation gongPassed(group).
  Rule riot_loosed when gonged(granary_noon) and not rioted(riot_hall) { Assert rioted(riot_hall). }
  Relation rioted(place).

  // The Council of the Schism: Selane arguing for the Covering, Amaru on the dais. A sentence at a touch.
  Observe schism_scene at schism when true "A council chamber. A young woman stands speaking, her hand raised. An old man sits on a dais. Every face in the room is turned to her.".
  Thing selane_words "the air in front of Selane's mouth" at schism {
    State unspoken "Selane's lips are parted on a word.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(selane_words).
  Measure sentences(entity).
  Rule selane_speaks when touched(selane_words) and sentences(selane_words) < 4 {
    Increase sentences(selane_words) by 1. Retract touched(selane_words). }
  Observe selane_one near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 1 "'Lirem's chains are longer every year,' Selane says, in Old Seridan, and stops.".
  Observe selane_two near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 2 "'It is not resting on the rock. It is going through it, and the stone below answers each time it speaks.'".
  Observe selane_three near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 3 "'A thing that speaks is not always speaking to you. A mason calls out the courses as he lays them.'".
  Discovery seed_building "Selane's argument, in her own voice: the Late Sun is not speaking to anyone; it is building, and calling its courses as it lays them, and it is going down toward something.".
  Observe selane_four near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 4 "'Cover it, father. Not because it is a god. Because it is a builder, and we do not know what for.' Her hand comes down. Amaru, on the dais, has not moved." teaches seed_building.
  Topic amaru_selane with amaru "Tell the king his daughter's argument, word for word" when knows(actor, seed_building) once {
    Says "You say it as she said it. It takes Amaru a long time to understand that you are not inventing it. 'A builder,' he says. Then, after a very long time: 'Say it again.' You do. He asks you a third time.".
    On discuss { Assert grieves(amaru). }
  }

  // The Riot Hall: the grain riot of 1,575 BP, two hundred Laid. Every word spoken aloud gives them five seconds.
  Observe riot_scene at riot_hall when true "A broad hall packed with people in mid-struggle: sickles raised, poles swinging, a woman pulled backward by the hair, a man on the floor with his arm over his face. In the middle of the crowd stands a door. On the wall by the entrance someone has written, in chalk, a single sign in a script of overlapping circles.".
  Observe chalk_read at riot_hall when travelsWith(saro, party) "'Quiet,' says Saro, reading the chalk. She says it in a whisper.".
  // Said before the riot is told, because a three-minute act passes the rules once, in order (ledger, 9).
  Rule speaking_door when state(riot_door, open_g) and not doorSpoken(riot_door) { Assert spokeAloud(party). Assert doorSpoken(riot_door). Increase wordsLaid(party) by 10. }
  Hazard riot "five seconds of the riot" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Rule riot_given_time when at(party, riot_hall) and (spokeAloud(party) or rioted(riot_hall)) and not riotStruck(party) says "Two hundred people take up their riot for five seconds: sickles, poles, screaming. Then they stop where they are." {
    Assert strikes(riot, party). Assert riotStruck(party). }
  Relation riotStruck(group).
  Rule riot_still when riotStruck(party) and not spokeAloud(party) and not at(party, riot_hall) { Retract riotStruck(party). }
  Rule riot_spent when rioted(riot_hall) and riotStruck(party) { Retract rioted(riot_hall). }
  Discovery reach_syllables "The syllables of the Seridane Reach's Grammar doors, read from the Long Hour.".
  Observe syllables_from_hour near party when knows(party, long_hour_read) and not knows(party, reach_syllables) "The Long Hour gives you every door in the Reach by the syllable it was laid from." teaches reach_syllables.
  Thing riot_door "the Grammar door" on riot_exit {
    State shut_g blocking "A door of course-glass stands among the rioters. In its floor, if you look, the riot goes on, smaller, as if seen through water.".
    State open_g "The Grammar door stands open.".
    Change speak_syllable "Speak the door's syllable aloud" from shut_g to open_g after learning reach_syllables.
    Change lay_syllable "Lay the door's syllable into it with the trowel" from shut_g to open_g needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Relation doorSpoken(entity).
  Hazard floor_drop "the floor course unlaid" means "Deal (3d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Action guess_syllable(actor: group, site: place) "Speak a syllable at the Grammar door, guessing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, riot_hall) and state(riot_door, shut_g)
      and not knows(actor, reach_syllables).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert strikes(floor_drop, actor). Assert spokeAloud(actor). Assert at(actor, reach_head). }
    Result "The floor course under you unlays, and you drop into its moment: the riot, all round you, very loud, for as long as you are falling. You come up out of it at the head of the Reach, bruised and shaking.".
  }
  // Speaking aloud in a laid room: talking to anyone, the company is heard, unless it whispers.
  Rule heard_aloud when addressed(?p, ?c) and company(?c) and at(?c, ?r) and laidRoom(?r) and not whispering(?c)
    and not spokeAloud(?c) { Assert spokeAloud(?c). Increase wordsLaid(?c) by 10. }
  Rule quiet_again when spokeAloud(?c) and company(?c) and not addressedAny(?c) { Retract spokeAloud(?c). }
  Query addressedAny(c: group) means addressed(?p, c).

  // The Bathhouse: steam so dense that light takes ten minutes to cross it. Gleaners nest here.
  Observe bath_scene at bathhouse when true "A Seridane bathhouse full of steam that stands like milk. When you hold up a light, its glow does not reach the far side for a long time; what you see across the room is ten minutes old.".
  Species gleaner "a gleaner" like great_centipede temperament defensive
    described "A thing the size of a hand, many-legged, of stopped iron: one of a swarm from another world, given work by the Masons. They gather what falls, and lay it.".
  Person gleaners "gleaners" at bathhouse {
    Role "a swarm of gleaners, nesting". Species gleaner. Numbers 4.
  }
  Observe gleaners_late at bathhouse when at(gleaners, bathhouse) "Across the steam, ten minutes ago, something many-legged was moving along the wall.".

  // The Quarried Gallery: the fourth Dane's reign, carried away; his keystone remains.
  Observe quarried_scene at quarried when true "A long hollow with smooth walls and tool-marks, as if a gallery had been carved out of the masonry and carried off. At its far end one block remains, carved with a name. Your eye will not stay on the name.".
  Thing dane_keystone "the fourth Dane's keystone" at quarried {
    State carved "A block of course-glass with a man laid in it, and a name cut over him that the eye slides off.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(dane_keystone).
  Observe dane_speaks near dane_keystone when touched(dane_keystone) and not knows(party, dane_name) "Under your hand the man in the block draws breath, and says his own name, and you hear it, and keep it." teaches dane_name.

  // The Silent Reach: a bare stem in a thirty-metre shaft, grown during the burial. The Plumb breaks in at 600 metres;
  // Saro's stair climbs the stem from the bottom, a step a day.
  Passage shaft_down "the stem, by looped rope" is shaft between shaft_top and plumb_mouth taking 30 minutes needing rope.
  Passage shaft_down2 "down the stem to Saro's stair" is shaft between plumb_mouth and saro_stair taking 30 minutes needing rope.
  Passage saro_steps "Saro's stair" is stair between saro_stair and shaft_bottom taking 30 minutes.
  Passage tip_down "the stem's foot" is passage between shaft_bottom and lreach_head taking 10 minutes.
  Observe shaft_scene at shaft_top when true "A vertical shaft thirty metres across and three hundred deep, its walls cut smooth. Down its centre runs a column of dark metal and clear glass twelve metres thick, glowing along its curves. Warm air rises. From below comes a hammering, regular and patient.".
  Observe plumb_mouth_scene at plumb_mouth when true "The Coverers' borehole comes out of the shaft wall here, a glass-lined mouth half a metre across. There is nothing to stand on but a lip of rock and the stem.".
  Observe saro_stair_scene at saro_stair when true "A helical stair is being laid up the stem from the bottom, one step a day. Its top step is new and bright.".
  Observe shaft_bottom_scene at shaft_bottom when true "The foot of the shaft. Everything that has ever fallen down it lies here half-laid into the floor: a cutter's pack, a goat, a stone.".
  Person gleaners_low "gleaners at the foot of the shaft" at shaft_bottom {
    Role "a swarm of gleaners, laying what has fallen". Species gleaner. Numbers 6.
  }
  Hazard long_fall "the long fall" means "Deal (6d6) physical damage to ally.".

  // The Listeners' Reach: recent history, mapped by Teodar's count.
  Passage lr_breach "a stopped storm" is passage between lreach_head and breach_moment taking 3 minutes hidden until listeners_count.
  Passage lr_keystones "a vaulted gallery" is passage between lreach_head and keystone_gallery taking 3 minutes.
  Passage lr_fair "a fair's gate" is passage between lreach_head and fair_moment taking 3 minutes.
  Passage fair_exit "the drum door" is doorway between fair_moment and tip_dome.
  Observe lreach_scene at lreach_head when true "The newest courses: the plateau's own last three hundred years, laid one a month.".
  // The Breach: year 352, in storm. Four figures in wet felt, one with an iron pin.
  Observe breach_moment_scene at breach_moment when true "A night of storm, stopped. A stone culvert, a sluice frame, four figures in wet felt, one with an iron pin in his hand.".
  Thing breach_words "the air near the four in the storm" at breach_moment {
    State still_storm "Rain hangs between you and them.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(breach_words).
  Observe breach_heard near breach_words when touched(breach_words) "A woman's voice in Tovashi, low, through the rain: 'Pull it, Bren. The fill will drink it.' A young man's: 'Ayzhe —' and the pin comes out of the frame in his hand." teaches breach_cut.
  // The Keystone Gallery: Ennick's held, Kell's dead and the Sixty, laid as ribs.
  Observe keystone_scene at keystone_gallery when true "A vaulted gallery whose ribs are people: men and women lying in clear glass, each with a small red brick carved with a knot above the chest, the way Ennick marks its held. At the far end, older ribs hold strangers in Tovash dress.".
  Observe doran_rib at keystone_gallery when not benighted(party) "One of the ribs is a thin man with his hands at his sides and his mouth a little open, and a fan of bright lines in the glass in front of his face where the sand was not quite clean. It is Doran, at the moment Ilis laid him." teaches held_feed.
  Thing keystones "the keystones" at keystone_gallery {
    State bearing "The keystones bear the courses above them.".
    State unlaid_k "The keystones are unlaid. Below this gallery the Undersun has dropped thirty metres and stopped.".
    Change unlay_keys "Unlay the keystones with the trowel" from bearing to unlaid_k needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Relation masonsComing(place).
  Rule lower_dropped when state(keystones, unlaid_k) and not masonsComing(ennick) says "Far below, the lower Undersun drops thirty metres and stops. Twenty years of growth, gone. The Masons at the Tip put down their work, and look up." {
    Assert masonsComing(ennick). }
  // The Fair: the Tovash fair of year 0. The way out is a Grammar door keyed to a beat.
  Observe fair_scene at fair_moment when true "The Tovash fair of year 0: horses, a cauldron, children with their arms out, and a drum held against a man's chest.".
  Thing drum_door "the drum door" on fair_exit {
    State shut_d blocking "A door of course-glass stands where the fair's gate was. Nothing is carved on it; in its floor a drum is being beaten, very small.".
    State open_d "The drum door stands open.".
    Change strike_drum "Strike the held drum in the moot song's count" from shut_d to open_d after learning moot_count.
    Change lay_drum "Lay the door's beat into it with the trowel" from shut_d to open_d needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Action guess_beat(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the held drum in a beat you guess" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, fair_moment) and state(drum_door, shut_d)
      and not knows(actor, moot_count).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert strikes(floor_drop, actor). }
    Result "The floor course unlays and drops you into the fair, a second of it: the drum, the horses, the children's voices, and the light coming up out of the ground. You climb out shaking.".
  }

  // U5, the Tip: Saro's workshop and the drill. Six Masons; under the floor, the Delver; a note once an hour.
  Observe tip_scene at tip_dome when true "At the bottom of the stem, a domed chamber where new courses glow bright along their edges. A low note sounds from below the floor, once an hour.".
  Person masons "six Masons" at tip_dome {
    Role "six figures very still around the walls, each holding a tool like a trowel". Ancestry human. Numbers 6. Peaceable.
  }
  Observe masons_seen near masons when at(masons, tip_dome) "Their hands have no temperature. Their faces are from six different worlds, and they all watch you the same way: with interest, and no fear at all.".
  Topic masons_were with masons "Ask the Masons who they were" when true once {
    Says "They answer one at a time, in the last languages they learned, and Tovashi after a moment, picked up from you. A smith. A ferryman. A woman who sang at funerals. None of them can say where; all of them can say what they made. 'This,' says the singer, and lays a hand on the course. 'This is better.'".
  }
  Discovery trowel_traded "The Masons will trade a trowel for a moment, and the price of a moment is one of your memories, cut out with a trowel.".
  Topic masons_trowel with masons "Ask the Masons for a trowel" when true once {
    Says "'A moment for a moment,' says the ferryman. 'One of yours. We cut it, you do not miss it. Nobody does.' He holds out his hand, palm up.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, trowel_traded). }
  }
  // The spare trowel is declared in moments.kyr, beside its kind: an Item sees only its own file's kinds (ledger, 25).
  Discovery trowel_paid "A memory cut, and a trowel given for it.".
  Measure memories(group).
  Initially Set memories(party) to 12.
  Action pay_memory(actor: group, site: place) "Let the Masons cut one of your memories, for a trowel" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, tip_dome) and knows(actor, trowel_traded)
      and memories(actor) >= 1 and not paidMemory(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease memories(actor) by 1. Assert paidMemory(actor). }
    Result "The ferryman lays his trowel against your temple, and something is gone. You do not know what. Nobody in the world will ever know what. He puts a trowel in your hand.".
  }
  Relation paidMemory(group).
  Observe trowel_given near party when paidMemory(party) and not knows(party, trowel_paid) "The trowel lies on the course at your feet where he set it." teaches trowel_paid.
  Species delver_kind "the Delver" like iron_golem temperament defensive
    described "The first Mason, which rode the seed down. Not human. It drills.".
  Person delver "the Delver" at tip_dome {
    Role "the first Mason, working in the drill-face under the floor". Species delver_kind. Level 12.
  }
  // Saro at the Tip: where she works, the courses grow ten times as fast.
  Topic saro_tip with saro travelling "Ask Saro what she will do here" when at(party, tip_dome) once {
    Says "Saro has her hand on the newest course already. 'Work,' she says. 'Here. It is going down to the stone that sings. I will help it go.' She looks at you with that great attention. 'You may stay. You may go. I am staying.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/company.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Company party "Your company" of 3 at road_end.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 12. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/dale.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "Merrowdale: a dry dale under a long straight ridge the village calls the Long Man, a lake behind it, and three days before the autumn storm.".

  // The dale, north to south: Hollow Water, the Long Man across the dale's throat, the low fields, Merrow.
  Place dale "Merrowdale" is region.
  Place hollow "Hollow Water" is wilderness within dale at 1, 0.
  Place long_man "the Long Man" is site within dale at 1, 1.
  Place fields "the low fields" is wilderness within dale at 1, 2.
  Place merrow "Merrow" is settlement within dale at 0, 2.
  Place south "the south road" is wilderness within dale at 0, 3.

  Place inn "the Drowned Ox" is building within merrow.
  Place chapel "the Chapel of the Ford" is building within merrow.
  Place mill "Teller's mill" is building within merrow.
  Place cottage "Gammer Coller's cottage" is building within merrow.
  Place hall "the Hall" is building within merrow.

  Place road_end "the end of the south road" is room within south at 0, 0.
  Place green "Merrow green" is room within merrow at 1, 2.
  Place taproom "the Drowned Ox" is room within inn at 1, 3.
  Place nave "the chapel" is room within chapel at 0, 2.
  Place vestry "the vestry" is room within chapel at 0, 3.
  Place millhouse "the millhouse" is room within mill at 2, 2.
  Place reeve_room "Gammer Coller's kitchen" is room within cottage at 0, 1.
  Place hall_floor "the Hall" is level within hall.
  Place undercroft "the Hall's undercroft" is level within hall.
  Place yard "the Hall yard" is room within merrow at 1, 0.
  Place study "the steward's study" is room within hall_floor at 0, 0.
  Place chamber "the steward's bedchamber" is room within hall_floor at 1, 0.
  Place cellar "the Hall cellar" is room within undercroft at 2, 0.
  Place race "the mill race" is room within merrow at 2, 1.
  Place low_field "the low field" is room within fields at 0, 1.
  Place springs "the Weeping Springs" is room within fields at 0, 0.
  Place landing "the mill landing" is room within fields at 1, 1.
  Place hollow_door "the Hollow Door" is room within fields at 1, 0.
  // Where people go who have left the dale: downriver on the barge.
  Place downriver "downriver" is room within south at 1, 0.

  Passage south_road "the south road" is road between road_end and green taking 30 minutes.
  Passage ox_door "the Ox's door" is door between green and taproom.
  Passage chapel_porch "the chapel porch" is doorway between green and nave.
  Passage vestry_door "the vestry door" is door between nave and vestry.
  Passage mill_lane "the mill lane" is path between green and race taking 10 minutes.
  Passage mill_door "the mill door" is door between race and millhouse.
  Passage reeve_door "Gammer Coller's door" is door between green and reeve_room.
  Passage hall_lane "the Hall lane" is road between green and yard taking 30 minutes.
  Passage study_door "the study door" is door between yard and study.
  Passage chamber_door "the bedchamber door" is door between study and chamber.
  Passage cellar_stair "the cellar stair" is stair between yard and cellar.
  Passage dyke_path "the dyke path" is path between green and low_field taking 20 minutes.
  Passage spring_path "the spring path" is path between low_field and springs taking 20 minutes.
  Passage beck_path "the beck path" is path between low_field and landing taking 20 minutes.
  Passage mill_steps "the mill steps" is steps between millhouse and landing.
  Passage wall_foot "the foot of the wall" is path between springs and hollow_door taking 20 minutes.
  Passage door_path "the beck side" is path between landing and hollow_door taking 20 minutes.

  // Who comes up the south road: a company of its own (company.kyr) when the dale is a campaign, the world's company
  // when it is a country reached across a march (placed.kyr).

  Observe road_scene at road_end when true "The south road comes up out of the willows into a dale of black, wet-smelling earth. At its head a long green ridge lies across the valley, dead straight, like a sleeper under a blanket. A village of grey stone sits below it with its back to the hill.".
  Observe green_scene at green when not drowned(green) "A green with a well and a lime tree, and grey houses with their backs to the hill. The chapel stands at the low end by the beck; the Drowned Ox faces it across the grass. Up the lane, the Hall's roofs show at the north end of the Long Man.".
  Observe green_drowned at green when drowned(green) "Brown water stands over the green to the height of a man's waist, and moves. The lime tree is full of thatch.".
  Observe taproom_scene at taproom when true "A low taproom smelling of peat and wet wool. A sign over the hearth shows an ox up to its horns in water, which the landlord says is a joke.".
  Observe nave_scene at nave when true "A plain chapel with a floor of flagstones worn into hollows. By the door stands the font: a square grey pillar, smooth as soap, notched all the way up one edge. The highest notch is level with the roof-beam.".
  Observe vestry_scene at vestry when true "A cupboard of a room, with the parish register chained to a shelf and a basin of cold water.".
  Observe millhouse_scene at millhouse when not drowned(millhouse) "The millhouse shakes with the wheel. Flour hangs in the air like smoke.".
  Observe race_scene at race when true "The mill race runs full and loud along its stone channel to the wheel, fuller than a beck this size has any right to.".
  Observe reeve_scene at reeve_room when true "A kitchen with a peat fire, a cat, and on pegs by the door a row of tools for ditches: spades, a slasher, a long hook.".
  Observe yard_scene at yard when true "A cobbled yard under the north end of the Long Man, where the ridge rises behind the Hall like a wall behind a house.".
  Observe yard_smashed at yard when state(cart, smashed) "Something walked through the yard gate without opening it.".
  Observe study_scene at study when true "A steward's study: a fire, a desk heaped with bills, and the Hall's accounts in a row of ledgers.".
  Observe chamber_scene at chamber when true "A narrow bedchamber over the yard, with a cold grate, a washstand, and a bed with curtains of faded green.".
  Observe cellar_scene at cellar when true "The Hall cellar is old at the back, older than the Hall: walls of smooth grey stone, fitted without mortar. Barrels stand along them, and the air at the back is colder than a cellar's should be.".
  Item bar "an iron bar" is crowbar at cellar.
  Observe bar_seen at cellar when at(bar, cellar) "An iron bar leans against the barrels, one end bright with scraped bronze.".
  Observe field_scene at low_field when not drowned(low_field) "A low field of black earth under the Long Man. The furrows hold water, and the grass is the bright green of a meadow that is turning into a bog.".
  Observe field_drowned at low_field when drowned(low_field) "The low field is under a hand's depth of water. The furrows are gone; reeds are coming up through it.".
  Observe springs_scene at springs when true "At the foot of the Long Man a row of small springs comes out of the turf, clear and very cold. They run into a ditch that runs to the mill.".
  Observe landing_scene at landing when true "A stone landing where the beck widens below the mill, with rings for mooring.".
  Observe hollow_door_scene at hollow_door when true "At the south end of the Long Man the beck comes out of the hill through a great round arch of grey stone, smooth and pale, glazed blue-green where the water runs. An iron grate closes it, newer than the arch by a thousand years.".
  Observe downriver_scene at downriver when true "The beck goes on south toward the river and the towns.".

  // The people of Merrow, and what they want.
  Person venn "Aldous Venn" at study {
    Role "steward of the Hall". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    Objects "Venn sees {?i} in your hands, and his face changes. 'That belongs to the Hall,' he says. 'Give it here.'".
  }
  Person dunnet "Dunnet" at yard {
    Role "foreman at the Hall". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Peaceable.
    Wants bandages. Wants tin_lantern.
    Objects "Dunnet looks at {?i}, and at you, and goes in to the steward without a word. The study door bangs.".
  }
  Initially Assert serves(dunnet, venn).
  Person ysolt "Mother Ysolt" at nave {
    Role "priest of the Chapel of the Ford". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Peaceable.
    Wants keeper_mask.
  }
  Event mask_buried near ysolt when keeps(ysolt, ?face) and itemKind(?face, keeper_mask) "Mother Ysolt takes the grey face in both hands and looks at it a long time. That evening she buries it in the chapel yard with the words for the dead, and rings the bell once." then {
    Assert buried(?face).
  }
  Relation buried(item).
  Person hob "Hob Teller" at millhouse {
    Role "the miller". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
  }
  Person nell "Gammer Coller" at reeve_room {
    Role "the dyke-reeve". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    Objects "'That is the reeve's rod,' says Gammer Coller, very quietly. 'It is not yours, and it is not mine to lose. Put it back.'".
  }
  Person martin "Martin Pask" at taproom {
    Role "landlord of the Drowned Ox". Profession innkeeper. Peaceable.
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 6.
    Sells torch for 1 coin from 6.
  }
  Person folk "the people of Merrow" at green {
    Role "villagers". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Observe folk_here at green when at(folk, green) and not storming() and not dark() "A few people are at the well, and stop talking to watch you come.".
  Topic folk_long_man with folk "Ask the people at the well about the Long Man" when true once {
    Says "'The Long Man's barrow,' says a woman with a basket of eggs. 'There's a giant king under it, that the Long Folk buried with his gold. You don't go up there after dark.' She nods at the ridge. 'The Mower walks.'".
  }
  Topic folk_mower with folk "Ask the people at the well about the Mower" when true once {
    Says "'Grey,' says a boy, before anyone can stop him, 'and taller than the chapel door. It came down onto the green last week and stood looking at the springs half the night, and Hob Teller hid in his own millpond.' His mother cuffs him, not hard.".
  }
  Topic folk_venn with folk "Ask the people at the well about the steward" when true once {
    Says "They look at one another. 'Owes money downriver, they say,' says the woman with the eggs. 'The barge comes up for his old metal. He'll have put that notice up because the Mower knocked his cart about.'".
  }
  Topic martin_news with martin "Ask Martin Pask what is new in Merrow" when true once {
    Says "'Storm coming,' says Martin, wiping a pot. 'Three days, Gammer Coller says, and she's never been wrong in my life. And the Heron's due up the beck tomorrow noon for the steward's cart. Cass Rowell drinks here.' He sets the pot down. 'If you're going after the Mower, the steward's your man. I'd want paying first.'".
  }

  // The steward's notice, the steward's bronze, and the steward's key.
  Discovery bounty_known "The notice on the Ox's door, in a clerk's hand: WHOEVER LAYS THE MOWER THAT WALKS THE LONG MAN SHALL HAVE FORTY CROWNS OF THE STEWARD. A. VENN, FOR THE LORD." {
    Source notice "the steward's notice on the Ox's door" at green readable by party.
    Known by venn.
  }
  Thing cart "the cart under the tarpaulin" at yard {
    Holds.
    State covered closed "A cart stands under a tarpaulin with its shafts down, the tarpaulin roped tight.".
    State uncovered "The cart's tarpaulin is thrown back.".
    State smashed "The cart lies on its side with its wheels smashed and its tarpaulin torn.".
    Change uncover "Untie the tarpaulin on the cart" from covered to uncovered.
  }
  // The bronze is the steward's, he says, and his foreman says so first.
  Rule dunnet_sees_cart when state(cart, uncovered) and together(dunnet, party) and serves(dunnet, venn) and not noticedCart(dunnet) says "'That's the steward's,' says Dunnet, and comes over, not quickly. 'You'll want to ask him before you go in there.'" { Assert noticedCart(dunnet). }
  Relation noticedCart(group).
  Item teeth "a sack of bell-teeth" is bell_teeth in cart owned by venn.
  Thing cellar_chest "a barrel by the cellar's back wall" at cellar {
    Holds.
  }
  // The grate key is on the steward's belt by day, and on its hook by the study door while he sleeps; he lends it
  // to whoever takes his forty crowns. He sleeps after supper, in the room behind the study.
  Rule venn_retires when dark() and at(venn, study) and able(venn) { Assert at(venn, chamber). }
  Rule venn_rises when not dark() and at(venn, chamber) and able(venn) { Assert at(venn, study). }
  Thing key_hook "the hook by the study door" at study {
    Holds.
    State worn closed "The steward wears a big iron key on his belt.".
    State hung "A big iron key hangs on the hook by the study door.".
    State empty "Nothing hangs on the hook by the study door.".
  }
  Item key "the steward's iron key" is cell_key in key_hook owned by venn.
  Rule venn_sleeps when dark() and state(key_hook, worn) and not lends(venn, key, ?c) { Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  Rule venn_wakes when not dark() and state(key_hook, hung) and not lends(venn, key, ?c) and inside(key, key_hook) { Assert state(key_hook, worn). }
  // The hook says what hangs on it: once the key is gone, nothing does.
  Rule hook_emptied when state(key_hook, hung) and not inside(key, key_hook) { Assert state(key_hook, empty). }
  Rule hook_filled when state(key_hook, empty) and inside(key, key_hook) { Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  Discovery ledger_known "Venn's ledger: twelve bronze teeth sold to Cass Rowell of the barge Heron this year, at eight crowns the tooth, against a debt of sixty crowns, with more to come." {
    Source ledger "the steward's ledger" at study readable by party.
    Known by venn.
  }
  Discovery cellar_known "Behind a barrel in the Hall cellar, a door has been set into a hole broken through the old grey wall, into the inside of the Long Man." {
    Found by searching cellar "Behind the last barrel the old wall has been broken through, and a heavy new door set into the hole. Cold, dry air comes round its edges.".
    Found by searching gallery "Low in the gallery wall an old breach has been fitted with a heavy new door. It does not give: it is barred from the other side.".
    Known by venn, dunnet.
  }

  // Venn hides the bronze in the cellar at nightfall on the first day, and loads it onto the barge when it comes.
  Rule teeth_hidden when watch(clock) >= 60 and inside(teeth, cart) { Retract inside(teeth, cart). Assert inside(teeth, cellar_chest). }
  // Loaded, the teeth are Cass's: on her deck at the landing, hers to sell back, and gone downriver when she goes.
  Rule teeth_loaded when at(cass, landing) and inside(teeth, cellar_chest) { Retract inside(teeth, cellar_chest). Retract owns(venn, teeth). Assert at(teeth, landing). Assert aboard(teeth). }
  Relation aboard(item).
  Rule cass_wants when aboard(teeth) and at(teeth, landing) and not forSale(teeth) { Assert forSale(teeth). Assert soldBy(teeth, cass). Set price(teeth) to 12. }
  Rule teeth_sail when aboard(teeth) and at(teeth, landing) and at(cass, downriver) { Assert at(teeth, downriver). }
  // Told what the bronze held shut, Cass will not carry it: she leaves it on the landing and has the Hall's plate instead.
  Topic cass_weir with cass "Tell Cass Rowell what the bronze was holding shut" when knows(actor, wall_known) and knows(actor, teeth_taken) and aboard(teeth) {
    Says "Cass hears you out without a word, looking past you at the hill. 'My father was under a weir on the Lune when it went,' she says. 'I'll not carry one downriver in a sack.' She whistles, and one of her hands sets the sack down on the landing stones. 'The steward owes me sixty crowns. I'll have them in silver before dusk, or I'll have his plate.'".
    On discuss { Retract aboard(teeth). Retract forSale(teeth). Retract soldBy(teeth, cass). Assert dunned(venn). }
  }
  Relation dunned(group). Relation ruined(group).
  Rule venn_ruined when dunned(venn) and at(cass, downriver) and not ruined(venn) { Assert ruined(venn). }
  Observe study_stripped at study when ruined(venn) "The dresser by the fire is bare: the Hall's plate has gone downriver on the Heron.".
  // Cass drinks at the Ox for an hour while her hands load.
  Rule cass_drinks when watch(clock) >= 186 and watch(clock) < 192 and at(cass, landing) { Assert at(cass, taproom). }
  Rule cass_back when watch(clock) >= 192 and at(cass, taproom) { Assert at(cass, landing). }
  // The Ox's cellar is the lowest in Merrow but the mill's: when the low field goes under, Martin bails.
  Observe ox_bailing at taproom when drowned(low_field) and not drawn(hollow) and not broke(long_man) "Martin Pask is bailing his cellar by the bucket and swearing at the hill. 'Never in my life,' he says. 'Not once, not in a wet year.'".
  Observe cass_at_ox at taproom when at(cass, taproom) "Cass Rowell sits alone by the fire with her boots on the fender, reading a letter and moving her lips.".
  // Merrow's evenings are spent in the Ox, and its nights in its own beds.
  Rule folk_evening when dark() and untilLight(clock) > 42 and at(folk, green) and not storming() and not lostToWater(folk) { Assert at(folk, taproom). }
  Rule folk_bed when at(folk, taproom) and untilLight(clock) <= 42 { Assert at(folk, green). }
  Observe green_night at green when dark() and not drowned(green) "The green is dark. Somebody's dog barks once.".
  Observe ox_evening_first at taproom when at(folk, taproom) and watch(clock) < 144 "The taproom is full and loud. Everybody has an opinion about the steward's notice, and nobody means to go up the hill after dark to earn it.".
  Observe ox_evening_second at taproom when at(folk, taproom) and watch(clock) >= 144 "The talk in the Ox is of the barge, and of the low field, where Ned Rook went in over his boots this afternoon by the springs, on ground that was dry at Lammas.".
  // Hob walks up to the springs at dusk with his spade, and stands looking at the water.
  Rule hob_walks when dark() and untilLight(clock) > 48 and at(hob, millhouse) and not confessed(hob) { Assert at(hob, springs). }
  Rule hob_home when at(hob, springs) and untilLight(clock) <= 48 { Assert at(hob, millhouse). }
  Observe hob_watching at springs when at(hob, springs) "Hob Teller stands at the springs in the dusk with a spade over his shoulder, looking at the water as a man looks at a debt.".


  // Dunnet hurt: an arm bound properly buys what wages would.
  Observe dunnet_sling at yard when hurt(dunnet) and at(dunnet, yard) "Dunnet sits on the mounting-block with his arm in a sling of sacking and his jaw set.".
  Event dunnet_bound near dunnet when keeps(dunnet, ?b) and itemKind(?b, bandages) and hurt(dunnet) "Dunnet lets you set the arm and bind it, and only swears once. 'The bar comes off the cellar door at dark,' he says. 'For you. Not for him.'" then {
    Retract hurt(dunnet). Assert promisedDoor(dunnet). Retract serves(dunnet, venn).
  }
  // Pell's lantern brought back: Dunnet tells it all, and then tells Mother Ysolt.
  Event pell_told near dunnet when keeps(dunnet, lantern) "Dunnet turns the lantern over and over in his hands and wipes the glass with his thumb. 'Pell's,' he says. 'The steward told them Pell went down the river in the spring. He never. The clay stood up and took him while we had the teeth out, and I ran.' He gets up. 'I'm going to tell Mother Ysolt. Then they can all know.'" then {
    Assert confessedPell(dunnet). Retract serves(dunnet, venn).
  }
  Relation confessedPell(group). Relation pellKnown().
  // He goes down to the chapel at dusk, and by morning the whole parish has it.
  Rule dunnet_to_chapel when confessedPell(dunnet) and dark() and at(dunnet, yard) { Assert at(dunnet, nave). }
  Rule pell_known when confessedPell(dunnet) and at(dunnet, nave) and not pellKnown() { Assert pellKnown(). Assert exposed(venn). }
  Observe dunnet_at_chapel at nave when at(dunnet, nave) "Dunnet sits on the bench by the font with Pell's lantern on his knees.".
  Observe pell_mourned at green when pellKnown() and at(folk, green) and not dark() "At the well they are talking low about Pell, and nobody says the steward's name, and everyone means it.".
  // Dunnet is owed his wages, and is frightened of what is behind the cellar door.
  Relation promisedDoor(group).
  Topic dunnet_fear with dunnet "Ask Dunnet about the Mower" when true once {
    Says "Dunnet looks at the hill. 'It's not the Mower I mind,' he says. 'It's what's in the wet tunnel. It stood up out of the floor at Pell and me, all mud, and came after us. I'm not going back through that door, not for the steward, not for anyone.'".
  }
  Topic dunnet_door with dunnet "Ask Dunnet what is behind the cellar door" when knows(actor, cellar_known) or state(cellar_door, barred) {
    Says "'The inside of the Long Man,' says Dunnet. 'Tunnels, dry as a church, all that grey stone. And the wheels. We had the teeth out of the big wheel in the wet tunnel, twelve of them, before the mud stood up.' He looks at his boots. 'The steward keeps it barred now.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, cellar_known). }
  }
  Action pay_dunnet(actor: group, site: place) "Give Dunnet three coin toward the wages he is owed" {
    Description "He is owed three months, and the steward will not pay.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(dunnet, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3
      and not promisedDoor(dunnet).
    On success {
      Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Increase quantity(dunnet, gold) by 3. Assert promisedDoor(dunnet).
      Retract serves(dunnet, venn).
    }
    Result "Dunnet counts the coins twice. 'The steward sleeps after supper,' he says, low. 'The bar comes off the cellar door at dark, and goes back on at cockcrow. That's all. I never saw you.'".
  }
  // Dunnet takes the bar off at dark and puts it back at cockcrow; a bar the company lifted itself is its own affair.
  Rule door_unbarred when promisedDoor(dunnet) and dark() and state(cellar_door, barred) { Assert state(cellar_door, unbarred). Assert dunnetsBar(cellar_door). }
  Rule door_rebarred when dunnetsBar(cellar_door) and not dark() and state(cellar_door, unbarred) and not at(party, cellar) { Assert state(cellar_door, barred). Retract dunnetsBar(cellar_door). }
  Relation dunnetsBar(entity).

  // Venn: what he says, and what he pays.
  Topic venn_bounty with venn "Ask Aldous Venn about the Mower" when not exposed(venn) and not hostile(venn, actor) {
    Says "'The Mower,' says Venn, and smiles as if it were a joke between gentlemen. 'The Long Man's ghost. It walks the crest at night and frightens the parish, and now it has taken to coming down into my yard. Forty crowns, and you may keep the mask it wears to show for it; Mother Ysolt will want to bury it.' He unhooks a big iron key from his belt and hangs it by the door. 'It lies up inside the hill by day, the men say. That key opens the grate at the Hollow Door.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bounty_known). Assert lends(venn, key, actor). Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  }
  Topic venn_bronze with venn "Ask Aldous Venn what was in the cart" when knows(actor, ledger_known) and not exposed(venn) and not hostile(venn, actor) {
    Says "Venn's smile stays where it is, but his eyes go to the ledgers. 'Old metal,' he says. 'Lumber from the Long Folk's mill under the hill. The estate has debts, and the hill is the estate's.' He spreads his hands. 'Nobody in Merrow ever had a use for it.'".
  }
  // Shown his own ledger beside what the bronze held shut, he gives up the key, and then the dale.
  Topic venn_shown with venn "Show Aldous Venn his own ledger, and tell him what the bronze held shut" when knows(actor, ledger_known) and knows(actor, teeth_taken) and not exposed(venn) {
    Says "Venn reads his own hand as if a stranger had written it. 'A sluice,' he says. 'Old metal off a sluice.' He sits down. 'Sixty crowns, and a letter from the Lord every week asking where they are.' He unhooks the iron key from his belt and hangs it by the door, and does not look at it. 'Take it. Do what you like with the hill.' When you go out he is writing, fast, to Cass Rowell.".
    On discuss { Assert exposed(venn). Assert lends(venn, key, actor). Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  }
  Relation exposed(group).
  Rule venn_flees when exposed(venn) and at(cass, landing) and able(venn) and not at(venn, landing) and not at(venn, downriver) { Assert at(venn, landing). }
  Rule venn_sails when exposed(venn) and at(venn, landing) and at(cass, downriver) { Assert at(venn, downriver). }
  Observe venn_waits at landing when exposed(venn) and at(venn, landing) "Aldous Venn sits on the Heron's hatch with a valise on his knees, and does not look up at the hill.".
  Action claim_bounty(actor: group, carrier: member, face: item, site: place) "Show Aldous Venn {face}" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(venn, site) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and ownedItem(face, carrier) and itemKind(face, keeper_mask) and not paidBounty(venn).
    On success { Decrease quantity(venn, gold) by 40. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 40. Assert paidBounty(venn). }
    Result "Venn turns the grey face over in his hands, and for a moment he looks old. Then he counts out forty crowns, most of them in silver he has clearly borrowed. 'Merrow will sleep tonight,' he says.".
  }
  Relation paidBounty(group).
  Initially Set quantity(venn, gold) to 40.

  // Mother Ysolt and the font.
  Topic ysolt_mower with ysolt "Ask Mother Ysolt about the Mower" when not convinced(ysolt) {
    Says "'The Long Man is restless,' says Mother Ysolt. 'He was a king, and a cruel one; the font is his tally, a notch for every sin, and the parish has prayed him down for two hundred years. Now he walks again. Bring me his mask and I will put it in the ground with the proper words, and he will lie still.'".
  }
  Relation convinced(group).
  Topic ysolt_notches with ysolt "Tell Mother Ysolt what the notches on the font are" when knows(actor, notches_known) and not convinced(ysolt) {
    Says "Mother Ysolt stands a long time at the font with her hand flat on the stone, looking up at the highest notch and the roof-beam beside it. 'The chapel step,' she says at last. 'The register says the water came to the chapel step.' She turns. 'If it comes again, it will not stop at the step. I will ring the bell, and Merrow will go up the hill to the Hall, and the steward can say what he likes.'".
    On discuss { Assert convinced(ysolt). }
  }
  Discovery wept_known "The parish register, two hundred years back: 'In the year the Long Man wept, the water came over the low field to the chapel step. The Mower walked by day as well as night, and in seven days the water went back. The lord's men had dug into the Barrow for its gold.'" {
    Source register "the parish register" at vestry readable by party.
    Known by ysolt.
  }

  // Hob Teller and the springs.
  Topic hob_springs with hob "Ask Hob Teller about the springs" when not confessed(hob) {
    Says "'Blessed springs,' says Hob. 'My father's wheel stood still every dry summer. This one turns day and night.' He does not look toward the hill.".
  }
  Relation confessed(group).
  Topic hob_cuts with hob "Show Hob Teller the spade-cuts at the springs" when knows(actor, cuts_known) and not confessed(hob) {
    Says "Hob goes white, then red. 'It was the drought,' he says. 'A few spits with the spade, in the spring, to let them run. They've run harder every week since.' He looks at his mill, the lowest house in Merrow. 'I'll stake them and clay them over tomorrow, before light. God help me, I'll do it.'".
    On discuss { Assert confessed(hob). }
  }
  Rule hob_staunches when confessed(hob) and state(cuts, open) and untilLight(clock) == 1 { Assert state(cuts, staunched). }
  Thing cuts "the cuts at the springs" at springs {
    State open "The springs pour out of the turf, cold and clear, more water than a few springs ought to give.".
    State staunched "The cuts at the springs have been staked and packed with clay. The water seeps instead of pouring.".
    Change staunch "Stake the spade-cuts and pack them with clay" from open to staunched needing digging or shovel after learning cuts_known.
  }
  Discovery cuts_known "Someone has cut the Weeping Springs wider with a spade, this year: the edges are still square." {
    Found by searching springs "Under the water the turf is cut in clean square bites, too regular for water to have made. A spade did this, not long ago.".
  }

  // Gammer Coller and her rod.
  Topic nell_rhyme with nell "Ask Gammer Coller about the Mower" when true once {
    Says "'There's a rhyme,' says Gammer Coller. 'When the Mower walks the crown, keep the willow-roots cut down. When the Mower walks the green, the water's coming in between. When the Mower walks by day, Merrow, take your bed away.' She pokes the fire. 'It's been walking the green this month. Nobody asked me.'".
  }
  Topic nell_rod with nell "Ask Gammer Coller about the rod by her door" when true once {
    Says "'The dyke-reeve's rod,' she says, and takes it down: black wood, with notched bronze on both ends. 'Every reeve has had it since there were reeves. You measure a ditch with it.' She runs her thumb along the notches. 'Not that the notches match any measure I know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, rod_seen). }
  }
  Topic nell_lend with nell "Ask Gammer Coller for the loan of her rod" when knows(actor, mower_keeps) and at(rod, reeve_room) {
    Says "She listens without a word while you tell her what the Mower does. Then she lays the rod on the table. 'I always thought it walked like a reeve,' she says. 'Bring it back.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(nell, rod, actor). }
  }
  Item rod "the dyke-reeve's rod" is sluice_rod at reeve_room hidden until rod_seen owned by nell.
  Discovery rod_seen "Gammer Coller keeps an old rod shod in notched bronze, the dyke-reeve's rod, by her door.".

  // Cass Rowell's barge, the Heron: up the beck at noon on the second day, away at dusk.
  Person cass "Cass Rowell" at downriver {
    Role "master of the barge Heron". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 3. Peaceable.
    Buys bell_teeth for 8 coin.
  }
  Person hands "the Heron's hands" at downriver {
    Role "bargemen". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 2.
  }
  Initially Assert serves(hands, cass). Initially Set quantity(cass, gold) to 60.
  Thing hold "the Heron's hold" at downriver {
    Holds.
  }
  Rule cass_comes when watch(clock) >= 168 and watch(clock) < 204 and at(cass, downriver) { Assert at(cass, landing). Assert at(hands, landing). Assert at(hold, landing). }
  Rule cass_goes when watch(clock) >= 204 and at(cass, landing) and able(cass) { Assert at(cass, downriver). Assert at(hands, downriver). Assert at(hold, downriver). }
  Observe heron_scene at landing when at(cass, landing) "The barge Heron lies at the landing, low in the water, with a brown sail furled and two bargemen sitting on the hatch.".
  Topic cass_trade with cass "Ask Cass Rowell what she is carrying" when true once {
    Says "'Whatever pays,' says Cass. 'Wool down, iron up. Bronze, when the steward has it. He owes me sixty crowns and pays me in old teeth.' She looks you over. 'If you've teeth to sell, I buy at eight. If you want them back, they cost twelve. That's trade.'".
  }

  // The steward's grate, and the key that opens it.
  Thing grate "the iron grate" on culvert {
    State locked blocking "The iron grate is locked with a padlock the size of a loaf.".
    State open "The iron grate stands open on its hinges.".
    Change unlock "Unlock the grate with the steward's key" from locked to open needing key.
  }
  Initially Assert keyholder(venn, grate).
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/placed.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  // The dale as a country beyond a march: the company that comes up the south road is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/wall.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "The Long Man: the crest a figure walks at night, and the grey galleries inside the hill.".

  Place inside "the galleries" is level within long_man.
  Place crest "the crest of the Long Man" is room within long_man at 1, 0.
  Place gauge_head "the gauge stone" is room within long_man at 2, 0.
  Place gallery "the grey gallery" is room within inside at 1, 1.
  Place sluice "the sluice chamber" is room within inside at 2, 2.
  Place rest "the keeper's niche" is room within inside at 0, 1.
  Place leak "the wet gallery" is room within inside at 1, 2.
  Place shaft_foot "the foot of the gauge shaft" is room within inside at 2, 1.
  // The clay core, where what the leak made of the clay goes when the leak is shut.
  Place core "the clay core" is room within inside at 0, 2.
  Initially Assert unlit(gallery). Initially Assert unlit(sluice). Initially Assert unlit(rest). Initially Assert unlit(leak).
  Initially Assert unlit(shaft_foot).

  Passage crest_steps "the steps up the Long Man" is steps between yard and crest taking 20 minutes.
  Passage valley_face "the valley face" is path between crest and springs taking 20 minutes.
  Passage crest_walk "the crest" is path between crest and gauge_head taking 10 minutes.
  Passage culvert "the culvert" is culvert between hollow_door and sluice taking 10 minutes.
  Passage broken_wall "the broken wall" is doorway between cellar and gallery hidden until cellar_known.
  Passage sluice_way "the sluice passage" is passage between gallery and sluice.
  Passage niche_way "the keeper's passage" is passage between gallery and rest.
  Passage wet_way "the wet passage" is passage between gallery and leak.
  Passage shaft_way "the shaft passage" is passage between gallery and shaft_foot.
  Passage gauge_shaft "the gauge shaft" is shaft between shaft_foot and gauge_head taking 30 minutes needing climbing or rope.
  Passage sinkhole "the sinkhole" is climb between crest and leak taking 20 minutes needing rope.

  // The bar is on the cellar side: only someone in the cellar can lift it.
  Thing cellar_door "the door in the broken wall" on broken_wall {
    State barred blocking "A heavy door closes the hole broken through the wall, barred on the cellar side.".
    State unbarred "The bar is off the door in the broken wall, and it stands a hand's width open on the dark.".
    Change lift "Lift the oak bar off the door in the broken wall" from barred to unbarred at cellar.
  }
  Initially Assert keyholder(venn, cellar_door).
  // Shut in behind a barred door, a company can always make itself heard: at a price.
  Action hammer_door(actor: group, site: place) "Hammer on the door until someone in the cellar hears" {
    Description "Somebody will come in the end. Everybody at the Hall will know who it was.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gallery) and state(cellar_door, barred)
      and knows(actor, cellar_known).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert state(cellar_door, unbarred). Assert hostile(venn, actor). }
    Result "You hammer on the oak until your hands ache. At last the bar scrapes off its brackets, and Dunnet's face looks in at you, white. 'The steward will hear of this,' he says, and he is right.".
  }

  Observe crest_scene at crest when not dark() "The crest of the Long Man is a dead-level walk of turf, wide as a lane. On one hand the dale falls away to Merrow's roofs; on the other, a long way down, lies Hollow Water, black and still, filling the valley to the hills. Nothing grows on the crest higher than a hand: every sapling has been cut off at the root, clean.".
  Observe crest_night at crest when dark() "By night the crest is a pale road between two darks: the dale's, with a few lights in it, and the lake's, with none.".
  Observe sinkhole_scene at crest when true "Halfway along, the turf has fallen into a raw hole a cart wide. Water drips somewhere far down in it.".
  Observe gauge_scene at gauge_head when true "At the north end of the crest a square grey stone stands over a square shaft going down into the hill. Notches are cut down every edge of the shaft, deeper than the light goes.".
  Observe gallery_scene at gallery when true "A tunnel lined with smooth grey stone, tall and narrow, as if cut for something taller than a man. The air is dry and still. Ways go off to either hand.".
  Observe sluice_scene at sluice when true "A chamber over the culvert, where the beck runs loud below an iron grating. Two great wheels of grey stone stand on their edges, set round with teeth of green bronze, and a third, smaller, works the shutter of the bottom sluice.".
  Observe rest_scene at rest when true "A niche in the gallery wall, taller than two men, with a ledge of grey stone at the back and tools laid on it in order: blades, hooks, a stone trowel, all of the same grey. Notches run in close rows up the walls.".
  Observe leak_scene at leak when not state(leak_gate, mended) "Water comes through a crack in the inner face of the gallery, a sheet of it, and runs away under the floor.".
  Observe leak_mended at leak when state(leak_gate, mended) "The wall of the gallery is wet, and no more.".
  Observe shaft_scene at shaft_foot when true "The bottom of a square shaft. Notches climb its four edges up into the dark, and the stone of the shaft-side toward the lake sweats.".

  // The Mower: it stands in its niche by day and walks the crest by night, and goes after its bronze.
  Person mower "the Mower" at rest {
    Role "the tall grey figure that walks the Long Man". Species automaton. Level 12.
    Wants bell_teeth.
  }
  Rule mower_rises when dark() and at(mower, rest) and able(mower) and not hunting(mower) { Assert at(mower, crest). }
  Rule mower_returns when not dark() and not at(mower, rest) and able(mower) { Assert at(mower, rest). Retract hunting(mower). }
  Relation hunting(group).
  // At midnight on the first night it comes down for the bronze that was in the cart, and finds the cart empty.
  Rule mower_hunts at yard when dark() and watch(clock) >= 96 and watch(clock) < 132 and state(cart, covered) and able(mower)
    says "Something tall comes over the yard wall without climbing it. The Mower goes to the cart, tears the tarpaulin away, finds nothing, and turns the cart over as if it were a barrow. A shaft flies. Dunnet, who came out with a lantern, goes down with a cry." {
    Assert state(cart, smashed). Assert hunting(mower). Assert at(mower, yard). Assert hurt(dunnet).
  }
  Relation hurt(group).
  Observe mower_crest at crest when dark() and at(mower, crest) "The Mower walks the crest, slowly, the length of it and back. Every few paces it stoops, and a long blade flicks, and something small falls." teaches mower_keeps.
  Observe count_matched at rest when knows(party, last_count) "The last row of notches on the niche wall is a count of days, and it stops at forty-one.".
  Observe mower_resting at rest when at(mower, rest) and able(mower) "The Mower stands in its niche: a figure taller than two men, grey and too smooth, with its long arms at its sides and a face like a blank mask. It does not move. On its breastplate, in the light, a row of notches." .
  Observe mower_yard at yard when at(mower, yard) "The Mower stands in the yard by the overturned cart, its blank face turned toward the cellar." .
  Discovery keeper_named "The notches on the Mower's breastplate, read: KEEPER OF THE WALL." {
    Found by searching rest with lore "The notches on the Mower's breastplate are writing, the same writing as on the walls. It says, as near as it can be read: KEEPER OF THE WALL.".
  }
  Discovery mower_keeps "The Mower keeps the Long Man: it cuts every sapling on the crest before its roots can crack the wall, and it goes after bronze taken from its wheels.".
  // Given back its bronze, it fits the teeth to the leak gate's wheel that night, and closes the gate.
  Event mower_mends near mower when keeps(mower, teeth) and not state(leak_gate, mended) "The Mower takes the sack of teeth in both hands, turns, and walks away into the hill. Some time later, deep inside the Long Man, something heavy closes with a sound like a bell." then {
    Assert state(leak_gate, mended).
  }
  Item mask "the Mower's mask" is keeper_mask at core.
  Rule mower_falls when dead(mower) and at(mower, ?p) and at(mask, core) { Assert at(mask, ?p). }
  // By day it stands still in its niche, and its face is a mask that a bar can lever off. That lays it, as Venn wants
  // and Ysolt prays for; and then nobody keeps the wall.
  Hazard unmasking "The mask levered off" means "Kill ally.".
  Action unmask_mower(actor: group, site: place) "Get the bar under the Mower's face and lever it off" {
    Description "By day it does not move. Whatever it is, its face is a mask, and a mask comes off.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mower, site) and at(mower, rest) and able(mower)
      and not dark() and holding(actor, crowbar) and not benighted(actor).
    On success { Assert strikes(unmasking, mower). Retract at(mask, core). Assert at(mask, rest). }
    Result "The bar goes in under the grey chin, and you lean on it. The mask comes away with a sound like a cracked bell, and the Mower folds down onto its ledge like a dropped coat, and is still.".
  }

  // The leak gate, and what the leak has made of the clay.
  Thing leak_gate "the bronze shutter" at leak {
    State jammed "A shutter of bronze teeth hangs half across the crack, on a wheel with twelve empty sockets.".
    State fitted "The bronze teeth are back in the shutter's wheel; it hangs open, ready to be turned.".
    State mended "The bronze shutter is closed across the crack, every socket of its wheel filled.".
    Change heave "Heave the shutter's wheel round and close it" from fitted to mended needing brawn.
  }
  Action fit_teeth(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Fit the bell-teeth back into the shutter's wheel" {
    Description "Twelve sockets, twelve teeth. They go in with a sound like a bell.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(leak_gate, site) and state(leak_gate, jammed)
      and memberOf(carrier, actor) and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(teeth, carrier).
    Time 6.
    Resolve drop(teeth, carrier).
    On success { Assert at(teeth, core). Assert state(leak_gate, fitted). }
    Result "One by one the teeth go into their sockets, and each one rings as it seats. When the twelfth is in, the wheel turns a finger's width under your hand.".
  }
  Person wet "the Wet" at leak {
    Role "a heaving mass of wet clay". Species slump. Level 5.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "At the far end of the wet gallery the floor heaves, and a shape stands up out of the clay, streaming, as tall as a door.".
    Comes "The Wet comes down the gallery at you, faster than mud should.".
  }
  // What the Wet took: the man who went in with Dunnet for the teeth.
  Item lantern "a miner's lantern" is tin_lantern at leak.
  Observe pell_seen at leak when at(lantern, leak) "At the far end of the gallery, half sunk in the clay, a man's lantern lies on its side, its glass packed with mud.".
  Rule wet_slumps at leak when state(leak_gate, mended) and at(wet, leak) says "The Wet sags, and sags, and is a heap of clay on the floor, and then is only floor." { Assert at(wet, core). }

  // The sluice: the bottom gate under the chamber. Opened, it fills the culvert and runs the beck high.
  Thing bottom_sluice "the bottom sluice" at sluice {
    State shut "The small wheel is turned home; the bottom sluice is shut.".
    State open dangerous "The small wheel is turned out, and below the grating the water roars.".
    Change open_it "Turn the small wheel and open the bottom sluice" from shut to open needing brawn.
    Change shut_it "Turn the small wheel home and shut the bottom sluice" from open to shut needing brawn.
  }
  Thing culvert_water "the water in the culvert" on culvert is scenery {
    State low "The beck runs ankle-deep along the culvert floor.".
    State high blocking dangerous "The culvert is full to the roof with fast brown water.".
  }
  Rule culvert_fills when state(bottom_sluice, open) and state(culvert_water, low) says "Somewhere below, the water changes its voice." { Assert state(culvert_water, high). }
  Rule culvert_drains when state(bottom_sluice, shut) and state(culvert_water, high) { Assert state(culvert_water, low). }
  Rule mower_guards_sluice when state(bottom_sluice, open) and together(mower, party) and able(mower) says "The Mower turns its blank face toward the open sluice, and then toward you." { Assert assails(mower, party). }

  // The gauge shaft and its notches.
  Discovery notches_known "The notches on the font are water heights, like the notches down the gauge shaft: the same cuts, the same spacing. The highest notch on the font is level with the chapel's roof-beam." {
    Source shaft_notches "the notches down the gauge shaft" at shaft_foot readable by party.
  }
  Discovery wall_known "The Long Man is a wall: it holds Hollow Water back from the dale, and the beck comes through it by a culvert.".
  Observe sluice_teaches at sluice when true "Above the grating the wheels and the culvert make plain what the Long Man is: not a barrow, a wall, with a lake behind it and a sluice through it." teaches wall_known.
  Observe teeth_missing at leak when not state(leak_gate, mended) "Fresh bright scars on the stone by the crack show where a bar has been used, and lately." teaches teeth_taken.
  Discovery teeth_taken "Twelve bronze teeth have been prised out of the wheel of the shutter that should close the leak in the Long Man.".

  // The storm comes on the third day; two hours after midnight the Long Man breaks, unless its leak is shut or the
  // lake is drawn down.
  Relation storming(). Relation broke(place). Relation drowned(place). Relation drawn(place).
  Rule storm_comes when watch(clock) >= 312 and not storming() and not calm(long_man) says "The wind goes round to the north, and the rain comes in over the fell in grey ropes." { Assert storming(). }
  Observe storm_scene at crest when storming() "Rain drives across the crest. Hollow Water has come up the lake face of the Long Man, grey and heaving, nearer than it was.".
  Rule field_wets when watch(clock) >= 240 and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drowned(low_field) { Assert drowned(low_field). }
  Rule long_man_breaks when watch(clock) >= 396 and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drawn(hollow) and not broke(long_man)
    says "In the dark, under the noise of the rain, there is another noise, very deep, like a wall falling a long way off. Then the sound of water." {
    Assert broke(long_man). Assert drowned(low_field). Assert drowned(green).
  }
  Hazard flood_waters "The flood" means "Deal (4d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Rule flood_takes when broke(long_man) and (at(party, green) or at(party, low_field) or at(party, landing) or at(party, millhouse) or at(party, nave) or at(party, taproom) or at(party, hollow_door) or at(party, springs))
    and not swept(party) { Assert strikes(flood_waters, party). Assert swept(party). }
  Relation swept(group).
  // Merrow on the hill, if Mother Ysolt rang the bell; otherwise Merrow in the low town when the water came.
  Rule bell_rung at green when storming() and convinced(ysolt) and at(folk, green)
    says "The chapel bell rings and rings, and doors open all over Merrow, and people go up the Hall lane in the rain with what they can carry." {
    Assert at(folk, yard). Assert at(ysolt, yard).
  }
  Relation lostToWater(group).
  Rule folk_lost when broke(long_man) and (at(folk, green) or at(folk, taproom)) { Assert lostToWater(folk). Assert at(folk, core). }
  Observe folk_saved at yard when at(folk, yard) and broke(long_man) "Merrow stands in the Hall yard in the rain, and looks down the lane at where it lived.".
  // The morning after the third night: the storm passes, and the dale is what the three days made it.
  Relation calm(place).
  Rule storm_passes when watch(clock) >= 432 and storming() says "The rain stops before dawn. The wind drops, and the dale lies under a washed, colourless sky." { Retract storming(). Assert calm(long_man). }
  Observe after_mended at green when calm(long_man) and not broke(long_man) and not drawn(hollow) "The beck runs brown but low between its banks, and nobody on the green is talking about the Long Man. The springs at its foot, people say, have nearly stopped.".
  Observe after_drawn at green when calm(long_man) and drawn(hollow) "Children stand on the dyke looking north, where the roofs of a grey town show above Hollow Water for the first time in a thousand years.".
  Observe after_broken at yard when calm(long_man) and broke(long_man) "Below the Hall the dale is one brown water from the ridge to the willows. The Long Man has a gap in it a hundred yards wide, and the lake is going out through it.".
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/water.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "Hollow Water: the lake behind the Long Man, the Water-House on its island, and the town under it.".

  Place lakeshore "the lakeshore" is room within hollow at 0, 1.
  Place deep "the deep water" is room within hollow at 1, 1.
  Place water_house "the Water-House" is room within hollow at 2, 0.
  Place drowned_street "the drowned street" is room within hollow at 2, 1.
  Place face_house "the face-house" is room within hollow at 3, 1.
  Place last_house "the last house" is room within hollow at 2, 2.

  Passage lake_face "the lake face of the Long Man" is path between crest and lakeshore taking 20 minutes.
  Passage punt_way "out on Hollow Water" is ferry between lakeshore and deep taking 30 minutes.
  Passage island_way "the island landing" is ferry between deep and water_house taking 30 minutes.
  Passage house_steps "the steps below the Water-House" is steps between water_house and drowned_street.
  Passage face_door "a tall narrow door" is doorway between drowned_street and face_house.
  Passage last_door "a barred door" is door between drowned_street and last_house.

  Thing punt "an old punt" on punt_way {
    State beached blocking "An old punt lies drawn up in the reeds, grey with weather, its pole across the thwarts.".
    State afloat "The punt rides at the edge of the reeds.".
    Change launch "Push the punt off the reeds" from beached to afloat needing brawn.
  }
  Thing steps_water "the water over the steps" on house_steps is scenery {
    State under blocking "Below the Water-House door, steps go down into the lake, and the lake closes over them.".
    State drawn "The steps go down from the Water-House door into a street of grey houses, wet and shining.".
  }

  Observe shore_scene at lakeshore when not drawn(hollow) "Reeds, and black water going away to the hills, so still it holds the sky. The cold comes off it like a cellar's. Far out, a square tower stands up out of the lake on an island no bigger than a barn.".
  Observe shore_drawn at lakeshore when drawn(hollow) "The lake has drawn back from the reeds a long stone's throw, leaving mud, and the stumps of trees older than any in the dale.".
  Observe deep_scene at deep when true "Out on the water the punt pole finds no bottom. The water is cold enough to ache, and too clear: far down, something pale, like a roof.".
  Observe house_scene at water_house when true "One room, square and tall, of the same grey stone as the Long Man. In the middle of the floor stands a wheel of grey stone on an axle as thick as a man, and round the walls, in rows from floor to ceiling, notches.".
  Observe socket_seen at water_house when knows(party, rod_seen) "In the hub of the great wheel is a socket, square, its edges notched in a close pattern: the pattern on the shoe of Gammer Coller's rod." teaches rod_fits.
  Observe street_scene at drowned_street when true "A street of houses of grey stone with their roofs on, silted to the sills and shining with water. The doors are tall and narrow, and over each one a short row of notches, a little higher or lower from door to door, as if each house had measured the water for itself.".
  Observe face_house_scene at face_house when true "A long low room with a kiln at the far end, its mouth stopped with clay. Shelves run the length of both walls, and on them stand moulds of grey clay, each the hollow of a long, smooth face with no eyes.".
  Discovery moulds_read "The keepers' faces were fired here in moulds and set on last. A keeper wakes when it is given its face, and stops when it loses it." {
    Found by searching face_house "In the last mould on the last shelf lies a face already fired: grey, smooth, blind, never fitted to anything. Round the mould's rim runs a count of days in notches, the time it took to make.".
  }
  Item spare_face "a grey face, fired and never fitted" is keeper_mask at face_house hidden until moulds_read.
  Thing last_bar "the bar across the last house's door" on last_door {
    State barred blocking "A bar of black oak lies across the door in iron brackets, on the street side.".
    State lifted "The oak bar leans against the wall beside the open door.".
    Change lift "Lift the bar from the door" from barred to lifted at drowned_street.
  }
  Observe last_house_scene at last_house when true "One room. A table is laid for four, with bowls, a jug, and bread gone to grey stone. Nothing has been moved but by the water.".
  Observe tally_seen at last_house when true "Down the door-post runs a tally of days, cut neat and even. It stops at forty-one." teaches last_count.
  Discovery last_count "The last house of the drowned town was barred from outside, with its table laid for a meal. The tally of days on its door-post stops at forty-one, the same count as the last notches in the keeper's niche. The Hesk meant to come back.".
  Thing toy_bell "a child's bell of weirstone" at last_house {
    State still "On the sill sits a child's toy, a little bell of grey weirstone no bigger than a fist.".
    Tries pushing.
  }
  Event bell_answered near toy_bell when tried(toy_bell, pushing) "It rings, clear and long. Far off, under the hill, something rings back, once." then {
    Assert rung(toy_bell).
  }
  Relation rung(entity).

  Discovery rod_fits "The square socket in the hub of the Water-House wheel is notched to the pattern of the dyke-reeve's rod: the rod is a key to it.".
  Discovery hesk_known "The words cut round the Water-House wall, read: WE GAVE THE LOW HOUSES TO THE WATER, SO THAT THE FIELDS WOULD BE DRY. WE WILL KEEP THE WALL AS WE KEPT THE HOUSES." {
    Found by searching water_house with lore "The notches round the walls are writing, the writing of the Mower's breastplate. Round and round the room, as near as it can be read: WE GAVE THE LOW HOUSES TO THE WATER, SO THAT THE FIELDS WOULD BE DRY. WE WILL KEEP THE WALL AS WE KEPT THE HOUSES.".
  }
  Discovery town_known "Under Hollow Water stands a town of the people who built the Long Man, drowned by its own builders.".
  Observe street_teaches at drowned_street when true "Whoever lived here walked out of these doors uphill, and let the water in after them." teaches town_known.

  // The master wheel: worked with the rod, it draws the lake down by a man's height in two hours.
  Thing wheel "the great wheel" at water_house {
    State set "The great wheel stands with its square socket uppermost.".
    State turned "The great wheel has been turned its full round; somewhere below, water is going out with a long sigh.".
    Change turn "Set the rod in the socket and turn the great wheel" from set to turned needing sluice_rod.
  }
  Measure drawsAt(place).
  Rule draw_begins when state(wheel, turned) and drawsAt(hollow) == 0 { Set drawsAt(hollow) to watch(clock). Increase drawsAt(hollow) by 12. }
  Rule lake_drawn when state(wheel, turned) and drawsAt(hollow) > 0 and watch(clock) >= drawsAt(hollow) and not drawn(hollow)
    says "Hollow Water goes down. It goes down the lake face of the Long Man a man's height, and the beck below the wall goes up the dale brown and roaring." {
    Assert drawn(hollow). Assert state(steps_water, drawn). Assert drowned(low_field). Assert drowned(millhouse).
  }
  Observe mill_drowned at millhouse when drowned(millhouse) "The beck has come in through the millhouse door. The wheel has stopped, jammed with branches, and Hob Teller is standing in his own millpond to the knees.".

  // The Old Jack keeps the deep water.
  Person jack "the Old Jack" at deep {
    Role "a pike as long as the punt". Species great_pike. Level 4.
    Temperament ambush.
    Warns "A shadow longer than the punt turns under the water, slowly, and comes up beneath you. It has seen you see it.".
    Comes "The water opens beside the punt, and the Old Jack comes up out of it with its mouth wide.".
  }

  // What the company is asked, and what it comes to see it must do.
  Objective lay_mower when knows(party, bounty_known) and not paidBounty(venn) and able(mower) and not knows(party, mower_keeps) "Aldous Venn will pay forty crowns for the Mower's mask.".
  Objective keep_wall when knows(party, teeth_taken) and knows(party, wall_known) and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drawn(hollow) and not broke(long_man) "The Long Man is leaking where its bronze was taken, and the storm is coming.".
  Objective warn_merrow when knows(party, notches_known) and not convinced(ysolt) and not broke(long_man) "If the Long Man goes, the water will come over the chapel roof. Someone should tell Mother Ysolt.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/clocks.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "Thrume: a salt town where people pay to sleep, a giants' hold on the ridge, a mountain that is a body, a city that farms dreams, a tomb built to kill, a palace in a sky a thousand years gone, and what lies under every sleep.".

  // The country. The fells are the titan's body; everything but the dream and the Between is inside them or on them.
  Place fells "the Thrume country" is region.
  Place lowroad "the salt road" is wilderness within fells at 0, 3.
  Place saltgrave "Saltgrave" is settlement within fells at 1, 3.
  Place fellside "the fellside" is wilderness within fells at 1, 2.

  // Three clocks run under everything.
  // Thrume's stirring: two now; one more each morning the Margravine's overseer cuts; at six the ground shakes, at
  // ten he wakes.
  Measure stirring(place). Measure nextCut(place). Relation woken(place). Relation shaken(place).
  Initially Set stirring(fells) to 2. Initially Set nextCut(fells) to 144.
  Rule cut_stirs when cutting(brannoc) and watch(clock) >= nextCut(fells) and not woken(fells) {
    Increase stirring(fells) by 1. Set nextCut(fells) to nextCut(fells) + 144.
  }
  Rule ground_shakes when stirring(fells) >= 6 and not shaken(fells)
    says "The ground moves. Not a tremor: a slow, enormous shifting, like a sleeper turning over. Dust comes down from every roof-beam in the country, and then it is still." {
    Assert shaken(fells).
  }
  Rule thrume_wakes when stirring(fells) >= 10 and not woken(fells) and not sealed(fells) and not sungClean(fells)
    says "Thrume wakes. There is a sound under everything, deeper than sound, and then the fells stand up. Rivers run backwards off their shoulders. Somewhere to the south, where the Ebb is, the land is lifted and set down again in another place." {
    Assert woken(fells).
  }

  // Thrume's breath: an hour in, an hour out, for ever. The Lungs, the Room of Three Breaths and the cloud-stair keep
  // its time.
  Relation exhaling(place). Measure nextBreath(place).
  Initially Assert exhaling(fells). Initially Set nextBreath(fells) to 6.
  Rule breath_in when exhaling(fells) and watch(clock) >= nextBreath(fells) { Retract exhaling(fells). Set nextBreath(fells) to watch(clock) + 6. }
  Rule breath_out when not exhaling(fells) and watch(clock) >= nextBreath(fells) { Assert exhaling(fells). Set nextBreath(fells) to watch(clock) + 6. }

  // The host of Harle crosses the Ebb at the start of the tenth day. What stands on the Shoulder road that morning is
  // what the company left there.
  Relation crossed(place).
  Rule harle_crosses when watch(clock) >= 1296 and not crossed(fells) says "Word comes up the salt road at a gallop: the Duke of Harle's host is over the Ebb." { Assert crossed(fells). }

  // How it ends. These hold for ever once true; the epilogue observations below read them.
  Relation sealed(place). Relation sungClean(place). Relation cutOut(place).
  Observe end_woken at market when woken(fells) "Saltgrave is gone. Where the town was, a slope of new scree runs down into a valley that was not there yesterday, and the fells to the north are not where they were. Something vast is walking away into the west, taking its time.".
  Observe end_sung at market when sungClean(fells) and not woken(fells) "The fells are quiet, the right kind of quiet. The red salt in the Salt Office's cellar has gone grey and crumbles at a touch. People who never slept well in Saltgrave sleep now.".
  Observe end_sealed at market when sealed(fells) and not sungClean(fells) "The fells are still. Nobody in Saltgrave sleeps well, and nobody can say why, and the dream-houses stay shut.".
  Observe end_cut at market when cutOut(fells) "The Salt Office is loading wagons of red salt for the river, under guard, day and night. The springs above the town are running low, though it has rained.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/company.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Company party "Your company" of 3 at salt_road.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 30. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 3.
}

data/adventures/thrume/hush.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "Hush: the city of the Quiet Court, grown in the hollow of the titan's skull, where nobody speaks aloud.".

  Place hushc "Hush" is settlement within fells at 2, 0.
  Place lull_house "House Lull" is building within hushc.
  Place pallor_house "House Pallor" is building within hushc.
  Place spire "the Abbess's spire" is building within hushc.
  Place grey_library "the Silent Library" is building within hushc.

  Place hush_gate "the gate of Hush" is room within hushc at 0, 1.
  Place hand_street "the Street of Hands" is room within hushc at 1, 1.
  Place thrall_market "the Thrall-Market" is room within hushc at 1, 2.
  Place lull_hall "the hall of House Lull" is room within lull_house at 2, 2.
  Place pallor_hall "the hall of House Pallor" is room within pallor_house at 0, 2.
  Place library_hall "the Silent Library" is room within grey_library at 0, 0.
  Place choir "the Choir" is room within hushc at 2, 1.
  Place spire_foot "the foot of the spire" is room within spire at 1, 0.
  Place spire_top "the Abbess's room" is room within spire at 2, 0.
  Place throat_head "the head of the long throat" is room within hushc at 3, 1.

  Passage hush_in "the gate of Hush" is arch between hush_approach and hush_gate taking 10 minutes.
  Passage hand_way "the Street of Hands" is path between hush_gate and hand_street taking 10 minutes.
  Passage market_way "the market steps" is path between hand_street and thrall_market taking 10 minutes.
  Passage lull_door "the door of House Lull" is door between thrall_market and lull_hall.
  Passage pallor_door "the door of House Pallor" is door between thrall_market and pallor_hall.
  Passage library_door "the library door" is door between hand_street and library_hall.
  Passage choir_way "the choir walk" is path between hand_street and choir taking 10 minutes.
  Passage spire_door "the spire door" is door between choir and spire_foot.
  Passage spire_stair "the spire stair" is steps between spire_foot and spire_top taking 10 minutes.
  Passage throat_way "the far street" is path between choir and throat_head taking 20 minutes.

  Observe hgate_scene at hush_gate when true "A city of grey stone grown rather than built, like coral, under a roof of bone so high it might be sky. Grey light comes from nowhere. There is no sound at all. People move in the streets, tall and soft-faced, and talk to each other with their long hands.".
  Observe street_scene at hand_street when true "The Street of Hands. The Court's people pass you without looking, their fingers moving. Here and there a human thrall walks behind one of them, eyes still and smiling, carrying something.".
  Observe tmarket_scene at thrall_market when true "A square of niches cut in the grey stone, like a dovecote for people. In each niche someone sleeps, propped up, with a crust of red salt on their lips. Their eyes are moving. Some of the Court stand before the niches with their faces very close to the sleepers' faces, not touching, and the sleepers' faces go slack, and the Court's faces grow pink.".
  Observe lull_scene at lull_hall when true "A soft room, warm, hung with grey stuffs that drink the light. It smells of milk and sleep. The people of House Lull lie on low couches like cats.".
  Observe pallor_scene at pallor_hall when true "A hard bright room. Spears of grey crystal racked on the walls. On a table, a sleeper is laid out, and he is having a nightmare, and three of House Pallor are standing over him, very close.".
  Observe glibrary_scene at library_hall when true "Shelves of grey scrolls, and the readers read them with their fingertips, eyes shut.".
  Observe choir_scene at choir when exhaling(fells) "The Choir: a round amphitheatre, full. The whole Court sits in rows with their faces turned up to the bone roof, and the roof is humming. Above them, through the bone, you can feel something enormous dreaming, and the Court is drinking it.".
  Observe choir_empty at choir when not exhaling(fells) "The amphitheatre stands empty and humming faintly, like a bell after it is struck.".
  Observe spirefoot_scene at spire_foot when true "The foot of a spire of grey crystal. Steps go up round the inside of it.".
  Observe spiretop_scene at spire_top when true "A small round room at the top of the spire, open to the bone roof. On a pedestal of grey crystal rests something like a great closed eyelid of red stone, as big as a shield, and it is warm.".
  Observe throat_scene at throat_head when true "At the edge of the city, where the grey coral stops, a great shaft goes down: smooth, ribbed, red at the bottom. The long throat. Warm air comes up it, and the slow sound of a heart.".

  Species court_kin "one of the Quiet Court" like mind_destroyer.
  Person weigher "the Weigher" at thrall_market {
    Role "master of the Thrall-Market". Species court_kin. Level 8. Peaceable.
  }
  Person col "Col Dunmore" at thrall_market {
    Role "a boy asleep in a niche, with salt on his lips". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Peaceable.
  }
  Thing col_niche "Col's niche" at thrall_market {
    State held "In a low niche at the end of a row, a boy of sixteen sleeps with his head against the stone and salt on his lips. He is very thin.".
    State broken "Col's niche is broken open, and empty.".
    Change smash_niche "Break Col's niche open" from held to broken needing brawn.
  }
  Topic weigher_col with weigher "Ask the Weigher the price of the boy in the end niche" when not freed(col) and state(col_niche, held) once {
    Says "The Weigher's long fingers move, and a thrall standing beside it speaks for it in a pleasant, empty voice. 'That one dreams of his father. Very rich. Ten coin.' The fingers move again. 'There are four hundred and twelve in the market. Do you want them all?'".
  }
  Action buy_col(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Weigher ten coin for Col Dunmore" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, thrall_market) and at(weigher, thrall_market) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 10 and not freed(col).
    Time 1.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Increase quantity(weigher, gold) by 10. Assert freed(col). Assert state(col_niche, broken). Assert at(col, chandlery_shop). }
    Result "The Weigher takes the coins without looking at them. A thrall lifts Col out of the niche like a sack, and he wakes, and does not know you, and then he does. He walks up the long way out without speaking. 'His mother,' he says once, at the gate, and that is all. Behind you, someone else is put in his niche.".
  }
  Rule col_snatched when state(col_niche, broken) and not freed(col)
    says "Col falls out of the broken niche into your arms, awake and screaming. Every face in the market turns. Across the square the door of House Pallor opens." {
    Assert freed(col). Assert at(col, chandlery_shop). Assert roused(hushc).
  }
  Observe col_home at chandlery_shop when freed(col) "Col Dunmore sits by the stove wrapped in a blanket, and his mother has not let go of his hand.".
  Topic col_thanks with col "Ask Col Dunmore what he saw below" when freed(col) and at(col, chandlery_shop) once {
    Says "Col looks at the stove. 'There's a palace,' he says. 'Up in the sky, inside the mountain. In the dream. They take you there and you walk about and it's beautiful. And she's there, the Abbess, at the top of a tower, at the end of a bridge. And under the bridge there's nothing.' He holds his mother's hand harder. 'Not nothing. Something that's hungry.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mouth_rumoured). }
  }
  Discovery mouth_rumoured "Under the bridge from the Abbess's tower in the dreamed palace there is something hungry.".

  // The Houses.
  Person lady_lull "the Lady of Lull" at lull_hall {
    Role "head of House Lull". Species court_kin. Level 10. Peaceable.
  }
  Relation lullPact(group).
  Topic lull_bargain with lady_lull "Ask the Lady of Lull what House Lull wants" when not lullPact(actor) {
    Says "A thrall at the couch's foot speaks for her. 'Sleep,' says the empty voice. 'Long, soft, sweet, for ever. The Abbess and House Pallor want him stirred, nearly woken, so the dreams are strong. Strong dreams are bitter. And if he wakes, there are no dreams at all.' The Lady's fingers move, slow. 'You want the Abbess's Eye. The Abbess sits with the Choir when he breathes out; her spire is empty then. Go with my sign and her guard will not see you, and leave by the servants' bone stair at the spire's foot; it goes down to the throat. Promise me he will sleep.'".
    On discuss { Assert lullPact(actor). Assert tolerates(spire_guard, actor). Assert knows(actor, choir_time). Assert knows(actor, bone_stair_known). }
  }
  Discovery bone_stair_known "From the foot of the Abbess's spire, a servants' stair of bone goes down to the head of the long throat." {
    Found by searching spire_foot "Behind the curve of the spire wall, a narrow stair of yellowed bone goes down, worn by small feet.".
  }
  Passage bone_stair "the servants' bone stair" is passage between spire_foot and throat_head taking 20 minutes hidden until bone_stair_known.
  Discovery choir_time "The Abbess goes down from her spire to sit with the Choir while Thrume breathes out.".
  Person pallor_guards "House Pallor" at pallor_hall {
    Role "the soldiers of House Pallor". Species court_kin. Level 9. Numbers 3. Temperament obedient.
    Uses go, assail. Plans 8 steps.
  }
  Pursuit pallor_hunt for pallor_guards "hunting the intruders through Hush" priority 20 when roused(hushc) and able(pallor_guards) seeks assails(pallor_guards, party).
  Rule pallor_sees when at(party, pallor_hall) and not roused(hushc)
    says "Three soft faces turn from the nightmare on the table toward you, all at once, like flowers to the sun." { Assert roused(hushc). }

  // The Silent Library.
  Discovery mouth_known "The grey scrolls of the Silent Library, read with the fingers: under every sleeping thing is the Between, where forgotten dreams fall, and in it the Mouth, which eats them. The Court is a seed of the Mouth. The Abbess serves it. In the Heart-Tomb below, the Keeper's Chair beside the heart opens on Thrume's dream, and from the dream a bridge goes down to the Between." {
    Source grey_scrolls "the grey scrolls" at library_hall readable by party.
  }

  // The Abbess and her Eye.
  Person abbess "the Abbess of Hush" at spire_top {
    Role "the Abbess of Hush". Species court_kin. Level 14. Peaceable.
    Objects "The Abbess's long hands go still. Every thrall in Hush turns, at once, toward you. Then the soft grey people come.".
  }
  Rule abbess_to_choir when exhaling(fells) and at(abbess, spire_top) { Assert at(abbess, choir). }
  Rule abbess_to_spire when not exhaling(fells) and at(abbess, choir) { Assert at(abbess, spire_top). }
  Rule abbess_angered when hostile(abbess, party) and not roused(hushc) { Assert roused(hushc). }
  Rule eye_missed when at(abbess, spire_top) and not inside(the_eye, pedestal) and not roused(hushc) and not sungClean(fells)
    says "Far off, at the top of the spire, something without a mouth screams, and every thrall in Hush screams with it, all at once, and then is silent. In the silence, doors open." {
    Assert roused(hushc).
  }
  Person spire_guard "the spire's guard" at spire_foot {
    Role "a tall one of the Court with a spear of grey crystal". Species court_kin. Level 9. Temperament obedient.
    Guards spire_stair.
    State watching blocking "A tall one of the Court stands at the foot of the spire stair with a spear of grey crystal, and its soft face follows you.".
  }
  Kind abbess_eye "the Abbess's Eye, a closed lid of warm red stone the size of a shield" is treasure worth 0 weighing 3.
  Thing pedestal "the grey pedestal" at spire_top {
    Holds.
  }
  Item the_eye "the Abbess's Eye" is abbess_eye in pedestal owned by abbess.

  Objective free_col when knows(party, col_gone) and knows(party, hush_named) and not freed(col) "Col Dunmore is in Hush.".
  Objective take_eye when knows(party, mouth_known) and inside(the_eye, pedestal) "The Abbess keeps the Eye; the Heart-Tomb's door needs it.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/placed.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  // Thrume as a country beyond a march: the company that comes in by the salt road is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
}

data/adventures/thrume/saltgrave.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "Saltgrave: the Salt Office, the dream-houses, the night carts.".

  Place salt_office "the Salt Office" is building within saltgrave.
  Place saltcellar "the Saltcellar" is building within saltgrave.
  Place red_lantern "the Red Lantern" is building within saltgrave.
  Place shrine "the Hearth-Mother's shrine" is building within saltgrave.
  Place chandlery "Dunmore's chandlery" is building within saltgrave.

  Place salt_road "the salt road below the town" is room within lowroad at 0, 0.
  Place market "the market square" is room within saltgrave at 1, 1.
  Place office_floor "the Salt Office" is room within salt_office at 2, 1.
  Place provost_room "the provost's room" is room within salt_office at 2, 0.
  Place inn_room "the Saltcellar's taproom" is room within saltcellar at 0, 1.
  Place lantern_front "the Red Lantern's front room" is room within red_lantern at 1, 2.
  Place smoke_room "the smoke-room" is room within red_lantern at 2, 2.
  Place lantern_back "the back room of the Red Lantern" is room within red_lantern at 2, 3.
  Place shrine_room "the shrine" is room within shrine at 0, 0.
  Place chandlery_shop "Dunmore's chandlery" is room within chandlery at 0, 2.
  Place miners_row "the miners' row" is room within saltgrave at 1, 0.
  Place carters_yard "the carters' yard" is room within saltgrave at 1, 3.
  Place cart_road "the cart road" is room within fellside at 1, 1.
  Place scree_foot "the foot of the scree road" is room within fellside at 0, 0.

  Passage salt_gate "the town gate" is road between salt_road and market taking 20 minutes.
  Passage office_door "the Salt Office door" is door between market and office_floor.
  Passage provost_door "the provost's door" is door between office_floor and provost_room.
  Passage inn_door "the Saltcellar's door" is door between market and inn_room.
  Passage lantern_door "the Red Lantern's door" is door between market and lantern_front.
  Passage smoke_curtain "the smoke-room curtain" is doorway between lantern_front and smoke_room.
  Passage lantern_back_door "the Lantern's back door" is door between smoke_room and lantern_back.
  Passage back_yard_gate "the yard gate behind the Lantern" is gate between lantern_back and carters_yard.
  Passage shrine_door "the shrine door" is door between market and shrine_room.
  Passage chandlery_door "Dunmore's door" is door between market and chandlery_shop.
  Passage row_lane "the row lane" is path between market and miners_row taking 10 minutes.
  Passage yard_lane "the yard lane" is path between market and carters_yard taking 10 minutes.
  Passage cart_track "the cart road" is road between carters_yard and cart_road taking 1 hour.
  Passage scree_lane "the north lane" is path between miners_row and scree_foot taking 30 minutes.

  Observe road_scene at salt_road when not dark() "The salt road comes up out of the river country between fields gone white at the edges, as if salted. Ahead, Saltgrave sits under the fells in its own dust: new timber, white roofs, a church tower with no church yet. Beyond the town the fells go up and up, brown and long and oddly smooth, like something lying under a blanket.".
  Observe road_night at salt_road when dark() "The town's lights are few and yellow. One lantern, red, burns later than the rest.".
  Observe market_scene at market when not dark() and not woken(fells) "A square of trodden white dust. Carts, salt-dust on everything, a dry pump, a notice on a post, and on one side a narrow house with a red lantern over its door, unlit by day.".
  Observe market_night at market when dark() and not woken(fells) "The square is empty but for a dog. Over the narrow house on the south side, the red lantern is lit.".
  Observe office_scene at office_floor when true "Scales, sacks, a long counter and a clerk behind it. On the wall a map of the workings, Number One to Number Four, and on Number Four someone has written CLOSED in red, and someone else has crossed it out.".
  Observe provost_scene at provost_room when true "A good room for a raw town: a carpet, a decanter, a strongbox. A ledger lies open on the desk.".
  Observe inn_scene at inn_room when true "Low beams, salt-cured hams, and miners drinking without talking. In the best corner a man in the Margravine's blue and silver eats alone, with a sword across the bench beside him.".
  Observe front_scene at lantern_front when true "A dim room hung with red cloth, warm and sweet-smelling, very quiet. A little table, and a chair behind it.".
  Observe smoke_scene at smoke_room when true "Pallets in a row, and on them people asleep with their eyes moving under the lids: miners, a girl in a good dress, an old man. A brazier burns something red that smells of iron and rain. Every sleeper's lips are moving, and they are all saying the same thing.".
  Observe back_scene at lantern_back when true "A storeroom: sacks of red salt, blankets, rope. A row of pegs by the yard gate, and on them the coats of people who are not wearing them.".
  Observe shrine_scene at shrine_room when true "A whitewashed room with a hearth for an altar. The fire on it is the only one in Saltgrave that never goes out. Prayers are nailed on the wall on scraps: for the men in the Number Four, for a son, for sleep.".
  Observe chandlery_scene at chandlery_shop when true "Candles, rope, lamp-oil, picks. Everything a mine needs, and too much of it, now the mine is shut.".
  Observe row_scene at miners_row when true "A double row of salt-white cottages. Forty doors have a twist of black wool on the latch: the families of the men the giants took.".
  Observe yard_scene at carters_yard when not dark() "A yard of salt-carts with their shafts down, and the stable smell. The carts have stood idle since the mine was shut; their axles are freshly greased.".
  Observe cart_road_scene at cart_road when true "The cart road climbs the fellside in long loops toward the black mouths of the workings. The turf on either side is warm to the hand.".
  Observe scree_foot_scene at scree_foot when true "The north lane gives out into scree. A path goes up it, very steep, toward the shoulder of the fells and a smudge of smoke under the glacier.".
  Passage scree_climb_long "the scree road" is path between scree_foot and scree_road taking 2 hours.

  // The Margravine's envoy, and the price on the thane.
  Person varne "Sir Odo Varne" at inn_room {
    Role "the Margravine's envoy". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 6. Peaceable.
  }
  Discovery bounty_known "The Margravine's notice: FOR THE HEAD OF THE GIANT MÓRRACH, THAT CALLS HIMSELF THANE, THE LORDSHIP OF HARROWBY AND ITS RENTS. SIR O. VARNE, FOR IDONY VASK, MARGRAVINE OF EBB." {
    Source notice "the notice on the market post" at market readable by party.
    Known by varne.
  }
  Topic varne_bounty with varne "Ask Sir Odo Varne about the giants" when true once {
    Says "'They came down off the fells four months ago,' says Varne, 'and smashed every mine-head we have, and carried off forty men, and burned the overseer in his house.' He wipes his knife. 'The Margravine must have the salt by the new moon. Harle's host will be at the Ebb by then, and the companies she means to hire want paying in something heavier than promises. Bring me the thane's head and you are lords. Overseer Brannoc has gone down the old adit with a crew to keep the salt coming meanwhile. He is not a man who stops.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bounty_known). Assert knows(actor, brannoc_below). }
  }
  Discovery brannoc_below "Overseer Brannoc has gone down the old adit of the Number Four with a crew, to keep cutting red salt for the Margravine.".
  Topic varne_truth with varne "Tell Sir Odo Varne what the red salt is" when knows(actor, thrume_known) and knows(actor, salt_is_blood) once {
    Says "Varne hears you out without interrupting, which is a courtesy you did not expect. At the end he is quiet a long time. 'If you are lying, you are the best liars I ever met,' he says. 'If you are not, the Margravine is cutting the throat of the ground she stands on.' He takes a folded paper from his coat, sealed in blue wax, writes on it, and holds it out. 'Brannoc obeys the seal. Not me. The seal. Give him this.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(varne, seal_letter, actor). Assert at(seal_letter, inn_room). }
  }
  Kind margrave_seal "a letter under the Margravine's blue seal" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0.
  Item seal_letter "an order under the Margravine's seal" is margrave_seal at limbo owned by varne.
  Place limbo "nowhere" is room within lowroad at 1, 0.

  // The provost and his ledger.
  Person hauk "Provost Lisle Hauk" at provost_room {
    Role "provost of the Salt Office". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    Objects "Hauk sees {?i} in your hands and goes the colour of tallow. 'That is the Office's,' he says. 'I will have the watch on you.'".
  }
  Discovery ledger_known "The Salt Office ledger: every week since spring, forty crowns in salt-silver from 'the Lantern, for quiet', in the provost's own hand. Beside the last three entries, a tally of carts: four, six, nine." {
    Source office_ledger "the Salt Office ledger" at provost_room readable by party.
    Known by hauk.
  }
  Topic hauk_lantern with hauk "Ask Provost Hauk about the Red Lantern" when not knows(actor, ledger_known) once {
    Says "'A respectable house,' says Hauk. 'Miners need their rest. The Office licenses it.' He moves the ledger an inch further from you without looking at it.".
  }
  Topic hauk_ledger with hauk "Ask Provost Hauk what the carts in his ledger carry" when knows(actor, ledger_known) once {
    Says "Hauk sits down. 'Sleepers,' he says, very low. 'The ones who sleep too deep to wake. She says they are taken up to the hot springs above the workings, to be cured. She pays for the carts. She pays for my not asking.' He looks at his hands. 'I have not asked. I have a daughter in Ebb.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, carts_known). }
  }

  // The dream-house.
  Person quietly "Mother Quietly" at lantern_front {
    Role "keeper of the Red Lantern". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    State smiling "Mother Quietly sits behind her little table with her hands folded, smiling. Her eyes do not move when she looks at you; her head does.".
    State emptied "Mother Quietly sits behind her little table with her hands folded. There is nobody behind her eyes at all.".
  }
  Person dreamers "the dreamers" at smoke_room {
    Role "sleepers on the pallets". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Discovery dream_shared "Everyone who sleeps on the red salt dreams the same dream: a palace in a sky too close to the ground, and a great slow heart beating under the floor.".
  Topic dreamers_dream with dreamers "Listen to what the sleepers are saying" when true once {
    Says "You lean close. They are all saying it, the girl in the good dress and the old man and the miners, in the same breath: 'The sky is so close. The floor is beating. The sky is so close. The floor is beating.' One of the miners opens his eyes, looks at you without seeing you, and says, quite clearly, 'He is turning over,' and sleeps again.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, dream_shared). }
  }
  Topic quietly_col with quietly "Ask Mother Quietly about Col Dunmore" when knows(actor, col_gone) and state(quietly, smiling) once {
    Says "'Such a sad boy,' says Mother Quietly. 'His father in the mine. He slept so beautifully.' Her head tilts; her eyes stay where they were. 'He has gone up to the springs, to be cured. They all go up, the deep sleepers. Would you like to rest a little? You look so tired.'".
  }
  Action rest_on_salt(actor: group, site: place) "Lie down on a pallet and breathe the red smoke" {
    Description "Mother Quietly says it is the best sleep in the world. The dreamers' faces say she may be right.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, smoke_room) and not dreamt(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert dreamt(actor). }
    Result "You sleep, and you are standing in a palace of white stone with the sky so close above it you could touch the clouds. Under the floor something vast is beating, very slowly, and the whole palace rises and falls with it like a chest. Far away, at the end of a long hall, someone grey with no mouth turns to look at you, and you wake on the pallet with your heart going like a bird's.".
  }
  Relation dreamt(group).
  // Seen only by those who have dreamt on the salt: what the Court's thralls look like to the dreaming.
  Person watcher "the grey thing behind Mother Quietly" at lantern_front {
    Role "something grey and soft-faced, standing where her shadow should be". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    Seen when dreamt(viewer).
  }
  Topic watcher_speaks with watcher "Look the grey thing in its soft face" when true once {
    Says "It has no mouth. It speaks anyway, inside your head, in the kindest voice you have ever heard: 'You slept so well. Come down and sleep with us. It is so quiet in Hush.' Mother Quietly, in front of it, smiles a little wider, as if she had said it.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hush_named). }
  }

  // The night carts.
  Person hushed "the night carters" at lantern_back {
    Role "two men with still eyes, who do not speak". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 2. Peaceable.
  }
  Relation carting(group). Relation ringBroken(group).
  Rule carters_out when dark() and at(hushed, lantern_back) and not ringBroken(hushed) and untilLight(clock) > 36 { Assert at(hushed, carters_yard). Assert carting(hushed). }
  Rule carters_back when at(hushed, carters_yard) and (untilLight(clock) <= 36 or ringBroken(hushed)) { Assert at(hushed, lantern_back). Retract carting(hushed). }
  Observe carts_by_night at carters_yard when carting(hushed) "Two men with still eyes are lifting sleepers out of the Lantern's back gate, wrapped in blankets, and laying them in a salt-cart like sacks. Nobody sleeping wakes. When the cart is full they lead the horse out on the cart road toward the workings, without a lantern." teaches carts_known.
  Discovery carts_known "By night the Red Lantern's carters carry the deepest sleepers up the cart road to the workings, in salt-carts.".

  // Breaking the ring: Mother Quietly cornered.
  Topic quietly_carts with quietly "Ask Mother Quietly where the carts go" when knows(actor, carts_known) and state(quietly, smiling) once {
    Says "Mother Quietly's smile does not change. Then it does not change for too long. Her hands come apart on the table, slowly, as if someone else were unfolding them, and she sits back. Her mouth opens. 'Down,' she says, in a voice with no breath behind it. 'Down to Hush, where it is quiet.' Then nothing is behind her eyes at all. Something drops from her fingers and rolls across the table: a grey pebble, humming.".
    On discuss { Assert state(quietly, emptied). Assert ringBroken(hushed). Assert knows(actor, hush_named). Assert knows(actor, quietly_emptied). }
  }
  Discovery hush_named "The sleepers carried from the Red Lantern go 'down to Hush, where it is quiet'.".
  Discovery quietly_emptied "Cornered, Mother Quietly was emptied like a cup by whatever was behind her, and dropped a grey humming stone.".
  Kind hush_stone "a grey pebble that hums at the edge of hearing" is treasure worth 1 weighing 0.
  Item hush_pebble "a grey humming pebble" is hush_stone at lantern_front hidden until quietly_emptied.

  // Hesper Dunmore and her son.
  Person hesper "Hesper Dunmore" at chandlery_shop {
    Role "chandler, whose son has not come home". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 8. Sells torch for 1 coin from 12. Sells rope for 1 coin from 4.
  }
  Discovery col_gone "Col Dunmore, sixteen, started sleeping at the Red Lantern after his father died in the Number Four, and has not come home in three nights.".
  Topic hesper_col with hesper "Ask Hesper Dunmore what is wrong" when true once {
    Says "'My boy,' says Hesper, and puts down the candle she was trimming. 'Col. His father died in the Number Four in the spring, and Col couldn't sleep, and someone told him about the Red Lantern. He slept there every night after. Three nights ago he didn't come home.' She looks at you. 'The watch says he's gone off to the giants for the bounty. He's sixteen and he's frightened of dogs. Will you look?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, col_gone). }
  }
  Topic hesper_news with hesper "Tell Hesper Dunmore where Col was taken" when knows(actor, hush_named) and knows(actor, col_gone) once {
    Says "Hesper listens with both hands flat on her counter. 'Down,' she says. 'Down where?' Then: 'No. Don't tell me. Bring him up.' She pushes a cloth of bread and cheese across the counter and will not take money for it.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, rations) by 2. }
  }

  // The shrine: rest, healing, and a priest who knows the old stories.
  Person agathe "Sister Agathe" at shrine_room {
    Role "keeper of the Hearth-Mother's fire". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 4. Peaceable.
    Offers healing "the Hearth-Mother's blessing and clean linen" for 2 coin.
  }
  Topic agathe_fells with agathe "Ask Sister Agathe about the fells" when true once {
    Says "'The old shepherds had a saying,' says Agathe. 'Walk soft on Thrume, he's only sleeping.' She smiles. 'They meant the giant in the stories. The one the hills were made from.' She looks at the prayers on the wall. 'Since the Number Four broke through, I have had more prayers for sleep than for anything else. People here cannot sleep, and when they do they all dream the same.'".
  }

  // The Saltcellar.
  Person landlord "Gil Sorrow" at inn_room {
    Role "landlord of the Saltcellar". Profession innkeeper. Peaceable.
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 8. Sells torch for 1 coin from 6.
  }

  // The miners' row: the families, and the way to the giants.
  Person wives "the miners' wives" at miners_row {
    Role "women of the miners' row". Ancestry human. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
  }
  Topic wives_giants with wives "Ask the miners' wives about the giants" when true once {
    Says "'They didn't kill anyone that night,' says a woman with a baby on her hip. 'Only the overseer, and that was the fire. They took the men out of the Number Four like you'd take kittens out of a well, and carried them up the scree road.' Another says: 'Aud Brenning's with them. Aud doesn't die easy.' The first: 'If you go up there for the Margravine's money, you can bring ours home while you're about it.'".
  }

  Objective find_col when knows(party, col_gone) and not freed(col) "Hesper Dunmore's son Col did not come home from the Red Lantern.".
  Objective lay_thane when knows(party, bounty_known) and not knows(party, thrume_known) "The Margravine will pay a lordship for Thane Mórrach's head.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/shoulder.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "The Shoulder Hall: the giants' hold on the ridge, forty miners held in it, and the keepers' way down into the body.".

  Place scree "the scree road" is wilderness within fells at 0, 1.
  Place hold "the Shoulder Hall" is site within fells at 1, 1.
  Place glacier "the Shoulder glacier" is wilderness within fells at 1, 0.
  Place cellars "the glacier cellars" is level within hold.

  Place scree_road "the top of the scree road" is room within scree at 0, 0.
  Place gate_yard "the gate-yard" is room within hold at 1, 2.
  Place kennels "the wolf-pens" is room within hold at 0, 2.
  Place long_hall "the long hall" is room within hold at 1, 1.
  Place thane_seat "the high seat" is room within hold at 1, 0.
  Place hearth "the mothers' hearth" is room within hold at 0, 1.
  Place barracks "the young bloods' house" is room within hold at 2, 1.
  Place pens "the thrall-pens" is room within hold at 2, 2.
  Place midden "the midden under the pens" is room within glacier at 2, 1.
  Place glacier_foot "the glacier's foot" is room within glacier at 1, 1.
  Place ice_cellar "the ice cellar" is room within cellars at 1, 0.
  Place cage_room "the cage of ice" is room within cellars at 2, 0.
  Place stair_head "the head of the Keepers' Stair" is room within cellars at 0, 0.
  Initially Assert unlit(ice_cellar). Initially Assert unlit(cage_room). Initially Assert unlit(stair_head).

  Passage scree_climb "the last of the scree" is path between scree_road and gate_yard taking 30 minutes.
  Passage kennel_gate "the wolf-pen gate" is gate between gate_yard and kennels.
  Passage hall_doors "the hall doors" is door between gate_yard and long_hall.
  Passage seat_steps "the steps to the high seat" is steps between long_hall and thane_seat.
  Passage hearth_way "the hearth passage" is doorway between long_hall and hearth.
  Passage bloods_door "the young bloods' door" is door between gate_yard and barracks.
  Passage pens_gate "the pens gate" is gate between gate_yard and pens.
  Passage midden_chute "the midden chute" is crawl between pens and midden taking 10 minutes needing climbing or rope.
  Passage midden_path "the ice under the midden" is path between midden and glacier_foot taking 20 minutes.
  Passage glacier_track "the edge of the glacier" is track between scree_road and glacier_foot taking 1 hour.
  Passage crevasse "the blue crevasse" is tunnel between glacier_foot and ice_cellar taking 20 minutes hidden until crevasse_known.
  Passage cellar_stair "the cellar stair" is stair between ice_cellar and long_hall.
  Passage cage_way "the cold passage" is passage between ice_cellar and cage_room.
  Passage keepers_arch "the keepers' arch" is arch between ice_cellar and stair_head.

  Observe sroad_scene at scree_road when not dark() "The scree gives out under a hold of black timber and grey stone that sits on the shoulder of the fells under a glacier, like a hut under a wave. Its doors are three times the height of a man.".
  Observe sroad_night at scree_road when dark() "Above you the hold's smoke-holes glow red. Somebody up there is singing, very low; you feel it in the stones before you hear it.".
  Observe gyard_scene at gate_yard when true "A yard of trodden snow and bones. The gate-posts are whole pine trunks. A pole of grey wood stands by the hall doors, hung with a hammer the size of a child.".
  Observe hall_scene at long_hall when not dark() "A hall long enough to race horses in, smoky, roofed with whole trees. Benches you would need a ladder for run down both sides of a fire-trench.".
  Observe hall_night at long_hall when dark() "The fire-trench is down to embers. Along both walls, on the benches and under them, giants sleep in their furs like a range of low hills, breathing slow. One of them is talking in its sleep.".
  Observe seat_scene at thane_seat when true "The high seat is a block of the mountain itself, left where it stood when the hall was built round it, polished by a thousand years of sitting. It is warm.".
  Observe hearth_scene at hearth when true "A round room, warm, smelling of milk and smoke. Four great pillars hold up the roof, and every one is carved from floor to rafters in lines too small for the hands that must have cut them.".
  Observe barracks_scene at barracks when true "Sleeping platforms, war-gear, and a table scored with a map of the dale below: Saltgrave, the mine-heads, the road. Someone has driven a knife through the town.".
  Observe pens_scene at pens when not freed(aud) and not razed(scree) "Forty miners in a pen of stakes, under a roof of hides. They are cold and filthy and alive, which they did not expect.".
  Observe pens_empty at pens when freed(aud) "The pen of stakes is empty, and the hides flap.".
  Observe pens_razed at pens when razed(scree) and not freed(aud) "Do not look at the pens.".
  Observe midden_scene at midden when true "The midden spills out from under the pens onto the ice. Above you a square chute goes up into the dark; there are hand-holds in it, worn.".
  Observe foot_scene at glacier_foot when not dark() "The glacier ends here in a wall of blue ice, cracked, sweating, groaning to itself in the sun.".
  Observe foot_night at glacier_foot when dark() "The glacier ends here in a wall of ice that is faintly blue even in the dark. It ticks and groans as the cold takes hold of it.".
  Observe icecellar_scene at ice_cellar when true "A cellar cut in the glacier. The walls are blue and give back no light. Joints of meat hang from hooks. A cold passage goes off to one side; on the other, an arch of old grey stone, older than the hall, opens on a stair going down.".
  Observe stairhead_scene at stair_head when true "A stair as wide as a road goes down into the mountain in long flights, the treads worn into dips by enormous feet. The air coming up it is warm, and smells faintly of blood and salt.".

  Discovery crevasse_known "A crevasse at the glacier's foot runs back under the hold, into its ice cellar." {
    Found by searching glacier_foot "Behind a slab of fallen ice a blue crevasse runs back into the glacier, and the air in it smells of smoke and meat.".
    Known by aud.
  }

  // The giants. Nothing in the hold is scaled to the company.
  Species shoulder_giant "a giant of the Shoulder" like colossus.
  Person morrach "Thane Mórrach" at thane_seat {
    Role "thane of the Shoulder Hall". Species shoulder_giant. Level 12. Peaceable.
    State presiding "Thane Mórrach sits the high seat with his hands on his knees: grey-bearded, heavy, very still, and twice as tall as the door you came in by.".
    State deposed "Thane Mórrach sits on the floor beside the high seat with his hands bound in front of him in a ship's cable. Skarn sits the seat.".
  }
  Person skarn "Skarn" at barracks {
    Role "first of the young bloods". Species shoulder_giant. Level 9. Temperament obedient.
    Uses go, assail. Plans 6 steps.
  }
  Person bloods "the young bloods" at barracks {
    Role "young giants spoiling for a war". Species shoulder_giant. Level 7. Numbers 3. Temperament obedient.
    Uses go, assail. Plans 6 steps.
  }
  Initially Assert serves(bloods, skarn).
  Person rememberer "the Rememberer" at hearth {
    Role "the thane's mother, keeper of the song". Species shoulder_giant. Level 10. Peaceable.
    Wants heart_salt.
  }
  Person wolves "the hold's wolves" at kennels {
    Role "frost wolves the size of ponies". Species frost_wolf. Numbers 2.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Two white wolves the size of ponies get up out of the straw, without hurry, and stand between you and everything else.".
  }

  // The hostages.
  Person aud "Aud Brenning" at pens {
    Role "foreman of the Saltgrave miners". Ancestry dwarf. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable.
  }
  Person kell "Tobias Kell" at pens {
    Role "a miner who will not meet your eye". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 2. Peaceable.
  }

  // The alarm. By day a stranger in the yard is challenged and has a little while to answer at the guest-pole; by
  // night the hold sleeps, and the long hall can be crept through by the light-footed.
  Relation roused(place). Relation guest(group). Relation freed(group). Relation gagged(group). Relation sawUs(group).
  Relation challenged(group). Measure answerBy(group).
  Rule seen_in_yard when at(party, gate_yard) and not dark() and not guest(party) and not roused(hold) and not challenged(party) and not sworn(morrach)
    says "A giant crossing the yard with a bucket stops, and looks down at you, and sets the bucket down. He says one word, a question, in a voice like a rockfall, and his eyes go to the pole by the hall doors and back to you." {
    Assert challenged(party). Set answerBy(party) to watch(clock) + 2.
  }
  Rule challenge_unanswered when challenged(party) and not guest(party) and not roused(hold) and watch(clock) >= answerBy(party)
    says "The giant with the bucket stops waiting. He shouts, and the hall doors bang open." { Assert roused(hold). }
  Rule seen_in_hall when (at(party, long_hall) or at(party, barracks)) and not dark() and not guest(party) and not roused(hold) and not sworn(morrach)
    says "A roar goes up from the benches." { Assert roused(hold). }
  // Crossing the sleeping hall: the light-footed pass; others may not.
  Relation crept(group).
  Rule hall_wakes when at(party, long_hall) and dark() and not guest(party) and not sworn(morrach) and not capable(party, stealth) and not roused(hold) and dice(long_hall) <= 35
    says "Your boot finds a bone in the dark. It cracks like a branch. Along the wall a shape the size of a hayrick sits up, and says something, and then shouts it." { Assert roused(hold). }
  Pursuit hunt for skarn "hunting the intruders" priority 20 when roused(hold) and able(skarn) seeks assails(skarn, party).
  Pursuit hunt_with for bloods "hunting the intruders with Skarn" priority 20 when roused(hold) and able(bloods) seeks assails(bloods, party).

  // Guest-right.
  Action ask_guest_right(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the guest-pole and ask for hall-right" {
    Description "The old law of the hills: whoever asks hall-right at the pole is under the thane's roof until they leave it, and may not lift a hand there.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gate_yard) and not guest(actor) and not roused(hold).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert guest(actor). Assert tolerates(morrach, actor). Assert tolerates(skarn, actor). Assert tolerates(bloods, actor). }
    Result "The hammer is almost too heavy to lift. The pole rings like a bell. The hall doors open, and a giant looks down at you for a long moment, and stands aside.".
  }
  Rule guest_broken when guest(party) and not sworn(morrach) and (at(party, pens) or at(party, ice_cellar) or at(party, barracks))
    says "Skarn's voice, from across the yard: 'Guests. Look where the guests are.' And then, louder, to the whole hold." {
    Retract guest(party). Retract tolerates(skarn, party). Retract tolerates(bloods, party). Retract tolerates(morrach, party). Assert roused(hold).
  }

  // Kell sells whoever comes to the pens, as soon as their backs are turned, unless Aud has him held.
  Rule kell_sees when at(party, pens) and not guest(party) and not sawUs(kell) { Assert sawUs(kell). }
  Rule kell_sells when sawUs(kell) and not at(party, pens) and not gagged(kell) and not roused(hold) and not freed(aud) and not sworn(morrach)
    says "From the pens behind you a man's voice goes up, high and clear, calling for Skarn by name." { Assert roused(hold). }
  Topic aud_kell with aud "Ask Aud Brenning about the man who won't look at you" when sawUs(kell) and not gagged(kell) once {
    Says "'Tobias Kell,' says Aud, not quietly. 'He showed them where we slept. He'll be shouting before you're over the stakes.' She looks at Kell, and two of her miners get up and sit down either side of him. 'Not today, Tobias.'".
    On discuss { Assert gagged(kell). }
  }
  Topic aud_deep with aud "Ask Aud Brenning why the giants came" when true once {
    Says "'We broke into something at the bottom of the Number Four,' says Aud. 'Red salt, a whole wall of it, and warm. Warm, under a mountain. The next week they came.' She lowers her voice. 'I kept a piece back. It's in the midden under us, wrapped in my shirt. I don't know why I did that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, salt_hidden). }
  }
  Discovery salt_hidden "Aud Brenning hid a lump of the red salt from the bottom of the Number Four in the midden under the pens.".
  Kind heart_salt "a lump of red heart-salt, warm to the touch" is treasure worth 40 weighing 1.
  Item salt_lump "a shirt wrapped round something warm" is heart_salt at midden hidden until salt_hidden.

  // The Rememberer.
  Discovery song_seen "The carvings on the hearth pillars are a song in the giants' writing, and it is about something they keep.".
  Observe pillars_teach at hearth when true "Close to, the lines on the pillars are writing, tiny and endless, the same few signs over and over: a mountain, a heart, a closed eye." teaches song_seen.
  Discovery thrume_known "Thrume is not a mountain. It is a titan, sleeping, and the range is its body; the red salt is its blood. The giants of the Shoulder are its keepers, and the mine is a wound.".
  Relation saltReturned(group).
  Event salt_given near rememberer when keeps(rememberer, ?s) and itemKind(?s, heart_salt)
    "The Rememberer holds the red salt against her blind eyes, then against her cheek, as you would a sick child's forehead. 'Warm,' she says. 'He is warm. They have cut him to the blood.'" then {
    Assert saltReturned(rememberer).
  }
  Topic rememberer_truth with rememberer "Ask the Rememberer who is warm" when saltReturned(rememberer) once {
    Says "She turns her face to you. 'Sit down, small ones. Thrume is not a mountain. Thrume is the last of the old ones, the ones who were here before the hills, and he sleeps, and the hills are him. We are his keepers. Your miners have cut into him to the blood, and he is beginning to dream.' Her hand finds the pillar beside her. 'When he dreams, things walk. You have one in our cellar.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, thrume_known). }
  }
  Discovery song_known "The keepers' song, as the Rememberer sang it: the names of the old ones, one by one, and Thrume's last. A song is a thing remembered by the living; nothing that eats forgetting can eat it.".
  Topic rememberer_song with rememberer "Ask the Rememberer to teach you the song" when knows(actor, thrume_known) and (dreamt(actor) or knows(actor, mouth_known)) once {
    Says "She is quiet a long time. She leans close and breathes in, as if smelling your hair. 'You have been in his dream,' she says. 'I can smell the sky on you.' Then: 'The song is not for small ones. Then: 'But the small ones are going where we cannot.' She sings. It is long, and very low, and your teeth ache with it, and it is only names: the old ones, one by one, the hills that walked, and last of all Thrume's. When she stops, you find you can sing it back to her, every name. 'Do not forget it,' she says. 'It is the one thing down there that cannot be eaten, while one of us remembers.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, song_known). }
  }
  Topic rememberer_cage with rememberer "Ask the Rememberer about the thing in the cellar" when knows(actor, thrume_known) once {
    Says "'The first of his dreams to walk,' she says. 'A dream of salt. We caught it in the snow below the workings, killing sheep, and the ice holds it. When he dreams harder, they will come out of the hills by dozens.' Her face turns toward the floor. 'Do not let it out. It is not wicked. It is only what he is dreaming, and he is dreaming badly.'".
  }

  // The thane: his terms, his ring, and the miners.
  Relation sworn(group).
  Topic morrach_why with morrach "Ask Thane Mórrach why he took the miners" when state(morrach, presiding) once {
    Says "The thane looks down at you for a long moment. 'Because they were cutting,' he says. His voice is very quiet for a voice that big. 'Your Margravine wants a war. My young bloods want a war. I want the cutting to stop. Forty of them in my pens and the cutting stops.' He opens one hand. 'And then she sent another down the old hole, with more men, and the cutting goes on.'".
  }
  Topic morrach_oath with morrach "Swear to Thane Mórrach that you will close the wound" when knows(actor, thrume_known) and state(morrach, presiding) and not sworn(morrach) {
    Says "The thane gets up. You had not seen him stand; it takes some time. He takes a ring from his finger, a ring of grey stone the size of a cart-wheel's hub, and puts it down on the floor in front of you. 'The keepers' ring,' he says. 'The arch in my cellar opens to it, and the stair below goes down into him, a long way down. Close the wound, small ones. Stop the cutting. And take your miners home; I have no more use for them.' Behind you, across the yard, someone throws a cup against a wall.".
    On discuss { Assert sworn(morrach). Assert guest(actor). Assert tolerates(morrach, actor). Assert tolerates(skarn, actor). Assert tolerates(bloods, actor). Assert at(thane_ring, thane_seat). Assert freed(aud). Assert at(aud, miners_row). Assert at(kell, miners_row). Retract roused(hold). }
  }
  Kind keepers_ring "the keepers' ring, a band of grey stone the size of a hub" is treasure worth 0 weighing 2.
  Item thane_ring "the keepers' ring" is keepers_ring at limbo.
  Thing keepers_door "the keepers' arch" on keepers_arch {
    State shut blocking "The arch of grey stone is closed by a slab with a round socket in it, as big as a hub, and worn smooth.".
    State open "The slab has gone down into the floor of the arch. Warm air comes up the stair beyond.".
    Change open_arch "Set the keepers' ring in the socket of the arch" from shut to open needing keepers_ring.
  }
  Observe miners_home at miners_row when freed(aud) "The twists of black wool are gone from the latches. Aud Brenning is going from door to door with a list in her hand, crossing names off.".
  Topic aud_home with aud "Ask Aud Brenning about the Number Four" when freed(aud) and at(aud, miners_row) once {
    Says "'The old adit,' she says. 'Brannoc went down it with twelve men and a quota. Below the old workings it comes out in the red, and below the red, I don't know. We never went past the warm face.' She folds the list. 'If you go down there, there's a rope ladder at the Number Four sump that goes further than we ever did. We found it there. We didn't put it there.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sump_ladder). }
  }
  Discovery sump_ladder "At the sump of the Number Four hangs a ladder that goes deeper than the miners ever went. They did not put it there." {
    Found by searching sump "Behind a fall of salt beside the sump a hole goes down, and a ladder of fine grey rope hangs into it.".
    Found by searching vein_foot "A ladder of fine grey rope hangs out of a hole in the cave roof, swaying in the warm air. It goes up toward the workings.".
  }

  // Skarn throws down the thane if the hold is roused and blood is spilled; the young bloods go to war.
  Relation razed(place). Relation coup(place).
  Rule skarn_rises when roused(hold) and (dead(bloods) or hurt(skarn)) and not coup(hold) and able(skarn)
    says "Somewhere in the hold a voice roars, and another answers it, and then the whole hall is shouting one name, and it is not the thane's." {
    Assert coup(hold). Assert state(morrach, deposed). Assert at(skarn, thane_seat).
  }
  Relation hurt(group).
  // The young bloods' clock: at dark on the second night they kill the miners and go down on Saltgrave, unless the
  // thane has given the miners up.
  Rule massacre when watch(clock) >= 216 and dark() and not freed(aud) and able(skarn) and not razed(scree)
    says "In the dark the hold wakes all at once: torches, a horn, and then from the pens a sound you will not forget. Then the young bloods go out of the gate and down the scree road toward Saltgrave, singing." {
    Assert razed(scree). Assert at(skarn, market). Assert at(bloods, market). Increase stirring(fells) by 1.
  }
  Observe market_raided at market when razed(scree) "Half the square is burnt. The pump is a stump. A giant's footprint is pressed into the dust in front of the Salt Office, deep enough to stand in.".

  // The thing in the ice.
  Thing ice_cage "the cage of ice" at cage_room {
    State frozen "In a cage of blue ice something white turns and turns like salt poured slowly into water. It has no face, and it is looking at you.".
    State melted "A pool of meltwater, and an empty cage, and a white crust like frost all across the floor.".
    Change melt "Melt the cage of ice with fire" from frozen to melted needing flame.
  }
  Person salt_dream "the salt-dream" at limbo {
    Role "a walking dream of salt". Species salt_elemental. Level 6.
    Temperament savage.
    Comes "The white thing pours out of the broken ice and comes at you, hissing like a struck match.".
  }
  Rule dream_loose when state(ice_cage, melted) and at(salt_dream, limbo) { Assert at(salt_dream, cage_room). }

  Objective free_miners when not freed(aud) and not razed(scree) "Forty miners are held in the Shoulder Hall, and the young bloods mean to kill them on the second night.".
  Objective learn_why when knows(party, song_seen) and not knows(party, thrume_known) "The giants keep something, and their song says what.".
  Objective close_wound when sworn(morrach) and cutting(brannoc) "You swore to Thane Mórrach to stop the cutting.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/tomb.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "The Heart-Tomb: the Hollow Smiths' killing gauntlet around the heart of Thrume. Every trap is an argument for their doctrine: what wakes, kills; what kills, wakes.".

  Place tomb "the Heart-Tomb" is site within fells at 3, 1.
  Place tomb_outer "the outer tomb" is level within tomb.
  Place tomb_halls "the halls of the tomb" is level within tomb.
  Place tomb_pit "the oubliette" is level within tomb.
  Place tomb_core "the core of the tomb" is level within tomb.

  Place tomb_mouth "the foot of the long throat" is room within tomb_outer at 0, 0.
  Place salt_landing "the head of the salt stair" is room within tomb_outer at 1, 0.
  Place hammer_hall "the hall of the hammers" is room within tomb_halls at 0, 0.
  Place doctrine_hall "the Hall of Doctrine" is room within tomb_halls at 1, 0.
  Place face_room "the Sleeper's Face" is room within tomb_halls at 2, 0.
  Place door_hall "the Hall of Doors" is room within tomb_halls at 2, 1.
  Place breaths_room "the Room of Three Breaths" is room within tomb_halls at 3, 1.
  Place gearworks "the Gearworks" is room within tomb_halls at 3, 0.
  Place warder_gallery "the gallery over the Warder" is room within tomb_halls at 4, 0.
  Place oubliette "the oubliette" is room within tomb_pit at 2, 1.
  Place false_heart "the Chamber of the Heart" is room within tomb_core at 0, 0.
  Place warder_hall "the Warder's corridor" is room within tomb_core at 1, 0.
  Place locks_room "the hall of the locks" is room within tomb_core at 2, 0.
  Place heart_chamber "the Keeper's Chair" is room within tomb_core at 3, 0.
  Initially Assert unlit(tomb_mouth). Initially Assert unlit(salt_landing). Initially Assert unlit(hammer_hall).
  Initially Assert unlit(face_room). Initially Assert unlit(door_hall). Initially Assert unlit(oubliette). Initially Assert unlit(warder_hall).
  Initially Assert unlit(locks_room).

  Passage long_throat "the long throat" is tunnel between throat_head and tomb_mouth taking 2 hours needing climbing or rope.
  Passage landing_way "the outer passage" is passage between tomb_mouth and salt_landing.
  Passage salt_stair "the salt stair" is stair between salt_landing and hammer_hall.
  Passage hammer_gate "the Gate of Three Hammers" is gate between hammer_hall and doctrine_hall.
  Passage doctrine_way "the end of the painted hall" is doorway between doctrine_hall and face_room.
  Passage behind_eye "the way behind the left eye" is crawl between face_room and door_hall hidden until eye_way_known.
  Passage true_door "the door that is not there" is doorway between door_hall and breaths_room hidden until true_door_known.
  Passage pit_climb "the oubliette shaft" is shaft between oubliette and door_hall one way taking 1 hour needing climbing or rope.
  Passage breath_way "the far side of the Room of Three Breaths" is passage between breaths_room and gearworks
    opening when exhaling(fells) "Between the Room of Three Breaths and the Gearworks the salt-dust is up in a roaring white wall, drawn in toward a grating as if into a mouth. Nobody crosses it on the in-breath.".
  Passage gallery_walk "the gallery walk" is passage between gearworks and warder_gallery.
  Passage core_stair "the core stair" is stair between gearworks and false_heart taking 10 minutes.
  Passage plinth_way "the way behind the plinth" is passage between false_heart and warder_hall hidden until plinth_known.
  Passage warder_end "the end of the Warder's corridor" is passage between warder_hall and locks_room.
  Passage heart_door "the Door of Three Locks" is door between locks_room and heart_chamber.
  Passage keepers_rise "the keepers' road" is passage between heart_chamber and stair_foot taking 3 hours
    opening when sungClean(fells) or sealed(fells) "A road goes up from the Keeper's Chair, closed by a slab carved with giants' signs; it opens only to keepers.".

  // What it costs.
  Hazard unmaking "Unmade" means "Kill ally.".
  Hazard tread_fall "The false tread" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Hazard bronze_blow "The bronze hammer's answer" means "Deal (3d6) necrotic damage to ally unless constitution save against (14).".
  Hazard lid_needle "The right lid's needle" means "Deal (1d6) poison damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13). Apply poisoned to ally for 3 turns unless constitution save against (12).".
  Hazard blades "The scything door" means "Deal (4d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Hazard brine_spray "The brine door" means "Deal (3d6) poison damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Hazard crushing "The falling door" means "Deal (4d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Hazard burning_salt "The burning door" means "Deal (3d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Hazard salt_choke "The in-breath's dust" means "Deal (1d6) poison damage to ally unless constitution save against (13).".
  Hazard scald "The Gearworks' steam" means "Deal (3d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Hazard ceiling_fall "The roof of the false heart" means "Deal (4d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Hazard stays_behind "The one who stays" means "Kill ally.".

  Observe tmouth_scene at tomb_mouth when true "The long throat ends on a floor of red stone, smooth as the inside of a cheek. Ahead, a passage. Cut over it, very small, in the smiths' square hand: TURN BACK. HE IS ONLY SLEEPING.".
  Observe landing_scene at salt_landing when true "A stair of white salt goes down into the dark, each tread cut sharp and unworn. Nobody has walked on it for a thousand years.".

  // 1. The salt stair: the third tread is no tread.
  Thing false_tread "the third tread of the salt stair" on salt_stair {
    State whole dangerous "The treads of the salt stair are cut sharp and white, every one alike.".
    State found "The third tread of the salt stair has fallen away on a hinge of salt into a black slot. There is room to step over it.".
    Hurts with tread_fall when whole then found.
  }
  Rule tread_shown when tried(false_tread, prodding) and state(false_tread, whole)
    says "The pole goes down on the third tread and the tread goes down with it, swinging away on a hinge of salt into a slot that goes down further than you can hear." {
    Assert state(false_tread, found).
  }

  // 2. The Gate of Three Hammers: iron wakes the sleeper; bronze wakes the dead; salt sleeps.
  Observe hammer_scene at hammer_hall when true "A gate of grey iron fills the hall's end. Three hammers hang before it on chains: one of iron, one of bronze, one of red salt. Cut over the gate: IRON WAKES THE SLEEPER. BRONZE WAKES THE DEAD. STRIKE WITH WHAT IS SLEEPING, AND PASS INSTEAD.".
  Thing gate_bar "the Gate of Three Hammers" on hammer_gate {
    State shut blocking "The grey gate is shut. It has no lock, no handle and no hinges you can see.".
    State open "The grey gate has swung inward, silent, on hinges that were not there before.".
  }
  Action strike_iron(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the gate with the iron hammer" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hammer_hall) and state(gate_bar, shut).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert strikes(unmaking, actor). Increase stirring(fells) by 1. }
    Result "The iron rings on the iron, and the ring goes on and on, down into the floor, and under your feet the whole mountain flinches. The one who swung the hammer is standing very still. Then they are not standing at all.".
  }
  Action strike_bronze(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the gate with the bronze hammer" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hammer_hall) and state(gate_bar, shut).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert strikes(bronze_blow, actor). Increase stirring(fells) by 1. }
    Result "The bronze booms. Something cold comes up out of the floor like water out of a sponge, and through whoever is nearest, and away.".
  }
  Action strike_salt(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the gate with the hammer of salt" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hammer_hall) and state(gate_bar, shut).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert state(gate_bar, open). }
    Result "The salt hammer makes no sound at all against the iron. It crumbles in your hand to red dust. The gate swings open.".
  }

  // 3. The Hall of Doctrine: it teaches, and it lies once, at the Smith-Master's order.
  Observe doctrine_scene at doctrine_hall when true "A long gallery, painted from floor to vault in colours a thousand years old. Panel after panel shows the smiths at their work in this tomb, as a lesson: a smith prodding a stair with a pole; a smith with a red hammer at a gate; a smith creeping past a great face by its left eye; a smith searching a wall between painted doors; a smith crossing a dusty room while a giant breathes out; three wheels, with a smith setting them. The last panel shows a smith kneeling to a figure in a crown, saying words.".
  Discovery panels_read "The Hall of Doctrine's last panels, read close: the wheels of the Gearworks set iron at rest, salt at rest, bone awake; and, under the kneeling smith, the doctrine, which the crowned figure answers.".
  Observe panels_teach at doctrine_hall when true "Close to, the panel of the wheels has words painted under each: IRON, REST. SALT, REST. BONE, WAKE. Under the kneeling smith: WHAT WAKES, KILLS." teaches panels_read.

  // 4. The Sleeper's Face: never go where he is awake.
  Observe sface_scene at face_room when true "The end of the hall is a face. A titan's face, cut in red stone, as tall as a house: eyes closed, mouth open. The mouth is perfectly black. Nothing in it reflects your light. It makes no sound, and the air does not move in it.".
  Action enter_mouth(actor: group, site: place) "Walk into the Sleeper's open mouth" {
    Description "It is wide enough for a cart. Beyond it there is only black.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, face_room).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert strikes(unmaking, actor). }
    Result "The first of you steps into the black, and is not anywhere. No sound. No sign. The black is just as it was.".
  }
  Thing left_lid "the Sleeper's left eyelid" at face_room {
    State lidded "The left eyelid of the face, on your left as you face it, is a slab of red stone as big as a door.".
    State pressed "The left eyelid has sunk into the stone, and behind it a low way runs back into the dark.".
    Tries pushing.
  }
  Thing right_lid "the Sleeper's right eyelid" at face_room {
    State lidded "The right eyelid of the face is a slab of red stone as big as a door, with a crack at its edge.".
    State sprung "A needle as long as a finger stands out of the crack at the right eyelid's edge.".
    Tries pushing.
  }
  Discovery eye_way_known "Behind the Sleeper's left eyelid, a low way runs on into the dark.".
  Observe eye_opens at face_room when state(left_lid, pressed) "Where the left eyelid was, a low way runs back into the dark." teaches eye_way_known.
  Rule left_gives when tried(left_lid, pushing) and state(left_lid, lidded)
    says "The left eyelid sinks under your hands with a sigh of air, like a sleeper's breath, and the stone behind it slides away." {
    Assert state(left_lid, pressed).
  }
  Rule right_bites when tried(right_lid, pushing) and state(right_lid, lidded)
    says "Something in the crack at the right lid's edge goes snick." {
    Assert state(right_lid, sprung). Assert strikes(lid_needle, party).
  }

  // 5. The Hall of Doors: every door you can see is a death; the door is the one that is not there.
  Observe doors_scene at door_hall when true "A long hall with six doors along its walls, three to a side, each of a different wood, each with a different handle: bone, bronze, iron, salt, glass, horn. The end wall is bare red stone.".
  Thing door_bone "the door with the bone handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of pale ash with a handle of bone.". State open "The ash door hangs open on a blank wall.". Change open_bone "Open the door with the bone handle" from shut to open. }
  Thing door_bronze "the door with the bronze handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of oak with a handle of bronze.". State open "The oak door hangs open on a blank wall, scored with blade-marks.". Change open_bronze "Open the door with the bronze handle" from shut to open. }
  Thing door_iron "the door with the iron handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of black yew with a handle of iron.". State open "The yew door hangs open on nothing; the floor beyond it was never there.". Change open_iron "Open the door with the iron handle" from shut to open. }
  Thing door_salt "the door with the salt handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of pine with a handle of white salt.". State open "The pine door hangs open on a wall of crumbled salt.". Change open_salt "Open the door with the salt handle" from shut to open. }
  Thing door_glass "the door with the glass handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of pear-wood with a handle of glass.". State open "The pear-wood door hangs open on a blackened wall.". Change open_glass "Open the door with the glass handle" from shut to open. }
  Thing door_horn "the door with the horn handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of elm with a handle of horn.". State open "The elm door hangs open on a slab of fallen stone.". Change open_horn "Open the door with the horn handle" from shut to open. }
  Relation sprungDoor(entity).
  Rule bone_door when state(door_bone, open) and not sprungDoor(door_bone) says "Behind the ash door is a wall, and the wall breathes out a fine white salt that burns the eyes and throat." { Assert sprungDoor(door_bone). Assert strikes(brine_spray, party). }
  Rule bronze_door when state(door_bronze, open) and not sprungDoor(door_bronze) says "The oak door opens on a wall, and out of a slot in the wall a blade the length of a man comes round at waist height." { Assert sprungDoor(door_bronze). Assert strikes(blades, party). }
  Rule iron_door when state(door_iron, open) and not sprungDoor(door_iron) says "The yew door swings outward and the floor under you swings with it, down." { Assert sprungDoor(door_iron). Assert at(party, oubliette). }
  Rule salt_door when state(door_salt, open) and not sprungDoor(door_salt) says "The salt handle crumbles. So does the wall behind the door, and the roof above it, all at once." { Assert sprungDoor(door_salt). Assert strikes(crushing, party). }
  Rule glass_door when state(door_glass, open) and not sprungDoor(door_glass) says "Behind the pear-wood door the air catches fire." { Assert sprungDoor(door_glass). Assert strikes(burning_salt, party). }
  Rule horn_door when state(door_horn, open) and not sprungDoor(door_horn) says "The elm door opens and the slab above it, which you had not noticed, comes down." { Assert sprungDoor(door_horn). Assert strikes(crushing, party). Increase stirring(fells) by 1. }
  Discovery true_door_known "In the bare end wall of the Hall of Doors, a door with no frame and no handle, cut so fine its edges are a hair." {
    Found by searching door_hall "You go over the bare end wall a hand's breadth at a time. Low down, a hair-fine line; then another, upright; then the shape of a door with no frame and no handle, which swings when you lean on it.".
  }
  Discovery iron_drop_known "Behind the door with the iron handle, the floor of the Hall of Doors swings down into a pit.".
  Observe iron_drop_seen at door_hall when state(door_iron, open) "Beyond the yew door the floor hangs down on a hinge over a black drop." teaches iron_drop_known.
  Passage iron_drop "the drop behind the yew door" is shaft between door_hall and oubliette one way hidden until iron_drop_known.
  Observe oubliette_scene at oubliette when true "A round pit of red stone, smooth, very deep. Far above, a square of less dark. On the floor, the bones of three people who were not patient, and scratched on the wall by one who was: THE SHAFT HAS HOLDS. FEEL FOR THEM.".

  // 6. The Room of Three Breaths: out is open.
  Observe breaths_scene at breaths_room when exhaling(fells) "A long room of red stone. A warm wind blows gently from a grating in the far wall, and the floor is drifted with salt-dust like snow, rippled. The far door stands clear.".
  Observe breaths_in at breaths_room when not exhaling(fells) "The wind in the long room has turned, and the salt-dust is up off the floor in a roaring white wall, pouring toward the grating in the far wall. You cannot see your hand.".
  Rule dust_chokes when at(party, breaths_room) and not exhaling(fells)
    says "The salt-dust is in your mouth, your nose, your eyes." { Assert strikes(salt_choke, party). }

  // 7. The Gearworks: iron at rest, salt awake, bone at rest. The painted panel lies.
  Observe gear_scene at gearworks when true "A chamber full of machinery: three great wheels standing on their edges, one of iron, one of red salt, one of bone, each as tall as a mill-wheel and each marked round its rim REST and WAKE. A lever as long as a spear stands up out of the floor. A stair goes down beyond a grating; a gallery goes off along the wall.".
  Thing iron_wheel "the iron wheel" at gearworks {
    State awake "The iron wheel stands with WAKE uppermost.". State rest "The iron wheel stands with REST uppermost.".
    Change iron_rest "Turn the iron wheel to REST" from awake to rest. Change iron_wake "Turn the iron wheel to WAKE" from rest to awake.
  }
  Thing salt_wheel "the salt wheel" at gearworks {
    State rest "The salt wheel stands with REST uppermost.". State awake "The salt wheel stands with WAKE uppermost.".
    Change salt_rest "Turn the salt wheel to REST" from awake to rest. Change salt_wake "Turn the salt wheel to WAKE" from rest to awake.
  }
  Thing bone_wheel "the bone wheel" at gearworks {
    State awake "The bone wheel stands with WAKE uppermost.". State rest "The bone wheel stands with REST uppermost.".
    Change bone_rest "Turn the bone wheel to REST" from awake to rest. Change bone_wake "Turn the bone wheel to WAKE" from rest to awake.
  }
  Thing great_lever "the great lever" at gearworks {
    State up "The great lever stands upright.". State down "The great lever is thrown down.".
    Change throw "Throw the great lever" from up to down.
  }
  Thing core_grating "the grating over the core stair" on core_stair {
    State shut blocking "A grating of grey iron closes the stair going down.".
    State open "The grating over the core stair stands open.".
  }
  Rule gears_right when state(great_lever, down) and state(iron_wheel, rest) and state(salt_wheel, awake) and state(bone_wheel, rest) and state(core_grating, shut)
    says "Somewhere in the walls a long chain runs, and the grating over the stair rises into the roof." { Assert state(core_grating, open). }
  Rule gears_wrong when state(great_lever, down) and state(core_grating, shut) and not (state(iron_wheel, rest) and state(salt_wheel, awake) and state(bone_wheel, rest))
    says "The lever goes down, and the wheels shudder, and every joint in the machinery blows white steam at once." { Assert strikes(scald, party). Assert state(great_lever, up). Increase stirring(fells) by 1. }

  // 8. The Warder: kills what moves while it is wound; it can be unwound only from the gallery above.
  Observe wgallery_scene at warder_gallery when true "A narrow gallery high in the wall over a long corridor. Below, a figure of grey iron stands in the middle of the corridor. Beside you, in the gallery wall, a great key is set in a spring-case, like a clock's.".
  Thing warder_spring "the Warder's spring" at warder_gallery {
    State wound "The great key stands in its spring-case, the spring tight.".
    State unwound "The great key has been turned back; the spring lies slack in its case.".
    Change unwind "Turn the great key back and let the Warder's spring run down" from wound to unwound needing brawn or lockwork.
  }
  Person warder "the Warder" at warder_hall {
    Role "a figure of grey iron, twice a man's height, with blades for hands". Species automaton. Level 14. Temperament obedient.
    Comes "The Warder moves. It is very fast for something so heavy.".
  }
  Rule warder_strikes when at(party, warder_hall) and state(warder_spring, wound) and able(warder) { Assert assails(warder, party). }
  Observe warder_still at warder_hall when state(warder_spring, unwound) "The Warder stands in the middle of the corridor with its blade-hands at its sides, run down, like a clock nobody wound.".

  // 9. The false heart, and the last of the Hollow Smiths.
  Observe fheart_scene at false_heart when not state(decoy, taken) "A chamber like the inside of a crown. On a plinth in the middle, a heart of red crystal as big as a cart, glowing, beating slowly, beautifully. Before it stands a tall figure in a smith's leather apron gone black with age, with a crown of iron on its skull, quite still.".
  Thing decoy "the great red heart" at false_heart {
    State resting "The heart of red crystal glows on its plinth.".
    State taken "The plinth is bare and cracked. Red crystal lies in shards across the floor.".
    Change pry "Prise the great red heart from its plinth" from resting to taken needing brawn.
  }
  Person ardath "the crowned figure" at false_heart {
    Role "a tall figure in a smith's apron, crowned with iron". Species lich. Level 13. Peaceable.
    State keeping "The crowned figure stands before the heart with its hands folded on a smith's hammer. It watches you with nothing in its eye-sockets.".
  }
  Rule ardath_rises when state(decoy, taken) and not hostile(ardath, party)
    says "The roof of the chamber comes down in red slabs. Through the dust the crowned figure lifts its hammer, and its voice is a forge-bellows: 'THIEF.'" {
    Assert strikes(ceiling_fall, party). Assert hostile(ardath, party). Assert assails(ardath, party). Increase stirring(fells) by 1.
  }
  Discovery plinth_known "Behind the plinth of the false heart, a way goes on, for those the crowned figure lets pass.".
  Topic ardath_doctrine with ardath "Say the doctrine of the Hollow Smiths to the crowned figure" when knows(actor, doctrine_known) and not hostile(ardath, actor) once {
    Says "'What wakes, kills,' you say. The crowned figure answers, in a voice like old iron: 'What kills, wakes.' It is quiet a long time. 'You are not ours. But you have our words.' It turns, and lays a hand on the plinth. 'This is a lie. I keep it so that thieves stop here. I have kept it for a thousand years. I do not remember why.' The plinth slides aside. 'The true heart is beyond. He is sleeping. Do not wake him. Do not kill him.' Its hand stays on the plinth. 'I was paid to kill him, once. We all were. I am sorry. Tell him I am sorry.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, plinth_known). }
  }

  // 10. The Door of Three Locks: the keepers' ring, the Smith-Master's hammer, the Abbess's Eye.
  Observe locks_scene at locks_room when true "A door of red stone, round, like a great closed eye. In it, three sockets: a round one the size of a hub; a narrow one the shape of a little hammer's head; and a broad shallow one, lid-shaped.".
  Thing ring_lock "the round socket" on heart_door {
    State empty blocking "The round socket in the door is empty.". State filled "The keepers' ring sits in the round socket.".
    Change set_ring "Set the keepers' ring in the round socket" from empty to filled needing keepers_ring.
  }
  Thing token_lock "the narrow socket" on heart_door {
    State empty blocking "The narrow socket is empty.". State filled "The Smith-Master's hammer sits in the narrow socket.".
    Change set_token "Set the Smith-Master's hammer in the narrow socket" from empty to filled needing smith_token.
  }
  Thing eye_lock "the lid-shaped socket" on heart_door {
    State empty blocking "The lid-shaped socket is empty.". State filled "The Abbess's Eye lies in the lid-shaped socket, and is open.".
    Change set_eye "Lay the Abbess's Eye in the lid-shaped socket" from empty to filled needing abbess_eye.
  }

  // 11. The Keeper's Chair.
  Observe chair_scene at heart_chamber when true "A small chamber, plain, round, warm. In the floor, in a basin of grey stone, the heart of Thrume: not crystal, flesh, dark red, the size of a cottage, beating once in a long while. The whole room moves with it. Beside the basin, a chair of grey stone, carved with the giants' signs, empty.".
  Relation seated(group).
  Passage into_dream "the dream beyond the Chair" is passage between heart_chamber and cloud_landing taking 1 hour
    opening when seated(party) "The Chair is empty. Whoever sits in it, the keepers say, sits in his dream.".
  Action sit_chair(actor: group, site: place) "Sit in the Keeper's Chair, and go into his dream" {
    Description "The stone is warm. The giants' signs on it are the same three, over and over: a mountain, a heart, a closed eye.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart_chamber) and not seated(actor) and not woken(fells).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert seated(actor). }
    Result "You sit. The heart beats, once, and the room goes away. You are standing on a cloud, and the cloud holds you, and above you a palace of white stone floats in a sky so close you could touch it.".
  }
  Action stay_keeper(actor: group, site: place) "One of you stays in the Chair, and keeps him sleeping" {
    Description "The keepers say someone must sit by the heart and sing, for ever, or he will stir again. Nobody who stays comes back.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart_chamber) and not sealed(fells) and not woken(fells) and not sungClean(fells).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert sealed(fells). Assert strikes(stays_behind, actor). Set stirring(fells) to 0. }
    Result "One of you sits down in the Chair, and puts a hand on the warm stone of the basin, and begins, very low, to hum. The heart slows. When the rest of you go, the one in the Chair does not look up.".
  }
  Action cut_heart(actor: group, site: place) "Cut into the heart of Thrume for the Margravine's salt" {
    Description "The heart is blood, and the blood is the red salt, and there is more of it here than in all the workings. Ebb would win its war.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart_chamber) and capable(actor, digging) and not cutOut(fells) and not woken(fells).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert cutOut(fells). Set stirring(fells) to 0. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 400. }
    Result "It takes a long time. The heart does not wake. It beats slower, and slower, and the red that comes out of it goes hard and glittering in the air as it runs, and you fill sack after sack. At the end it beats once more, and then it does not, and the whole mountain is very still, and very cold.".
  }
  Action wake_heart(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the heart of Thrume, and wake him" {
    Description "What kills, wakes.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart_chamber) and not woken(fells).
    Time 1.
    On success { Set stirring(fells) to 10. }
    Result "You strike. The heart stops. Then it beats, once, so hard you are thrown off your feet, and again, and again, faster, and the floor tilts, and does not tilt back.".
  }

  Objective cross_tomb when at(party, tomb_mouth) and not seated(party) "The heart of Thrume lies at the bottom of the Hollow Smiths' tomb.".
}

Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The fortnight ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Tessary keeps its days by the ebbs. Low water comes twice a day, about the eleventh hour and about the eleventh of
  // the night, and lasts some five hours each time; while it lasts the outer basin drains through the Throat and
  // Lowtide stands out of the water. The night ebb at two in the morning is the one the city counts: each is a night of
  // the fortnight. On the first, the eighth and the fifteenth it is a spring ebb, the lowest of all, and on those
  // nights the Balance takes its interest. The fifteenth is the Feast of Settlement, when the war note falls due.
  Query lowWater() means hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) <= 14 or hour(clock) >= 22 or hour(clock) <= 2.
  // The hour the water turns, when anyone still down in Lowtide had better be on a roof.
  Query turning() means hour(clock) == 14 or hour(clock) == 2.
  Measure night(place). Relation counted(place).
  // The first night counted is the first two o'clock at least five hours after the company comes.
  Rule night_turns when hour(clock) == 2 and not counted(ossel) and watch(clock) >= 30 {
    Increase night(ossel) by 1. Assert counted(ossel). }
  Rule night_passes when hour(clock) != 2 and counted(ossel) { Retract counted(ossel). }
  Query springNight() means night(ossel) == 1 or night(ossel) == 8 or night(ossel) == 15.
  // From the evening of the fourteenth night's day the city is keeping the Feast.
  Query feastEve() means night(ossel) >= 14.

  // Where word of the city's doings reaches the company: anywhere in Tessary, not under the sea. A company that has
  // been below hears what happened when it comes up.
  Relation cityRoom(place).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(throat_head).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(tidewall).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(legion_yard).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(tideline_steps).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(scriveners_row).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(terraces).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(withies).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(landgate).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(saltgate).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(pans).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(teazle_room).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(drum_taproom).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(sault_office).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(warehouse_floor).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(cistern).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(muster_hall).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(seals_hall).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(seals_inner).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(exchequer_room).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(pounce_stall).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(council_chamber).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(kings_rooms).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(marrable_room).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(chapel).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(chandlery).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(causeway_end).
  Query inTessary() means at(party, ?p) and cityRoom(?p).

  // ── The calling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At a spring ebb the Balance calls a dozen of the collateral, in the order of the Muster's roll. They come down
  // through the Withies in step, barefoot, set their boots together on the top step and walk out over the wet sand
  // toward the Hall of Oaths. In the morning their families find the boots.
  Measure held(place). Measure callings(place). Relation bootsOnSteps(place). Relation callingDue(place).
  Initially Set held(ossel) to 138. Initially Set callings(ossel) to 0.
  Rule calling_due when counted(ossel) and springNight() and night(ossel) < 15 and callings(ossel) < night(ossel) and not interestPaid(ossel) {
    Assert callingDue(ossel). Set callings(ossel) to night(ossel). }
  Relation interestPaid(place).
  Rule interest_waived when counted(ossel) and springNight() and callings(ossel) < night(ossel) and interestPaid(ossel) {
    Set callings(ossel) to night(ossel). Retract interestPaid(ossel). }
  Rule calling_happens when callingDue(ossel) {
    Retract callingDue(ossel). Increase held(ossel) by 12. Assert bootsOnSteps(ossel). Assert calledLast(ossel). }
  Relation calledLast(place).
  Rule boots_taken when bootsOnSteps(ossel) and hour(clock) == 9 { Retract bootsOnSteps(ossel). }
  Rule calling_told at tideline_steps when calledLast(ossel) says "They come down through the Withies a little after two, twelve of them, in step, though nobody is calling the step. Barefoot. Their eyes are open. At the top of the Tideline Steps each of them stops, and stoops, and sets his boots side by side on the stone, toes to the water, and straightens, and walks down into the sea. The water is very low. They walk out over the sand toward the walls in the basin, getting smaller, keeping step, until the dark has them." teaches calling_witnessed { Retract calledLast(ossel). }
  Rule calling_unseen when calledLast(ossel) { Retract calledLast(ossel). }
  Discovery calling_witnessed "At the spring ebb, twelve veterans of the Long Muster walked barefoot and in step down the Tideline Steps and out across the drained basin toward the drowned city, as if called, and left their boots paired on the top step.".
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/compan:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // The company of the campaign played alone: one traveller come down the marsh road with a little coin (placed.kyr is
  // the world's own company, come in by the Causeway).
  Company party "You" of 1 at causeway_end.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 12. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
}

Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The Assessor about the city ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // By day the inventory in the Withies; by night the Tideline Steps, watching the water.
  Rule tally_to_steps when hour(clock) >= 21 and at(tally, withies) and not travelsWith(tally, party) and not tallyBelow(ossel) {
    Retract at(tally, withies). Assert at(tally, tideline_steps). }
  Rule tally_to_withies when hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 21 and at(tally, tideline_steps) and not travelsWith(tally, party) and not tallyBelow(ossel) {
    Retract at(tally, tideline_steps). Assert at(tally, withies). }
  Relation tallyBelow(place).
  // What the Assessor does with a contradiction: a filing.
  Relation tallyHeardPrior(place). Relation tallyKnowsDominion(place).
  Topic tell_tally_prior with tally "Tell the Assessor that the city promised its soldiers land and a pension before it pledged them" when knows(actor, enlist_promise) and knows(actor, promise_weight) and not tallyHeardPrior(ossel) once {
    Says "The Assessor stops writing. 'The recruiting bill,' they say. 'Eleven years ago. The pledge was twelve.' They are silent for a while. 'No. The bill is eleven years old; the Muster was raised eleven years ago; the note was drawn when the war was a year old. The promise to the soldiers was made first.' They look at the ledger as if it had said something rude. 'A prior promise, of the same weight, to the same persons, unkept. And the city pledged those persons to us as if they were its own.' A long pause. 'That is not on my inventory. I find I cannot stop thinking about it.'".
    On discuss { Assert tallyHeardPrior(ossel). }
  }
  Topic tell_tally_dominion with tally "Tell the Assessor that the Factor means to buy the note in order to govern the city" when knows(actor, sault_bid) and not tallyKnowsDominion(ossel) once {
    Says "'To govern,' says the Assessor. 'With the collateral.' Their voice does not change; the ruled lines on their face do. 'A note may be taken up at foreclosure by whoever pledges its weight. It may not be taken up for dominion. That is the ninth chapter.' They write for some time. 'I will file an objection to the Factor's bid with the Broker's superiors. It will be heard. Whether it is heard in time I cannot say.'".
    On discuss { Assert tallyKnowsDominion(ossel). }
  }
  Relation objectionFiled(place).
  Rule objection_heard when tallyKnowsDominion(ossel) and night(ossel) >= 12 and not objectionFiled(ossel) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel) { Assert objectionFiled(ossel). Assert brokerSuspended(ossel). }

  // The indictment: only an Assessor who has seen the Room of Defaults, and kept faith with the company that showed
  // it to them, will bring it.
  Action ask_indictment(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Assessor to indict the Comptroller before the Assembly" {
    Speaker tally. Time 1.
    Grave "If the Assembly finds against him, the Comptroller will unravel, or at best be put down from his office; and the Assessor will have done the gravest thing a Scruple can do.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and travelsWith(tally, actor) and tallySawDefaults(ossel)
      and not brokeFaith(actor) and not indictmentFiled(ossel) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel) and not caughtCopying(actor)
      and (tallyHeardPrior(ossel) or keptFaith(actor) or tallyKnowsDominion(ossel)).
    On success { Assert indictmentFiled(ossel). Retract travelsWith(tally, actor). Assert tallyBelow(ossel). Assert at(tally, clerks_hall).
      Assert holdingAdmits(actor). }
    Result "The Assessor is quiet for a long time. 'Yes,' they say. 'It must be one of us, and it must be someone who has read the entry, and I have read it.' They take out a fresh sheet and write on it, standing, in a hand that does not shake. When they have done they fold it once. 'The Assembly will sit in the Weighing Chamber on the night of the Settlement, from midnight, and the Notary will come out of the Holding to sit with it. I will be there. You should be there; you read it with me.' They look at you. 'I am leaving you here. I have a great deal to prepare and I find I would rather be alone.'".
  }
  Rule indictment_spoken when indictmentFiled(ossel) and swornSilence(party) and not forswornParty(party)
    says "Somewhere under the sea a promise of silence you made to the Comptroller breaks, and you feel it go, a cold hand laid flat between your shoulders." {
    Assert forswornParty(party). }

  // ── The Release ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Durrance, if she is free and has thought it through, can call the Muster to the Oath Stone on the night of the
  // Feast to release the city from its promise to them; the Factor's men will try to break it up.
  Relation releaseCalled(place). Relation releaseGathered(place). Relation releaseBroken(place). Relation releaseHeld(place).
  Query cityPaying() means votePassed(ossel) and not sealStolen(ossel).
  Topic ask_release with durrance "Ask Durrance to call the Muster to the Oath Stone on the night of the Feast, to release the city" when durranceKnowsRelease(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) and not releaseCalled(ossel) and not cityPaying() and night(ossel) <= 14 and not serves(durrance, sault) once {
    Says "Durrance has had her days to think, and she has thought. 'Eleven years,' she says. 'And the Board votes no, or yes and then lets the Factor walk off with the Seal, and either way the lads stay under the sea.' She stands up. 'So we do it. The Muster on the Stone at the Feast, as many as I can get, and we say it: we hold you quit. Keep your land. Keep your pension. Give us back our own.' She laughs, short. 'I'll have to tell them it was my idea. They'll never stand for it if it was a stranger's.' She looks at you. 'The Factor will send her lightermen. Be there.'".
    On discuss { Assert releaseCalled(ossel). }
  }
  Rule release_gathers when releaseCalled(ossel) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 22 and not releaseGathered(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and at(durrance, ?p) {
    Assert releaseGathered(ossel). Retract at(durrance, ?p). Assert at(durrance, legion_yard). }
  Rule release_gathers_with when releaseCalled(ossel) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 22 and not releaseGathered(ossel) and travelsWith(durrance, party) {
    Assert releaseGathered(ossel). }
  Observe release_scene at legion_yard when releaseGathered(ossel) and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel) "The Legion Yard is full of soldiers. Not in step, not in ranks: a crowd of men and women in old red coats and whatever else they have, with lanterns, thousands of them, filling the Yard and the wall-walk and the lane, and more coming. Durrance stands on the Oath Stone's plinth with one hand on the Stone. It is very quiet for so many people. Out on the Tidewall the Feast's bonfires are burning, and the city's year of contracts is going up in sparks.".
  Rule lightermen_come when releaseGathered(ossel) and hour(clock) == 23 and night(ossel) == 14 and able(lightermen) and not saultStopped(ossel) and at(lightermen, ?p) and not at(lightermen, legion_yard) and not fiskTurned(fisk) {
    Retract at(lightermen, ?p). Assert at(lightermen, legion_yard). }
  Rule lightermen_at_yard at legion_yard when at(lightermen, legion_yard) and releaseGathered(ossel) and at(party, legion_yard) and not assails(lightermen, party) and able(lightermen) and not released(ossel)
    says "There is a shout from the gate. Sault's lightermen are coming through the crowd with cudgels, shoving, a dozen of them, making for the plinth." {
    Assert assails(lightermen, party). }
  Rule release_broken when releaseGathered(ossel) and at(lightermen, legion_yard) and able(lightermen) and hour(clock) == 0 and not at(party, legion_yard) and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel) {
    Assert releaseBroken(ossel). }
  Rule release_broken_told when releaseBroken(ossel) and not knows(party, release_broken_known)
    and inTessary() says "Word comes from the Legion Yard: the Factor's lightermen broke up the Muster at the Oath Stone with cudgels, and the Watch stood by, and Durrance was carried off the plinth with a broken head." teaches release_broken_known { }
  Discovery release_broken_known "The Factor's lightermen broke up the Muster's gathering at the Oath Stone on the Feast night.".
  Relation saultStopped(place).
  Action stand_release(actor: group, site: place) "Stand with the Muster at the Oath Stone while they say it" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, legion_yard) and releaseGathered(ossel)
      and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) >= 23
      and not (at(lightermen, legion_yard) and able(lightermen)).
    On success { Assert released(ossel). }
    Result "Durrance says it first, alone, with her hand on the Stone, in a voice that carries to the back of the Yard without being raised: 'The city of Tessary promised me land and a pension if I came home. I came home. I hold it quit.' Then the Third Company says it, ragged, and then the Yard, all of it, eight thousand voices or near enough, not together, a long rolling noise like surf: I hold it quit. And under your feet, under the Yard, under the Tidewall and the drowned streets, something very large and very far down settles by a hair's breadth, like a pan of a scale coming level.".
  }
  Rule release_by_itself when releaseGathered(ossel) and hour(clock) == 1 and night(ossel) == 14 and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel)
    and not (at(lightermen, legion_yard) and able(lightermen)) { Assert released(ossel). }

  // ── The Assembly ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation assemblySits(place). Relation assemblyHeard(place). Relation mercyAsked(place). Relation comptrollerUnravelled(place).
  Relation comptrollerDeposed(place).
  Rule assembly_convenes when indictmentFiled(ossel) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 0 and not assemblySits(ossel) {
    Assert assemblySits(ossel). Retract at(tally, clerks_hall). Assert at(tally, weighing_chamber).
    Retract at(comptroller, comptroller_office). Assert at(comptroller, weighing_chamber). }
  Observe assembly_scene at weighing_chamber when assemblySits(ossel) and not noteVoid(ossel) "The Assembly of the Scruples is sitting. They stand in rows on the floor of the nave under the Balance, all of them, grey and pale and silent, with their ruled hands folded. At the foot of the Balance the Notary stands, come out of the Holding for the first time in five hundred years, a figure drawn in lines of light. The Comptroller stands alone before it. The Assessor stands alone before him, with one folded sheet.".
  Action testify(actor: group, site: place) "Testify before the Assembly to what you read in the Room of Defaults" {
    Time 2.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, weighing_chamber) and assemblySits(ossel)
      and knows(actor, note_designed) and not assemblyHeard(ossel).
    On success { Assert assemblyHeard(ossel). }
    Result "You tell them what you read, and where, and when, and who was with you. The floor of the nave registers every word; the ruled lines along the walls brighten and hold. Nobody interrupts. When you have finished the Notary turns its face of lines to the Comptroller. He does not deny it. He cannot. 'I would draw it again,' he says, to the Assembly, to the Balance, to the nine black lights at the far edge of everything. 'It was the only way to close the hole.'".
  }
  Action ask_mercy(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Assembly to put the Comptroller down from his office, and spare him unravelling" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, weighing_chamber) and assemblyHeard(ossel)
      and not mercyAsked(ossel) and not noteVoid(ossel).
    On success { Assert mercyAsked(ossel). }
    Result "There is a long silence in the nave. Then the Notary speaks. 'A promise made to be broken is no promise,' it says. 'That is the law. What becomes of the one who made it is the Assembly's.' It looks at the Assessor. The Assessor looks at the Comptroller for a long time. 'He has kept the ledger for eleven hundred years,' they say. 'Let him keep the archive. Under supervision. Without the black glass.' And the rows of grey figures bow, all together, which is apparently how the Scruples vote.".
  }
  Rule note_voided when assemblySits(ossel) and hour(clock) == 1 and night(ossel) == 14 and not noteVoid(ossel) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel)
    says "In the Weighing Chamber the Notary lays a line of light through the sheet of black glass in the pan, end to end, and the glass goes grey, and then clear, and then is nothing. 'Void,' it says. 'A promise made to be broken is no promise. The collateral is released.' The pointer of the Balance swings, a long slow arc, and stops where it stops: not level. There is still a hole in the ledger the size of a city. But it is the Comptroller's, now, and not the Muster's." {
    Assert noteVoid(ossel). }
  Rule comptroller_unravels when noteVoid(ossel) and not mercyAsked(ossel) and not comptrollerUnravelled(ossel)
    says "The Comptroller does not cry out. The ruled lines of his face begin to come apart, very slowly, like a page left in rain, and then less slowly, and then he is a coat with nobody in it, standing at the foot of the Balance with its hands out, as if it wanted to be given something. Two of the Weights come and lead it away toward the stair, quite gently. Nobody watches it go except the Assessor." {
    Assert comptrollerUnravelled(ossel). Retract at(comptroller, weighing_chamber). }
  Rule comptroller_put_down when noteVoid(ossel) and mercyAsked(ossel) and not comptrollerDeposed(ossel) { Assert comptrollerDeposed(ossel). }

  // ── The Factor on the night ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // If her broker is suspended she comes to the Weighing Chamber herself, with lightermen, by the cistern and the
  // drowned streets, to pledge in person at foreclosure; if he is not, her bid is lodged on the fourteenth day.
  Relation saultBidLodged(place). Relation saultInChamber(place). Relation saultWarden(place).
  Rule bid_lodged when night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 12 and not brokerSuspended(ossel) and able(sault) and not saultBidLodged(ossel) {
    Assert saultBidLodged(ossel). }
  Rule sault_goes_down when night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 23 and brokerSuspended(ossel) and able(sault) and not saultInChamber(ossel) and at(sault, ?p) and not saultStopped(ossel) {
    Assert saultInChamber(ossel). Retract at(sault, ?p). Assert at(sault, weighing_chamber). Retract peaceable(sault). }
  Observe sault_in_chamber at weighing_chamber when saultInChamber(ossel) and at(sault, weighing_chamber) and not matured(ossel) "Factor Sault is here, in the nave of the Weighing Chamber, in a sea-cloak still wet from the Hall of Oaths, with a lantern and two lightermen and a paper in her hand. She is looking up at the Balance with her mouth slightly open, like anyone. Then she sees you, and puts the look away. 'Of course,' she says. 'Of course it's you.'".
  Topic sault_terms with sault "Put terms to the Factor: take up the note and call the Muster out only to send them home to their land" when (saultInChamber(ossel) or saultExposed(ossel) or brokerSuspended(ossel)) and knows(actor, sault_bid) and knows(actor, salt_springs) and not saultWarden(ossel) and not matured(ossel) and able(sault) once {
    Says "Factor Sault hears you out with her head on one side. 'Warden of the Settlement,' she says. 'Hold the note and never use it but to send them home. And for that?' You tell her: the salt springs of Hethra, which the war was fought for, and which nobody else in Tessary knows how to work. She laughs. 'You've been talking to Amaury.' She is quiet a long time. 'They'd still owe me,' she says. 'The city. For ever.' She looks at the Balance. 'All right. Write it down, whatever you people write it on. I'll swear it. I'd rather be owed than hated, and I'd rather be either than beaten.'".
    On discuss { Assert saultWarden(ossel). }
  }
  Action stop_sault(actor: group, site: place) "Stand between the Factor and the Balance" {
    Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(sault, site) and saultInChamber(ossel) and able(sault)
      and not saultWarden(ossel) and not matured(ossel) and not assails(sault, actor).
    On success { Assert assails(sault, actor). Assert assails(lightermen, actor). }
    Result "'Don't,' says Factor Sault, almost kindly, and draws.".
  }
  Rule lightermen_with_sault when saultInChamber(ossel) and at(lightermen, ?p) and not at(lightermen, weighing_chamber) and able(lightermen) {
    Retract at(lightermen, ?p). Assert at(lightermen, weighing_chamber). }
  Rule sault_beaten when saultInChamber(ossel) and not able(sault) and not saultStopped(ossel) { Assert saultStopped(ossel). }
  Rule sault_captured when captured(sault, party) and at(party, ?p)
    says "You come round on the floor of the nave with your head ringing. Factor Sault is standing over you, wiping her hands. 'Stay down,' she says. 'It's nearly two.'" {
    Retract captured(sault, party). }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(sault).

  // The Assessor's last resort: in the chamber at the Settlement, with nothing else left, they can take the black
  // glass out of the pan and break it. A Scruple who breaks the note breaks a promise held by the Balance.
  Action ask_tear(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Assessor to take the War Note out of the pan and break it" {
    Speaker tally. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "The Assessor will be breaking a promise the Balance holds. You know what happens to a Scruple who does.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, weighing_chamber) and at(tally, weighing_chamber)
      and tallySawDefaults(ossel) and not indictmentFiled(ossel) and not brokeFaith(actor) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) >= 0
      and hour(clock) < 2 and not released(ossel) and not deedsDelivered(ossel) and not noteTorn(ossel).
    On success { Assert noteTorn(ossel). Assert tallyUnravelled(ossel). Retract travelsWith(tally, actor). Retract willing(tally, actor). Assert tallyBelow(ossel). }
    Result "The Assessor looks at you, and then up at the Balance, for a long moment. 'Yes,' they say. 'Somebody should break it who knows what it is.' They climb the side of the pan like a child climbing into a boat, and walk across the bottom of it to the sheet of black glass, and pick it up in both ruled hands, and break it over their knee. It breaks like ice. The pointer of the Balance swings, slowly, all the way across the dial. And the ruled lines on the Assessor's face begin, very gently, to come undone. 'Oh,' they say, looking at their hands. 'That is what it feels like.' They sit down in the bottom of the pan. 'Tell the child,' they say, 'that the eel was very kind,' and then there is nobody in the grey coat at all.".
  }
  Rule tally_with_party_down when travelsWith(tally, party) and at(party, weighing_chamber) and not at(tally, weighing_chamber) { Assert at(tally, weighing_chamber). }
  Rule tally_off_floor when at(tally, weighing_chamber) and travelsWith(tally, party) and not at(party, weighing_chamber) { Retract at(tally, weighing_chamber). }

  // ── The Settlement ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At the fifteenth spring ebb the note matures. What is true of the city at that moment decides what follows.
  Rule maturity when night(ossel) == 15 and not matured(ossel) { Assert matured(ossel). Assert settling(ossel). }
  Relation settling(place).
  Rule settle_kept when settling(ossel) and deedsDelivered(ossel) { Retract settling(ossel). Assert keptPromise(ossel). Assert discharged(ossel). }
  Rule settle_released when settling(ossel) and released(ossel) { Retract settling(ossel). Assert discharged(ossel). }
  Rule settle_void when settling(ossel) and noteVoid(ossel) { Retract settling(ossel). Assert discharged(ossel). }
  Rule settle_torn when settling(ossel) and noteTorn(ossel) { Retract settling(ossel). Assert discharged(ossel). }
  // A bid for dominion, objected to by an Assessor, fails; a Warden's bid, sworn to send the Muster home, does not.
  Rule settle_taken when settling(ossel) and (saultBidLodged(ossel) or (saultInChamber(ossel) and able(sault) and not saultStopped(ossel)))
    and (not objectionFiled(ossel) or saultWarden(ossel)) {
    Retract settling(ossel). Assert saultHoldsNote(ossel). }
  Rule settle_foreclosed when settling(ossel) { Retract settling(ossel). Assert foreclosed(ossel). }
  // Discharged: every oath in the pan goes home.
  Rule held_wake when discharged(ossel) and heldNow(?s) { Retract heldNow(?s). Retract asleep(?s). Assert cameHome(?s). Assert wokeHome(?s). }
  Rule held_warden when saultHoldsNote(ossel) and saultWarden(ossel) and heldNow(?s) { Retract heldNow(?s). Retract asleep(?s). Assert cameHome(?s). Assert wokeHome(?s). }
  Rule held_count when (discharged(ossel) or saultWarden(ossel) and saultHoldsNote(ossel)) and held(ossel) > 0 { Set held(ossel) to 0. }
  Rule settlement_heard at ranks when discharged(ossel) and not knows(party, held_woke)
    says "All down the Ranks the sleepers open their eyes, together, as if a drum had beaten the stand-down. They look at their hands. They look at each other. Somebody laughs. Somebody starts to cry. Then, without anyone giving the order, they turn, all of them, and begin to walk back across the white floor toward the Door, in step, because they do not know how not to." teaches held_woke { }
  Rule settlement_seen when discharged(ossel) and not at(party, ranks) and not knows(party, held_woke)
    and inTessary() says "At two in the morning, all over the Withies, people wake for no reason and go out onto the boardwalks. The basin is out, lower than anyone has ever seen it. And out in the drowned city, very small, coming up the steps of the Hall of Oaths and across the Forum in the starlight, barefoot and in their shirts and in step, a hundred and sixty soldiers of the Long Muster are walking home." teaches held_woke { }
  Discovery held_woke "At the Settlement the note was discharged, and the held of the Long Muster woke and walked home.".
  Rule muster_called when saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not saultWarden(ossel) and not knows(party, muster_called_known)
    says "At two in the morning, all over Tessary, the soldiers of the Long Muster get up out of their beds, the old ones and the young ones and the one-armed ones, and dress, and go out into the streets, and walk in step through the dark to Saltgate, where Factor Sault is waiting for them on the steps of her countinghouse with a lantern. Her voice carries a long way in the quiet. 'Good morning, lads,' she says. 'You're paid from today.'" teaches muster_called_known { }
  Discovery muster_called_known "At the Settlement Factor Sault took up the War Note and called the Long Muster to Saltgate.".
  Rule muster_warden when saultHoldsNote(ossel) and saultWarden(ossel) and not knows(party, muster_called_known)
    says "At two in the morning the soldiers of the Long Muster wake in their beds all over the city, every one of them, for no reason, and lie listening. Nothing calls them. Out in the drowned city, in the starlight, a hundred and sixty more are walking home across the Forum, and at the head of them, in a wet sea-cloak with a lantern, the Factor of the Salt Moiety is picking her way over the weed and swearing." teaches muster_called_known { }
  Rule foreclosure_told when foreclosed(ossel) and not knows(party, foreclosed_known)
    and inTessary() says "At two in the morning nothing happens. The basin is out, lower than anyone remembers; the Tidewall bonfires have burned down to red; the last contracts of the year are ash. Nobody walks into the sea. Nobody walks out of it. Only, a long way out past the Hall of Oaths, where the outer bar meets the open water, the sea for a moment shows a sky full of stars that are not the stars over Tessary, very bright and close, and then is the sea again." teaches foreclosed_known { }
  Discovery foreclosed_known "At the Settlement the War Note fell in and nobody took it up. The held stay held, and the ledger is uneven at Tessary.".

  // ── What became of them ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Told in the morning after the Settlement, before the book closes.
  Query morning() means night(ossel) >= 15 and hour(clock) >= 7.
  Relation toldFates(place).
  Rule fate_tally_reformer when morning() and noteVoid(ossel) and not tallyFreed(ossel) and not told_tally(ossel) says "The Ninth Assessor sits now at the Comptroller's desk, which they have had moved into the Hall of Clerks where everyone can see it. They have begun to go through the ledger from the first page, with the old city's hole in it, and to write in the margin, for each entry, whether it was honest. It will take them, they estimate, four hundred years. They seem, as far as anyone can tell with a Scruple, happy." { Assert told_tally(ossel). }
  Rule fate_tally_freed when morning() and tallyFreed(ossel) and not told_tally(ossel) says "There is a new stall on Scriveners' Row: CONTRACTS READ, DISPUTES WEIGHED, NO LIES TOLD (NONE). The scrivener behind it has a grey coat and ruled hands and a name nobody in Tessary has heard before, which by the end of the winter nobody finds strange. Pounce says it is unfair competition. Brother Tolley says it is the saint come home. Wick brings them an eel every Fourth-day, and they eat it." { Assert told_tally(ossel). }
  Rule fate_tally_unravelled when morning() and tallyUnravelled(ossel) and not told_tally(ossel) says "Wick Teazle sits on the Tideline Steps every evening at the ebb, with an eel in a paper cone, and watches the doorways of Lowtide where the hollow men stand, looking for one in a grey coat. He has not seen it yet. He does not know what he would do if he did. He thinks he would give it the eel." { Assert told_tally(ossel). }
  Rule fate_tally_plain when morning() and not tallyFreed(ossel) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel) and not noteVoid(ossel) and not told_tally(ossel) says "The Ninth Assessor went below at the Settlement with the inventory complete. The children of the Withies still call the stair at the end of the boardwalk Tally's Step, though none of them can say why." { Assert told_tally(ossel). }
  Relation told_tally(place). Relation told_durrance(place). Relation told_quire(place). Relation told_sault(place).
  Rule fate_durrance_release when morning() and released(ossel) and not told_durrance(ossel) says "Agathe Durrance never takes a penny of the pension she released. She runs the Muffled Drum with Hannelore now, and the Third Company's drum hangs over the bar with its head bare, and on the night of every spring ebb she beats the stand-down on it, at two in the morning, for anyone who might be listening." { Assert told_durrance(ossel). }
  Rule fate_durrance_sault when morning() and serves(durrance, sault) and not told_durrance(ossel) says "Sergeant Durrance sergeants the Factor's Muster, in a good coat, and is fair to them, and is paid, and does not go into the Muffled Drum any more." { Assert told_durrance(ossel). }
  Rule fate_durrance_held when morning() and heldNow(durrance) and not told_durrance(ossel) says "Sergeant Durrance is still standing in the Ranks of the Holding, asleep, with her hands at her sides. At the Muffled Drum her boots stand on the bar under the covered drum, and nobody touches them." { Assert told_durrance(ossel). }
  Rule fate_durrance_home when morning() and not heldNow(durrance) and not serves(durrance, sault) and not released(ossel) and not told_durrance(ossel) says "Sergeant Durrance goes back to the Muffled Drum and drinks one pot, standing, and then goes down to the Tideline Steps to meet the ones coming home, and calls the roll for them on the top step, every name, in order, until her voice goes." { Assert told_durrance(ossel). }
  Rule fate_quire_confessed when morning() and quireConfessed(ossel) and not told_quire(ossel) says "Absalom Quire is put out of the Exchequer by the Board in a vote of seven to nothing, and goes to live in two rooms in the Lettered Quarter, and writes letters for people who cannot, at Pounce's old rates, which annoys Pounce. He is sleeping again." { Assert told_quire(ossel). }
  Rule fate_quire_dead when morning() and quireDrowned(ossel) and not told_quire(ossel) says "Brother Tolley hangs a weight in Saint Evenhand's for Absalom Quire: lead, for a debt. It is the only one in the chapel nobody paid for." { Assert told_quire(ossel). }
  Rule fate_sault_exposed when morning() and saultExposed(ossel) and not saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not told_sault(ossel) says "Factor Sault keeps her pans and her ships and loses her chair on the Board, and is seen every evening on the Tidewall eating eels out of a paper cone, as cheerful as ever, and doing sums." { Assert told_sault(ossel). }
  Rule fate_sault_warden when morning() and saultWarden(ossel) and saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not told_sault(ossel) says "Factor Sault holds the War Note in a frame on the wall of her countinghouse, and never calls on it, and works the salt springs of Hethra by treaty with a king who finds her very amusing. The city owes her everything. She reminds it daily." { Assert told_sault(ossel). }

  // ── Endings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Ending kept "The Kept Promise" when morning() and keptPromise(ossel) "In the spring the old estates of the Moieties along the Ossel are surveyed into strips, and eight thousand soldiers and their families go upriver with ploughs bought on the city's credit, which is now bad, because the city has nothing; but the city kept its word, and the Balance under the sea is level, and the Scruples go back to writing down the small promises of fishwives. The Board meets in a Council House with boarded windows. On the twelfth of Haying there is no procession for the Kneeling. Instead, in the Withies, somebody's mother puts a recruiting bill in the fire, and everyone stands round and watches it burn.".
  Ending release "The Release" when morning() and released(ossel) "The Muster saved the city twice. The second time it paid for the privilege with every penny the city had promised it, and the city knows it, and does not know what to do with the knowledge. The Board votes the Muster a medal. The Muster does not come to collect it. Instead, the veterans of Tessary go to work, on the pans and the boats and in the Lettered Quarter, owing nobody anything, and when the Board next wants a war it finds that nobody in the Withies will answer a drum, and has to think of something else.".
  Ending void "The Void Note" when morning() and noteVoid(ossel) "The note is void and the Muster is home, and the city owes nothing to the Balance and its soldiers everything, as before; the Board will hear the question of the Settlement again in the spring, and this time the public bench will be full. Under the sea the Scruples have a new Comptroller who keeps a hole in the ledger the size of a city in plain sight, and on certain nights, far out past the bar, the sea at Tessary shows other stars. The fishermen have stopped being frightened of it. They say it is good for the eels.".
  Ending torn "The Broken Note" when morning() and noteTorn(ossel) "The note is broken, and the Muster is home, and nobody in Tessary but you knows exactly how. The Scruples enter it as a default by an officer of the Balance, and say nothing more; the Board says nothing at all. In Lowtide the mudlarks say there is a new hollow man in the doorways of the bath-house, in a grey coat, who stands very still and does not come out, and who once, at the turn of the tide, held out a hand ruled like paper to a child, palm up, as if to show it was empty.".
  Ending warden "The Warden of the Settlement" when morning() and saultHoldsNote(ossel) and saultWarden(ossel) "The held come home, and the Muster belongs to Factor Sault, who will never call it; the city's debt has become a debt to one woman, who can count, and does, out loud, at every meeting of the Board. The veterans go upriver to land that is theirs in all but law, under the Warden of the Settlement, who visits every autumn with seed-corn and a ledger. It is not justice. It is something people can live in, which in Tessary is often the best on offer.".
  Ending factor "The Factor's Tessary" when morning() and saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not saultWarden(ossel) "The Muster belongs to Factor Sault. Within the week the Board, which has no army and no money and no more chairs than it has frightened councillors, gives her the Great Seal and the title of Warden of the City. Tessary is better run than it has been in a century. The soldiers are fed and paid and housed, and stand on the Tidewall in her coats, and nobody in the city is sure any more what they would do if they were told to do something terrible, and the soldiers least of all.".
  Ending foreclosure "Foreclosure" when morning() and foreclosed(ossel) "Nothing happens, which is the worst of it. The held stay held. The Board says nothing; there is no money to say anything with. The rest of the Muster goes back to the boardwalks and the pans and waits for the next spring ebb, which does not come, because there is nothing left owing, only something forfeit. In the Withies they hang the boots from the eaves of the stilt-houses, pair by pair. And out past the bar, on more nights every month, the sea shows stars that are not Tessary's, very close, and once in the winter something comes up the Throat on the flood that was not born in Imbar, and the Scruples, who might have known what it was, have closed the black wall and do not answer.".

  // ── Objectives ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Objective find_davy when knows(party, notice_read) and not knows(party, davy_went) and heldNow(davy) "Nan Teazle of the Withies wants to know where her son Davy went when he walked into the sea.".
  Objective follow_davy when knows(party, davy_went) and not knows(party, held_alive) and heldNow(davy) "Davy Teazle walked into the sea at the spring ebb. Where did he go, and why do the soldiers keep step as they go?".
  Objective why_held when knows(party, held_alive) and not knows(party, collateral) and not matured(ossel) "The soldiers who walk into the sea are held, not dead. Who is holding them, and for what?".
  Objective what_owed when knows(party, collateral) and not knows(party, promise_weight) and not matured(ossel) "The city pledged its soldiers' oaths against a debt. What does it owe, and how can it be paid?".
  Objective pay_it when knows(party, promise_weight) and not voted(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "The War Note is paid if the city keeps its promise of land and a pension to every soldier who came home. The Board votes on the thirteenth day, and has no money.".
  Objective save_durrance when knows(party, durrance_next) and night(ossel) < 8 and not durranceSafe() and not heldNow(durrance) "Sergeant Durrance is on the next page of the roll, and will walk into the sea at the eighth night's spring ebb.".
  Objective carry_deeds when knows(party, deeds_for_held) and not deedsDelivered(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "The deeds of the held must be put into their hands in the Holding before the note falls due at two in the morning after the Feast.".
  Objective feast_release when releaseCalled(ossel) and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "Durrance will call the Muster to the Oath Stone on the night of the Feast, to release the city. The Factor's lightermen will come.".
  Objective feast_assembly when indictmentFiled(ossel) and not noteVoid(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "The Assembly of the Scruples sits in the Weighing Chamber from midnight on the night of the Feast. The Assessor asked you to be there.".
  Objective sault_bid_known when knows(party, sault_bid) and not matured(ossel) and not saultWarden(ossel) and not saultStopped(ossel) "Factor Sault means to take up the War Note when it falls in, and govern Tessary with the Muster.".

  // The module is seen through when the note is discharged, or held by a Warden sworn to send the Muster home.
  Goal discharged(ossel) or saultWarden(ossel) and saultHoldsNote(ossel).
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/holdin:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The Holding ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Where pledged things are kept against their promises, and forfeit things for ever: beyond the Balance, a white
  // floor under no sky. Everything here has a tag. (A contribution to Imbar's cosmology for canon review: the Kept's
  // tradition, not a narrator's fact. See doc/adventures/what-tessary-owes/03-revised-design.md.)
  Place holding_plane "the Holding" is plane.
  Place white_floor "the white floor" is region within holding_plane.
  Place holding "the Holding" is site within white_floor at 0, 0.
  Place threshold "the threshold of the Holding" is room within holding at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place sheaves "the field of sheaves" is room within holding at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place folded_lake "the folded lake" is room within holding at 2, 0 outdoors.
  Place notary_desk "the Notary's desk" is room within holding at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place tags "the avenue of tags" is room within holding at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place ranks "the Ranks" is room within holding at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Place far_edge "the far edge" is room within holding at 2, 2 outdoors.

  // The Door stands open on the night of the Settlement; at other times only to the Assessor and whoever goes with
  // them, or to whomever the Comptroller admits.
  Relation holdingAdmits(group).
  Query doorOpen() means feastEve() and hour(clock) >= 18 or night(ossel) >= 15 or travelsWith(tally, party) or holdingAdmits(party).
  Passage holding_door "the Door of the Holding" is passage between weighing_chamber and threshold
    opening when doorOpen() "The Door of the Holding stands at the end of the nave with the white floor showing through it, and when you walk toward it you do not come any nearer.".
  Passage floor_n "the white floor" is passage between threshold and sheaves taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_lake "the white floor" is passage between sheaves and folded_lake taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_desk "the white floor" is passage between threshold and notary_desk taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_tags "the white floor" is passage between notary_desk and tags taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_sheaves_tags "the white floor" is passage between sheaves and tags taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_ranks "the white floor" is passage between tags and ranks taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_edge "the white floor" is passage between ranks and far_edge taking 30 minutes.
  Passage floor_lake_edge "the white floor" is passage between folded_lake and far_edge taking 30 minutes.

  Observe threshold_scene at threshold when true "You step through and there is no sky. There is a floor, white, faintly ruled, going on in every direction until it is too far to see, and there is a light that comes from nowhere and casts no shadows. Behind you the Door stands on its own, with the nave of the Weighing Chamber dim inside it like a room seen through a window at night. Ahead, in rows that go on past seeing, things stand on the floor with tags tied to them.".
  Observe sheaves_scene at sheaves when true "A field of sheaves, standing in stooks on the white floor, gold and dry and smelling of August: a harvest, a whole country's harvest, acres of it. The tag on the nearest stook is old leather, and the writing on it says, in a script like the Scruples', a king's word that his people would not starve, given in a year of famine, and broken.".
  Observe lake_scene at folded_lake when true "A lake, folded. That is the only way to say it: a lake has been folded like linen, in squares, and laid on the floor in a stack higher than a house, and you can see through the folds the reeds and the fish and a little boat, very small and perfectly still, caught between two layers of water. Its tag is the size of a door.".
  Observe tags_scene at tags when true "An avenue of tags with nothing tied to them: little white tags on cords, hanging from a rail at the height of your eyes, thousands of them, stirring though there is no wind. Each has a name on it in the ruled script. These are the names of the Scruples, pledged at their births. Some are very old. Some are new, and the ink still wet.".
  Observe ranks_scene at ranks when true "The Ranks. Soldiers of the Long Muster, standing in files on the white floor as if on parade, barefoot, in their shirts, their eyes closed, their hands at their sides. They are breathing, very slowly, all together. There are a hundred and fifty of them, and more; there are faces you have seen on the boardwalks of the Withies, and faces you have seen only on the Assessor's pages. Nobody has tied tags to them. Their tags are in the Weighing Chamber, in the pan.".
  Observe desk_scene at notary_desk when true "A white desk stands on the white floor with nothing round it for a long way in any direction: a clerk's desk, sloped, with an inkwell, and a rail behind it hung with keys that have no doors. There is no chair. Whoever works here does not sit.".
  Observe durrance_held near durrance when heldNow(durrance) and at(durrance, ranks) and asleep(durrance) "At the end of the Third Company's file, a little apart, as a sergeant stands, Agathe Durrance is asleep on her feet, barefoot, with her chin up as if on parade.".
  Observe davy_held near davy when heldNow(davy) and asleep(davy) "In the Third Company's file, between a big man with a burned hand and a boy who cannot be more than seventeen, Davy Teazle is asleep in his shirt. His feet are bare and very white. He looks cold.".
  Observe edge_scene at far_edge when true "The floor ends. It does not drop away; it stops, and beyond it is dark that is not night, and in the dark, very far off, there are nine points of black light, arranged in no shape you know, perfectly still. The air here is cold and smells of iron. Something about the nine points makes you want very much to look somewhere else.".
  Observe ranks_count at ranks when held(ossel) > 150 "The files are longer than they were. New faces at the ends of them, in their shirts, with their eyes closed.".

  // The Notary: the Balance's own clerk, who keeps the Holding and sits with the Assembly at a Settlement.
  Person notary "the Notary" at notary_desk {
    Role "a figure at a white desk, made of fine ruled lines of light, as a drawing of a clerk is made of lines". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns it. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The figure at the desk looks up. It has no face, only the lines where a face would be drawn, very close together, and when it speaks the lines move. 'Weighed,' it says, in a voice like a page turning. 'Come in. Everything here is accounted for.'".
  }
  Topic notary_place with notary "Ask the Notary what this place is" when true once {
    Says "'The Holding,' says the Notary. 'Where what is pledged is kept against the promise it was pledged for, until the promise is kept or released, and where what is forfeit is kept for ever.' Its lines move. 'A harvest. A lake. A singer's voice, in a jar, over there; she pledged it against her lover's return, and he came home, and she has never come for it. I do not know why. People are not always in a hurry for what is theirs.'".
  }
  Topic notary_lights with notary "Ask the Notary about the nine black lights at the far edge" when true once {
    Says "The Notary is quiet for a long time. 'Security,' it says at last. 'For the oldest promise this floor holds. The Scruples call it the Fastening; your priests have other words. The nine jewels your songs remember are the tallies of it, and what they tally is held there.' Its lines grow very close together. 'I do not discuss the terms. I will say that they are being kept. I will say that at one place in Imbar the ledger is uneven, and the fastening there is slack, and it is the place you came from.'".
  }
  Topic notary_redeem with notary "Ask the Notary how the held may be redeemed" when true once {
    Says "'Three ways,' says the Notary. 'The debt is paid, and all that was pledged for it goes home. The debt is released, by the one it is owed to, and all goes home. Or a single thing is redeemed by another pledge of its weight, laid on this desk.' It turns a page that is not there. 'A soldier's oath weighs about what a person's name weighs, and everything they carry of worth. I make that observation to everyone who asks. Very few people ask twice.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, redeem_by_pledge). }
  }
  Discovery redeem_by_pledge "In the Holding a single held thing may be redeemed by laying another pledge of its weight on the Notary's desk: a soldier's oath weighs about what a person's name weighs, and everything they carry of worth.".
  Topic notary_comptroller with notary "Ask the Notary about the Comptroller's default" when knows(actor, note_designed) once {
    Says "'Entered in his hand eleven hundred years ago,' says the Notary. 'An honest entry.' The lines of its face do not move at all. 'The note he drew for your city was not honest. I hold what I am given. I do not choose what I am given. If the Assembly sits at the Settlement and finds the note drawn to be broken, I will hold that too.' A pause. 'He has been very unhappy. I make that observation as well.'".
  }
  // A goose, pledged in a wager three hundred years ago and forfeit, who has views.
  Person old_goose "a goose" at sheaves {
    Role "a grey goose with a tag round its neck, three hundred years forfeit". Species goose_kind. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
  }
  Observe old_goose_scene near old_goose when at(old_goose, sheaves) "Among the sheaves a grey goose is eating a king's harvest, one grain at a time, with the air of someone who has been doing it for a very long while and intends to go on. The tag round her neck says she was wagered on a horse-race in the Ossel country three hundred and four years ago, by a miller, who lost. When she sees you she hisses, on principle.".
  Topic notary_goose with notary "Ask the Notary about the goose" when true once {
    Says "'Forfeit,' says the Notary. 'A miller wagered her on a horse and the horse lost. She is the property of the Balance. She has eaten approximately a third of the harvest of Old Ennelmark.' Its lines move in a way that might be a sigh. 'Nothing forfeit to the Holding ages. Nothing in the Holding can be made to leave it. I have tried.'".
  }

  // ── The held ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person held_files "the held of the Long Muster" at ranks {
    Role "soldiers asleep on their feet, in files". Ancestry human. Numbers 1. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
  }
  Initially Assert asleep(held_files).
  Person davy "Davy Teazle" at ranks {
    Role "a private of the Long Muster, asleep on his feet, in his shirt". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Peaceable. Pronouns he.
  }
  Initially Assert asleep(davy). Initially Assert heldNow(davy).
  Relation davyWoke(place).
  Action wake_davy(actor: group, site: place) "Lay Davy's coat over his shoulders" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(davy, site) and carries(actor, davy_coat)
      and heldNow(davy) and not davyWoke(ossel).
    On success { Assert davyWoke(ossel). Retract asleep(davy). }
    Result "You put the red coat round his shoulders, the darned elbow and all, and he shivers once, the whole length of him, and opens his eyes. 'Mam?' he says. Then he sees you, and the white floor, and the files of sleepers going away on either side of him, and his face does the thing a face does when a dream turns out not to be one. 'I put my boots together,' he says. 'Didn't I? She'll never believe it.'".
  }
  Topic davy_talk with davy "Ask Davy what it is like here" when davyWoke(ossel) and heldNow(davy) once {
    Says "'Like standing guard,' says Davy. 'Only nobody comes to relieve you.' He pulls the coat round himself. 'I can't move my feet. I've tried. I can hear the others breathing. Sometimes somebody talks in his sleep, the Lucey twins mostly, they always did.' He looks at you. 'Are we coming home? Tell me straight. The army never told anyone anything straight.'".
  }
  Rule davy_sleeps_again when davyWoke(ossel) and heldNow(davy) and not at(party, ranks) { Assert asleep(davy). }
  Rule davy_wakes_again when davyWoke(ossel) and heldNow(davy) and at(party, ranks) and asleep(davy) { Retract asleep(davy). }

  // Durrance, if she was taken: her own oath, said to her to its last words, wakes her.
  Relation durranceWoke(place).
  Action wake_durrance(actor: group, site: place) "Say the Muster's oath to Durrance, to the very end: 'until it release me'" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(durrance, site) and heldNow(durrance)
      and knows(actor, oath_words) and not durranceWoke(ossel).
    On success { Assert durranceWoke(ossel). Retract asleep(durrance). }
    Result "You say it into her face, the way she said it to you in the Drum: I swear to keep the city of Tessary, its walls and its people, while I live or until it release me. At release her eyes open. She looks at you for a long moment without knowing you, and then knowing you. 'Until it release me,' she says. 'Nobody ever listens to that part.' She tries to move her feet, and cannot. 'Well,' she says. 'Here I am, then. Where's the one doing the calling? I said I'd like to look at them.'".
  }
  Rule durrance_sleeps_again when durranceWoke(ossel) and heldNow(durrance) and not at(party, ranks) { Assert asleep(durrance). }
  Rule durrance_wakes_again when durranceWoke(ossel) and heldNow(durrance) and at(party, ranks) and asleep(durrance) { Retract asleep(durrance). }

  // The deeds of the held, put into their hands before the Settlement: the city's promise, kept to every soldier.
  Action deliver_deeds(actor: group, site: place) "Go down the files putting a sealed deed into every hand" {
    Description "A hundred and sixty-odd deeds, name by name. It will take a while.".
    Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, ranks) and carries(actor, held_deeds)
      and not deedsDelivered(ossel) and not matured(ossel).
    On success { Assert deedsDelivered(ossel). }
    Result "You go down the files with the casket open, reading the names off the deeds, finding the faces. Pike. Haskett. Moll Bryer. The Lucey twins, side by side. Teazle, D. Every hand takes the paper as you put it there, the way a sleeping hand will close on whatever is put in it, and holds it. When you come to the end of the last file the casket is empty, and all down the Ranks, very faintly, there is a sound like a great many people breathing out.".
  }

  // ── The pledge ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // One pledge to a person, for there is one name to a person: laid on the Notary's desk, it redeems one held thing.
  Relation pledgedSelf(group). Relation redeemedBy(group, group). Relation tallyFreed(place). Relation tallyNameFound(group).
  Observe tally_tag at tags when knows(party, tally_name_known) and not tallyFreed(ossel) "In the ninth row, near the end, a tag hangs whose ink is twenty-nine years old. You know it is the Assessor's before you read it. It is a short name. It would sound strange in Tessary, and then, after a while, it would not.".
  Discovery tally_name_known "The Assessor's name hangs in the avenue of tags in the Holding, pledged at their birth.".
  Topic tally_name with tally "Ask the Assessor what their name is" when tallySawDefaults(ossel) and not knows(actor, tally_name_known) once {
    Says "The Assessor looks at you for a long time. 'It is held,' they say. 'In the ninth row of the avenue of tags. I have never seen it. One is not shown one's name.' A pause. 'I find, since the Room of Defaults, that I would like to know what it is. I note that. I do not know what to do with it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, tally_name_known). }
  }
  Action pledge_for_davy(actor: group, site: place) "Lay your name and everything you carry of worth on the Notary's desk, to redeem Davy Teazle" {
    Speaker notary. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "A name pledged to the Holding is held. It is not given back.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(notary, site) and knows(actor, redeem_by_pledge)
      and heldNow(davy) and not pledgedSelf(actor) and not discharged(ossel).
    On success { Assert pledgedSelf(actor). Assert redeemedBy(davy, actor). Set quantity(actor, gold) to 0. Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "You say your name, the whole of it, and the Notary writes it on a tag, and ties the tag to the rail with the others, and it hangs there stirring. 'Held,' it says. 'Teazle, D., redeemed.' Your purse is empty; you did not see it go. When you try to think of your own name it is there, still, but at a distance, like a word in a language you used to speak. 'You will be called something,' says the Notary. 'People always are.'".
  }
  Action pledge_for_durrance(actor: group, site: place) "Lay your name and everything you carry of worth on the Notary's desk, to redeem Agathe Durrance" {
    Speaker notary. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "A name pledged to the Holding is held. It is not given back.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(notary, site) and knows(actor, redeem_by_pledge)
      and heldNow(durrance) and not pledgedSelf(actor) and not discharged(ossel).
    On success { Assert pledgedSelf(actor). Assert redeemedBy(durrance, actor). Set quantity(actor, gold) to 0. Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "You say your name, the whole of it, and the Notary writes it on a tag and ties it to the rail. 'Held,' it says. 'Durrance, A., redeemed.' Your purse is empty. Your own name, when you reach for it, is there, but at a distance, like the name of a town you passed through once.".
  }
  Action pledge_for_tally(actor: group, site: place) "Lay your name and everything you carry of worth on the Notary's desk, to redeem the Assessor's name" {
    Speaker notary. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "A name pledged to the Holding is held. It is not given back. The Assessor's, redeemed, is theirs.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(notary, site) and knows(actor, redeem_by_pledge)
      and knows(actor, tally_name_known) and not tallyFreed(ossel) and not pledgedSelf(actor) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel).
    On success { Assert pledgedSelf(actor). Assert tallyFreed(ossel). Set quantity(actor, gold) to 0. Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "The Notary goes down the avenue of tags without seeming to walk, and comes back with one small white tag in the lines of its hand, and lays it on the desk, and ties yours in its place. 'A Scruple's name, redeemed,' it says. 'That has not happened before.' Its lines move. 'They will not be able to lie any more easily than they could. But they will be able to leave.'".
  }
  Relation tallyUnravelled(place).
  Rule redeemed_go_home when redeemedBy(?s, ?c) and heldNow(?s) {
    Retract heldNow(?s). Retract asleep(?s). Assert cameHome(?s). Assert wokeHome(?s). }
  Relation wokeHome(group).
  Rule davy_home when wokeHome(davy) and at(davy, ranks) { Retract at(davy, ranks). Assert at(davy, teazle_room). }
  Rule durrance_home when wokeHome(durrance) and at(durrance, ranks) { Retract at(durrance, ranks). Assert at(durrance, drum_taproom). }
  Rule comptroller_redeems when redeemedByComptroller(davy) and heldNow(davy) and lowWater() and dark() {
    Retract heldNow(davy). Retract asleep(davy). Assert cameHome(davy). Assert wokeHome(davy). }
  Rule davy_back_told when wokeHome(davy) and not knows(party, davy_back)
    says "Word runs along the Withies faster than the tide: Davy Teazle woke up on the Tideline Steps in his shirt with his boots beside him, and walked home, and put his boots on the mat inside his mother's door, side by side." teaches davy_back { }
  Discovery davy_back "Davy Teazle has come home to the Withies.".
  Event nan_pays near nan when knows(party, davy_back) and nanOffer(party) and not nanPaid(party) "Nan Teazle puts a tin in your hands without a word. Nine coin in it. Davy is asleep in the cupboard bed behind her, in his coat, with his boots on." then {
    Increase quantity(party, gold) by 9. Assert nanPaid(party). }
  Event nan_pays_knowing near nan when toldNan(party) and nanOffer(party) and heldNow(davy) "Before you go, Nan Teazle puts a tin in your hands. 'Nine coin,' she says. 'You told me where he is. That was the bargain.'" then {
    Increase quantity(party, gold) by 9. Assert nanPaid(party). }
  Relation nanPaid(group).
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/lowtid:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── Lowtide ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Eleven hundred years ago the sea came over the Aenean city in a night and kept it. Its streets lie in the outer
  // basin under four fathoms at high water; at low water they drain through the Throat and stand out for a few hours,
  // weeded, wet, picked over by mudlarks, used by smugglers, and haunted. The Hall of Oaths, the old city's court, is
  // at the bottom of the basin, and the wall at the back of it is the way down to the Strongrooms.
  Place throat_foot "the foot of the Throat Stair" is room within lowtide at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place colonnade "the Weed Colonnade" is room within lowtide at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place forum "the Drowned Forum" is room within lowtide at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place scales_street "the Street of Scales" is room within lowtide at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place aqueduct_foot "under the Aqueduct" is room within lowtide at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place aqueduct_top "the top of the Aqueduct" is room within lowtide at 0, 2 outdoors.
  Place landing "the ebb-runners' landing" is room within lowtide at 3, 1 outdoors.
  Place bath_house "the bath-house" is building within lowtide.
  Place bath_hall "the bath-house hall" is room within bath_house at 2, 2.
  Place plunge "the plunge-room" is room within bath_house at 3, 2.
  Place bath_dome "the top of the bath-house dome" is room within lowtide at 2, 3 outdoors.
  Place oath_house "the Hall of Oaths" is building within lowtide.
  Place oath_court "the Hall of Oaths" is room within oath_house at 1, 2.

  Passage throat_stair "the Throat Stair" is steps between throat_head and throat_foot
    opening when lowWater() "The Throat Stair goes down into green water and does not come up. The basin is full.".
  Passage colonnade_way "the colonnade" is arch between throat_foot and colonnade.
  Passage forum_steps "the forum steps" is steps between colonnade and forum.
  Passage scales_way "the Street of Scales" is path between forum and scales_street taking 5 minutes.
  Passage aqueduct_way "the lane to the aqueduct" is path between forum and aqueduct_foot taking 5 minutes.
  Passage pier "the broken pier" is passage between aqueduct_foot and aqueduct_top needing climbing or rope
    opening when lowWater() "The broken pier stands up out of the sea. The water is over everything below it.".
  Passage landing_way "the quay steps" is steps between scales_street and landing.
  Passage bath_door "the bath-house door" is doorway between scales_street and bath_hall.
  Passage plunge_arch "the plunge-room arch" is arch between bath_hall and plunge.
  Passage dome_stair "the dome stair" is passage between bath_hall and bath_dome
    opening when lowWater() "The dome stair goes down into black water.".
  Passage hall_steps "the Hall steps" is steps between forum and oath_court.
  Passage runners_tunnel "the ebb-runners' tunnel" is tunnel between landing and cistern taking 20 minutes.
  Initially Assert unlit(plunge). Initially Assert unlit(oath_court).

  // What floods, and what does not: the landing is a raised quay at the tunnel's mouth; the aqueduct and the dome
  // stand above the highest water.
  Relation floods(place).
  Initially Assert floods(throat_foot). Initially Assert floods(colonnade). Initially Assert floods(forum).
  Initially Assert floods(scales_street). Initially Assert floods(aqueduct_foot). Initially Assert floods(bath_hall).
  Initially Assert floods(plunge). Initially Assert floods(oath_court).
  Relation lowtideRoom(place).
  Initially Assert lowtideRoom(throat_foot). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(colonnade). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(forum).
  Initially Assert lowtideRoom(scales_street). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(aqueduct_foot). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(aqueduct_top).
  Initially Assert lowtideRoom(landing). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(bath_hall). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(plunge).
  Initially Assert lowtideRoom(bath_dome). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(oath_court).

  // ── The water ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe water_low near party when at(party, ?p) and floods(?p) and lowWater() and not turning() "Water stands in the low places and runs in the gutters, going out. Somewhere far off, toward the Throat, the sea is a long way away.".
  Observe water_turning near party when at(party, ?p) and floods(?p) and turning() "The water in the gutters has stopped running out. Now it is running back. A wet line is creeping up the steps of the nearest house, and from the direction of the Throat comes a sound like a mill-race opening.".
  Observe table_says near party when at(party, ?p) and floods(?p) and turning() and carries(party, ?t) and itemKind(?t, tide_table) "By Wick's table the basin fills on the hour. The drawing of the wave with teeth is underlined twice.".
  Observe refuge_high near party when at(party, ?p) and lowtideRoom(?p) and not floods(?p) and not lowWater() "The sea is in. Green water lies over Lowtide from the Tidewall to the outer bar, with the tops of colonnades standing up out of it, and gulls on them. You are above it, and will be until the ebb.".
  Hazard drowning "Rolled through the Throat by the flood" means "Deal (2d4) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Rule swept when at(party, ?p) and floods(?p) and not lowWater()
    says "The flood comes back through the Throat all at once, a brown wall of it shouldering down the streets. It takes your feet. It takes everything. You are rolled, and dragged, and something hits you, and there is no up; and then there is, and air, and you are being carried out along the pan-dykes with the weed and the timber, and you crawl out at last onto the salt crust east of the city and lie there, coughing up the sea. Your purse is lighter." {
    Retract at(party, ?p). Assert at(party, pans). Assert strikes(drowning, party). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 3. Assert sweptOnce(party). }
  Relation sweptOnce(group).

  // ── The places ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe throat_foot_scene at throat_foot when true "The stair comes down the face of the Tidewall into a gully of wet stone and kelp. The noise of the Throat is very loud here: the basin draining past you through the one deep channel, brown and quick. Ahead, through a gap in the old sea-wall, a street begins.".
  Observe colonnade_scene at colonnade when true "A street of columns, their tops lost, their shafts furred with weed that lies flat in the direction the water went. Between the columns, doorways, full of sand to the lintel. Anemones the colour of raw meat have opened in the wet, and close if you go near.".
  Observe forum_scene at forum when true "The old city's market square, a hundred paces across, paved in great slabs, most of them still there. The fountain in the middle is a heap of stone with a crab on it. On every side the fronts of buildings stand roofless, their windows full of sky. At the south end, broad steps go down to a building with no windows at all.".
  Observe forum_larks at forum when lowWater() and not dark() "Mudlarks are working the square with buckets and rakes, children mostly, and a few old men who have been children here for sixty years. They lift their heads to look at you, and go back to work.".
  Observe forum_dark at forum when dark() "In the dark the square is a pale floor, and the buildings round it are holes. Things move in the wet places. It is very quiet except for the Throat.".
  Observe scales_scene at scales_street when true "A street of shops, by the look of it: every doorway has a stone counter, and every counter a pair of carved scales. Eleven hundred years have not worn the scales off. At the far end, a quay stands up out of the sand, higher than the street, with steps.".
  Observe aqueduct_foot_scene at aqueduct_foot when true "The aqueduct comes in over the basin on three arches from somewhere that is now open sea, and stops in mid-air above a heap of its own fallen stones. One pier still stands to the top. Its stones are stepped and broken; there is a rusted ring set in it, high up, where somebody has knotted rope before.".
  Observe aqueduct_top_scene at aqueduct_top when true "The water-channel along the aqueduct's top is a yard wide and dry, and you can lie in it out of the wind. From here the whole of Lowtide is laid out like a plan: the colonnade, the forum, the dome of the bath-house, the windowless Hall at the bottom of everything, and beyond it all the outer bar, and the sea.".
  Observe bath_hall_scene at bath_hall when true "A hall of benches round a dry basin, under a dome that has kept its roof. Light comes down through the hole at the top of the dome in a white post. Against one wall, a stair winds up inside the dome's thickness. On the other side an arch opens on darkness, and the air that comes out of it is cold and smells of nothing at all.".
  Observe plunge_scene at plunge when true "The plunge-room: a deep square pool, dry, its floor a bed of silt. Round its edge, against the walls, things are standing that look at first like coats hung on pegs, and then do not.".
  Observe dome_scene at bath_dome when true "The dome's top is a broad shallow cap of stone with the light-hole in the middle of it, crusted with gull-lime. It stands above the highest water. People have sat out tides here before: there are names scratched in the stone, and a tally of days.".
  Observe court_scene at oath_court when true "The Hall of Oaths has no windows. It is a long room of black stone, the same black as the Oath Stone in the Legion Yard, dry, except for the sea's tidemark half way up the walls, as if the water had come in and thought better of it. The walls are carved from floor to tidemark with ruled lines, ledger on ledger, and on the end wall, where a judge's seat would be, there is no seat, only an inscription in Aenean letters a foot high, and under it a plain black wall.".

  // ── The ebb-runners ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Factor Sault's people in Lowtide. They work the old city for bronze and dressed stone, run untaxed salt through the
  // cistern, and for eleven years carried the city's interest silver down to the Hall of Oaths. They take prisoners:
  // whoever they beat wakes on the Pans.
  Person slake "Bettany Slake" at landing {
    Role "who runs the ebb-runners, in a fisherman's smock with a cutlass through the belt". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 3. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "A woman in a smock stands up off a crate with a cutlass in her hand and puts her other hand up, palm out. 'That's far enough,' she says. 'This is a working quay.'".
    Comes "'Right,' says Bettany Slake, almost sorry, and the ebb-runners come off the crates.".
    Pleads "Bettany Slake puts her cutlass down on the stones. 'All right,' she says. 'All right. You've made your point.'".
  }
  Person runners "the ebb-runners" at landing {
    Role "three of Bettany Slake's people, with hooks and short clubs". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Numbers 3. Pronouns they.
    Temperament territorial.
  }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(slake). Initially Assert takesPrisoners(runners).
  Initially Assert serves(runners, slake). Initially Assert serves(slake, sault).
  Observe landing_scene at landing when true "A stone quay at the end of the Street of Scales, high enough that the flood laps its top and goes no further. Crates, coils of rope, a brazier, a long boat drawn up on rollers. A low tunnel goes back into the quay wall, toward the city, with lamps on hooks along it. On a post by the tunnel mouth hangs a board scored with notches.".
  Rule runners_captured when captured(slake, party) or captured(runners, party)
    says "You come round on the salt crust east of the city at the edge of a pan, with a headache and an empty feeling at your belt. Someone has carried you up the tunnel and dumped you here. Someone has also been through your purse." {
    Retract captured(slake, party). Retract captured(runners, party). Retract at(party, landing). Assert at(party, pans).
    Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 5. }
  Topic slake_quay with slake "Ask Bettany Slake what the ebb-runners do" when true once {
    Says "'Salvage,' says Bettany. 'Bronze, dressed stone, whatever the sea's been keeping. All above board, in the Factor's name.' She spits over the edge of the quay. 'And what goes up and down that tunnel is the Factor's business and mine, and not a thing a stranger wants to be curious about, if the stranger likes the shape of his head.'".
  }
  Topic slake_silver with slake "Ask Bettany Slake what she carried to the Hall of Oaths" when knows(actor, collateral) or knows(actor, note_terms) once {
    Says "Bettany looks at you a long moment. 'Silver,' she says. 'Every month for eleven years. The city's, in the Factor's boats, down the tunnel and across at the ebb and into the Hall, and left in the niche by the wall, and the next ebb it was gone.' She shrugs. 'Then in the summer there wasn't any silver, and we stopped. And at the next spring ebb the first of them walked past us across the Forum with their eyes open.' She looks away. 'I don't carry anything to that Hall any more. Only the Factor's letters.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sault_courier). }
  }
  Discovery sault_courier "For eleven years the ebb-runners carried the city's interest silver, in Factor Sault's boats, down to the Hall of Oaths. The Factor has known the whole arrangement from the beginning." {
    Source runners_board "the notched board on the post by the tunnel" at landing readable by party.
  }
  Relation slakeLetsPass(group).
  Action pay_slake(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Bettany Slake five coin for the use of her quay" {
    Speaker slake. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(slake, site) and able(slake)
      and not tolerates(slake, actor) and not hostile(slake, actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 5.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Increase quantity(slake, gold) by 5. Assert tolerates(slake, actor). Assert tolerates(runners, actor). Assert slakeLetsPass(actor). }
    Result "Bettany weighs the coins in her palm, and bites one, and pockets them. 'Quay's yours,' she says. 'Don't touch the crates.'".
  }
  Topic slake_factor with slake "Tell Bettany Slake you work for the Factor" when hiredBySault(actor) and not tolerates(slake, actor) once {
    Says "'Do you,' says Bettany. She looks you up and down. 'She said she'd hired someone to go asking. All right. Mind yourself on the quay.' She sits back down on her crate.".
    On discuss { Assert tolerates(slake, actor). Assert tolerates(runners, actor). Assert slakeLetsPass(actor). }
  }
  Thing runners_box "the ebb-runners' lockbox" at landing {
    Holds.
    State locked closed "An iron-bound lockbox is chained to the boat's thwart.".
    State open "The lockbox stands open.".
    Change pick "Pick the lockbox" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    Change smash "Smash the lockbox open" from locked to open needing brawn.
  }
  Item sault_letter "a letter in the Factor's hand" is letter_kind in runners_box.
  Kind letter_kind "a sealed letter" is gear worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A letter folded small and sealed with salt-white wax, stamped with a pair of crossed rakes.".
  // What is seen taken, by those who keep the quay.
  Rule box_watched when state(runners_box, open) and perceives(slake, party) and able(slake) and not hostile(slake, party)
    says "'Oi,' says Bettany Slake, and her cutlass comes out." { Assert hostile(slake, party). Assert assails(runners, party). }
  Discovery sault_bid "Factor Sault has written to a broker of the Scruples offering to bid for the War Note at its foreclosure, and to pledge her own house to the Balance as surety: 'The Board will not pay. When the Feast passes, I will take up the note, and with it the Muster, and Tessary will be governed by someone who can count.'".
  Action read_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Break the wax and read the Factor's letter" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and carries(actor, sault_letter) and not benighted(actor)
      and not knows(actor, sault_bid).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, sault_bid). }
    Result "It is addressed to the Broker of the Fourth Pan, the Strongrooms, by hand of B. Slake. 'Sir. You will have had my earlier. I repeat my offer: when the city's note falls in at the Feast and is offered at foreclosure, I bid for it, and I will pledge House Sault entire as surety, which your Comptroller will find to weigh what it needs to. The Board will not pay; I have seen to that, and if I had not, the treasury would. I will take up the note and with it the Muster. They will be fed and paid and housed. Tessary will be governed by someone who can count. Burn this. I. Sault, Factor.'".
  }

  // Councillor Haverick's goose, taken off the Terraces by the ebb-runners for their Feast.
  Species goose_kind "a goose" like hen tame described "A big white goose with an orange bill and an opinion of everyone.".
  Person plum "Mistress Plum" at landing {
    Role "a large white goose in a crate, very much offended". Species goose_kind. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
  }
  Observe plum_crate near plum when at(plum, landing) and not plumLoose(ossel) "In a crate by the brazier a big white goose is hissing steadily at the ebb-runners, who are ignoring it. A ribbon round its neck says PLUM in gold thread.".
  Relation plumLoose(place). Measure distractedUntil(place).
  Action release_plum(actor: group, site: place) "Knock the peg out of the goose's crate" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, landing) and at(plum, landing) and not plumLoose(ossel).
    On success { Assert plumLoose(ossel). Assert acceptsEscort(plum, actor). Assert unseen(actor, slake). Assert unseen(actor, runners).
      Assert tolerates(slake, actor). Assert tolerates(runners, actor). Retract assails(slake, actor). Retract assails(runners, actor).
      Set distractedUntil(ossel) to watch(clock) + 3. }
    Result "The peg comes out and the crate door falls open and Mistress Plum comes out of it like a cannonball, wings out, neck out, screaming, and goes straight for the nearest ebb-runner's ankles. In a moment the whole quay is chasing a goose round the brazier and the goose is winning. Nobody is looking at you at all.".
  }
  Rule distraction_ends when plumLoose(ossel) and watch(clock) >= distractedUntil(ossel) and unseen(party, slake) {
    Retract unseen(party, slake). Retract unseen(party, runners). }
  Rule distraction_over when plumLoose(ossel) and watch(clock) >= distractedUntil(ossel) and tolerates(slake, party) and not slakeLetsPass(party) and not hostile(slake, party) {
    Retract tolerates(slake, party). Retract tolerates(runners, party). }
  Observe plum_loose near plum when plumLoose(ossel) and not following(plum, party) and not plumHome(ossel) "Mistress Plum stands on a bollard with her wings half open, daring anyone to try it.".

  // ── The Forsworn ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Aenean oath-breakers whose bindings unravelled when they broke a promise the Balance held. What is left of them
  // stands in the plunge-room and comes to the sound of swearing, and to whoever has broken a promise held below.
  Species forsworn_kind "a Forsworn" like revenant temperament savage
    described "A thing like a person-shaped hollow, wearing the rags of an Aenean robe. Where its face should be there is a darkness with the texture of torn paper.".
  Person forsworn "the Forsworn" at plunge {
    Role "hollow people in the rags of Aenean robes". Species forsworn_kind. Level 2. Numbers 2. Pronouns they.
    Comes "The coats on the pegs come off the walls. They come round the dry pool toward you without any sound at all, with their hands out, as if they wanted to be given something.".
    Lair plunge.
  }
  // A company that has broken a promise held below is followed through Lowtide by the Forsworn, as the tide turns.
  Relation forswornParty(group).
  Rule forsworn_follow when forswornParty(party) and at(party, ?p) and floods(?p) and turning() and able(forsworn) and not at(forsworn, ?p) and not dark()
    says "Something is standing in the nearest doorway that was not there a moment ago: a coat with nobody in it, turned toward you." {
    Retract at(forsworn, plunge). Assert at(forsworn, ?p). Assert assails(forsworn, party). }

  // ── The Hall of Oaths ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery compact_read "The inscription in the Hall of Oaths is the drowned city's compact with the keepers of the Balance: 'THE SEA SHALL NOT HAVE THIS CITY WHILE THE LEDGER KEEPS. WHO COMES TO THE LEDGER COMES TO BE WEIGHED.' The sea had the city all the same.".
  Action read_compact(actor: group, site: place) "Puzzle out the Aenean inscription on the end wall" {
    Time 3.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, oath_court) and not benighted(actor)
      and not knows(actor, compact_read) and not travelsWith(tally, actor).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, compact_read). }
    Result "Letter by letter, with the ruled walls watching. The Aenean is formal, legal, very old, and plain once you have the first word: THE SEA SHALL NOT HAVE THIS CITY WHILE THE LEDGER KEEPS. And under it, smaller, over the black wall: WHO COMES TO THE LEDGER COMES TO BE WEIGHED. You look up at the tidemark half way up the walls, and think about the sea, and what it had.".
    Otherwise "You can make out a word here and there, CITY and SEA and something that might be LEDGER or might be SCALES, but the sense of it slides away from you in the dark.".
  }
  Observe tally_reads at oath_court when travelsWith(tally, party) and not knows(party, compact_read) and not benighted(party) "The Assessor stops in front of the end wall and reads it aloud, in a flat clear voice, as a clerk reads a clause. 'The sea shall not have this city while the ledger keeps. Who comes to the ledger comes to be weighed.' They are quiet a moment. 'That is the compact of the old city with the Balance. It is a famous text. I have never seen it.' Another pause. 'The sea had the city. I had not thought about that before.'" teaches compact_read.
  // The black wall: open to the Scruples, to the called, and to whoever says the words on it and means them.
  Relation weighedAt(group, place).
  Action say_words(actor: group, site: place) "Put your hand on the black wall and say 'I come to the ledger to be weighed'" {
    Grave "The words are written on a wall that hears them. Below, what you say is held to.".
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, oath_court) and knows(actor, compact_read)
      and not weighedAt(actor, oath_court).
    On success { Assert weighedAt(actor, oath_court). Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "The stone is warm under your hand, warm as a sleeping animal. You say the words, and for a moment you feel it: a weighing, as if you were standing in one pan of a scale with something enormous in the other, and the beam lifting, considering. Then the wall under your hand is not there.".
  }
  Relation registered(group).
  Passage black_wall "the black wall" is passage between oath_court and long_stair
    opening when travelsWith(tally, party) or weighedAt(party, oath_court) or registered(party) "A plain wall of black stone, warm to the touch, with no door in it.".
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/people:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── What can be known ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The facts of the adventure, in the order a company is likely to come by them. Each is a step in what the
  // vanishings turn out to be.
  Discovery notice_read "Nan Teazle, an eel-wife of the Withies, offers her savings for news of her son, Private Davy Teazle of the Long Muster, who set his boots on the Tideline Steps at the last spring ebb and walked into the sea." {
    Source notice "a notice on the Landgate board" at landgate readable by party.
  }
  Discovery enlist_promise "Eleven years ago, raising the Long Muster, the city of Tessary promised land and a pension to every soldier who came home. It was cried in every square and printed on every bill." {
    Known by nan, durrance, marrable, quire, sault.
  }
  Discovery hall_of_oaths_way "The called walk out across the drained basin to the Hall of Oaths in Lowtide and go in at a wall where there is no door." {
    Known by wick.
  }
  Discovery roll_order "The called go in the order of the Long Muster's roll, Third Company first, a dozen at each spring ebb." {
    Known by durrance, tally.
  }
  Discovery durrance_next "Sergeant Agathe Durrance is on the next page of the roll. Unless something changes she will be called at the eighth night's spring ebb." {
    Known by durrance, tally.
  }
  Discovery council_knows "Treasurer Quire keeps a list, in his own hand, of every veteran called since the summer, a hundred and thirty-eight names, each with an address and a sum of money sent. The Exchequer knows the vanished are not deserters." {
    Source quire_list "a list in the Treasurer's hand, under a paperweight" at exchequer_room readable by party.
  }
  Discovery collateral "The Muster's oaths, sworn on the Oath Stone, were pledged as security on a debt the city owes to the keepers of an engine under the sea. At each spring ebb a dozen are taken as interest." {
    Known by tally, quire, sault, comptroller.
  }
  Discovery note_terms "The War Note: twelve years ago Tessary borrowed, from the Scruples who keep the Balance under the sea, the right to call an oath King Amaury's ancestor swore to the Aenean emperors. The Long Muster's oaths were pledged as collateral; interest was paid in silver each month; the principal falls due at the Feast of Settlement in the twelfth year, and may be paid only in a kept promise of equal weight." {
    Known by tally, quire, sault, comptroller.
  }
  Discovery promise_weight "In the Scruples' reckoning only a promise of a whole people to a whole people weighs as much as the War Note, and Tessary has made one such promise: land and a pension for every soldier who came home. If the city keeps it, the debt is paid." {
    Known by tally, comptroller.
  }
  Discovery held_alive "The called are not dead. They are held in the Holding, beyond the Balance, standing asleep, until their oaths are redeemed." {
    Known by tally, comptroller.
  }
  Discovery kneeling_felt "King Amaury did not kneel at Sedge Ford of his own will. He felt a hand on the back of his neck, he says, nine hundred years old, and his knees went into the river." {
    Known by amaury.
  }
  Discovery kneeling_bought "The Kneeling at Sedge Ford was bought: Tessary called in an oath Amaury's ancestor swore to the Aenean emperors, borrowed from under the sea, and the king's body kept his ancestor's word.".
  Discovery oath_words "The Muster's oath, sworn hand on the Oath Stone: 'I swear to keep the city of Tessary, its walls and its people, while I live or until it release me.'" {
    Known by durrance, marrable, fisk.
  }
  Discovery evenhand_tale "Saint Evenhand, say the brothers of his chapel, was a clerk who came up out of the sea when the old city drowned, with ruled lines on his skin, and lived among the people of the new city weighing their quarrels, and never once told a lie.".

  // What a company that knows two things comes to see for itself.
  Observe kneeling_seen near party when knows(party, kneeling_felt) and knows(party, note_terms) and not knows(party, kneeling_bought) "You put them side by side: the old oath of Amaury's line in the War Note, and the hand Amaury felt on his neck at the ford. The miracle the city keeps a saint's day for was paid for, by the month, in silver and then in soldiers." teaches kneeling_bought.

  // ── The Landgate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person tolley "Brother Tolley" at chapel {
    Role "the brother who keeps Saint Evenhand's". Ancestry human. Profession priest. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Offers healing "a dressing, a prayer and a weight hung for you" for 2 coin.
  }
  Topic tolley_weights with tolley "Ask Brother Tolley about the hanging weights" when true once {
    Says "'Promises,' says Brother Tolley, and touches one so that it turns on its cord. 'A man who wants a thing kept hangs its weight here. Brass for a marriage. Lead for a debt. This one, a stone off the beach, a girl hung for her sweetheart in the Muster.' He looks up at them, hundreds, turning. 'Eleven years of war, and the cords are getting thin. The saint holds the scales, you see. He doesn't put his thumb on them.'".
  }
  Topic tolley_saint with tolley "Ask Brother Tolley who Saint Evenhand was" when true once {
    Says "'A clerk of the drowned city,' says Tolley, 'who came up out of the sea the night it went down. That is the old story. He had lines on his skin like a ledger, and he could not tell a lie, and he lived among the first people of Tessary weighing their quarrels for them, and they trusted him because he could not be bought or frightened or flattered. He never went back.' He smiles. 'The scholars say he is a story about a set of scales. I say a set of scales is a story about a man like that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, evenhand_tale). }
  }
  Topic tolley_calling with tolley "Ask Brother Tolley about the soldiers walking into the sea" when knows(actor, notice_read) or knows(actor, calling_witnessed) once {
    Says "Tolley's hand finds the nearest weight and holds it still. 'Nan Teazle's boy was the first I buried with no body,' he says. 'I have said the office over eleven pairs of boots since. The Board says they are deserters. A deserter takes his boots.' He lets the weight go. 'Talk to the clerk in grey, if you can make him answer. He was in here yesterday, reading the cords. He said they were all of them accurate.'".
  }

  Person pitch "Jory Pitch" at chandlery {
    Role "a ship's chandler". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 8.
    Sells rope for 1 coin from 4.
    Sells torch for 1 coin from 6.
    Sells lantern for 3 coin from 2.
    Sells lamp_oil for 1 coin from 6.
    Sells oilskin for 2 coin from 3.
    Sells bandages for 1 coin from 4.
    Sells chapbook for 1 coin from 2.
  }
  Kind chapbook "a chapbook of ballads" is gear worth 1 weighing 0
    described "Twenty pages of cheap reed-paper, badly printed: 'The Drowned Bell', 'Sally of the Withies', 'The Soldier's Return' and nine more, with a woodcut of a ship on the cover.".
  Kind oilskin "an oilskin" like cloak worth 2 weighing 2
    described "A fisherman's coat of oiled canvas, stiff as a board and smelling of linseed. Water runs off it.".
  Topic pitch_tide with pitch "Ask Jory Pitch about the tides" when true once {
    Says "'Twice a day it goes out and twice it comes back, same as anywhere,' says Pitch, 'only here when it goes out it goes out properly. Low water's about eleven of the morning and eleven of the night, give or take, and five hours of it. Then it turns. And when it turns in the basin it doesn't come in, it comes back, all at once through the Throat like it's been sent for.' He taps the counter. 'Rope. Anyone going down into Lowtide wants rope, and something to stand on.'".
  }

  // ── The Withies: Nan and Wick Teazle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person nan "Nan Teazle" at teazle_room {
    Role "an eel-wife of the Withies". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
    Greets "Nan Teazle looks up from the trap she is mending and does not get up.".
  }
  Person wick "Wick Teazle" at withies {
    Role "a mudlark, about ten, with a tray on a string". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Sells tide_table for 1 coin from 3.
    Sells aenean_coin for 1 coin from 9.
  }
  Kind tide_table "a tide-table" is gear worth 1 weighing 0
    described "A square of reed-paper ruled in a child's careful hand: the hours of low water for the fortnight, the turn marked each time with a drawing of a wave with teeth.".
  Kind aenean_coin "a genuine Aenean coin" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A disc of greenish metal with a face on it, stamped, rather recently, by someone who had seen an Aenean coin once and liked it.".
  Discovery davy_went "Davy Teazle came home with the Muster, sat on his mother's step for a week without saying much, and at the last spring ebb got up in his sleep, went down the Tideline Steps barefoot and walked into the sea." {
    Known by nan, wick.
  }
  Topic nan_davy with nan "Ask Nan about Davy" when not cameHome(davy) once {
    Says "'He came home on the Tuesday with the rest of them,' says Nan, 'and he sat on that step out there for a week. Didn't say much. Ate what I put down. Then the spring ebb, the night after the new moon, I wake up and he's going down the ladder in his shirt. I called him. He didn't turn round.' Her needle goes in and out of the net. 'He set his boots on the top step. Side by side. I had to tell him every night of his life to put his boots together and he never once did it, and he set them on the step like a gentleman's valet. They taught him that.' She bites the cord. 'Then he walked into the sea.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, davy_went). }
  }
  Relation nanOffer(group).
  Topic nan_reward with nan "Ask Nan what she is offering" when not cameHome(davy) and not nanOffer(actor) once {
    Says "'Nine coin,' says Nan. 'It's in a tin. And all the eels you can eat for a twelvemonth, which you'll be sick of in a week.' She looks at you properly for the first time. 'I don't need him back. I'm not a fool. I need to know where he went. If he's down there drowned, I need to know where, so I can say so to the brother at the chapel and have him say the office over something that isn't a pair of boots.'".
    On discuss { Assert nanOffer(actor). }
  }
  Topic nan_bill with nan "Ask Nan about the recruiting bill on her shelf" when true once {
    Says "'LAND AND A PENSION FOR EVERY MAN WHO COMES HOME,' says Nan, without looking at it. 'They cried that in the Withies with a drum. Davy was seventeen. He came home Tuesday with a red coat and a paper that says he's owed eleven years' pay, and the Exchequer has no money to pay it with, and the Board's to hear the question of the land on the thirteenth day. The question.' She snorts. 'They've had eleven years to think of the answer.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, enlist_promise). }
  }
  Topic nan_alive with nan "Tell Nan that Davy is alive" when knows(actor, held_alive) and knows(actor, davy_went) and not toldNan(actor) once {
    Says "Nan Teazle puts the net down. She sits very still for a long time with her hands in her lap. 'Asleep,' she says at last. 'Standing up. Under the sea.' She gets up and takes Davy's red coat off its peg and holds it, and then holds it out to you. 'If you're going where he is, take him this. He'll be cold. He was always cold.' Her voice does not change at all. 'And tell him to put his boots on.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldNan(actor). }
  }
  Relation toldNan(group).
  Item davy_coat "Davy Teazle's red coat" is soldier_coat at teazle_room hidden until coat_given.
  Kind soldier_coat "a red coat of the Long Muster" like cloak worth 0 weighing 2
    described "A soldier's coat, red gone brown at the shoulders, with the Muster's brass buttons and a darn at the elbow in someone's careful wool.".
  Discovery coat_given "Nan Teazle has given you Davy's coat to take to him.".
  Action take_coat(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Take Davy's coat from Nan" {
    Speaker nan. Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(nan, site) and toldNan(actor)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient) and not knows(actor, coat_given).
    Resolve acquire(davy_coat, soldier_coat, recipient).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, coat_given). Retract at(davy_coat, teazle_room). }
    Result "Nan lays the coat over your arm, and smooths the darn at the elbow once with her thumb, and lets go.".
  }
  Initially Assert lends(nan, davy_coat, party).

  Topic wick_night with wick "Ask Wick about the night Davy went" when not cameHome(davy) once {
    Says "'I followed him,' says Wick, fast, as if he has been waiting to be asked. 'All the way down the Steps and out on the sand, it was a spring ebb, you can walk right out. There were twelve of them and they kept step and nobody was calling it. Out past the colonnade, across the Forum. Into the Hall of Oaths.' He lowers his voice. 'There's no door in the Hall of Oaths. It's a wall at the back. I've felt it. They walked into the wall and it let them, and then it was a wall again.' He considers. 'I'll show you, if you like. A coin. Two if you want the tide-table too, which you do.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hall_of_oaths_way). }
  }
  Topic wick_lowtide with wick "Ask Wick about Lowtide" when true once {
    Says "'It's the old city,' says Wick. 'You go down the Throat Stair at low water and it's all streets, with weed in, and you can find things. Coins.' He rattles his tray. 'You've got five hours, about. When the tide turns you get up high, the aqueduct or the top of the bath-house dome, and you sit there till it goes out again, and you don't go in the bath-house, not ever, because the hollow men are in the bath-house.' He thinks. 'And keep out of the way of the ebb-runners at the landing. They don't like being looked at.'".
  }
  Topic wick_hollow with wick "Ask Wick about the hollow men" when true once {
    Says "Wick stops grinning. 'They were people,' he says. 'Old ones, from when the city was up. Mudlarks see them sometimes in the doorways when the water's coming. They're like coats with nobody in. They come if you swear. My nan says they come for anyone who's broke a promise, so I never promise anything.' He holds out a coin. 'Genuine Aenean. One coin. I'm not promising it's genuine.'".
  }
  Topic wick_grey with wick "Ask Wick about the clerk in grey" when true once {
    Says "'That's Tally,' says Wick. 'I called him that because he's always counting. He asked me my name and wrote it down and asked was I sure. He knows everyone's name in the Withies now. He knows Davy's. He said Davy was on page four.' Wick scuffs the boards. 'He doesn't eat anything. I gave him an eel and he thanked me and wrote it down and put it in his pocket.'".
  }

  // ── The Muffled Drum: Sergeant Durrance and the Muster ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person sedge "Hannelore Sedge" at drum_taproom {
    Role "who keeps the Muffled Drum". Ancestry human. Profession innkeeper. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 6.
  }
  Topic sedge_drum with sedge "Ask Hannelore Sedge about the drum over the bar" when true once {
    Says "'The Third Company's,' says Hannelore. 'Agathe brought it home. She tied the cloth over it herself. Nobody plays it till the last of the Third comes home, she says, and since the summer that's been looking like never.' She wipes the bar. 'Don't touch it. I mean that kindly.'".
  }
  Person durrance "Agathe Durrance" at drum_taproom {
    Role "a sergeant of the Long Muster, out of uniform". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 4. Trait brave. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Sergeant Durrance looks at you over her pot the way she has looked at nineteen years of recruits.".
    Joins "Durrance finishes her pot and stands, and is suddenly a sergeant again. 'Right,' she says. 'Let's go and look at where I'm going.'".
    Leaves "'I'll be at the Drum,' says Durrance. 'Where else.'".
  }
  Topic durrance_vanished with durrance "Ask Durrance about the soldiers who have gone into the sea" when true once {
    Says "'Third Company,' says Durrance. 'All of them. Pike, Haskett, Moll Bryer, the Lucey twins, Davy Teazle. And in order. You know what order? Roll order. Alphabet by platoon, the way the paymaster calls it.' She drinks. 'I've had nineteen years of roll calls. Somebody is calling the roll, and it isn't anybody in this city. Next spring ebb it's Ruddock, Saye, Tobin, Oddie, Amsel. And then it's a page turn, and the top of the next page is me.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, roll_order). Assert knows(actor, durrance_next). }
  }
  Topic durrance_will with durrance "Ask Durrance what she means to do when it is her turn" when knows(actor, durrance_next) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'Go,' says Durrance. 'What do you think?' She puts her hand flat on the table. 'I put this hand on the Stone in the Yard nineteen years ago and swore. Nobody made me. I swore to keep the city, and I've kept it, through two sieges and Sedge Ford and the winter at Galt. If the city's calling me in, I go in.' She looks at her hand. 'I'd like to know who's doing the calling, mind. That's all. I'd like to look at them.'".
  }
  Topic durrance_oath with durrance "Ask Durrance what the oath on the Stone says" when true once {
    Says "Durrance doesn't have to think. ''I swear to keep the city of Tessary, its walls and its people, while I live or until it release me.'' She shrugs. 'Hand on the Stone, say it once, the recruiting sergeant slaps your back and you're the city's. Nobody listens to the words. I listened. I was that kind of recruit.' A short laugh. 'Until it release me. It never has. I've never heard of anyone it did.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, oath_words). }
  }
  Topic durrance_ford with durrance "Ask Durrance about Sedge Ford" when true once {
    Says "'I was ten yards off,' says Durrance. 'Their king came down the bank on a grey horse with his whole household round him. We were finished. We knew it, they knew it. And in the middle of the river he gets off his horse, and goes down on his knees in the water, and holds out his sword to Captain Ancrum hilt first.' She turns her pot. 'People say he looked like a man praying. He didn't. He looked like a man being pushed down by a hand on the back of his neck. And there wasn't anybody behind him.'".
  }
  Topic durrance_join with durrance "Ask Durrance to come with you into Lowtide" when knows(actor, hall_of_oaths_way) and knows(actor, durrance_next) and not willing(durrance, actor) and not travelsWith(durrance, actor) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "Durrance looks at you a long moment. 'To the Hall of Oaths,' she says. 'Where they go in.' She pushes her pot away. 'Yes. I'd like to see the door before I walk through it. And you'll want someone who can hold a line when the tide comes, and that's me.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(durrance, actor). }
  }
  Initially Set hire(durrance) to 0.

  Person fisk "Benno Fisk" at drum_taproom {
    Role "a corporal of the Long Muster, in a new coat". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
  }
  Initially Assert serves(fisk, sault).
  Topic fisk_work with fisk "Ask Fisk where he got the new coat" when true once {
    Says "'Factor Sault,' says Fisk, and smooths it. 'Best employer in Tessary. Day's pay for a day's work, and she knows your name. She knew my name before I knew hers.' He winks. 'Night work too, for them as don't ask questions. Carrying. Down Saltgate way, under the warehouse. Pays double.' He drinks. 'I don't ask questions.'".
  }
  Topic fisk_board with fisk "Ask Fisk what the Muster thinks of the Board" when true once {
    Says "'The Board?' says Fisk. 'The Board sent us to Hethra for eleven years and now it's going to hold a meeting about whether it owes us. A meeting.' He laughs, not pleasantly. 'There's lads at the Muster hall say if the Board votes no, they'll go up the Terraces and ask again, louder. The Factor says not to. The Factor says leave it to her.'".
  }

  // ── Saltgate: Factor Sault ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person sault "Imma Sault" at sault_office {
    Role "Factor of the Salt Moiety". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 5. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Factor Sault looks up from her ledgers and wipes her fingers on a cloth and holds out her hand, salt and all.".
  }
  Relation hiredBySault(group).
  Topic sault_work with sault "Ask the Factor about the veterans who have gone into the sea" when not hiredBySault(actor) once {
    Says "'My lads,' says Factor Sault. 'Forty of them on my books at the Muster hall, and six of the forty gone into the water since the summer, and the Board says deserters.' She snorts. 'Deserters. Men who'd come to me for work at dawn every day for a month. You're a stranger here, which is useful: nobody's paying you to see nothing. Find out who's taking them, and how, and bring it to me. Twenty coin.' She holds your eye. 'And if the grey clerk who goes about writing down their names is any part of it, I want to know what he writes.'".
    On discuss { Assert hiredBySault(actor). }
  }
  Topic sault_board with sault "Ask the Factor what she thinks of the Board" when true once {
    Says "'The furniture?' Factor Sault laughs. 'Eight chairs, five of them inherited. They started a war over salt springs they could have bought for a tenth of what it cost, borrowed to fight it, and now the bill's come in, they want to send it to the men who did the fighting.' She spreads her hands, salt-cracked. 'I came up off the pans. I could tell you the name of every rake in my yards. They couldn't tell you the name of one soldier who died for them. Somebody in this city has to be able to count.'".
  }
  Topic sault_muster with sault "Ask the Factor about her hiring hall" when true once {
    Says "'No man turned away who wore the coat,' says Sault. 'It costs me. The Board was supposed to look after them and didn't, so I do.' She shrugs. 'And they work, and they're grateful, and in a city that's about to have eight thousand angry soldiers in it, I would rather they were grateful to me than to anyone else. I don't pretend it's charity.'".
  }
  // What she pays for: the grey clerk's inventory, copied.
  Item inventory_copy "a copy of the Assessor's inventory" is ledger_copy at tideline_steps hidden until inventory_copied.
  Kind ledger_copy "a copied page of an inventory" is gear worth 1 weighing 0
    described "Names in a careful hand you made yourself from someone else's careful hand, in roll order, with a column of marks no one in Tessary could read.".
  Discovery inventory_copied "You have copied pages of the Assessor's inventory: the Muster's names in roll order, those called and those to come.".
  Relation saultInformed(group). Relation caughtCopying(group).
  // By night the Assessor stands on the Tideline Steps watching the water, with the ledger open on the step beside them.
  Action copy_inventory(actor: group, site: place) "Copy the pages of the Assessor's ledger, open on the step behind them" {
    Time 2.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, tideline_steps) and at(tally, tideline_steps)
      and dark() and not travelsWith(tally, actor) and not knows(actor, inventory_copied) and not caughtCopying(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, inventory_copied). Assert knows(actor, roll_order). Assert knows(actor, durrance_next). }
    On failure { Assert caughtCopying(actor). }
    Result "The Assessor stands at the water's edge with their back to you, quite still, and the ledger lies open on the step in the lamplight. You copy two pages by its light, names in roll order and columns of marks you cannot read, and the Assessor does not turn round. Third Company. Page four: Teazle, D. Page five, near the top: Durrance, A.".
    Otherwise "You have copied half a page when the Assessor says, without turning round, 'That is the property of the Balance.' They come and close the ledger, and take it up, and look at you with no expression at all. 'I note it,' they say.".
  }
  Event sault_paid near sault when keeps(sault, inventory_copy) "Factor Sault reads the pages through twice, running a salt-cracked finger down the names, stopping at some. 'Roll order,' she says. 'Well, well.' She counts twenty coin onto the ledger without looking at them. 'You've earned it. I'll not forget it.' She folds the pages away into her coat." then {
    Assert saultInformed(sault). Decrease quantity(sault, gold) by 20. Increase quantity(party, gold) by 20. }
  Initially Set quantity(sault, gold) to 60.

  // ── The Lettered Quarter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person quire "Absalom Quire" at exchequer_room {
    Role "Treasurer of Tessary". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "The Treasurer looks up as if he had been expecting someone else, or everyone, and blinks.".
  }
  Topic quire_vanished with quire "Ask the Treasurer about the soldiers who have gone into the sea" when not knows(actor, council_knows) once {
    Says "'Deserters,' says Quire, too quickly. 'That is the Board's finding. Men who have been away eleven years do not always want to come home to what they left.' He moves a paperweight on his desk from one stack to another and back. 'I'm sorry. I am very tired. Is there anything else?'".
  }
  Relation quireConfided(group).
  Topic quire_list_asked with quire "Ask the Treasurer about his list of names" when knows(actor, council_knows) and not quireConfided(actor) once {
    Says "Quire looks at the list for a long time. 'A hundred and thirty-eight,' he says. 'I send their mothers something every month. Out of my own salary, which the city also does not pay.' He takes off his spectacles. 'I signed it. Twelve years ago. We went down under the sea, six of us, and they showed us a thing like a ledger the size of a ship, and an old man who could not lie read us the terms, and we signed, because we were going to lose the war, and we won.' His hands are shaking. 'The Muster's oaths. As collateral. I put my name to eight thousand men like a farmer putting up his cows.'".
    On discuss { Assert quireConfided(actor). Assert knows(actor, collateral). }
  }
  Topic quire_terms with quire "Ask the Treasurer what the city must do to pay" when quireConfided(actor) and not knows(actor, promise_weight) once {
    Says "'Keep a promise,' says Quire. 'Of equal weight. Their words.' He laughs, horribly. 'Do you know what weighs as much as a king's ancestral oath, in their scales? A promise of a whole people to a whole people. And there is exactly one of those in the city's books, and I have it by heart: land and a pension for every man who comes home. It would cost two hundred thousand marks. The treasury has nothing. The Board will vote no on the thirteenth day, because there is no money, and on the fifteenth the note falls due, and then...' He doesn't finish.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, promise_weight). Assert knows(actor, enlist_promise). }
  }

  Person pounce "Hesketh Pounce" at pounce_stall {
    Role "a scrivener of the Row". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
  }
  Topic pounce_trade with pounce "Ask Pounce about his trade" when true once {
    Says "'Contracts drawn, contracts read, contracts explained,' says Pounce. 'The first is easy, the second is a skill, the third is extra because nobody likes what I tell them.' He sands a page. 'Tessary is a city where a fishwife will sue a gull. I have made a good living out of it for thirty years. I keep every draft I ever wrote, you know. A scrivener who burns his drafts is a scrivener who gets sued.'".
  }
  Topic pounce_council with pounce "Ask Pounce whether he has ever drawn a contract for the Board" when true once {
    Says "Pounce's pen stops. 'Once,' he says. 'Twelve years ago. A fair copy of an instrument, done at night in the Council House with a councillor at my elbow and sworn to silence after. Strangest thing I ever copied. Half of it was in a hand I had never seen and had to copy by shape.' He looks at you sideways. 'I kept my draft. Of course I kept my draft. I am sworn to silence, mind. But a scrivener's drafts are his own property, and his property is for sale, and it is no breach of silence to sell a man a piece of paper he will read for himself.' He names the price: 'Six coin.'".
    On discuss { Assert pounceOffered(actor). }
  }
  Relation pounceOffered(group).
  Item pounce_draft "Pounce's draft of the War Note" is draft_kind at pounce_stall hidden until draft_bought.
  Kind draft_kind "a scrivener's draft" is gear worth 1 weighing 0
    described "Six closely written pages of reed-paper, foxed and folded, the draft of a fair copy: a contract between the city of Tessary and a party named only as the Ledger Below.".
  Discovery draft_bought "Pounce has sold you his twelve-year-old draft of the Board's secret instrument.".
  Action buy_draft(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Pay Pounce six coin for his old draft" {
    Speaker pounce. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pounce, site) and pounceOffered(actor)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient)
      and not knows(actor, draft_bought) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6.
    Resolve acquire(pounce_draft, draft_kind, recipient).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Increase quantity(pounce, gold) by 6. Assert knows(actor, draft_bought). Retract at(pounce_draft, pounce_stall). }
    Result "Pounce goes to a chest and comes back with six pages folded small, and counts your coins before he lets go of them. 'You did not get these from me,' he says. 'You got them from a man you met in a tavern who resembled me.'".
  }
  Action read_draft(actor: group, site: place) "Read Pounce's draft of the War Note" {
    Time 2.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and carries(actor, pounce_draft) and not benighted(actor)
      and not knows(actor, note_terms).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, note_terms). }
    Result "You read it through twice. The city's half is plain Tessarine legal hand: the city of Tessary, as heir to the Aenean emperors in the matter of oaths, borrows the calling of an oath sworn by the house of Hethra, &c. The other half is in a script Pounce copied by shape, ruled like a ledger; but the terms are restated in the city's hand at the foot, as terms are. The Long Muster's oaths as surety. Silver monthly. And at the Feast of Settlement in the twelfth year, the principal, to be paid in a kept promise of equal weight. The Treasurer's signature. Five councillors'. And a sixth mark that is not a signature at all, only a set of ruled lines.".
  }
  Action explain_draft(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Pounce two coin to explain the clause about equal weight" {
    Speaker pounce. Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pounce, site) and carries(actor, pounce_draft)
      and knows(actor, note_terms) and not knows(actor, promise_weight) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Increase quantity(pounce, gold) by 2. Assert knows(actor, promise_weight). Assert knows(actor, enlist_promise). }
    Result "Pounce puts on a second pair of spectacles over the first. 'Equal weight,' he says. 'Weight of what? Not silver, or it would say silver. A promise of equal weight to an oath that bound a royal house for nine hundred years.' He taps the page. 'A people's promise, then, to a people. Has this city ever made one?' He answers himself before you can. 'Land and a pension for every man who comes home. I drew the recruiting bills. So if the city keeps that, it pays this.' He takes off both pairs of spectacles. 'And if it doesn't, it doesn't. That will be two coin. I did say nobody likes what I tell them.'".
  }

  // The Office of Seals: the queue, and the Keeper of the Seal.
  Person queue "the queue" at seals_hall {
    Role "who have been waiting since breakfast, or Tuesday, or longer, each with a document". Ancestry human. Numbers 1. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
  }
  Topic queue_asked with queue "Ask the queue how long they have been waiting" when true once {
    Says "Several people answer at once. A man with a deed: 'Since breakfast.' A woman with a marriage contract: 'Since Tuesday.' An old man near the front, without turning round: 'My father held this place in the queue before me. I am sealing the lease he came to seal. It has run out, but it is the principle.'".
  }
  Person deckle "Ulric Deckle" at seals_inner {
    Role "Keeper of the Great Seal". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Wants seal_kind.
  }
  Relation reachedKeeper(group).
  Action wait_in_queue(actor: group, site: place) "Take your place in the queue" {
    Description "It moves. Slowly, but it moves.".
    Time 18.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(queue, site) and not reachedKeeper(actor)
      and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 15.
    On success { Assert reachedKeeper(actor). }
    Interrupted when threatened(actor).
    Result "Three hours later, having learned the life history of a rope-maker's widow and the full grounds of a dispute about a fence, you reach the grille. A clerk looks at you over it. 'Business?' And, since you have none he recognises: 'The Keeper will see you. The Keeper sees everyone who reaches the grille. It is the law.' He opens the door.".
  }
  Thing grille "the grille" on seals_grille {
    State shut blocking "A clerk behind the grille admits whoever reaches the head of the queue, and nobody else.".
    State open "The clerk has opened the grille for you.".
  }
  Query keeperSends() means deedsSealed(ossel) or sealStolen(ossel) or votePassed(ossel) and night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) >= 15.
  Rule grille_opens when (reachedKeeper(party) or keeperSends()) and state(grille, shut) { Assert state(grille, open). }
  Rule grille_shuts when state(grille, open) and not reachedKeeper(party) and not keeperSends() { Assert state(grille, shut). }
  Rule grille_closes_at_night when dark() and reachedKeeper(party) and not at(party, seals_inner) and not keeperSends() { Retract reachedKeeper(party). }
  Topic deckle_seal with deckle "Ask the Keeper about the Great Seal" when true once {
    Says "'The Seal of Tessary,' says Deckle, and lifts the glass bell an inch as if letting it breathe. 'What it seals, the city has done. A deed sealed here is land given. A treaty sealed here is peace made. If the Board were to vote the Veterans' Settlement' (he says it the way one says the name of a disease) 'every one of eight thousand deeds would have to pass under this hand. My clerks could do it in a night and a day, if they did nothing else.' He lowers the bell. 'Nobody has asked them to.'".
  }

  // ── The Terraces ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person marrable "Ysbel Marrable" at marrable_room {
    Role "who sits for the Eel Moiety on the Board, a veteran with one sleeve pinned up". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
  }
  Topic marrable_vote with marrable "Ask Councillor Marrable how the vote will go" when not voted(ossel) once {
    Says "'Badly,' says Marrable. 'Eight chairs. Mine is yes. Old Lisle has buried two sons in Hethra; he's yes, if he's awake. Salt is Sault's and Sault says no, there's no money, which is true. Rope is Dauntry and Dauntry votes the way Sault tells him. Greaves and Vantage are the furniture and will not give an inch of their land. Paper is Haverick, who cares about nothing but his goose, and Ship is Orme, who will vote for whatever he thinks will be paid for.' She counts on one hand, which takes no time. 'I need five. I have two.'".
  }
  Topic marrable_sway with marrable "Ask Councillor Marrable what would change their minds" when not voted(ossel) once {
    Says "'Proof,' says Marrable. 'They call the vanished deserters because if they're not deserters, something worse is happening and somebody on the Board knows what. Show them the Treasurer knows. Show them why. Bring them someone they can't call a liar.' She looks at the pinned sleeve. 'And keep the Muster off the Terraces. If soldiers come up that hill shouting the night before, Orme and Lisle will vote no out of fright and I won't blame them.'".
  }
  Person amaury "Amaury of Hethra" at kings_rooms {
    Role "King of Hethra, a hostage in Tessary". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 6. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "The King of Hethra looks up from his draughts board. 'A visitor,' he says. 'How unusual. Sit, sit. I am allowed visitors. I am allowed everything except the door.'".
  }
  Topic amaury_kneeling with amaury "Ask the King about the Kneeling at Sedge Ford" when true once {
    Says "'Ah,' says the King. 'The famous kneeling.' He moves a draught. 'I had won. You understand that? I had your city's Muster pinned against the river and I rode down to accept its surrender. And in the middle of the ford I felt a hand. Here.' He touches the back of his neck. 'Old. Patient. Quite certain of its rights. Nine hundred years old, I would say, if a hand can be old. And my knees went into the water and my sword went out hilt first and I heard my own voice yielding the kingdom.' He looks at the board. 'Your saint's day for it is the twelfth of Haying. I watch the procession from this window. It is the only day of the year I drink before noon.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, kneeling_felt). }
  }
  Relation amauryPlayed(group).
  Action play_amaury(actor: group, site: place) "Play the King a game of Hethran draughts" {
    Speaker amaury. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(amaury, site) and not amauryPlayed(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert amauryPlayed(actor). Assert amauryWon(actor). }
    On failure { Assert amauryPlayed(actor). }
    Result "It is a long game, and the King talks all through it, about his horses, the weather in the hills, the absurdity of a city that keeps its prisoner in better rooms than its Treasurer. Somewhere in the second hour you see the trap he has been building on the left side of the board, and walk round it, and he sits back. 'You see what's in front of you,' he says. 'That is rarer than it should be. Come again.'".
    Otherwise "It is a long game, and the King talks all through it, and in the second hour springs a trap on the left side of the board that he has been building since the first move. 'Hethran draughts,' he says kindly, sweeping up your pieces, 'is a game for people who expect to lose a war. Come again.'".
  }
  Relation amauryWon(group).
  Relation amauryWillTestify(group).
  Topic amaury_told with amaury "Tell the King how Sedge Ford was won" when knows(actor, note_terms) and not amauryWillTestify(actor) once {
    Says "The King hears you out without moving a piece. When you have done, he laughs, quite quietly, for a long time. 'An oath of my house,' he says, 'to the Aenean emperors. Bought back off a shelf under the sea by a city of paper-makers, for silver, on the never-never.' He wipes his eyes. 'And then paid for in their own soldiers when the silver ran out. Oh, that is good. That is the best thing I have heard in a year.' He stops laughing. 'If you want this told to the Board in a voice they cannot dismiss as a stranger's, I will tell it. They will have to let me out of these rooms to hear it, and I should like to see the inside of their chamber, and the painting.' He moves a draught at last. 'I should like very much to see their faces.'".
    On discuss { Assert amauryWillTestify(actor). Assert knows(actor, kneeling_felt). }
  }
  Topic amaury_wants with amaury "Ask the King what he wants" when true once {
    Says "'To go home,' says the King. 'My ransom is a sum your Board cannot ask for and my people cannot pay, which suits both of them. And to know what happened to me in that river.' He sets a piece down very precisely. 'A man can lose a kingdom and live. I find it is harder to have been made to give it away.'".
  }

  // ── The Ninth Assessor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A clerk of the Scruples, sent up to inventory the collateral before the note falls due. Exact; unable to lie;
  // answers what it is asked and nothing it is not.
  Person tally "the Ninth Assessor" at withies {
    Role "a clerk in a grey coat with a ledger, whose skin is faintly ruled like paper". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns they. Manner stoic.
    Called "Tally".
    Seen when not tallyUnravelled(ossel).
    Greets "The clerk in grey looks up from the ledger. Close to, the skin of their face and hands is very faintly ruled, like a page, in lines as fine as hairs. 'Good day,' they say. 'You are not on my inventory.'".
    Joins "'Our inquiries coincide,' says the Assessor, and closes the ledger on a ribbon. 'I will accompany you. I will note anything you do that bears on the collateral.'".
    Leaves "'I shall continue the inventory,' says the Assessor. 'I am on page nine.'".
  }
  Initially Set hire(tally) to 0.
  Topic tally_who with tally "Ask the clerk in grey who they are" when true once {
    Says "'I am the Ninth Assessor of the Scruples,' says the clerk. 'I am taking an inventory.' A pause, which seems to be for you to say something, and when you do not: 'The children call me Tally. It is not my name. My name is held. Tally is accurate as a description, and I do not object to it.'".
  }
  Topic tally_counting with tally "Ask the Assessor what they are counting" when true once {
    Says "'The Long Muster,' says the Assessor, 'page by page, in the order of its roll.' They make a small mark. 'I am not at liberty to say why. The affairs of a debtor are not discussed with a third party. You are a third party.' A pause, quite friendly. 'You may ask me anything. I will not lie to you. I will decline a great deal.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, roll_order). }
  }
  Topic tally_where with tally "Ask the Assessor where the soldiers you saw walk into the sea have gone" when knows(actor, calling_witnessed) and not knows(actor, held_alive) once {
    Says "The Assessor considers whether this is the affair of a debtor, and decides, visibly, that what you saw with your own eyes is your own affair. 'Into the Holding,' they say, 'where pledged things are kept. They are not harmed. They are held. They stand asleep with the rest of what has been pledged and forfeit, and they do not age.' A pause. 'You are distressed. I am sorry. It is a lawful collection.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, held_alive). }
  }
  Topic tally_discharge with tally "Ask the Assessor what would bring the held home" when knows(actor, held_alive) and not knows(actor, release_law) once {
    Says "'The discharge of the debt they stand surety for,' says the Assessor, as if reading it. 'A debt is discharged in two ways. It is kept, or it is released: if the one to whom a promise was made says freely to the one who made it, I hold you quit, that weighs in the Balance exactly as the keeping does.' A pause. 'People forget the second. Nobody releases anybody. I have often wondered why.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, release_law). }
  }
  Topic tally_confirm with tally "Ask the Assessor whether the city pledged its soldiers' oaths" when (knows(actor, council_knows) or quireConfided(actor)) and not knows(actor, collateral) once {
    Says "'You have seen the Treasurer's list,' says the Assessor. 'Then you have it from the debtor's own officer, and I may confirm what he has let you see.' They open the ledger flat. 'The oaths of the Long Muster, sworn on the instrument the city calls the Oath Stone, are pledged as security on a debt the city owes to the Balance. Since the silver stopped in the summer, interest has been taken in oaths at each spring ebb, in the order of the roll.' They close it. 'Some of the collateral has died since it was pledged, of wounds and of drink. I am noting that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, collateral). }
  }
  Topic tally_debt with tally "Ask the Assessor what the city borrowed" when knows(actor, collateral) and not knows(actor, note_terms) once {
    Says "'The terms are the debtor's affair,' says the Assessor. And then, with great exactness: 'The city made a fair copy of the instrument in its own hand, as a debtor must. Its Board had it made at night by a scrivener of the Row, under an oath of silence.' They look at you. 'In my experience of this city, a scrivener keeps his drafts. I say so as an observation about scriveners.'".
  }
  Topic tally_how with tally "Ask the Assessor what promise would weigh as much as the War Note" when knows(actor, note_terms) and not knows(actor, promise_weight) once {
    Says "'I am not permitted to advise the debtor,' says the Assessor. 'You are not the debtor.' They consider this for some time. 'A promise is weighed by who makes it and to whom, and what it binds. An oath of a royal house to an empire is very heavy. Only a promise of a whole people to a whole people would balance it. I have read the city's books. It has made one.' They look, for the first time, faintly uncomfortable. 'I cannot tell you which. I can tell you that it is printed on a bill on the shelf of a house in this ward, and that I have read it there.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, promise_weight). }
  }
  Topic tally_next with tally "Ask the Assessor whose names are on the next page" when knows(actor, roll_order) and night(ossel) < 8 once {
    Says "The Assessor opens the ledger at a ribbon. 'Ruddock, J., private. Saye, W., private. Tobin, M., private. Oddie, F., drummer. Amsel, K., private. Then the page turns. Durrance, A., sergeant, Third Company, nineteen years' service.' They look up. 'Then Elcock, Fane, Garrow, Hobb, Ince and Jessup. Twelve.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, durrance_next). }
  }
  Topic tally_join with tally "Ask the Assessor to come with you to the Hall of Oaths" when knows(actor, hall_of_oaths_way) and knows(actor, held_alive) and not willing(tally, actor) and not travelsWith(tally, actor) once {
    Says "'The Hall of Oaths,' says the Assessor. 'The way down.' They are quiet, and you have the impression of a calculation being done. 'I am to return below before the Feast in any case, to report. If you are going that way, I will take you through the wall, and note what you do on the other side of it.' They hold out a hand, ruled like a page. 'I must ask you to promise not to lie to me. It is a small thing, for you. You will find it is not small below.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(tally, actor). Assert promisedTally(actor). }
  }
  Relation promisedTally(group).
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/placed:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // The Ossel delta as a country beyond a march: the company that comes in along the Causeway is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/plot.k:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The state of the city's affairs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Relations shared by every movement: who is held, whether the Board has voted, how the note stands.
  Relation heldNow(group). Relation voted(place). Relation votePassed(place).
  // At the Settlement the note is discharged (kept, released or voided), or it falls in: foreclosed, or taken up.
  Relation discharged(place). Relation foreclosed(place). Relation saultHoldsNote(place).
  Relation keptPromise(place). Relation released(place). Relation noteVoid(place). Relation noteTorn(place).
  Relation matured(place).

  // ── Factor Sault's undertakings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What she does whether or not anyone interferes: makes the vanished out to be deserters; buys what she can of the
  // Muster; leans on the Treasurer; keeps the Board from voting the Settlement by whatever it takes; and, when the
  // Feast passes, takes up the note. Her lightermen do the heavy work and take prisoners rather than kill.
  Person lightermen "Sault's lightermen" at warehouse_floor {
    Role "three big men in salt-stiff jerkins, with cudgels". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 3. Pronouns they.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Three big men in salt-stiff jerkins step out from between the stacks. 'Warehouse is shut,' says the biggest.".
    Comes "Sault's lightermen come at you with their cudgels up, not hurrying, the way men do who have done this before.".
    Pleads "The last of the lightermen backs off with his hands open. 'Not paid enough,' he says. 'Not for this.'".
  }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(lightermen). Initially Assert serves(lightermen, sault).
  Rule lightermen_captured when captured(lightermen, party) and at(party, ?p)
    says "You wake on the salt crust out on the Pans, at dawn, with a split lip and your purse lighter. Somebody has left you a cup of water, which is the Factor all over." {
    Retract captured(lightermen, party). Retract at(party, ?p). Assert at(party, pans). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 4. }

  // What the Factor says, seeing her letter in a stranger's hand: nothing.
  Observe sault_sees_letter near sault when carries(party, sault_letter) and not knows(party, sault_saw_letter) "The Factor's eyes go to the letter in your hand, with her own wax on it, and come back to your face. She says nothing about it at all. She goes on talking about the price of peat." teaches sault_saw_letter.
  Discovery sault_saw_letter "Factor Sault has seen her letter in your hands.".

  // What the city shows a company that comes back to it, of what was done while it was away.
  Observe drum_boots at drum_taproom when durranceCalled(ossel) and heldNow(durrance) "Agathe Durrance's boots stand on the bar of the Muffled Drum, side by side, toes to the door, under the drum with the cloth over it. Nobody drinks at that end of the bar.".
  Observe exchequer_shut at exchequer_room when quireDrowned(ossel) "The Treasurer's room has been shut up. The cot is stripped, the ledgers stacked, and someone has tied a black ribbon round the empty bottle and left it on the desk.".
  Observe terraces_riot at terraces when riotHappened(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "Glass glitters in the gutters of the Terraces. The Council House windows are boarded, and men of the Watch stand on its portico with pikes, looking anxious.".
  Observe marrable_abed at marrable_room when marrableHurt(ossel) "Ysbel Marrable is sitting up in a chair by the window with her head bandaged and one eye closed. 'They didn't take the other arm,' she says. 'Considerate of them.'".
  Observe landgate_lost at landgate when voted(ossel) and not votePassed(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "On the board, the Speaker's notice: the question of the Veterans' Settlement is lost, the city having no money. Pasted over half of it, the old recruiting bill: LAND AND A PENSION FOR EVERY MAN WHO COMES HOME.".
  Observe landgate_carried at landgate when votePassed(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "On the board, in fresh print: THE VETERANS' SETTLEMENT IS CARRIED. Someone has drawn a pair of scales on it in charcoal, and someone else a goose.".

  // 1. The whisper: from the second day, bills on the Landgate board and talk in the Withies.
  Relation whispered(place).
  Rule whisper_starts when night(ossel) >= 2 and not whispered(ossel) { Assert whispered(ossel). }
  Observe whisper_bill at landgate when whispered(ossel) and not voted(ossel) "A new bill on the board, printed, not handwritten, on good paper: DESERTERS. Those who have left their homes by night since the summer are absconders from the city's service and from their just debts. Information to the Watch. Beneath it, in pencil, someone has written: MY BOY NEVER OWED ANYONE A PENNY.".
  Observe whisper_withies at withies when whispered(ossel) and not dark() and not voted(ossel) "Two women on the boardwalk stop talking as you pass. You catch the word deserter, and the other one saying, quite loudly, that she'd like to see the man who printed it come and say it here.".

  // 2. The Sergeant's silver: on the fifth day she offers to pay the next spring ebb's interest herself, in silver, if
  // Durrance will sergeant her Muster. Durrance takes it only if she has learned what the city did with her oath and
  // nothing yet of what Sault means to do with it.
  Relation durranceKnowsSold(group). Relation durranceKnowsFraud(group). Relation durranceKnowsRelease(group).
  Relation durranceKnowsSault(group). Relation saultOffered(place). Relation durranceSaults(place).
  Rule silver_offered when night(ossel) >= 5 and hour(clock) == 12 and not saultOffered(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) {
    Assert saultOffered(ossel). }
  Rule silver_taken when saultOffered(ossel) and durranceKnowsSold(durrance) and not durranceKnowsSault(durrance)
    and not durranceSaults(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and night(ossel) < 8 {
    Assert durranceSaults(ossel). Assert interestPaid(ossel). Assert serves(durrance, sault). }
  Observe durrance_refused near durrance when saultOffered(ossel) and not durranceSaults(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and night(ossel) < 8 and not knows(party, sault_offer_known) "'The Factor sent for me,' says Durrance. 'Offered to pay the silver for the next ebb out of her own pocket, all twelve of us, if I'd sergeant her Muster after.' She turns her pot. 'I told her I'd sworn already. Once is enough for anyone.'" teaches sault_offer_known.
  Observe durrance_took near durrance when durranceSaults(ossel) and not knows(party, sault_offer_known) "Durrance has a new coat on, a good one, and does not meet your eye. 'The Factor's paying the next ebb's silver,' she says. 'All twelve. Out of her own pocket. And I'm her sergeant after.' She drinks. 'The city sold my oath. The Factor bought it back. I don't see the difference, and nor will Ruddock's mother.'" teaches sault_offer_known.
  Discovery sault_offer_known "Factor Sault offered to pay the next spring ebb's interest in silver from her own purse if Sergeant Durrance would sergeant her Muster.".
  Topic tell_durrance_sold with durrance "Tell Durrance what the city did with the Muster's oaths" when knows(actor, collateral) and not durranceKnowsSold(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "Durrance hears you out. Then she sits for a long time looking at the drum over the bar with the cloth on it. 'Collateral,' she says at last. 'Like a cow.' She laughs, once. 'Nineteen years. I buried the whole of the Second Platoon at Galt in one trench. And the Board had us in a pawnshop the whole time.' She finishes her pot. 'Well. It's still my oath. They sold it. I didn't.'".
    On discuss { Assert durranceKnowsSold(durrance). }
  }
  Topic tell_durrance_sault with durrance "Tell Durrance what the Factor means to do with the note" when knows(actor, sault_bid) and not durranceKnowsSault(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'Govern,' says Durrance. 'With us.' She puts her pot down carefully. 'Not pay us. Own us. Call us out of wherever we are and stand us on the Tidewall in her coats.' Her face does not change. 'She'd feed us. She'd be better than the Board. I'd still be a cow.'".
    On discuss { Assert durranceKnowsSault(durrance). }
  }
  Rule durrance_quits_sault when durranceSaults(ossel) and durranceKnowsSault(durrance) and serves(durrance, sault)
    says "Durrance takes off the Factor's coat and folds it and leaves it on the bench." { Retract serves(durrance, sault). }
  Topic tell_durrance_fraud with durrance "Tell Durrance that the note was drawn to fail" when knows(actor, note_designed) and not durranceKnowsFraud(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "Durrance listens with her hands flat on the table. When you have finished she is quiet so long that Hannelore comes over to see if she is all right. 'A promise made to be broken,' she says. 'By them. The ones who keep the books.' She looks at her right hand, the one she laid on the Stone. 'Then what did I swear to? A trap?' She stands up. 'An oath sworn into a fraud is no oath. My grandmother could have told them that. I'm not going in when the drum goes. And I'm not going to let anyone else go either.'".
    On discuss { Assert durranceKnowsFraud(durrance). }
  }
  Topic tell_durrance_release with durrance "Tell Durrance that a promise can be discharged by release" when knows(actor, release_law) and not durranceKnowsRelease(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'Released,' says Durrance slowly. 'If the one it was made to says, I hold you quit.' She is looking at the drum. 'The city promised us land and pension. That's the promise in their scales. And it's ours. It was made to us.' Her hand closes. 'So if we let them off it. If the Muster stood on the Stone and said, we hold you quit, keep your land...' She stops. 'Then the debt's paid. With our pensions. And the lads come home.' She laughs, not happily. 'Eleven years, and we save the city twice, and the second time we pay for it. Let me think. Don't ask me today. Let me think.'".
    On discuss { Assert durranceKnowsRelease(durrance). }
  }

  // 3. The eighth night: Durrance walks. A company with her an hour before the ebb can hold her back; the drum over
  // the Drum's bar, uncovered and beaten to the stand-down, breaks the step of any soldier of the Third who hears it.
  Relation durranceWalking(place). Relation heldBack(group). Relation drumBeaten(place). Relation elcockTaken(place).
  Relation durranceCalled(place).
  Query durranceSafe() means durranceSpared(ossel) or interestPaid(ossel) or heldBack(durrance) or durranceKnowsFraud(durrance).
  Rule durrance_walks when night(ossel) == 7 and hour(clock) == 1 and not durranceWalking(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance)
    and not durranceSafe() { Assert durranceWalking(ossel). }
  Event durrance_walks_seen near durrance when durranceWalking(ossel) and not heldBack(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) and hour(clock) == 1
    "Durrance stands up. She does it all at once, the way a soldier stands when an officer comes in, and her pot goes over and she does not look at it. Her eyes are open. She is listening to something. Then she bends and begins, very neatly, to unlace her boots.".
  Action hold_durrance(actor: group, site: place) "Get hold of Durrance and keep her from the Steps" {
    Description "She is a sergeant of nineteen years and she is not awake.".
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(durrance, site) or travelsWith(durrance, actor))
      and durranceWalking(ossel) and not heldBack(durrance) and not triedHolding(actor) and hour(clock) == 1.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert heldBack(durrance). }
    On failure { Assert triedHolding(actor). }
    Result "You get your arms round her from behind and she throws you off as if you were a coat, and you get them round her again, and this time you hang on, and go down with her, and lie on her on the boards while she fights in perfect silence with her eyes open. It goes on a long time. Then, all at once, she goes slack, and blinks, and says in her own voice, 'Get off me, you great lump.'".
    Otherwise "You get hold of her and she simply walks on, and takes you with her a step, and puts you down against the wall with one hand, quite gently, as if you were in her way. Then she goes out barefoot into the night.".
  }
  Relation triedHolding(group).
  Thing third_drum "the Third Company's drum" at drum_taproom {
    State muffled "Over the bar hangs a regimental drum with a black cloth tied over its head.".
    State bare "The Third Company's drum hangs over the bar with its head bare.".
    Change uncover "Pull the cloth off the Third Company's drum and beat the stand-down" from muffled to bare.
  }
  Rule drum_breaks when state(third_drum, bare) and durranceWalking(ossel) and not heldBack(durrance) and hour(clock) == 1
    says "The drum is very loud in the low room. Rap, rap, and the long roll, and rap: the stand-down, that every soldier of the Muster has heard at the end of every day for eleven years. Durrance stops with one boot off. All over the Withies, in the stilt-houses, you hear other things stop: a door, a ladder, someone on the boardwalk. Durrance sits down, hard, on the floor, and looks at the boot in her hand as if she has never seen it." {
    Assert heldBack(durrance). Assert drumBeaten(ossel). }
  Rule drum_offends when state(third_drum, bare) and not drumBeaten(ossel) and at(party, drum_taproom)
    says "Hannelore Sedge comes round the bar and puts the cloth back over the drum's head, and ties it, and looks at you. 'I said don't,' she says. 'I said it kindly.'" {
    Assert state(third_drum, muffled). }
  Rule durrance_goes when night(ossel) == 8 and callings(ossel) == 8 and not durranceCalled(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance)
    and not durranceSafe() {
    Assert durranceCalled(ossel). Assert heldNow(durrance). Assert asleep(durrance). Retract travelsWith(durrance, party).
    Retract willing(durrance, party). Assert at(durrance, ranks). Retract serves(durrance, sault). }
  Relation heldRoom(place). Initially Assert heldRoom(ranks).
  Rule durrance_leaves_place when heldNow(durrance) and at(durrance, ?p) and not heldRoom(?p) { Retract at(durrance, ?p). }
  Rule durrance_gone_told when durranceCalled(ossel) and not knows(party, durrance_gone)
    and inTessary() says "In the morning Hannelore Sedge stands Agathe Durrance's boots on the bar of the Muffled Drum, side by side, toes to the door, under the drum with the cloth over it. Nobody drinks there all day." teaches durrance_gone { }
  Discovery durrance_gone "Sergeant Durrance answered the drum at the eighth night's spring ebb, and walked into the sea.".
  // Whoever is passed over, the weight is the weight: another goes in their place.
  Rule elcock_goes when night(ossel) == 8 and callings(ossel) == 8 and not elcockTaken(ossel) and not interestPaid(ossel)
    and (durranceSpared(ossel) or heldBack(durrance) or durranceKnowsFraud(durrance)) and not heldNow(durrance) {
    Assert elcockTaken(ossel). }
  Rule elcock_told when elcockTaken(ossel) and not knows(party, elcock_known)
    and inTessary() says "In the morning there are twelve pairs of boots on the Tideline Steps. The eleventh pair is small, and very new, and belongs to Robin Elcock, who was a drummer, and was nineteen." teaches elcock_known { }
  Discovery elcock_known "Durrance was not taken at the eighth night's ebb. Robin Elcock, a drummer of nineteen, was taken in her place.".
  Topic durrance_elcock with durrance "Tell Durrance who went in her place" when knows(actor, elcock_known) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'Elcock,' says Durrance. 'Robin Elcock. He couldn't keep time. I used to make him march at the back so the step wouldn't go to pieces.' She looks at the drum. 'He went in my place.' A long silence. 'Right. Then I owe him. And I pay what I owe, which is more than this city does.'".
    On discuss { Assert durranceOwes(durrance). }
  }
  Relation durranceOwes(group).

  // 4. The Treasurer: on the ninth day the Factor goes to see him. Unless someone has given him a reason to live, on
  // the tenth night he walks down the Throat Stair into the full basin.
  Relation quirePressed(place). Relation quireHope(group). Relation quireDrowned(place). Relation quireWillConfess(group).
  Rule quire_pressed when night(ossel) >= 9 and hour(clock) == 11 and not quirePressed(ossel) { Assert quirePressed(ossel). }
  Observe quire_after at exchequer_room when quirePressed(ossel) and not quireDrowned(ossel) and not quireHope(quire) "Quire has not slept. The bottle is empty. 'The Factor came,' he says to you, or to the room. 'She sat in that chair and told me what would happen to me when the Board learns what I signed. Very kindly. She brought eels.'".
  Topic quire_hope with quire "Tell the Treasurer that the called are alive, and that the debt can still be paid" when knows(actor, held_alive) and knows(actor, promise_weight) and quireConfided(actor) and not quireHope(quire) and not quireDrowned(ossel) once {
    Says "Quire stares at you. 'Alive,' he says. 'Asleep. All of them.' He takes his spectacles off, and puts them on, and takes them off. 'And if the Board keeps the promise, they come home.' He stands up, too fast, and holds the desk. 'Then somebody has to tell the Board why. And it has to be the man who signed.' He looks at the empty strongboxes along the wall. 'I'll do it. On the thirteenth day, in front of all of them. It will finish me. Good.'".
    On discuss { Assert quireHope(quire). Assert quireWillConfess(quire). }
  }
  Rule quire_walks when night(ossel) == 10 and hour(clock) == 4 and quirePressed(ossel) and not quireHope(quire) and not quireDrowned(ossel) {
    Assert quireDrowned(ossel). Retract at(quire, exchequer_room). }
  Rule quire_found when quireDrowned(ossel) and not knows(party, quire_dead)
    and inTessary() says "Word goes along the Tidewall in the morning: the Treasurer went down the Throat Stair before dawn, into the full basin, with his coat buttoned. The fishermen brought him up at the ebb. In his coat was a list of a hundred and thirty-eight names." teaches quire_dead { }
  Discovery quire_dead "Treasurer Quire drowned himself at the Throat on the tenth night, with the list of the called in his coat.".

  // 5. Councillor Pell's chair, and Orme's: the Board as it stands, and what can move it on the thirteenth day.
  // 6. The attempt on Marrable, the night before the eleventh ebb, if the vote looks as if it might pass.
  Measure support(place). Relation marrableHurt(place). Relation marrableGuarded(place). Relation attemptMade(place).
  Query looksLikely() means quireWillConfess(quire) or amauryWillTestify(party) or carries(party, sault_letter) or at(plum, terraces) or plumHome(ossel).
  Rule attempt_on_marrable when night(ossel) == 10 and hour(clock) == 23 and looksLikely() and not attemptMade(ossel) and at(lightermen, ?p) {
    Assert attemptMade(ossel). Retract at(lightermen, ?p). Assert at(lightermen, marrable_room). }
  Rule attempt_succeeds when attemptMade(ossel) and at(lightermen, marrable_room) and hour(clock) == 0 and not at(party, marrable_room)
    and not marrableGuarded(ossel) and not marrableHurt(ossel) and able(lightermen) {
    Assert marrableHurt(ossel). Retract at(lightermen, marrable_room). Assert at(lightermen, warehouse_floor). }
  Rule attempt_guarded when attemptMade(ossel) and at(lightermen, marrable_room) and hour(clock) == 0 and marrableGuarded(ossel) and not at(party, marrable_room) {
    Retract at(lightermen, marrable_room). Assert at(lightermen, warehouse_floor). Assert attemptFoiled(ossel). }
  Relation attemptFoiled(place).
  Rule attempt_foiled_told when attemptFoiled(ossel) and inTessary() and not knows(party, attempt_foiled_known)
    says "Word in the morning: three men came to Councillor Marrable's door in the night, and found four veterans of the Third on her step, and went away again." teaches attempt_foiled_known { }
  Discovery attempt_foiled_known "The Factor's lightermen came for Councillor Marrable in the night and found her step guarded.".
  Rule attempt_met at marrable_room when attemptMade(ossel) and at(lightermen, marrable_room) and at(party, marrable_room) and not assails(lightermen, party) and able(lightermen)
    says "Boots on the step, and the door goes in. Three big men in salt-stiff jerkins, with cudgels, who stop when they see that Marrable is not alone." {
    Assert assails(lightermen, party). }
  Rule marrable_hurt_told when marrableHurt(ossel) and not knows(party, marrable_beaten)
    and inTessary() says "Word comes up from the Terraces in the morning: Councillor Marrable was beaten in her own house in the night, by men nobody saw the faces of. She is alive. She will not be at the Board on the thirteenth day." teaches marrable_beaten { }
  Discovery marrable_beaten "Councillor Marrable was beaten in her house the night before the eleventh ebb, and will not be able to speak at the Board.".
  Topic ask_guard with durrance "Ask Durrance to put some of the Third on Councillor Marrable's step" when not heldNow(durrance) and not marrableGuarded(ossel) and night(ossel) < 11 and (knows(actor, sault_bid) or knows(actor, note_designed) or durranceKnowsSold(durrance)) once {
    Says "'Ysbel Marrable?' says Durrance. 'She carried me off the field at Galt with one arm.' She turns on the bench and whistles, and four of the Third look up from four pots. 'Councillor Marrable's step,' she says. 'Nights. Till the Board sits. Nobody goes in that isn't asked.' They go.".
    On discuss { Assert marrableGuarded(ossel). }
  }

  // 7. The riot: the night before the vote, the Factor's men among the veterans at the Exchequer and up the Terrace
  // Steps, unless Fisk will not lead them, or someone the Muster listens to stands them down.
  Relation fiskTurned(group). Relation riotHappened(place). Relation riotCalmed(place). Relation riotGathering(place).
  Topic turn_fisk with fisk "Tell Fisk what the Factor means to do with the Muster" when knows(actor, sault_bid) and not fiskTurned(fisk) once {
    Says "Fisk's grin goes. He reads it twice in your face. 'Own us,' he says. 'With a note. Like a debt.' He takes the new coat off and looks at it. 'She knew my name before I knew hers.' He drops the coat on the floor. 'There's a thing she wants done the night before the Board sits. Lads up the Terrace Steps with torches, shouting. She said it'd show the Board what eight thousand angry soldiers look like.' He shakes his head. 'Not me. Not now. And I'll tell the others why.'".
    On discuss { Assert fiskTurned(fisk). Retract serves(fisk, sault). }
  }
  Rule riot_gathers when night(ossel) == 12 and hour(clock) == 20 and not fiskTurned(fisk) and not riotGathering(ossel) and not voted(ossel) and at(fisk, ?p) {
    Assert riotGathering(ossel). Retract at(fisk, ?p). Assert at(fisk, scriveners_row). }
  Observe riot_scene at scriveners_row when riotGathering(ossel) and not riotHappened(ossel) and not riotCalmed(ossel) "The Row is full of soldiers. Two hundred of them, more, in red coats, with torches, and more coming up from the Withies. Fisk is on a scrivener's desk shouting about the Board. The crowd is not quite a mob yet. It is waiting for something to make it one.".
  Action calm_riot(actor: group, site: place) "Get up on a desk beside Fisk and talk the Muster down" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, scriveners_row) and riotGathering(ossel)
      and not riotHappened(ossel) and not riotCalmed(ossel) and not triedCalming(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert riotCalmed(ossel). }
    On failure { Assert triedCalming(actor). }
    Result "You tell them what is true: that the Board will vote tomorrow, and that if soldiers go up the Terraces tonight with torches, Orme and old Lisle will vote no out of fright, and the Factor knows it, and that is why they are here. It takes a long time, and some of them shout you down, and then one of them says, 'That's right,' and then a lot of them say it. By midnight the Row is empty, and the torches are going home through the Withies in twos and threes.".
    Otherwise "You get up on the desk and they shout you off it.".
  }
  Relation triedCalming(group).
  Action durrance_stands_down(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Durrance to stand the Muster down" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, scriveners_row) and riotGathering(ossel)
      and not riotHappened(ossel) and not riotCalmed(ossel) and travelsWith(durrance, actor) and not serves(durrance, sault).
    On success { Assert riotCalmed(ossel). }
    Result "Durrance does not get up on anything. She walks into the middle of the Row and says, not very loudly, 'Third Company. Fall in.' And they do, the ones who were Third, from all over the crowd, and the ones who were not stop to watch. She looks at them for a long time. 'Go home,' she says. 'The Board sits tomorrow. Let them do their own dirty work.' And they go.".
  }
  Rule riot_breaks when riotGathering(ossel) and hour(clock) == 23 and not riotCalmed(ossel) and not riotHappened(ossel) {
    Assert riotHappened(ossel). }
  Rule riot_told when riotHappened(ossel) and not knows(party, riot_known)
    and inTessary() says "In the night the soldiers went up the Terrace Steps with torches, two hundred of them, shouting for the Board. Somebody threw a stone through the Council House window. Nobody was killed. By morning the Terraces are full of the Watch, and the Board is frightened, which is what somebody wanted." teaches riot_known { }
  Discovery riot_known "On the night before the vote soldiers went up the Terrace Steps with torches and broke the Council House windows. The Board is frightened.".
  Rule riot_ends when riotCalmed(ossel) and at(fisk, scriveners_row) { Retract at(fisk, scriveners_row). Assert at(fisk, drum_taproom). }
  Rule riot_over when riotHappened(ossel) and at(fisk, scriveners_row) and night(ossel) >= 13 { Retract at(fisk, scriveners_row). Assert at(fisk, muster_hall). }

  // ── The Board sits ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // On the thirteenth day, from ten in the morning to two in the afternoon, the Board of Moieties hears the question of
  // the Veterans' Settlement. Whoever is in the chamber may lay before it what they have.
  Person board "the Board of Moieties" at council_chamber {
    Role "the councillors in their carved seats". Ancestry human. Numbers 1. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Seen when inSession().
  }
  Query inSession() means night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 14 and not voted(ossel).
  Rule sault_sits when inSession() and at(sault, sault_office) { Retract at(sault, sault_office). Assert at(sault, council_chamber). }
  Rule sault_leaves when not inSession() and at(sault, council_chamber) { Retract at(sault, council_chamber). Assert at(sault, sault_office). }
  Rule marrable_sits when inSession() and at(marrable, marrable_room) and not marrableHurt(ossel) { Retract at(marrable, marrable_room). Assert at(marrable, council_chamber). }
  Rule marrable_home when not inSession() and at(marrable, council_chamber) { Retract at(marrable, council_chamber). Assert at(marrable, marrable_room). }
  Observe session_scene at council_chamber when inSession() "The Board of Moieties is sitting. Seven of the eight carved seats are full; the Salt chair is Factor Sault's, and she sits in it with her arms folded, eating nothing for once. Councillors Greaves and Vantage, the furniture, in velvet. Old Lisle asleep or nearly. Haverick of Paper, red-eyed. Orme of Ship, doing sums on his cuff. Dauntry of Rope, looking at Sault. The public bench is full of red coats. The Speaker is reading the question aloud, slowly, as if hoping it will go away.".
  Observe session_marrable at council_chamber when inSession() and at(marrable, council_chamber) "Ysbel Marrable stands at the Eel chair with her pinned sleeve, waiting her turn to speak, and when it comes she speaks for a quarter of an hour without notes, and does not raise her voice once.".
  Observe session_empty_eel at council_chamber when inSession() and marrableHurt(ossel) "The Eel chair is empty. Everybody looks at it and nobody mentions it.".
  Relation boardSawList(place). Relation boardSawTerms(place). Relation boardSawBid(place). Relation amauryTestified(place).
  Relation quireConfessed(place). Relation plumHome(place). Relation saultExposed(place).
  Action lay_list(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Board what is on the Treasurer's list" {
    Time 1. Speaker board.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(board, site) and inSession() and knows(actor, council_knows)
      and not boardSawList(ossel).
    On success { Assert boardSawList(ossel). }
    Result "You tell them: a hundred and thirty-eight names, in the Treasurer's own hand, each with an address and a sum of money sent to the family every month since the summer. Nobody sends money to the mothers of deserters. Orme stops doing sums on his cuff. Haverick looks at Greaves. Greaves looks at the ceiling.".
  }
  Action lay_terms(actor: group, site: place) "Read the Board the terms of the War Note" {
    Time 1. Speaker board.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(board, site) and inSession() and knows(actor, note_terms)
      and not boardSawTerms(ossel).
    On success { Assert boardSawTerms(ossel). }
    Result "You read them the terms. The calling of the oath of Hethra. The Muster as surety. Silver monthly. The principal at the Feast, in a kept promise of equal weight. When you come to the signatures, three of the councillors in the room are on it, and they know it, and the public bench knows it by the time you have finished the sentence. The noise from the red coats is like surf.".
  }
  Action lay_bid(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Board the Factor's letter" {
    Time 1. Speaker board.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(board, site) and inSession() and carries(actor, sault_letter)
      and not boardSawBid(ossel).
    On success { Assert boardSawBid(ossel). Assert saultExposed(ossel). }
    Result "You read them the Factor's letter: I will take up the note and with it the Muster, and Tessary will be governed by someone who can count. Factor Sault does not interrupt. When you have finished she stands up, quite unhurried, and looks round the chamber at each of them, and at the public bench. 'Every word,' she says. 'Somebody should.' And walks out. Dauntry of Rope sits for a moment, and then, very slowly, as if testing whether it is allowed, takes his eyes off her empty chair.".
  }
  Event amaury_testifies at council_chamber when inSession() and amauryWillTestify(party) and not amauryTestified(ossel) "The doors open and the King of Hethra comes in between two guards, in a plain coat, and walks up to the painting of the Kneeling and stands under it. 'I am told,' he says to the Board, pleasantly, 'that this city has been paying for my knees.' And he tells them about the hand on the back of his neck, and the oath of his house, and the silver, and when he has done the Speaker has to call for order three times." then {
    Assert amauryTestified(ossel). }
  Event quire_confesses at council_chamber when inSession() and quireWillConfess(quire) and not quireConfessed(ossel) and not quireDrowned(ossel) "Treasurer Quire gets up from the officers' bench, where he is not supposed to speak, and speaks. 'I signed it,' he says. 'Twelve years ago. So did you, Greaves, and you, Vantage, and Dauntry. We put the Muster up as surety for a miracle, and the miracle came, and the bill has come after it.' He puts his list on the Speaker's table. 'Those men are not deserters. They are asleep under the sea, and if this Board keeps its promise to them, they come home. If it does not, the rest follow them.' He sits down. He is shaking. Nobody looks at him." then {
    Assert quireConfessed(ossel). Assert boardSawList(ossel). }
  Rule quire_at_board when inSession() and quireWillConfess(quire) and at(quire, exchequer_room) { Retract at(quire, exchequer_room). Assert at(quire, council_chamber). }
  Rule quire_back when not inSession() and at(quire, council_chamber) { Retract at(quire, council_chamber). Assert at(quire, exchequer_room). }
  Rule amaury_comes when inSession() and amauryWillTestify(party) and at(amaury, kings_rooms) { Retract at(amaury, kings_rooms). Assert at(amaury, council_chamber). }
  Rule amaury_back when not inSession() and at(amaury, council_chamber) { Retract at(amaury, council_chamber). Assert at(amaury, kings_rooms). }

  // Haverick's goose, home.
  Person haverick "Lucius Haverick" at terraces {
    Role "who sits for the Paper Moiety on the Board, distraught". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
  }
  Topic haverick_goose with haverick "Ask Councillor Haverick what the matter is" when not plumHome(ossel) once {
    Says "'Plum,' says Councillor Haverick. 'Mistress Plum. A goose, sir, a white goose of the old Paper strain, the last of her line. Taken off my lawn on the night of the Muster's homecoming, by persons. I have posted a reward. I have posted three.' He wipes his eyes. 'People think it absurd. A goose. I have no children, sir. I have a goose.'".
  }
  Event plum_home near haverick when following(plum, party) and at(party, terraces) and at(haverick, terraces) and at(plum, ?p) "Mistress Plum sees Councillor Haverick across the Terraces and goes for him at a run, wings out, honking like a wagon with a bad axle, and he goes down on his knees in his good stockings and gathers her up, and she bites him on the ear, and he weeps. 'Anything,' he says to you, over her. 'Anything at all. Name it.' And then, before you can: 'The Settlement? The Paper chair will vote for it. Plum would want me to. She has a great respect for soldiers.'" then {
    Assert plumHome(ossel). Retract following(plum, party). Retract at(plum, ?p). Assert at(plum, terraces). }

  // The count, at two in the afternoon, in one breath.
  Relation counting(place).
  Rule vote_begins when night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) == 14 and not voted(ossel) and not counting(ossel) {
    Assert counting(ossel). Set support(ossel) to 2. }
  Rule vote_marrable when counting(ossel) and marrableHurt(ossel) { Decrease support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_marrable(ossel). }
  Rule vote_plum when counting(ossel) and plumHome(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_plum(ossel). }
  Rule vote_list when counting(ossel) and boardSawList(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_list(ossel). }
  Rule vote_terms when counting(ossel) and boardSawTerms(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_terms(ossel). }
  Rule vote_quire when counting(ossel) and quireConfessed(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_quire(ossel). }
  Rule vote_amaury when counting(ossel) and amauryTestified(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_amaury(ossel). }
  Rule vote_bid when counting(ossel) and boardSawBid(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_bid(ossel). }
  Rule vote_riot when counting(ossel) and riotHappened(ossel) { Decrease support(ossel) by 2. Assert counted_riot(ossel). }
  Relation counted_marrable(place). Relation counted_plum(place). Relation counted_list(place). Relation counted_terms(place).
  Relation counted_quire(place). Relation counted_amaury(place). Relation counted_bid(place). Relation counted_riot(place).
  Rule vote_carried when counting(ossel) and support(ossel) >= 5 {
    Retract counting(ossel). Assert voted(ossel). Assert votePassed(ossel). }
  Rule vote_lost when counting(ossel) and support(ossel) < 5 {
    Retract counting(ossel). Assert voted(ossel). }
  Rule vote_carried_told when votePassed(ossel) and inTessary() and not knows(party, vote_known)
    says "At two in the afternoon the Board of Moieties votes on the Veterans' Settlement. The bell on the Council House rings, and goes on ringing, and down in the Withies people come out onto the boardwalks to listen, and somebody shouts, and then everybody does. Land and a pension for every soldier who came home. Carried." teaches vote_known { }
  Rule vote_lost_told when voted(ossel) and not votePassed(ossel) and inTessary() and not knows(party, vote_known)
    says "At two in the afternoon the Board of Moieties votes on the Veterans' Settlement, and the Council House bell does not ring. The question is lost. There is no money, says the Speaker's notice on the Landgate board, and the city will not make promises it cannot keep. Under it, by evening, someone has pasted the old recruiting bill: LAND AND A PENSION FOR EVERY MAN WHO COMES HOME." teaches vote_known { }
  Discovery vote_known "The Board of Moieties has voted on the Veterans' Settlement.".

  // ── The Seal ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A Settlement voted is not a Settlement kept: eight thousand deeds must pass under the Great Seal. The night the
  // vote is carried, the Factor's men come for it.
  Relation sealStolen(place). Relation sealGuarded(place). Relation sealTried(place).
  Item great_seal "the Great Seal of Tessary" is seal_kind at seals_inner.
  Kind seal_kind "a disc of dark bronze the size of a plate" is treasure worth 0 weighing 4
    described "The Great Seal of Tessary: a pair of scales over a wave, and round the rim, in old letters, WHAT IS SEALED IS DONE.".
  Initially Assert owns(deckle, great_seal).
  Topic deckle_warned with deckle "Warn the Keeper that the Factor's men will come for the Seal tonight" when votePassed(ossel) and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not sealTried(ossel) and (knows(actor, sault_bid) or knows(actor, riot_known) or knows(actor, marrable_beaten)) once {
    Says "Deckle looks at you as if you had suggested the sea might come in. 'The Seal,' he says, 'has not left this room in three hundred years.' Then he looks at the bell glass, and at the door, which has a lock a child could open. 'The Watch is the Factor's,' he says slowly. 'Everybody knows that.' He sits down. 'I shall sit up with it. I shall sit up with it myself. And if you know anyone who would sit up with me, who carries something heavier than a pen...'".
    On discuss { Assert deckleWarned(deckle). }
  }
  Relation deckleWarned(group).
  Topic ask_guard_seal with durrance "Ask Durrance to put a guard on the Office of Seals tonight" when votePassed(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not sealTried(ossel) and not serves(durrance, sault) once {
    Says "'The Seal,' says Durrance. 'Of course. She'll not let a vote stop her.' She is already on her feet. 'Six of the Third, inside the Office, round the Keeper's table. They can sleep in the morning. They've slept in worse.'".
    On discuss { Assert sealGuarded(ossel). }
  }
  Topic fisk_guard_seal with fisk "Ask Fisk to get some of the lads round the Office of Seals tonight" when votePassed(ossel) and fiskTurned(fisk) and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not sealTried(ossel) once {
    Says "'The Seal,' says Fisk, and laughs. 'That's where she'll go, isn't it. Course it is. Eight thousand deeds and not one of them worth the paper without it.' He is already pulling on his old coat, the red one. 'I know every lad she's paying. I'll have the ones she isn't in the Keeper's room by dark, and the ones she is can come and try it.'".
    On discuss { Assert sealGuarded(ossel). }
  }
  Topic marrable_guard_seal with marrable "Ask Councillor Marrable to put a guard on the Seal tonight" when votePassed(ossel) and not marrableHurt(ossel) and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not sealTried(ossel) and (knows(actor, sault_bid) or knows(actor, riot_known) or knows(actor, marrable_beaten)) once {
    Says "Marrable looks at you for a moment, and then at her one hand. 'She'll go for it tonight,' she says. 'Of course she will.' She stands. 'The Eel Moiety has boatmen who have never once in their lives done what the Watch told them. I'll have six of them in the Keeper's room by dark, with oars.'".
    On discuss { Assert sealGuarded(ossel). }
  }
  Rule seal_raid when votePassed(ossel) and night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) == 23 and not sealTried(ossel) and able(lightermen) and at(lightermen, ?p) {
    Assert sealTried(ossel). Retract at(lightermen, ?p). Assert at(lightermen, seals_inner). }
  Rule seal_raid_met at seals_inner when sealTried(ossel) and at(lightermen, seals_inner) and at(party, seals_inner) and not assails(lightermen, party) and able(lightermen) and not sealStolen(ossel)
    says "The door of the Keeper's room is forced from the hall side. Three lightermen, cudgels out, who had expected an old man." {
    Assert assails(lightermen, party). }
  Rule seal_taken when sealTried(ossel) and at(lightermen, seals_inner) and hour(clock) == 0 and not at(party, seals_inner)
    and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not sealHidden(ossel) and able(lightermen) and at(great_seal, seals_inner) {
    Assert sealStolen(ossel). Retract at(great_seal, seals_inner). Assert inside(great_seal, sault_strongbox).
    Retract at(lightermen, seals_inner). Assert at(lightermen, warehouse_floor). }
  Rule seal_bed when sealTried(ossel) and at(lightermen, seals_inner) and hour(clock) == 0 and sealHidden(ossel) and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not at(party, seals_inner) {
    Retract at(lightermen, seals_inner). Assert at(lightermen, warehouse_floor). Assert sealRaidFoiled(ossel). }
  Rule seal_kept when sealTried(ossel) and at(lightermen, seals_inner) and hour(clock) == 0 and sealGuarded(ossel) and not at(party, seals_inner) {
    Retract at(lightermen, seals_inner). Assert at(lightermen, warehouse_floor). Assert sealRaidFoiled(ossel). }
  Relation sealRaidFoiled(place).
  Rule seal_kept_told when sealRaidFoiled(ossel) and inTessary() and not knows(party, seal_kept_known)
    says "In the night three lightermen broke into the Office of Seals and found the Keeper's room full of people who had been waiting up for them, and left faster than they came." teaches seal_kept_known { }
  Discovery seal_kept_known "The Factor's lightermen tried for the Great Seal in the night and were driven off.".
  Rule seal_stolen_told when sealStolen(ossel) and not knows(party, seal_gone)
    and inTessary() says "The Office of Seals does not open in the morning. The Keeper is sitting on the step in his nightshirt with his head in his hands: the Great Seal was taken in the night, and without it not one deed of the Settlement can be sealed." teaches seal_gone { }
  Discovery seal_gone "The Great Seal of Tessary was stolen the night after the vote. Without it the Settlement's deeds cannot be sealed.".
  Thing sault_strongbox "the Factor's strongbox" at sault_office {
    Holds.
    State locked closed "Behind the Factor's desk stands an iron strongbox the size of a dog kennel.".
    State open "The Factor's strongbox stands open.".
    Change pick "Pick the strongbox" from locked to open needing lockwork at sault_office.
  }
  Rule seal_back when sealStolen(ossel) and (keeps(deckle, great_seal) or at(great_seal, seals_inner)) { Retract sealStolen(ossel). Retract inside(great_seal, sault_strongbox). }
  Event seal_returned near deckle when keeps(deckle, great_seal) "The Keeper takes the Seal from you in both hands and holds it against his chest like a child that was lost in a market. Then he puts it under its glass, and rings for his clerks, and they come running, all of them, with their sleeves rolled up." then {
    Retract keeps(deckle, great_seal). Assert at(great_seal, seals_inner). }

  // The deeds: sealed through the fourteenth day if the vote passed and the Seal is under its glass. The deeds for the
  // held cannot be put into their hands in Tessary.
  Relation deedsSealed(place). Relation deedsDelivered(place).
  Rule deeds_sealed when votePassed(ossel) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 16 and not sealStolen(ossel) and at(great_seal, seals_inner) and not deedsSealed(ossel) {
    Assert deedsSealed(ossel). }
  Rule deeds_sealed_told when deedsSealed(ossel) and inTessary() and not knows(party, deeds_sealed_known)
    says "All day the Office of Seals has worked with its doors shut and every clerk in the Lettered Quarter borrowed; by four in the afternoon the last deed has passed under the Seal, and they begin carrying them out to the Withies in baskets, with the Muster's own sergeants calling the names. Land and a pension. A deed to every hand." teaches deeds_sealed_known { }
  Discovery deeds_sealed_known "The deeds of the Settlement have been sealed and given out.".
  Item held_deeds "the deeds of the held" is deeds_kind at seals_inner hidden until deeds_for_held.
  Kind deeds_kind "a casket of sealed deeds" is gear worth 0 weighing 3
    described "A cedar casket with a hundred and sixty-odd deeds in it, each sealed with the scales and the wave: land and a pension, made out to soldiers of the Long Muster who are not in Tessary to receive them.".
  Discovery deeds_for_held "The deeds made out to the held cannot be put into their hands in Tessary. They wait in a casket at the Office of Seals for whoever will carry them down.".
  Rule deeds_casket at seals_inner when deedsSealed(ossel) and not knows(party, deeds_for_held)
    says "On the Keeper's table, apart from the rest, stands a cedar casket. 'The deeds of the ones who are not here,' says Deckle. 'The Settlement says every hand. I cannot put these into a hand.' He looks at you. 'I am told that somebody may know where those hands are.'" teaches deeds_for_held { }
  Initially Assert lends(deckle, held_deeds, party).
  Action take_deeds(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Take the casket of the held's deeds from the Keeper" {
    Speaker deckle. Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(deckle, site) and knows(actor, deeds_for_held)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient) and at(held_deeds, site).
    Resolve acquire(held_deeds, deeds_kind, recipient).
    On success { Retract at(held_deeds, site). }
    Result "Deckle puts the casket in your arms. It is heavier than paper should be. 'Every hand,' he says. 'That is what it says. Every hand.'".
  }
  Rule deeds_word when deedsSealed(ossel) and not knows(party, deeds_word_known) and not at(party, seals_inner)
    and inTessary() says "A boy from the Office of Seals finds you: the Keeper asks for you. There is a casket of deeds that nobody in Tessary can deliver." teaches deeds_word_known { }
  Discovery deeds_word_known "The Keeper of the Seal has a casket of deeds for the held, and asks for you.".
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/strong:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The Strongrooms ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Under the Hall of Oaths, cut in the bedrock of the delta by people of the Mathematical Age: white stone that hums,
  // rooms that weigh whoever stands in them, and at the bottom the Balance, which makes a sworn promise binding in the
  // prima materium. The Scruples keep it. They were the drowned city's clerks; a thousand years beside the Balance have
  // made them pale, long-lived, unable to lie, and ruled like paper. Each pledged their name to it at birth.
  Place strongrooms "the Strongrooms" is site within ossel at 2, 0.
  Place sr_head "the stair-head" is level within strongrooms.
  Place sr_halls "the halls of the Scruples" is level within strongrooms.
  Place sr_deep "the deep rooms" is level within strongrooms.
  Place long_stair "the head of the Long Stair" is room within sr_head at 1, 0 underground.
  Place antechamber "the Antechamber of Weights" is room within sr_halls at 1, 0 underground.
  Place clerks_hall "the Hall of Clerks" is room within sr_halls at 1, 1 underground.
  Place archive "the Archive of Instruments" is room within sr_halls at 0, 1 underground.
  Place defaults_room "the Room of Defaults" is room within sr_halls at 0, 2 underground.
  Place dormitory "the standing dormitory" is room within sr_halls at 2, 1 underground.
  Place comptroller_office "the Comptroller's office" is room within sr_halls at 1, 2 underground.
  Place gallery "the Counterweight Gallery" is room within sr_deep at 1, 0 underground.
  Place weighing_chamber "the Weighing Chamber" is room within sr_deep at 1, 1 underground.

  Passage long_stair_way "the Long Stair" is stair between long_stair and antechamber taking 20 minutes.
  Passage ante_door "the inner door of the Antechamber" is doorway between antechamber and clerks_hall.
  Passage archive_arch "the archive arch" is arch between clerks_hall and archive.
  Passage defaults_door "the door of the Room of Defaults" is door between archive and defaults_room.
  Passage dorm_way "the dormitory passage" is doorway between clerks_hall and dormitory.
  Passage office_door "the Comptroller's door" is door between clerks_hall and comptroller_office.
  Passage counting_stair "the Counting Stair" is stair between clerks_hall and gallery.
  Passage chamber_door "the counterweight door" is door between gallery and weighing_chamber.

  Observe long_stair_scene at long_stair when true "Behind the black wall the dark is dry and smells of stone dust and, faintly, of hot metal. A stair goes down, straight and steep and very long, cut in white rock that gives back a little light of its own. You can hear a hum, below the edge of hearing, in your teeth.".
  Observe ante_scene at antechamber when true "A square white room with a floor of a single slab, smooth as a pond. When you step onto it the slab gives, very slightly, as a pan of a balance gives, and steadies. Around the walls ruled lines run at the height of a man's mouth, and as you speak they brighten along their length, and fade, as if writing down what was said. A notice in three scripts, one of them Tessarine: WHAT IS SAID HERE IS HELD.".
  Observe hall_scene at clerks_hall when true "A long white hall full of desks, and at the desks the Scruples, writing: forty or fifty of them in grey, pale as candles, the ruled lines on their hands and faces moving a little as they move. Nobody speaks above a murmur. The pens make a sound like rain. At the end of the hall a stair goes down; beside it, a door with the word COMPTROLLER cut over it, and nothing else.".
  Observe archive_scene at archive when true "Shelves to the ceiling, and the ceiling out of sight. On them, not books, but instruments: slabs, rolls, tablets, sheets of something like black glass, each with a tag. Every promise the Balance has ever held is here, the Scruples say, from the oath of a king to the bet of a fishwife. In the far wall, a door bound in iron with a single word on it in the ruled script, which you cannot read, and which nobody here looks at.".
  Observe defaults_scene at defaults_room when true "A small room, which is the surprise. After the archive's endless shelves, this is a cupboard: one table, one lamp that lights when you come in, one ledger. The ledger is thin. The Scruples do not record many defaults.".
  Observe dorm_scene at dormitory when true "The Scruples sleep standing. Rows of them along the walls in a dim room, eyes closed, hands folded, breathing very slowly and all together. Some have tags at their wrists, like the instruments in the archive. A very young Scruple at the end of a row has a book open under her folded hands.".
  Observe office_scene_c at comptroller_office when true "A white room with nothing in it but a desk, a chair that has never been sat in, and the Comptroller standing behind the desk. On the desk lies one sheet of black glass, ruled, which he has been reading for a very long time.".
  Observe gallery_scene at gallery when true "A gallery cut through the rock with the hum much louder here, a sound you feel in your breastbone. At the far end a door of white metal with no handle stands between two great pans hung on chains from the roof. One pan holds a block of lead cut with nine ruled lines. The other is empty, and the door does not open. Along the wall, on a rack, a set of brass weights, each with its number of lines. Over the door: NINE AGAINST NINE.".
  Observe chamber_scene_w at weighing_chamber when true "The Weighing Chamber is a nave, cut out of the bottom of the world. The Balance hangs in it from a beam lost in the dark overhead: two pans each the size of a fishing boat, and a pointer as tall as a mast at rest against a dial of ruled lines. In one pan, very small at the bottom of it, lies a single sheet of black glass. In the other are oaths: not things but the shapes of things, eight thousand faint warm shapes like breath on a cold window, each the size of a hand laid flat. Beyond the Balance, at the end of the nave, is a door with no frame, standing on its own, through which you can see a white floor going on for ever.".
  Observe chamber_level at weighing_chamber when not discharged(ossel) "The pointer leans a hair's breadth toward the black glass, and the oaths in the other pan stir now and then, like sleepers.".

  // ── The Scruples ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person scruples "the Scruples at their desks" at clerks_hall {
    Role "clerks of the Balance, writing". Ancestry human. Numbers 1. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
  }
  Topic scruples_asked with scruples "Ask the clerks at the desks what they are writing" when true once {
    Says "The nearest clerk finishes the line before looking up. 'Promises,' she says. 'As they are kept. A fishwife in the Withies has paid her rent. A ferryman has sworn to his wife on the Tideline Steps that he will not drink, and has drunk, and it is a small thing and the Balance has noted it. A great deal of the city stands on the old instruments without knowing it, you see. We write what is kept and what is not.' She dips her pen. 'Mostly it is not.'".
  }
  Person copyist "the Fourteenth Copyist" at clerks_hall {
    Role "a very young Scruple with ink on her ruled fingers and a bad habit of looking at the stair". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Wants chapbook.
  }
  Topic copyist_surface with copyist "Ask the Copyist about the surface" when true once {
    Says "The Copyist puts her pen down with enormous care. 'Is it true,' she says, very low, 'that up there people say things they do not mean? All the time? And nothing happens?' Before you can answer: 'Someone left a book in the Hall of Oaths with the silver once. Poems. In Tessarine. I have read it two hundred and eleven times.' She looks at the stair. 'There is one about a woman who promises to wait for a sailor and does not. And it is sad. And nobody unravels. I have never understood anything so well.'".
  }
  Relation copyistFriend(group).
  Event copyist_book near copyist when keeps(copyist, ?b) and itemKind(?b, chapbook) "The Copyist takes the chapbook in both hands and does not open it, as if it might go off. 'Twelve new ones,' she says. 'Twelve.' She puts it inside her coat, against her ruled skin. 'I am in your debt. I know exactly how much. If there is a door down here you need opened, I can file for it. I am very good at forms.'" then {
    Assert copyistFriend(party). }
  Discovery release_law "In the Scruples' law a promise is discharged in two ways: when it is kept, and when the one it was made to holds the promisor quit. A release freely given weighs as much as the keeping." {
    Known by copyist, comptroller, tally.
  }
  Topic copyist_release with copyist "Ask the Copyist how a promise can be discharged" when true once {
    Says "'Two ways,' says the Copyist promptly, as if reciting. 'Kept, or released. If I promise you a thing, and give it, it is kept. If I promise you a thing and you say to me, freely, I hold you quit of it, that is a release, and in the Balance it weighs the same as the keeping.' She frowns. 'People forget the second. It is in the first chapter. I think people stop reading after the first page.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, release_law). }
  }
  Discovery assembly_law "Any Scruple may indict another before the Assembly of the Scruples. The Assembly meets in the Weighing Chamber at the Settlement, and the Notary sits with it. It has happened twice in a thousand years.".
  Topic copyist_assembly with copyist "Ask the Copyist whether a Scruple can be called to account" when knows(actor, compact_read) once {
    Says "The Copyist goes quite still. 'An indictment,' she says. 'Before the Assembly. Any of us may bring one against any other, even the least against the greatest. It is in the second chapter.' She swallows. 'It has happened twice. The Assembly sits in the Weighing Chamber at a Settlement, and the Notary comes out of the Holding to sit with it, and what is found is found. Both times, the one indicted...' She stops, and makes a small gesture of something coming apart. 'Why do you ask?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, assembly_law). }
  }
  Action copyist_files(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Copyist to file for the Room of Defaults to be opened to you" {
    Speaker copyist. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(copyist, site) and copyistFriend(actor)
      and state(defaults_lock, locked).
    On success { Assert state(defaults_lock, open). }
    Result "The Copyist fills out a form requesting the form for a request, and then the request, and takes them up the hall to a desk, and from that desk to another, and comes back an hour later with the iron key on a ribbon. 'An inspection of records in the course of an inventory,' she says. 'The Ninth Assessor's inventory. They will not mind. They are very thorough.' She looks at the key. 'Nobody has asked to see that room in my lifetime.'".
  }

  // ── The weighing floor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What is said on the Antechamber's floor is held. A company that comes down from Tessary, where people swear about
  // everything, may say something it will have to keep.
  Relation sworeToFind(group).
  Action swear_find(actor: group, site: place) "Say, 'I'll find Davy Teazle if it kills me'" {
    Description "It is the kind of thing anyone says.".
    Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, antechamber) and knows(actor, davy_went)
      and not sworeToFind(actor) and heldNow(davy).
    On success { Assert sworeToFind(actor). Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "The ruled lines round the walls brighten all along their length, and hold, and fade. The floor under you dips a hair, and steadies. Somewhere far below, something has written it down.".
  }
  Observe swore_noted near tally when sworeToFind(party) and travelsWith(tally, party) and at(party, antechamber) "'That was held,' says the Assessor, looking at the walls. 'I would not have said if it kills me.'".

  // ── Lies to the Assessor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Assessor asked a promise of honesty at the Hall of Oaths; below, it is held.
  Relation askedEmployer(group). Relation keptFaith(group). Relation brokeFaith(group).
  Observe tally_asks near tally when travelsWith(tally, party) and at(party, antechamber) and hiredBySault(party) and not askedEmployer(party) "On the weighing floor the Assessor stops and turns to you. 'A question,' they say, 'which I should have asked above. Are you in anyone's employ in this matter?'".
  Action tell_tally_truth(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Assessor that Factor Sault hired you to find out who takes the veterans" {
    Speaker tally. Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, antechamber) and travelsWith(tally, actor)
      and hiredBySault(actor) and not askedEmployer(actor).
    On success { Assert askedEmployer(actor). Assert keptFaith(actor). }
    Result "The lines on the walls brighten and fade. 'The Factor of the Salt Moiety,' says the Assessor. 'Who carried the silver.' They write it down. 'Thank you. That cannot have been comfortable to say. I will remember that you said it here.'".
  }
  Action lie_to_tally(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Assessor that you are in no one's employ" {
    Speaker tally. Time 0.
    Grave "You promised the Assessor not to lie to them, and here what is said is held.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, antechamber) and travelsWith(tally, actor)
      and hiredBySault(actor) and not askedEmployer(actor).
    On success { Assert askedEmployer(actor). Assert brokeFaith(actor). Assert forswornParty(actor). }
    Result "The ruled lines round the walls go dark, all of them at once, and the floor under you drops a finger's breadth and does not come up. The Assessor looks at the walls, and at you. They do not say anything. They write something down, and close the ledger, and do not open it again for a long while.".
  }

  // ── The Room of Defaults ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing defaults_lock "the iron door" on defaults_door {
    State locked blocking "The door of the Room of Defaults is bound in iron and locked.".
    State open "The iron door of the Room of Defaults stands open.".
    Change pick "Pick the lock of the iron door" from locked to open needing lockwork at archive.
  }
  Action tally_opens(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Assessor to open the Room of Defaults in the course of the inventory" {
    Speaker tally. Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, archive) and travelsWith(tally, actor)
      and knows(actor, compact_read) and state(defaults_lock, locked) and not brokeFaith(actor).
    On success { Assert state(defaults_lock, open). }
    Result "The Assessor looks at the iron door for some time. 'The compact of the old city is not on my inventory,' they say. 'But the city of Tessary claims the old city's oaths as its heir, and so its defaults are the city's defaults, and so they bear on the collateral.' They lay a ruled hand flat on the iron, and the lock turns over inside the door with a sound like a slow bell. 'I find that I want to see it,' they say. 'I note that I want to.'".
  }
  Discovery default_record "The Room of Defaults records the drowned city's compact as broken eleven hundred years ago, in the Comptroller's own hand: 'The sea had the city. The ledger did not keep. Default entered by the clerk who swore it.' Beside the entry, in the same hand, a reckoning runs down the margin for a thousand years, and ends in fresh ink: 'Tessary, heir. War note drawn. Repayment set at a weight the heir cannot meet. At foreclosure, eight thousand oaths fall in, and the hole is closed.'" {
    Source defaults_ledger "the thin ledger on the table" at defaults_room readable by party.
  }
  Discovery note_designed "The War Note was drawn to fail. The Comptroller swore the drowned city's compact eleven hundred years ago and could not keep it; his default left a hole in the Balance's ledger. He set Tessary's repayment at a weight its heir could never meet, so that at foreclosure the Muster's oaths would fall into the Holding and fill the hole he made.".
  Observe designed_seen near party when knows(party, default_record) and knows(party, note_terms) and not knows(party, note_designed) "You read the reckoning again with the War Note in your head, and it is not a reckoning. It is a plan. The repayment was never meant to be made. A thousand years of trying to close one hole, and then, at last, a city poor enough and desperate enough to sign." teaches note_designed.
  Relation tallySawDefaults(place).
  Event tally_reads_defaults at defaults_room when travelsWith(tally, party) and knows(party, default_record) "The Assessor reads the ledger over your shoulder, and then reads it again, alone, with their finger on the lines, the way a child reads. When they straighten, the ruled lines on their face have gone faint, as if something had rubbed at them. 'He swore the compact,' they say. 'He did not keep it. And he has drawn the city's note so that it cannot be paid, so that the Muster will fall in and cover it.' A long pause. 'A promise made in order to be broken is not a promise. It is the first thing we are taught. It is the gravest thing one of us can do.' They close the ledger very gently. 'I do not know what I am going to do.'" then {
    Assert tallySawDefaults(ossel). }

  // ── The Counterweight Gallery ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The door to the Weighing Chamber opens when the empty pan is made to balance the nine-line lead: a test every
  // Scruple passes as a child. The brass on the rack is two, three, four and five.
  Thing door_pan "the empty pan" at gallery {
    Holds.
    State hanging "The empty pan hangs high on its chains, the lead's pan low.".
  }
  Initially Assert receptacle(door_pan).
  Kind brass_two "a brass weight of two lines" is gear worth 1 weighing 2 described "A flat brass weight with two ruled lines cut across it.".
  Kind brass_three "a brass weight of three lines" is gear worth 1 weighing 3 described "A flat brass weight with three ruled lines cut across it.".
  Kind brass_four "a brass weight of four lines" is gear worth 1 weighing 4 described "A flat brass weight with four ruled lines cut across it.".
  Kind brass_five "a brass weight of five lines" is gear worth 1 weighing 5 described "A flat brass weight with five ruled lines cut across it.".
  Item w_two "a brass weight of two lines" is brass_two at gallery.
  Item w_three "a brass weight of three lines" is brass_three at gallery.
  Item w_four "a brass weight of four lines" is brass_four at gallery.
  Item w_five "a brass weight of five lines" is brass_five at gallery.
  Query panBalanced() means (inside(w_four, door_pan) and inside(w_five, door_pan) and not inside(w_two, door_pan) and not inside(w_three, door_pan))
    or (inside(w_two, door_pan) and inside(w_three, door_pan) and inside(w_four, door_pan) and not inside(w_five, door_pan)).
  Thing counter_door "the white door" on chamber_door {
    State shut blocking "The white door between the pans has no handle, and does not open.".
    State open "The white door stands open, the pans level on their chains.".
  }
  Rule door_balances at gallery when panBalanced() and state(counter_door, shut)
    says "The empty pan sinks, slowly, and the lead rises to meet it, and the two hang level. The pointer between them settles on its mark. Without any sound, the white door opens." { Assert state(counter_door, open). }
  Rule door_unbalances when not panBalanced() and state(counter_door, open) and not chamberOpened(ossel) { Assert state(counter_door, shut). }
  Relation chamberOpened(place).
  Observe pan_wrong at gallery when not panBalanced() and inside(?w, door_pan) "The pan has something in it, and has moved, but the pointer between the pans has not come to its mark.".

  // The Weights: bailiffs of stone and bronze, who seize the forsworn and those in default.
  Species weight_kind "a Weight" like bronze_construct temperament obedient
    described "A figure of bronze and white stone twice the height of a man, with a pair of scales cast into its chest where a heart would be. It does not move unless something is owed.".
  Person weights "the Weights" at gallery {
    Role "two bailiffs of bronze and white stone, standing either side of the door". Species weight_kind. Level 6. Numbers 2. Pronouns they.
  }
  Initially Assert tolerates(weights, party).
  Initially Assert peaceable(weights).
  Rule weights_seize when forswornParty(party) and at(party, ?p) and at(weights, ?p) and peaceable(weights)
    says "The Weights turn their heads, both together, with a grinding of bronze. The scales in their chests have tipped." {
    Retract peaceable(weights). Retract tolerates(weights, party). Assert assails(weights, party). }

  // ── The Comptroller ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Eldest of the Scruples. He swore the drowned city's compact, and has kept the ledger for eleven hundred years
  // since he failed to keep his word. He cannot lie. He can choose what to say.
  Person comptroller "the Comptroller" at comptroller_office {
    Role "eldest of the Scruples, very tall and very thin, the ruled lines on his face so close they look like shading". Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 9. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "The Comptroller looks up from the black glass. His eyes are the colour of old paper. 'You have come down,' he says, 'from the debtor's city. Very well. You may ask.'".
  }
  Topic comptroller_note with comptroller "Ask the Comptroller about the War Note" when true once {
    Says "'A loan,' says the Comptroller. 'The city wished to call an oath its predecessors were owed. It could not pay for the calling. We lent it, against security, as is our office.' He touches the black glass. 'Every promise the Balance holds is a thread in the fastening of things. When one is called, the ledger is drawn down by its weight, and the weight must be restored, or the fastening slackens. You have heard, I suppose, that the planes were fastened apart. This is one of the places where they were fastened. I am not concerned with your city's poverty. I am concerned with the ledger.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, note_terms). }
  }
  Relation comptrollerAlly(group). Relation brokerSuspended(place).
  Topic comptroller_bid with comptroller "Tell the Comptroller that the Factor means to buy the note" when knows(actor, sault_bid) and not comptrollerAlly(actor) once {
    Says "For the first time the Comptroller looks at you directly. 'Buy it,' he says. 'At foreclosure.' The ruled lines on his face tighten. 'It is lawful. A note in default may be taken up by whoever pledges its weight. And then the holder may call the collateral out, to service as sworn, and the oaths leave the Holding, and the weight with them.' He is silent a while. 'That must not happen. Bring me what she has written, in her hand, and I will suspend the broker she has suborned. Whatever else she does, she will have to do in person, in this chamber, on the night.' He bows very slightly. 'In this, we want the same thing.'".
    On discuss { Assert comptrollerAlly(actor). }
  }
  Event broker_suspended near comptroller when keeps(comptroller, sault_letter) "The Comptroller reads the Factor's letter once, and lays it on the black glass, and the glass takes it, the way still water takes a dropped page. 'The Broker of the Fourth Pan is suspended,' he says. 'If the Factor wants the note, she will come to the Weighing Chamber on the night of the Settlement and pledge in person.' He looks at you. 'Thank you. The ledger is in your debt. I do not say that often.'" then {
    Assert brokerSuspended(ossel). }
  Relation durranceSpared(place). Relation promisedLetter(group).
  Topic comptroller_spare with comptroller "Ask the Comptroller to strike Sergeant Durrance from the next page" when knows(actor, durrance_next) and night(ossel) < 8 and not durranceSpared(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'The page will be read,' says the Comptroller. 'Twelve oaths. The weight is the weight.' He considers you. 'But the order of the roll is a convenience, not a term. I can have the sergeant passed over. Elcock, who is next, will go in her place, and the one after Jessup in his.' He lets that sit. 'I will do it for a promise, made here, where it is held: that you will bring me, before the Settlement, the Factor's bid in her own hand.'".
  }
  Action promise_comptroller(actor: group, site: place) "Promise the Comptroller the Factor's letter before the Settlement, so that Durrance is passed over" {
    Speaker comptroller. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "A promise made to the Comptroller is held by the Balance. If it is not kept by the Feast, it is broken; and Elcock goes into the sea in Durrance's place.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(comptroller, site) and knows(actor, durrance_next)
      and night(ossel) < 8 and not durranceSpared(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and not keeps(comptroller, sault_letter).
    On success { Assert durranceSpared(ossel). Assert promisedLetter(actor). Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "The Comptroller takes a pen and writes one line on the black glass, and the glass takes the ink. 'Durrance, A., passed over,' he says. 'Elcock, R., to be called in her place.' He does not look up. 'Elcock is nineteen. He was a drummer. I mention it because you will want to know what you have done, and I do not say things that are not so.'".
  }
  Rule letter_promise_kept when promisedLetter(party) and keeps(comptroller, sault_letter) { Retract promisedLetter(party). Assert keptFaith(party). }
  Rule letter_promise_broken when promisedLetter(party) and feastEve() and hour(clock) >= 18
    says "Somewhere under the sea a line is drawn through a promise you made, and you feel it, exactly as if a cold hand had been laid flat between your shoulders and then taken away. The Comptroller's letter was not brought." {
    Retract promisedLetter(party). Assert forswornParty(party). }
  Topic comptroller_drowned with comptroller "Ask the Comptroller about the drowned city's compact" when knows(actor, compact_read) and not knows(actor, note_designed) once {
    Says "The Comptroller does not move at all. 'That is not a matter of the note,' he says. 'You will not find me willing to discuss it.' And then, because he cannot leave a false impression standing, and you see him know it: 'I do not say that there is nothing to discuss. I say that I will not discuss it.' He looks back down at the black glass. 'You may go.'".
  }
  Relation comptrollerConfronted(group). Relation silenceOffered(group). Relation swornSilence(group).
  Topic comptroller_confronted with comptroller "Put the reckoning in the Room of Defaults to the Comptroller" when knows(actor, note_designed) and not comptrollerConfronted(actor) once {
    Says "The Comptroller listens to the end. He cannot say it is not so, and he does not try. 'I swore the compact,' he says. 'I was younger than your Assessor. The sea came over the old city in one night and the ledger did not keep, and I wrote the default in my own hand, as one must.' He lays his hand on the black glass. 'For eleven hundred years there has been a hole in the ledger the size of a city, and through it the fastening has slackened, here, at this one place. On some nights the sea out there shows stars that are not ours. I have tried to fill it honestly. I have tried for a thousand years.' He looks up. 'Then your city came, poor, at war, desperate. I drew the note so that it would fail. Eight thousand oaths, held asleep and unharmed, against the fastening of the world. I would draw it again.'".
    On discuss { Assert comptrollerConfronted(actor). Assert silenceOffered(actor). }
  }
  Action swear_silence(actor: group, site: place) "Promise the Comptroller your silence, and take Davy Teazle out of the Holding for it" {
    Speaker comptroller. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "A promise of silence made here is held. If you speak of the reckoning to anyone after, you are forsworn.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(comptroller, site) and silenceOffered(actor)
      and not swornSilence(actor) and heldNow(davy) and not indictmentFiled(ossel).
    On success { Assert swornSilence(actor). Assert registered(actor). Assert redeemedByComptroller(davy). }
    Result "'Then it is held,' says the Comptroller, and writes on the black glass. 'Teazle, D., private, redeemed from the Holding by order of the Comptroller.' He does not look up. 'He will wake on the Tideline Steps at the next ebb with his boots beside him. Go home. You have done a good thing for one family, and nothing at all for the rest, and you knew that when you chose.'".
  }
  Relation redeemedByComptroller(group). Relation indictmentFiled(place).

}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/voices:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── Where people are in the day ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Factor eats her supper on the Tidewall every evening, from a paper cone, standing up; Wick works Lowtide at the
  // day's ebb with the other mudlarks.
  Rule sault_to_wall when hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 21 and at(sault, sault_office) and not inSession() and not feastEve() {
    Retract at(sault, sault_office). Assert at(sault, tidewall). }
  Rule sault_from_wall when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 18) and at(sault, tidewall) {
    Retract at(sault, tidewall). Assert at(sault, sault_office). }
  Observe sault_eels near sault when at(sault, tidewall) "Factor Sault is leaning on the parapet with a paper cone of hot eels, watching her ships come in on the evening tide, and nodding to every second person who passes. Most of them nod back.".
  Rule wick_to_forum when hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 14 and at(wick, withies) { Retract at(wick, withies). Assert at(wick, forum). }
  Rule wick_from_forum when (hour(clock) >= 14 or hour(clock) < 10) and at(wick, forum) { Retract at(wick, forum). Assert at(wick, withies). }
  Observe wick_digging near wick when at(wick, forum) "Wick is up to his knees in a drain at the edge of the square with a rake, a bucket and an expression of total professional absorption.".
  Observe wick_swept near wick when sweptOnce(party) and not knows(party, wick_teased) "Wick looks you up and down. 'You got rolled,' he says, delighted. 'Didn't you. Out through the Throat. Everybody does once.' He considers. 'Most people only once.'" teaches wick_teased.
  Discovery wick_teased "Wick knows you were caught by the flood.".

  // ── Sergeant Durrance, on the way ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Event durrance_forum at forum when travelsWith(durrance, party) "Durrance stands at the edge of the Forum and looks across it, the way she would look at a field before crossing it under fire. 'Out past the colonnade,' she says, 'across the Forum, into the Hall. Wick's route.' She sets off across the slabs in a straight line, not hurrying, as if she were walking it for someone.".
  Event durrance_hall at oath_court when travelsWith(durrance, party) and not benighted(party) "Durrance goes to the end wall and puts her hand flat on the black stone, the way she put it on the Stone in the Yard nineteen years ago, and takes it away again quickly, as if it were hot. 'Same stone,' she says. 'Same as the Yard.' She wipes her hand on her coat. 'Well. Now I know what I swore on.'".
  Event durrance_landing at landing when travelsWith(durrance, party) and at(slake, landing) "Durrance and Bettany Slake look at each other across the quay, two people who have each run something hard for a long time, and something like respect passes between them without either of them saying anything.".
  Event durrance_floor at antechamber when travelsWith(durrance, party) "Durrance looks at the ruled lines round the walls, and at the notice, and closes her mouth with a snap. 'Not a word,' she says, very quietly, and the lines brighten along their length at every syllable of it. She glares at them. After that she doesn't speak at all until you are off the floor.".
  Event durrance_chamber at weighing_chamber when travelsWith(durrance, party) "Durrance stands a long time looking up into the second pan, at the faint warm shapes of the oaths. 'That's us,' she says at last. 'Eight thousand.' She shakes her head. 'You'd think we'd weigh more.'".
  Event durrance_ranks at ranks when travelsWith(durrance, party) "Durrance walks slowly down the Third Company's file, saying the names under her breath as she passes each face. Pike. Haskett. Moll Bryer. The Lucey twins. She stops in front of a boy at the end, and straightens his collar, and goes on.".
  Event durrance_ranks_elcock at ranks when travelsWith(durrance, party) and elcockTaken(ossel) "At the end of the file Durrance stops in front of a thin boy with a drummer's calluses on his hands. 'Elcock,' she says. 'You never could keep time.' She stands there a while. Then she comes back, and does not say anything for some time.".
  Event durrance_yard at legion_yard when travelsWith(durrance, party) and not feastEve() "Durrance stops at the Yard gate and does not go any further. She looks at the Oath Stone across the empty parade ground for a long moment. 'Nineteen years,' she says. 'Come on. I don't like it here.'".

  // ── The Assessor, on the way ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Event tally_drum at drum_taproom when (travelsWith(tally, party) or at(tally, drum_taproom)) and not durranceCalled(ossel) and not heldBack(durrance) "The Assessor stands looking up at the drum over the bar with the black cloth tied over its head. 'That drum beat the Third Company's muster on the day it swore,' they say. 'The calling speaks to what an oath was sworn by: the stone, and the drum. I note that a cloth does not stop it.' A pause. 'I would not be surprised if it answered to the drum in other ways. I make no recommendation.'".
  Event tally_forum at forum when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Assessor stands in the middle of the Forum and turns slowly round, looking at everything. 'It is smaller than in the records,' they say. 'Everything is.' They bend and touch a paving slab with one ruled finger, very gently, as if it might mind.".
  Event tally_landing at landing when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Assessor looks at the ebb-runners' boat for a long time. 'The niche by the black wall,' they say. 'Where the silver was left. Every month for eleven years I took it out and weighed it and entered it. I did not think about who carried it.' They write something down.".
  Event tally_stone at legion_yard when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Assessor goes straight to the Oath Stone and lays a hand on it, and the fine ruled lines cut in its face brighten for a moment under their palm, and fade. 'An instrument of the Balance,' they say. 'Salvaged. The city does not know what it has. It swears its soldiers on it the way a child plays with a sword.'".
  Event tally_chapel at chapel when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Assessor walks slowly under the hanging weights, reading them. 'All accurate,' they say. Then they look up at the saint over the altar, holding his scales level, and stand quite still. 'There was a clerk who went up,' they say at last, 'when the old city drowned. We are told about him in the nursery. As a warning.' They look at the scales a while longer. 'I had not known he was a saint.'".
  Event tally_tags at tags when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Assessor walks down the avenue of tags with their eyes fixed straight ahead. 'I will not look for mine,' they say, before you can ask. 'One is not shown one's name.' They walk a little faster.".
  Event tally_ranks at ranks when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Assessor goes along the files with the ledger open, checking the faces against the names, as they have done in the Withies every day. Every one is there. When they reach the end they close the ledger and stand for a moment with their hand on it, and their face does something you have not seen it do before.".
  // "Wait here a minute."
  Relation tallyWaiting(place). Measure tallyWaitFrom(place). Measure tallyWaited(place).
  Action tally_wait(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Assessor to wait here a minute" {
    Speaker tally. Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and travelsWith(tally, actor) and not tallyWaiting(ossel).
    On success { Retract travelsWith(tally, actor). Assert at(tally, site). Assert willing(tally, actor). Assert tallyWaiting(ossel).
      Set tallyWaitFrom(ossel) to watch(clock) * 10. }
    Result "'A minute,' says the Assessor, and opens the ledger.".
  }
  Rule tally_rejoined when tallyWaiting(ossel) and travelsWith(tally, party) { Retract tallyWaiting(ossel). }
  Rule tally_counts when tallyWaiting(ossel) and perceives(party, tally) and watch(clock) * 10 - tallyWaitFrom(ossel) > 30 and tallyWaited(ossel) == 0 {
    Set tallyWaited(ossel) to watch(clock) * 10 - tallyWaitFrom(ossel). }
  Rule tally_says_minutes near tally when tallyWaiting(ossel) and tallyWaited(ossel) > 0
    says "'You said a minute,' says the Assessor, closing the ledger on their finger. 'It has been {tallyWaited(ossel)} minutes. I have noted it.' A pause. 'I do not mind. I note it because it is so.'" {
    Retract tallyWaiting(ossel). Set tallyWaited(ossel) to 0. }
  Rule tally_waits_quietly when tallyWaiting(ossel) and perceives(party, tally) and watch(clock) * 10 - tallyWaitFrom(ossel) <= 30 and tallyWaited(ossel) == 0 { Retract tallyWaiting(ossel). }

  // ── What the careless swear on the weighing floor costs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation foundDavy(group).
  Rule found_davy when sworeToFind(party) and at(party, ranks) and not foundDavy(party) { Assert foundDavy(party). Assert keptFaith(party). }
  Rule swear_unkept when sworeToFind(party) and matured(ossel) and not foundDavy(party) and heldNow(davy) and not forswornParty(party)
    says "Somewhere under the sea a line is drawn through something you said once on a white floor without thinking: I'll find Davy Teazle if it kills me. You did not find him. It did not kill you. The Balance does not care which part you meant." {
    Assert forswornParty(party). }

  // ── What the Factor does with what she is given ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // With the Assessor's pages she knows the roll order, and goes to Durrance two days sooner.
  Rule silver_offered_early when saultInformed(sault) and night(ossel) >= 3 and hour(clock) == 12 and not saultOffered(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) {
    Assert saultOffered(ossel). }
  // A Keeper warned takes the Seal to bed with him.
  Relation sealHidden(place).
  Rule seal_hidden when deckleWarned(deckle) and votePassed(ossel) and night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) == 22 and not sealHidden(ossel) and not sealGuarded(ossel) {
    Assert sealHidden(ossel). }

  // ── What the King knows of the war ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery salt_springs "What the war was fought for: the salt springs of Hethra on the upper Ossel, which make a white salt finer than anything from the Pans. Nobody in Tessary knows how to work them except, the King says, one person who has asked him about them twice.".
  Topic amaury_springs with amaury "Ask the King what the war was really for" when amauryPlayed(actor) or amauryWillTestify(actor) once {
    Says "'Salt,' says the King, as if it were obvious. 'The springs at Hethra-under-Fell. White salt, fine as flour; your Pans make grey. Your Board wanted them because they are worth more than the Pans. Your Factor wanted them because she understood that.' He moves a piece. 'She has written to me. Twice. Very civil letters, about the working of brine. She is the only person in this city who has asked me a sensible question in a year.' He smiles. 'If I were your Board I would be frightened of her. I am not your Board. I find her rather good company.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, salt_springs). }
  }
}

data/assembly/vocabulary.kyr:
Module assembly "What a world is made of, for assembling one" {
  Description "The assembler's commitments are facts in this vocabulary. Geography comes from region modules; kits add powers and what they do to the land. Facts are only ever added while a world is assembled.".
  Kind place. Kind group. Kind sitekind. Kind terrainkind. Kind kit.
  // Geography, read from region modules: areas (settlements, wild country, sites) and the rooms on the ways between.
  Relation region(place). Relation terrain(place, terrainkind). Relation company(group).
  Relation settlement(place). Relation wilds(place). Relation site(place, sitekind).
  Relation within(place, place).
  // A settlement's open middle, where news is heard and trouble arrives; and who keeps its inn.
  Relation square(place, place). Relation keeper(group, place).
  // A room on a road through wild country, a landmark travellers know, a narrow place a road cannot avoid.
  Relation waypoint(place). Relation landmark(place). Relation chokepoint(place). Relation onRoad(place).
  Relation siteKind(place, sitekind).
  Relation adjacent(place, place).
  // Hours between two places by the quickest known way.
  Measure hours(place, place).
  // Powers and their hold on the land.
  Relation power(group). Relation folk(group, entity).
  Relation holds(group, place). Relation raids(group, place). Relation ambushes(group, place).
  Relation tolls(group, place). Relation buysFrom(group, place). Relation serves(group, group).
  Relation buried(place, entity). Relation beneath(place, place).
  // The people a power acts through, as the modules that placed it name them: its chief, its fighting band.
  Relation chief(group, group). Relation band(group, group). Relation bountyOn(place, group).
  // A place given over to one placement's purpose; another kit does not take it.
  Relation taken(place, kit).
  Query free(p: place) means not taken(p, ?k).
  Goal false.
}

